INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(97,'MAIC:BX:00097',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,'extracellular acidification from conditioning pH 7.2/2 mM Ca2+ to pH 5.0 (proton activation; opening kinetics from excised outside-out patches) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 1.0','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,4.1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'4.1','ms','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OUTSIDE_OUT','Xenopus oocyte','Xenopus laevis oocyte (stage V-VI), hASIC1a',NULL,5.0,'110 mM NaCl, 2.0 mM CaCl2, 10 mM HEPES-NaOH (MES-NaOH for pH<6.8)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ASIC-00124','However, the opening time constant at pH5 of MTSET- modified V414C and N416C, measured from outside-out patches was not different from that of WT (5.2 ± 1.5 and 4.4 ± 1.6 ms, respectively, compared to 4.1 ± 1.0 ms, n=3), excluding this possibility.','Results, ''The movement of the lower palm determines the desensitization kinetics'', final paragraph','medium','stimulus_type as-printed: OTHER. WT comparator from the same sentence/n=3. Channel OPENING time constant (tau_act analog) at pH5, text-printed with n=3; verify-stage field for this paper was tau_inact (figure-only), these printed values are the opening (activation) constants, not desensitization. Proton-gated activation kinetics, not mechanical stimulus. Error statistic not stated (no SEM/SD label). MTSET rows: V414C/N416C Cys mutants after extracellular MTSET modification (positively charged adduct = mimic of charged side chain; the Arg-mutant mimic experiments carry no printed numerics). Patch holding potential for the outside-out experiments not stated (macroscopic TEVC in this paper was at -60 mV).','asic1a_human_oocyte_outsideout_ph5_openingtau_WT','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',85,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(98,'MAIC:BX:00098',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,'voltage step to -80 mV on cell-attached patch (intracellular w.r.t. pipette); pipette pressure series (negative/positive 5 and 10 in. H2O) applied as mechanosensitivity test | TEMPERATURE-AS-REPORTED: 19-21','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'3-5','pS','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','Xenopus oocyte','Xenopus laevis oocyte, alpha beta gamma rENaC (2.5 ng each subunit cRNA)',NULL,7.5,'ND-96 (96 mM NaCl, 1 MgCl2, 2 KCl, 1.8 CaCl2, 5 HEPES, pH 7.5)','ND-96 + 5 mM Ba++, 100 uM DIDS, 100 uM niflumic acid',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ASIC-00125','Cell-attached membrane patches were clamped to -80 mV, intracellular with respect to patch pipette. In ENaC-expressing oocytes, a channel with 3-5 pS conductance was observed with open and closed time constants on the order of seconds.','Results, single-channel analysis section (Fig. 13 area); solutions per Materials and Methods','high','stimulus_type as-printed: OTHER. ENaC mechano-controversy REBUTTAL paper — conductance rowed normally per round ruling; its negative-mechano conclusion is contest documentation, not a row: ''We conclude that alphabeta-gamma rENaC is not directly mechanosensitive when expressed in a system that can produce a channel with identical properties to those found in native epithelia'' (abstract) — channel activity unaffected by negative/positive pipette pressures of 5 in. H2O (Po ~0.35 under control, unchanged by pressure; 10 in. H2O also without effect, 5 further experiments), rebutting Ismailov 1996 bilayer alphabeta-gamma mechano-activation. As-printed RANGE value (3-5 pS, no single float, no error statistic). Open/closed time constants ''on the order of seconds'' = order-of-magnitude only, archived. mechano_gating_contested context: the 3-5 pS channel''s identity as rENaC rests on ENaC-expressing vs water-injected oocyte controls.','renaoc_abg_rat_oocyte_cell-attached_-80mV_unitary-gs',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',86,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(99,'MAIC:BX:00099',4,NULL,NULL,20,'flow-mediated laminar shear stress 0.12 dynes/cm2 via vertical pipette perfusion (1.5 ml/min), whole-cell Na+ current fit over first 40 s of LSS | STIMULUS: 0.12 dyn/cm2 | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 3.2 (sd)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,10600.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10.6',NULL,'SHEAR_STRESS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TEVC','Xenopus oocyte','Xenopus laevis oocyte, C. elegans DEG/ENaC degenerin channel complex',NULL,7.4,'NaCl-110 (110 mM NaCl, 2 mM KCl, 1.54 mM CaCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4)',NULL,-60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ASIC-00126','The dashed lines in c and d indicate the average values of the magnitude ( I LSS / I basal = 2.4 ± 0.6) and time constant (τ = 10.6 ± 3.2 s) of the LSS response in oocytes expressing MEC-4d.','Figure 6 legend (dashed reference line; values printed in legend text)','high','REPORTED UNIT IS S (10.6 s = 10600 ms): unit column left blank because the tau storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-printed. MEC-4d = MEC-4(A713T) gain-of-function degenerin-site mutant; ''MEC-4d group'' = cRNA mixture MEC-2 + MEC-6 + MEC-10 in the presence of MEC-4d (Fig 6 legend). Time constant of channel activation by LSS from exponential fit of the current increase within the first 40 s; mean ± S.D. throughout (Experimental procedures). n not printed for this group. Mechanogating attribution: direct LSS response of the heterologously expressed channel complex (not mutant epistasis). Values printed in figure legend, not main text. [s-unit tau_act: canonical tau_act_ms column expects ms — loader must convert (x1000) or route via schema_gap; flagged to avoid ms/s 1000x hazard]','mec-4d_A713T+mec-10+mec-2+mec-6_oocyte_tevc_lss0.12dyn_tau',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',87,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(100,'MAIC:BX:00100',4,NULL,NULL,20,'flow-mediated laminar shear stress 0.12 dynes/cm2 via vertical pipette perfusion (1.5 ml/min), whole-cell Na+ current fit over first 40 s of LSS | STIMULUS: 0.12 dyn/cm2 | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 1.7 (sd)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,4600.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'4.6',NULL,'SHEAR_STRESS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TEVC','Xenopus oocyte','Xenopus laevis oocyte, C. elegans DEG/ENaC degenerin channel complex',NULL,7.4,'NaCl-110 (110 mM NaCl, 2 mM KCl, 1.54 mM CaCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4)',NULL,-60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ASIC-00127','The dashed line indicates the average values of the magnitude ( I LSS / I basal ) and kinetics ( Tau ) of LSS response in oocytes expressing homomeric MEC-4d channels (no MEC-10: I LSS / I basal = 1.6 ± 0.5; τ = 4.6 ± 1.7 s).','Figure 1 legend (dashed reference line; values printed in legend text)','high','REPORTED UNIT IS S (4.6 s = 4600 ms): unit column left blank because the tau storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-printed. Homomeric MEC-4d channels (no MEC-10; MEC-2+MEC-6 present in cRNA mixture per Fig 1 legend); faster but diminished LSS response vs MEC-10-containing complex (I_LSS/I_basal 1.6±0.5). Mean ± S.D. n not printed. Values printed in figure legend, not main text. [s-unit tau_act: canonical tau_act_ms column expects ms — loader must convert (x1000) or route via schema_gap; flagged to avoid ms/s 1000x hazard]. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mec-4d_A713T_homomer_no-mec-10(+mec-2+mec-6)_oocyte_tevc_lss0.12dyn_tau',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',87,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(101,'MAIC:BX:00101',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,'fluid-jet LSS through vertical pipette above oocyte (1.6 ml/min) at 17°C; ENaC current isolated with 5 uM benzamil; biexponential (17/30/37 C) or monoexponential (25 C) fit of whole-cell current activation | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2.15 (sem)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,25900.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'25.9',NULL,'SHEAR_STRESS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TEVC','Xenopus oocyte','Xenopus laevis oocyte, wild-type mouse alpha-beta-gamma ENaC',17.0,7.4,'TEV solution (110 mM NaCl, 2 mM KCl, 1.54 mM CaCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4)','pipettes 3 M KCl',-60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ASIC-00128','Table 1. _Effects of temperature on parameters of ENaC activation by LSS_ | Temperature, °C | Delay, s | τ 1, s | τ 2, s | n | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ; | 17°C | 0.68±0.05[*](https://journals.physiology.org/doi/full/10.1152/ajprenal.00455.2006#T1FN1) | 25.90±2.15 | 1.21±0.34 | 15','Results, Table 1 ''Effects of temperature on parameters of ENaC activation by LSS'' (17°C row; values are means ± SE); methods per ''Two-electrode voltage clamp''','high','REPORTED UNIT IS S (25.9 s = 25900 ms): unit column left blank because the tau storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-printed. Fitted exponential time constant of ENaC activation by laminar shear stress (round ruling: ENaC shear tau table counts). tau1 = slow component, tau2 = fast component of the biexponential activation (I = c + a1*e^-t/tau1 + a2*e^-t/tau2); 25 C fit is monoexponential (single tau). Mean ± SE. Whole-cell TEVC macroscopic current kinetics of the heterologously expressed channel (not a composite tissue measure). Quote is the Table 1 header plus the temperature row as printed (markdown table with journal footnote links). [s-unit tau_act: canonical tau_act_ms column expects ms — loader must convert (x1000) or route via schema_gap; flagged to avoid ms/s 1000x hazard]. [F-004:undetermined] junction not certifiable offline (no fulltext corpus (abstract-only fallback); classified 2026-08-31)','enac_mouse-abg_oocyte_tevc_lss-fluid-jet_17C_tau1_slow','15','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',88,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
