INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(108,'MAIC:BX:00108',4,NULL,NULL,21,'approximate reversal potentials for Na+ and K+ from 160 mV/200 ms ramps under pH 6.0 proton-gated currents; P_K/P_Na = exp(F(Vrev,Na - Vrev,K)/RT) (GHK, T = 274 K as printed)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.0',NULL,'OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TEVC','Xenopus oocyte','Xenopus laevis oocyte, mouse ASIC1a (E18'' unnatural-residue substitution via nonsense suppression)',NULL,6.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ASIC-00135','Although currents at oocytes expressing E18’€ channels were relatively small (Figure 4—figure supplement 1), we could measure approximate reversal potentials for Na+ and K+ and establish that PNa+/PK+ was reduced to unity for E18’€ (Figure 4B), thus verifying that E18’ negative charge is essential for Na+ selectivity.','Results, ''E18'' determines selective Na+ conductance'' (Figure 4B)','medium','stimulus_type as-printed: OTHER. Value printed as the word ''unity'' (=1), not a digit — no error statistic or n printed for this point. E18''€ = glutamate replaced by the isosteric but uncharged 4-nitro-2-aminobutyric acid (''€''); establishes E18'' negative charge as essential for ASIC1a Na+ selectivity. Dimensionless ratio. schema_gap: no ratio column in DB (reversal_potential_mv only a partial proxy). WT and mutant relative permeability ratios (Li+/K+/Cs+, Fig 1E and Fig 4A) are figure-only and archived. Temperature: methods state T = 274 K in the GHK constant (as printed, likely a typo for recording temperature); recording temperature not stated otherwise.','asic1a_mouse_e18''-unchanged-isostere(4-nitro-2-aminobutyric-acid)_oocyte_tevc_pna-pk',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',89,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(109,'MAIC:BX:00109',4,NULL,NULL,22,'perfusion-rate steps 0.5 -> 5 ml/min (NaCl-110 buffer, whole-cell Na+ current); ion-selectivity I-V −140 to +40 mV in 20-mV steps with Na+/Li+/K+-conducting buffers (NaCl replaced by equal-molar LiCl/KCl, pH 8); amiloride dose-response 10^-7-10^-3 M, 30 s per concentration','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-20','mV','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TEVC','Xenopus oocytes injected with mouse ASIC2aG430V cRNA (± mouse ENaC β and γ cRNAs)','Xenopus laevis oocyte',NULL,8.0,'NaCl-110: 110 mM NaCl, 2 mM KCl, 1.54 mM CaCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 8 (NaOH); K+-conducting buffer: NaCl replaced by equal-molar KCl (KOH to pH 8)','3 M KCl (TEVC recording pipettes, 0.3-3 MOhm)',-100.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ASIC-00139','Both ASIC2aG430V and ASICG430V2a+βγENaC are K+ permeable with a reverse potential of -20 mV (Fig. 3, A and B).','Results (ion selectivity of ASIC2aG430V ± βγENaC; Fig 3, A and B)','high','stimulus_type as-printed: OTHER. [supplemental_verified] 2026-11-08 v1.1 batch 3 -> gapfill1_verified.json full_text record re-open (data/asic/literature/raw/gapfill1_verified.json; in-pool rank-30 out-of-benchmark paper, no pool-external tag). K+-permeability E_rev: amiloride-sensitive I-V with K+ as major conducting ion (I-V −140 to +40 mV; plotted −120 to +40; amiloride subtraction with 1 mM). One printed value covers BOTH constructs — one row, both named in condition_key; n = 20 (ASIC2aG430V) and 18 (ASIC2aG430V+βγENaC) oocytes, mean ± SD (Fig 3C/D legend) — n column left blank (two cohorts behind one value), n_cells NOT listed (reported). SOURCE TEXT GARBLE preserved verbatim: the Results sentence prints ''ASICG430V2a+βγENaC'' (construct name transposed; the intended construct is ASIC2aG430V+βγENaC per the figure panels and the rest of the paper) — quote kept as-printed, garble disclosed here. Companion Li+ sentence (''lower currents with Li+ as the charge carrier'') is qualitative -> no row; ''No difference in ion selectivity was observed between ASIC2aG430V and ASICG430V2a+βγENaC'' stays context. U+2212 minus flattened to ASCII ''-'' per layer glyph convention. SHI-2026 ARCHIVE (not rowed): Iflow/Ibasal fold ratios (2x for ASIC2aG430V/ASIC2aG430V+βENaC; ~4x with γENaC or β+γ; Fig 4B legend ''approximately four-fold'') are whole-cell CURRENT fold ratios — no schema kind (threshold_fold_shift is a threshold-fold semantic, current ratios are not thresholds); registered in the builder note as schema-gap backlog. pH 8->4 jump amplitudes are proton-gating (pH50-family no-schema-home backlog). Baseline amplitudes −447.3 ± 42.2 pA (ASIC2a+βγENaC) vs −152.2 ± 36.8 pA (ASIC2a) are whole-cell magnitudes (osca Imax-archive precedent). Endogenous oocyte acid currents (βγENaC-only 136 ± 84 nA, n = 9 vs non-injected 186 ± 105 nA, n = 8, p = 0.30) are not channel parameters. Archive spans in extract_quotes_supplemental-v1.json.','erev_K-conducting_mASIC2aG430V_homomer-and-mASIC2aG430V-betagENaC_heteromer_oocyte_tevc',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',91,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(110,'MAIC:BX:00110',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pressure ramps/steps across the patch; tension computed from Laplace''s law with video-imaged patch radius of curvature | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.8','T50',NULL,NULL,11.8,'dyn/cm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11.8','dyn/cm','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified E. coli MscL-6His reconstituted in azolectin liposomes (giant proteoliposomes)',NULL,NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCL-EX-00001','The patches were fit as a group to a single Boltzmann function with T 1/2 = 11.8 ± 0.8 dyn/cm and a maximal slope of 0.61 ± 0.17 dyn/cm per e-fold change of P o / P c .','Results (Fig 4, group Boltzmann fit)','high','dyn/cm IS a legal TensionUnit value and numerically equal to mN/m (1 dyn/cm = 1 mN/m); kept as-reported with unit_db=dyn/cm, no conversion applied. tau_act Y-flag: kinetics are Markov transition RATE CONSTANTS k_ij (Table III, s^-1; rate-limiting k12 = 0.0016 ± 0.0052 s^-1 at zero tension), not time constants; 1/k conversion forbidden (as-reported rule) -> no tau row. structure_function Y-flag: closed-open in-plane area change ~6.5 nm2 (6 nm2 abstract-level) and pore-dimension estimates (Table IV) have no parameter_kind home (pore diameter explicitly out of the vocabulary) -> no rows. Activation pressure RANGES (spheroplast patches 70-200 mmHg, liposome patches 40-150 mmHg) are per-prep activation ranges, not midpoints -> no p50 rows, recorded here. n unstated for the group fit.','reconstituted proteoliposome patch, purified E. coli MscL, group Boltzmann fit of Po(T)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',115,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(111,'MAIC:BX:00111',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pressure ramps/steps across the patch; tension computed from Laplace''s law with video-imaged patch radius of curvature | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.17',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.61,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.61','dyn/cm','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified E. coli MscL-6His reconstituted in azolectin liposomes (giant proteoliposomes)',NULL,NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCL-EX-00002','The patches were fit as a group to a single Boltzmann function with T 1/2 = 11.8 ± 0.8 dyn/cm and a maximal slope of 0.61 ± 0.17 dyn/cm per e-fold change of P o / P c .','Results (Fig 4, group Boltzmann fit)','high','slope of the Po/Pc Boltzmann in dyn/cm per e-fold (tension-axis factor, same convention family as Sorum 2024 TREK-1 2.3 mN/m; NOT the mmHg^-1 exponent coefficient of Honore 2006/Lauritzen 2005 — do not pool conventions without conversion). Companion estimate from 11 Po(P) curves rescaled to T1/2 = 11.81 dyn/cm: slope factor 0.63 ± 0.08 dyn/cm (Fig 5) — not rowed separately. Abstract rounds to 0.63 dyn/cm per e-fold.','reconstituted proteoliposome patch, purified E. coli MscL (same group fit as T1/2 row)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',115,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(112,'MAIC:BX:00112',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pressure ramps/steps across the patch; tension computed from Laplace''s law with video-imaged patch radius of curvature | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.23 (sd)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,3570.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'3.57',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified E. coli MscL-6His reconstituted in azolectin liposomes (giant proteoliposomes)',NULL,NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCL-EX-00003','Table I Conductance of the Different States of MscL Obtained Using the Program SKM State Conductance SD r pore ns ns nm C1 0 — 0 S2 1.03 0.3 0.8 S3 2.53 0.14 1.4 S4 3.23 0.168 1.7 O5 3.57 0.23 1.8 C, closed; S, substate; and O, fully open state. The mean conductance and SD are shown.','Table I (conductances of closed/substate/open levels)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). Table I column header carries the unit (''ns'', i.e. nS); errors are SD per the table caption (''The mean conductance and SD are shown''). Recording conditions per the source legend of the analysed traces: ''symmetrical 200 mM KCl 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2; membrane potential, 20mV'' (sign not stated). Corroborating text span for the fully open state: ''G MscL is the maximal conductance of a single MscL channel (typically 3.5-3.7 nS)''. Substates are legitimate conductance rows (condition_key names the substate); C1 (closed) carries no conductance. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','reconstituted proteoliposome patch, purified E. coli MscL, fully open state O5, SKM idealization',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',115,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
