e is 2006 Mar 15 (benchmark CSV year 2005 kept for the join). DeltaG0 column (kT) has no parameter_kind home -> not rowed.','liposome-reconstituted recombinant E. coli MscL RKKQQ (E107Q/E108Q), bath pH 5.5, Boltzmann fit of Po vs suction, +30 mV','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',129,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(198,'MAIC:BX:00198',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure (suction) applied to the patch pipette at +30 mV; Po vs pressure fitted with a Boltzmann distribution | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.6',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'5.0','mm Hg-1','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','recombinant 6xHis E. coli MscL (RKKEE wild type and charged-cluster mutants) reconstituted into liposomes',NULL,NULL,7.0,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH (pH adjusted per condition)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH (same pH as bath)',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCL-EX-00089','TABLE 2. Summary of Boltzmann parameters of the wild-type MscL and the MscL channels harboring mutations within the charged cluster Mutation pH p 1/2 (mm Hg) 1/ α (mm Hg −1 ) Δ G 0 (kT) n RKKEE 7.0 76.3 ± 4.3 5.0 ± 0.6 15.8 ± 1.4 4 EEKKR 7.0 84.2 ± 5.5 5.1 ± 0.2 16.4 ± 1.2 4 RKKEE 5.5 120.2 ± 8.2 4.4 ± 0.2 26.9 ±1.3 4 RKKQQ 7.0 130.3 ± 8.8 5.0 ± 0.4 26.1 ± 1.2 4 QQQEE 7.0 118.6 ± 7.3 5.1 ± 0.4 23.8 ± 1.7 5 RKKQQ 9.5 124.0 ± 11.3 4.9 ± 0.6 25.7 ± 2.2 4 RKKQQ 5.5 89.0 ± 7.7 7.0 ± 0.3 13.0 ± 1.4 4','Table 2 (1/alpha column; alpha is the slope factor describing sensitivity to negative pressure)','high','1/alpha carries mm Hg^-1 as printed in the table header (''mm Hg −1''; superscript flattened in transcription); unit kept as-reported, unit_db blank (schema hill_slope is unitless — treat 1/alpha as the pressure-axis exponent-coefficient convention of Honore 2006 / Lauritzen 2005, NOT the tension-axis dyn/cm-per-e-fold factor of Sukharev 1999 — do not pool conventions without conversion). Remaining 1/alpha values (4.4/5.1/5.0/5.1/4.9/7.0) stay in the Table 2 quote; ''without change in the pressure sensitivity α'' makes the WT pH 7.0 value representative. conductance flag: ''changes in pH did not affect the conductance of the channel'' — no numeric conductance in text -> no row.','liposome-reconstituted recombinant E. coli MscL wild type (RKKEE), bath pH 7.0 (same fit as the p50 row)','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',129,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(199,'MAIC:BX:00199',6,NULL,NULL,42,'increasing negative pressure (suction) applied to the patch pipette at Vp = +30 mV; AxoPatch 200B, sampled 5 kHz, filtered 1 kHz',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60.0,'%',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'60','%','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified E. coli MscL (WT / Q65E / Q65R / A64E / A64R) reconstituted in negatively charged liposomes (DOPC:DOPG 70:30)',NULL,NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES (symmetrical; recording-buffer pH not stated)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES (symmetrical; recording-buffer pH not stated)',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCL-EX-00095','We observed a ~60% increase in the amount of pressure required for channel first opening when reconstituted in negatively charged liposomes (Q65E: 55.75 ± 2.18 mmHg vs WT: 34.57 ± 2.14 mmHg), and a rightward shift of the activation curve of the channel (Fig. 4).','Results (Q65E in negatively charged liposomes; Fig 4)','high','[supplemental_verified] [pool-external] 2026-11-07 landscape scan (PR #134) -> pool-external verification (data/mscl/literature/raw/pool_external_verified.json); supplemental-verified entry, in_benchmark=N. Explicitly stated numeric fold/percent shift -> threshold_fold_shift schema_gap (layer ruling; loader migrates to threshold_shift_value). ''~60% increase'' as-printed (value_relation ''~'', no error term -> error_type none). Underlying endpoint values rowed as the two pressure_threshold rows of the same figure. DURU ARCHIVE (not rowed): tau_act ''unclear'' — kinetics are central to the title but no tau/time-constant value in main text; MD ''kinetics'' are trajectory-level (pore diameter/water count vs time at 35 pN pulling + 30 mN/m tension), quoted sentence ''wild-type MscL and Q65R exhibited rapid and extensive pore opening over a shorter timeframe'' is qualitative -> no row. conductance ''unclear'' — no numeric in main text; Q65R ''affected the unitary conductance'' and Q65E flickering ''making it difficult to determine unitary conductance'' are referenced to supplement Fig S2 (supplement-only) -> no row. MscS numbers are reference-channel data (co-expressed/co-reconstituted internal standard; MscL/MscS ratio 1.33-1.84 = MscL-relative comparative quantitation) -> never rowed. EPR spin-label mobility and MD pore geometry are not channel parameters. Archive spans in literature/raw/extract_quotes_supplemental-v1.json.','liposome (DOPC:DOPG 70:30) reconstituted E. coli MscL Q65E vs WT (Duru 2026), first-opening pressure fold increase, +30 mV','>5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',130,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(200,'MAIC:BX:00200',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,'increasing negative pressure (suction) applied to the patch pipette at Vp = +30 mV; AxoPatch 200B, sampled 5 kHz, filtered 1 kHz | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2.3 (sem)','P50',53.8,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'53.8','mmHg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified E. coli MscL (WT / Q65E / Q65R / A64E / A64R) reconstituted in negatively charged liposomes (DOPC:DOPG 70:30)',NULL,NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES (symmetrical; recording-buffer pH not stated)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES (symmetrical; recording-buffer pH not stated)',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCL-EX-00096','However, when reconstituted in negatively charged liposomes, Q65R slightly decreased the pressure sensitivity of the channel (activation midpoint: WT = 53.8 ± 2.3 mmHg and Q65R = 61.5 ± 2.5 mmHg), affected the unitary conductance of the channel (Fig. S2) and right shifted the channel opening probability curve (Fig. 4).','Results (Q65R in negatively charged liposomes; Fig 4)','high','[supplemental_verified] [pool-external] 2026-11-07 landscape scan (PR #134) -> pool-external verification (data/mscl/literature/raw/pool_external_verified.json); supplemental-verified entry, in_benchmark=N. WT midpoint rowed ONCE from the Q65R sentence (unsigned as printed); the Fig-6 A64 section reprints the same WT value SIGNED (''WT = -53.8 ± 2.3 mmHg'') — signed/unsigned as-printed convention declared, one WT endpoint row only. ''activation midpoint''/''midpoint activation'' = Boltzmann curve midpoint -> p50 (true midpoint, not an onset). Signed/unsigned as-printed (suction magnitudes unsigned in the Fig-4 sentence; A64 series signed-negative in the Fig-6 sentence — convention declared per row). mean ± s.e.m. DURU ARCHIVE (not rowed): tau_act ''unclear'' — kinetics are central to the title but no tau/time-constant value in main text; MD ''kinetics'' are trajectory-level (pore diameter/water count vs time at 35 pN pulling + 30 mN/m tension), quoted sentence ''wild-type MscL and Q65R exhibited rapid and extensive pore opening over a shorter timeframe'' is qualitative -> no row. conductance ''unclear'' — no numeric in main text; Q65R ''affected the unitary conductance'' and Q65E flickering ''making it difficult to determine unitary conductance'' are referenced to supplement Fig S2 (supplement-only) -> no row. MscS numbers are reference-channel data (co-expressed/co-reconstituted internal standard; MscL/MscS ratio 1.33-1.84 = MscL-relative comparative quantitation) -> never rowed. EPR spin-label mobility and MD pore geometry are not channel parameters. Archive spans in literature/raw/extract_quotes_supplemental-v1.json.','liposome (DOPC:DOPG 70:30) reconstituted E. coli MscL WT (Duru 2026), Boltzmann activation midpoint, +30 mV','>5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',130,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(201,'MAIC:BX:00201',6,NULL,NULL,41,'increasing negative pressure (suction) applied to the patch pipette at Vp = +30 mV; AxoPatch 200B, sampled 5 kHz, filtered 1 kHz | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2.5 (sem)','P50',61.5,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'61.5','mmHg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified E. coli MscL (WT / Q65E / Q65R / A64E / A64R) reconstituted in negatively charged liposomes (DOPC:DOPG 70:30)',NULL,NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES (symmetrical; recording-buffer pH not stated)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES (symmetrical; recording-buffer pH not stated)',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCL-EX-00097','However, when reconstituted in negatively charged liposomes, Q65R slightly decreased the pressure sensitivity of the channel (activation midpoint: WT = 53.8 ± 2.3 mmHg and Q65R = 61.5 ± 2.5 mmHg), affected the unitary conductance of the channel (Fig. S2) and right shifted the channel opening probability curve (Fig. 4).','Results (Q65R in negatively charged liposomes; Fig 4)','high','[supplemental_verified] [pool-external] 2026-11-07 landscape scan (PR #134) -> pool-external verification (data/mscl/literature/raw/pool_external_verified.json); supplemental-verified entry, in_benchmark=N. ''activation midpoint''/''midpoint activation'' = Boltzmann curve midpoint -> p50 (true midpoint, not an onset). Signed/unsigned as-printed (suction magnitudes unsigned in the Fig-4 sentence; A64 series signed-negative in the Fig-6 sentence — convention declared per row). mean ± s.e.m. DURU ARCHIVE (not rowed): tau_act ''unclear'' — kinetics are central to the title but no tau/time-constant value in main text; MD ''kinetics'' are trajectory-level (pore diameter/water count vs time at 35 pN pulling + 30 mN/m tension), quoted sentence ''wild-type MscL and Q65R exhibited rapid and extensive pore opening over a shorter timeframe'' is qualitative -> no row. conductance ''unclear'' — no numeric in main text; Q65R ''affected the unitary conductance'' and Q65E flickering ''making it difficult to determine unitary conductance'' are referenced to supplement Fig S2 (supplement-only) -> no row. MscS numbers are reference-channel data (co-expressed/co-reconstituted internal standard; MscL/MscS ratio 1.33-1.84 = MscL-relative comparative quantitation) -> never rowed. EPR spin-label mobility and MD pore geometry are not channel parameters. Archive spans in literature/raw/extract_quotes_supplemental-v1.json.','liposome (DOPC:DOPG 70:30) reconstituted E. coli MscL Q65R (Duru 2026), Boltzmann activation midpoint, +30 mV','>5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',130,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(202,'MAIC:BX:00202',6,NULL,NULL,43,'increasing negative pressure (suction) applied to the patch pipette at Vp = +30 mV; AxoPatch 200B, sampled 5 kHz, filtered 1 kHz | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2.9 (sem)','P50',-72.7,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-72.7','mmHg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified E. coli MscL (WT / Q65E / Q65R / A64E / A64R) reconstituted in negatively charged liposomes (DOPC:DOPG 70:30)',NULL,NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES (symmetrical; recording-buffer pH not stated)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES (symmetrical; recording-buffer pH not stated)',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCL-EX-00098','When we reconstituted purified mutants (A64E & A64R) in negatively charged liposomes (DOPC70:DOPG30), we saw that these mutations decreased the sensitivity of the channel to membrane tension (midpoint activation: WT = -53.8 ± 2.3 mmHg, A64E -72.7 ± 2.9 mmHg, A64R -78.1 ± 3.2 mmHg), resulting in a rightward shift in the Boltzmann distribution curve of the channel (Fig. 6).','Results (A64 lipid-interaction mutants; Fig 6)','high','[supplemental_verified] [pool-external] 2026-11-07 landscape scan (PR #134) -> pool-external verification (data/mscl/literature/raw/pool_external_verified.json); supplemental-verified entry, in_benchmark=N. Fig 6 legend prints no n -> n blank, n_cells listed in mimic_gaps. ''activation midpoint''/''midpoint activation'' = Boltzmann curve midpoint -> p50 (true midpoint, not an onset). Signed/unsigned as-printed (suction magnitudes unsigned in the Fig-4 sentence; A64 series signed-negative in the Fig-6 sentence — convention declared per row). mean ± s.e.m. DURU ARCHIVE (not rowed): tau_act ''unclear'' — kinetics are central to the title but no tau/time-constant value in main text; MD ''kinetics'' are trajectory-level (pore diameter/water count vs time at 35 pN pulling + 30 mN/m tension), quoted sentence ''wild-type MscL and Q65R exhibited rapid and extensive pore opening over a shorter timeframe'' is qualitative -> no row. conductance ''unclear'' — no numeric in main text; Q65R ''affected the unitary conductance'' and Q65E flickering ''making it difficult to determine unitary conductance'' are referenced to supplement Fig S2 (supplement-only) -> no row. MscS numbers are reference-channel data (co-expressed/co-reconstituted internal standard; MscL/MscS ratio 1.33-1.84 = MscL-relative comparative quantitation) -> never rowed. EPR spin-label mobility and MD pore geometry are not channel parameters. Archive spans in literature/raw/extract_quotes_supplemental-v1.json.','liposome (DOPC:DOPG 70:30) reconstituted E. coli MscL A64E (Duru 2026), Boltzmann activation midpoint, +30 mV',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',130,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
