INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(207,'MAIC:BX:00207',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1-s linear pressure ramps + 30-s pressure steps from a high-speed pressure clamp (ALA HSPC-1); GsMTx4 applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) side in 5 uM steps, 5 min equilibration','P50',-123.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-123','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00001','Table 1. MscS kinetic parameters obtained from the two-state fits ( Fig. 5 B ) GsMTx4 0 μ M 10 μ M | Ascending ramp parameters | p 1/2 = -123 mm Hg | p 1/2 = -108 mm Hg | γ 1/2 = 5.50 mN/m | γ 1/2 = 4.83 mN/m | k o = 7.01e-6 s -1 | k o = 2.4e-3 s -1 | k 1 = 2.54 | k 1 = 1.54 | Descending ramp parameters | p ′ 1/2 = -88 mm Hg | p ′ 1/2 = -43 mm Hg | γ ′ 1/2 = 3.93 mN/m | γ ′ 1/2 = 1.92 mN/m | k ′ o = 2700 s -1 (constrained) | k ′ o = 200 s -1 (constrained) | k ′ 1 = -1.37 | k ′ 1 = -1.49 | Thermodynamic parameters for the C↔O transition | Δ A = 16.2 nm 2 | Δ A = 12.6 nm 2 | Δ E = 19.7 kT | Δ E = 11.3 kT','Table 1 (ascending ramp parameters; patch of Fig 5 B)','high','suction midpoint printed negative in the source (p 1/2 = -123 mm Hg); value kept as-reported. tau_act Y-flag: kinetics are two-state RATE CONSTANTS (Table 1 k_o 7.01e-6 -> 2.4e-3 s^-1 ascending, k''o 2700 -> 200 s^-1 constrained descending; ''closing rates extrapolated to zero pressure were 2700 s^-1 and 200 s^-1''), not time constants — 1/k conversion forbidden (as-reported rule) -> no tau_act row. tau_inact Y-flag: adaptation quantified as rate constants (Fig 4 C ''Rate constants of MscS desensitization versus suction pressure normalized to p0.5'') and the inactivation-rate protocol itself was ''precluded by peptide-slowed closure'' -> no tau_inact row. The ''adaptation ... with a relaxation time of 0.1-0.3 s'' sentence describes patch-membrane stress relaxation (the STIMULUS changing), not channel kinetics -> no row. ENERGY/AREA parameters (no parameter_kind home, archived): ΔE 19.7 kT -> 11.3 kT; ΔA 16.2 -> 12.6 nm2; open-state stabilization ~8 kT (~9 kT is the MscL paralog value); barrier change 5.8 kT; per-subunit 1.8 kT. Paralog MscL-side Fig 3 numerics excluded (18 ± 4% shift n = 4, -163/-203 mmHg example patch, ΔE_C→O = 50 kT literature assumption).','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, ascending ramp, QuB two-state fit (Fig 5 B / Table 1), 0 µM GsMTx4 (control)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(208,'MAIC:BX:00208',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1-s linear pressure ramps + 30-s pressure steps from a high-speed pressure clamp (ALA HSPC-1); GsMTx4 applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) side in 5 uM steps, 5 min equilibration | MODULATOR: GsMTx4 (potentiator) 10 µM','P50',-108.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-108','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00002','Table 1. MscS kinetic parameters obtained from the two-state fits ( Fig. 5 B ) GsMTx4 0 μ M 10 μ M | Ascending ramp parameters | p 1/2 = -123 mm Hg | p 1/2 = -108 mm Hg | γ 1/2 = 5.50 mN/m | γ 1/2 = 4.83 mN/m | k o = 7.01e-6 s -1 | k o = 2.4e-3 s -1 | k 1 = 2.54 | k 1 = 1.54 | Descending ramp parameters | p ′ 1/2 = -88 mm Hg | p ′ 1/2 = -43 mm Hg | γ ′ 1/2 = 3.93 mN/m | γ ′ 1/2 = 1.92 mN/m | k ′ o = 2700 s -1 (constrained) | k ′ o = 200 s -1 (constrained) | k ′ 1 = -1.37 | k ′ 1 = -1.49 | Thermodynamic parameters for the C↔O transition | Δ A = 16.2 nm 2 | Δ A = 12.6 nm 2 | Δ E = 19.7 kT | Δ E = 11.3 kT','Table 1 (ascending ramp parameters; patch of Fig 5 B)','high','GsMTx4 SENSITIZES MscS (lowers the midpoint, slows closure/recovery) — the opposite of its inhibitory effect on eukaryotic stretch-activated channels; modulator_role ''potentiator'' is the closest enum. suction midpoint printed negative in the source; value kept as-reported.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, ascending ramp, QuB two-state fit (Fig 5 B / Table 1), 10 µM GsMTx4 (cytoplasmic)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(209,'MAIC:BX:00209',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1-s linear pressure ramps + 30-s pressure steps from a high-speed pressure clamp (ALA HSPC-1); GsMTx4 applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) side in 5 uM steps, 5 min equilibration','P50',-88.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-88','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00003','Table 1. MscS kinetic parameters obtained from the two-state fits ( Fig. 5 B ) GsMTx4 0 μ M 10 μ M | Ascending ramp parameters | p 1/2 = -123 mm Hg | p 1/2 = -108 mm Hg | γ 1/2 = 5.50 mN/m | γ 1/2 = 4.83 mN/m | k o = 7.01e-6 s -1 | k o = 2.4e-3 s -1 | k 1 = 2.54 | k 1 = 1.54 | Descending ramp parameters | p ′ 1/2 = -88 mm Hg | p ′ 1/2 = -43 mm Hg | γ ′ 1/2 = 3.93 mN/m | γ ′ 1/2 = 1.92 mN/m | k ′ o = 2700 s -1 (constrained) | k ′ o = 200 s -1 (constrained) | k ′ 1 = -1.37 | k ′ 1 = -1.49 | Thermodynamic parameters for the C↔O transition | Δ A = 16.2 nm 2 | Δ A = 12.6 nm 2 | Δ E = 19.7 kT | Δ E = 11.3 kT','Table 1 (descending ramp parameters; patch of Fig 5 B)','high','suction midpoint printed negative in the source; descending-ramp (closing-branch) midpoint documents the GsMTx4-increased gating hysteresis — distinct condition from the ascending row. tau_act Y-flag: kinetics are two-state RATE CONSTANTS (Table 1 k_o 7.01e-6 -> 2.4e-3 s^-1 ascending, k''o 2700 -> 200 s^-1 constrained descending; ''closing rates extrapolated to zero pressure were 2700 s^-1 and 200 s^-1''), not time constants — 1/k conversion forbidden (as-reported rule) -> no tau_act row. tau_inact Y-flag: adaptation quantified as rate constants (Fig 4 C ''Rate constants of MscS desensitization versus suction pressure normalized to p0.5'') and the inactivation-rate protocol itself was ''precluded by peptide-slowed closure'' -> no tau_inact row. The ''adaptation ... with a relaxation time of 0.1-0.3 s'' sentence describes patch-membrane stress relaxation (the STIMULUS changing), not channel kinetics -> no row. ENERGY/AREA parameters (no parameter_kind home, archived): ΔE 19.7 kT -> 11.3 kT; ΔA 16.2 -> 12.6 nm2; open-state stabilization ~8 kT (~9 kT is the MscL paralog value); barrier change 5.8 kT; per-subunit 1.8 kT. Paralog MscL-side Fig 3 numerics excluded (18 ± 4% shift n = 4, -163/-203 mmHg example patch, ΔE_C→O = 50 kT literature assumption).','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, descending ramp, QuB two-state fit (Fig 5 B / Table 1), 0 µM GsMTx4 (control)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(210,'MAIC:BX:00210',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1-s linear pressure ramps + 30-s pressure steps from a high-speed pressure clamp (ALA HSPC-1); GsMTx4 applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) side in 5 uM steps, 5 min equilibration | MODULATOR: GsMTx4 (potentiator) 10 µM','P50',-43.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-43','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00004','Table 1. MscS kinetic parameters obtained from the two-state fits ( Fig. 5 B ) GsMTx4 0 μ M 10 μ M | Ascending ramp parameters | p 1/2 = -123 mm Hg | p 1/2 = -108 mm Hg | γ 1/2 = 5.50 mN/m | γ 1/2 = 4.83 mN/m | k o = 7.01e-6 s -1 | k o = 2.4e-3 s -1 | k 1 = 2.54 | k 1 = 1.54 | Descending ramp parameters | p ′ 1/2 = -88 mm Hg | p ′ 1/2 = -43 mm Hg | γ ′ 1/2 = 3.93 mN/m | γ ′ 1/2 = 1.92 mN/m | k ′ o = 2700 s -1 (constrained) | k ′ o = 200 s -1 (constrained) | k ′ 1 = -1.37 | k ′ 1 = -1.49 | Thermodynamic parameters for the C↔O transition | Δ A = 16.2 nm 2 | Δ A = 12.6 nm 2 | Δ E = 19.7 kT | Δ E = 11.3 kT','Table 1 (descending ramp parameters; patch of Fig 5 B)','high','GsMTx4 SENSITIZES MscS (lowers the midpoint, slows closure/recovery) — the opposite of its inhibitory effect on eukaryotic stretch-activated channels; modulator_role ''potentiator'' is the closest enum. suction midpoint printed negative in the source; value kept as-reported.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, descending ramp, QuB two-state fit (Fig 5 B / Table 1), 10 µM GsMTx4 (cytoplasmic)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(211,'MAIC:BX:00211',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1-s linear pressure ramps + 30-s pressure steps from a high-speed pressure clamp (ALA HSPC-1); GsMTx4 applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) side in 5 uM steps, 5 min equilibration','T50',NULL,NULL,5.5,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'5.5','mN/m','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00005','Table 1. MscS kinetic parameters obtained from the two-state fits ( Fig. 5 B ) GsMTx4 0 μ M 10 μ M | Ascending ramp parameters | p 1/2 = -123 mm Hg | p 1/2 = -108 mm Hg | γ 1/2 = 5.50 mN/m | γ 1/2 = 4.83 mN/m | k o = 7.01e-6 s -1 | k o = 2.4e-3 s -1 | k 1 = 2.54 | k 1 = 1.54 | Descending ramp parameters | p ′ 1/2 = -88 mm Hg | p ′ 1/2 = -43 mm Hg | γ ′ 1/2 = 3.93 mN/m | γ ′ 1/2 = 1.92 mN/m | k ′ o = 2700 s -1 (constrained) | k ′ o = 200 s -1 (constrained) | k ′ 1 = -1.37 | k ′ 1 = -1.49 | Thermodynamic parameters for the C↔O transition | Δ A = 16.2 nm 2 | Δ A = 12.6 nm 2 | Δ E = 19.7 kT | Δ E = 11.3 kT; In control, the midpoint pressure ( p 0.5 ) measured with the ascending ramp was assumed to correspond to tension of 5.5 mN/m, which reflects average tension in both monolayers in adapted patches.','Table 1 (ascending ramp parameters) + pressure-to-tension calibration sentence','medium','tension conversion is ANCHORED, not directly fitted: the control ascending midpoint (-123 mm Hg) ''was assumed to correspond to tension of 5.5 mN/m'' (calibration anchor of the Sukharev 2002 lineage); all other gamma values are derived from midpoint ratios x that anchor. Rowed as the paper''s own stated Table 1 values with the derivation declared -> confidence medium. Descending values are the closing-branch (hysteresis) midpoints. [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, ascending ramp, tension-converted midpoint (Table 1), 0 µM GsMTx4 (control)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
