os x that anchor. Rowed as the paper''s own stated Table 1 values with the derivation declared -> confidence medium. Descending values are the closing-branch (hysteresis) midpoints. GsMTx4 sensitizes MscS -> modulator_role ''potentiator'' (it inhibits eukaryotic SACs; opposite sign here). [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, descending ramp, tension-converted midpoint (Table 1), 10 µM GsMTx4 (cytoplasmic)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(215,'MAIC:BX:00215',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'sequential 1-s pressure ramps after 5-min equilibration at each GsMTx4 concentration (0-20 µM, 5 µM steps)','P50',-95.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-95','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00009','We increased the concentration of GsMTx4 in the bath sequentially in 5 μ M steps from 0 to 20 μ M, and allowed 5 min to equilibrate at each concentration. The addition of 5 μ M peptide shifted the gating midpoint from -95 mmHg to -82 mmHg (∼14%), and the shift saturated at -78 mm Hg (or 18%) with 15–20 μ M.','Results (Fig 2 A; statistics of shifts across nine patches in Fig 2 C)','high','midpoint of the Fig 2 A concentration-series patch (distinct patch/condition from the Table 1 QuB-analysis rows; control baseline -95 vs -123 mmHg reflects patch geometry). Suction printed negative; value as-reported. Saturating-concentration row: the source states the 15-20 µM range (no single value) -> modulator_concentration left blank, range in condition_key.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, 1-s ramps, GsMTx4 concentration series (Fig 2), 0 µM GsMTx4 (control)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(216,'MAIC:BX:00216',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'sequential 1-s pressure ramps after 5-min equilibration at each GsMTx4 concentration (0-20 µM, 5 µM steps) | MODULATOR: GsMTx4 (potentiator) 5','P50',-82.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-82','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00010','We increased the concentration of GsMTx4 in the bath sequentially in 5 μ M steps from 0 to 20 μ M, and allowed 5 min to equilibrate at each concentration. The addition of 5 μ M peptide shifted the gating midpoint from -95 mmHg to -82 mmHg (∼14%), and the shift saturated at -78 mm Hg (or 18%) with 15–20 μ M.','Results (Fig 2 A; statistics of shifts across nine patches in Fig 2 C)','high','midpoint of the Fig 2 A concentration-series patch (distinct patch/condition from the Table 1 QuB-analysis rows; control baseline -95 vs -123 mmHg reflects patch geometry). Suction printed negative; value as-reported. Saturating-concentration row: the source states the 15-20 µM range (no single value) -> modulator_concentration left blank, range in condition_key. GsMTx4 sensitizes MscS -> ''potentiator''.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, 1-s ramps, GsMTx4 concentration series (Fig 2), 5 µM GsMTx4',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(217,'MAIC:BX:00217',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'sequential 1-s pressure ramps after 5-min equilibration at each GsMTx4 concentration (0-20 µM, 5 µM steps) | MODULATOR: GsMTx4 (potentiator)','P50',-78.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-78','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00011','We increased the concentration of GsMTx4 in the bath sequentially in 5 μ M steps from 0 to 20 μ M, and allowed 5 min to equilibrate at each concentration. The addition of 5 μ M peptide shifted the gating midpoint from -95 mmHg to -82 mmHg (∼14%), and the shift saturated at -78 mm Hg (or 18%) with 15–20 μ M.','Results (Fig 2 A; statistics of shifts across nine patches in Fig 2 C)','high','midpoint of the Fig 2 A concentration-series patch (distinct patch/condition from the Table 1 QuB-analysis rows; control baseline -95 vs -123 mmHg reflects patch geometry). Suction printed negative; value as-reported. Saturating-concentration row: the source states the 15-20 µM range (no single value) -> modulator_concentration left blank, range in condition_key. GsMTx4 sensitizes MscS -> ''potentiator''.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, 1-s ramps, GsMTx4 concentration series (Fig 2), 15-20 µM GsMTx4 (saturating)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(218,'MAIC:BX:00218',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1-s linear pressure ramps + 30-s pressure steps from a high-speed pressure clamp (ALA HSPC-1); GsMTx4 applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) side in 5 uM steps, 5 min equilibration | MODULATOR: GsMTx4 (potentiator)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,14.0,'%',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14','%','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00012','We increased the concentration of GsMTx4 in the bath sequentially in 5 μ M steps from 0 to 20 μ M, and allowed 5 min to equilibrate at each concentration. The addition of 5 μ M peptide shifted the gating midpoint from -95 mmHg to -82 mmHg (∼14%), and the shift saturated at -78 mm Hg (or 18%) with 15–20 μ M.','Results (Fig 2; source phrase ''∼14%'')','medium','paper''s own explicitly stated % midpoint shift — delta_p50_* is pressure-unit-only in the schema and the magnitude is stated as a percentage, so it routes to schema_gap (threshold_fold_shift kind; unit ''%'' as reported). Absolute endpoints are rowed as the p50 rows above. ''Fig. 2 C presents the statistics from nine independent patches of midpoint shifts'' (n not restated for this sentence). The Table 1 patch''s own 13% shift (p0.5 -123 -> -108 mm Hg) and the ~26% log(k) pressure-scale shift are noted, not rowed. GsMTx4 sensitizes MscS -> ''potentiator''.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, 5 µM GsMTx4: midpoint vs 0 µM control',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(219,'MAIC:BX:00219',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1-s linear pressure ramps + 30-s pressure steps from a high-speed pressure clamp (ALA HSPC-1); GsMTx4 applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) side in 5 uM steps, 5 min equilibration | MODULATOR: GsMTx4 (potentiator)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,18.0,'%',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18','%','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00013','We increased the concentration of GsMTx4 in the bath sequentially in 5 μ M steps from 0 to 20 μ M, and allowed 5 min to equilibrate at each concentration. The addition of 5 μ M peptide shifted the gating midpoint from -95 mmHg to -82 mmHg (∼14%), and the shift saturated at -78 mm Hg (or 18%) with 15–20 μ M.','Results (Fig 2; source phrase ''(or 18%)'')','medium','paper''s own explicitly stated % midpoint shift — delta_p50_* is pressure-unit-only in the schema and the magnitude is stated as a percentage, so it routes to schema_gap (threshold_fold_shift kind; unit ''%'' as reported). Absolute endpoints are rowed as the p50 rows above. ''Fig. 2 C presents the statistics from nine independent patches of midpoint shifts'' (n not restated for this sentence). The Table 1 patch''s own 13% shift (p0.5 -123 -> -108 mm Hg) and the ~26% log(k) pressure-scale shift are noted, not rowed. GsMTx4 sensitizes MscS -> ''potentiator''.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, 15-20 µM GsMTx4 (saturating): midpoint vs 0 µM control',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(220,'MAIC:BX:00220',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'inactivation by a prolonged subsaturating pressure step, then pressure released to zero; recovery monitored with a train of short saturating test pulses; exponential fit of peak-current recovery','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1300.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.3',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 + 0.4 M sucrose','200 mM KCl, 5 mM CaCl2, 45 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES-KOH, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00015','The time-dependence of peak current recovery fit with an exponential provided the characteristic time. The control population recovered with a τ = 1.3-1.6 s, and 5 μ M peptide slowed the recovery approximately fourfold.','Results (Fig 6, A-C)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS SECONDS: unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to ms at load. recovery from inactivation (I→C) explicitly attributed to the MscS population -> rowable tau_deact per the MscS adaptation ruling. Reported as a RANGE across patches: lower bound stored as value with value_relation ''~'', full interval in error_type=range (TRPV4 range convention). 5 µM GsMTx4 ''slowed the recovery approximately fourfold'' / ''∼4.5-fold'' — fold only, no absolute tau stated -> no peptide-condition tau row (1.4x4.5 arithmetic forbidden). Fig 6 legend: ''GsMTx4 slows the process of recovery ∼4.5-fold''. Discussion cites a prior ''fast (1-2 s) recovery from inactivation'' — consistent, not rowed separately.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, recovery after prolonged subsaturating step, train of short saturating test pulses (Fig 6), 0 µM GsMTx4',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',92,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(221,'MAIC:BX:00221',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1-s linear pressure ramps ending with a 2-s saturating plateau (also 2.7-240 mmHg/s ramps and 20-s prepulse protocols) from an HSPC-1 high-speed pressure clamp | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 31','P50',188.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'188','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','giant E. coli spheroplasts in a triple-mutant (mscL-/mscS-/mscK-) background expressing WT MscS','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES titrated to pH 7.4 with KOH (symmetrical; NaCl variant where indicated)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES titrated to pH 7.4 with KOH (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00016','Among five representative patches studied with standard borosilicate pipettes (see materials and methods), the average p 1/2 was 188 ± 31 mm Hg, which can be accounted for by differences in pipette size and patch geometry.','Results (Activation curves...; Fig 1)','high','own-data population midpoint (n = 5 patches; error type not stated). Pressure-to-tension conversion uses the LITERATURE anchor ''equating the tension at the pressure midpoint ... to 5.5 dyne/cm'' (Cui and Adler 1996 / Sukharev 2002) -> no t50 row for the anchor (intro-cited calibration value; task access_note already swapped the threshold quote to this own-data sentence). Ramp-rate check: ''Patches subjected to various pressure ramps from 2.7 to 240 mmHg/s revealed a midpoint of activation almost independent of rate.'' tau_inact Y-flag: inactivation phases WERE fitted with single exponentials (I(t)=Ae^-t/τ+C) but the tau_i(V) values appear only as Fig 5 B inset / Fig 6 B plots — no numeric tau in text -> no row. conductance Y-flag: own Fig 3 A single-channel amplitude analysis states no numeric conductance; the 1-nS mentions are prior-work references (Martinac et al. 1987; Levina et al. 1999) -> no conductance row. ENERGY/AREA parameters archived (no parameter_kind home): ΔE = 24 ± 4 kT, ΔA = 18 ± 3 nm2 (n = 27); single-patch 27 ± 2 kT / 20 ± 1.6 nm2 (n = 11); barrier 10.6 nm2 smaller than open state; gating charge +0.8 per heptamer; pore ~7 A water-accessible lumen, ''expanded by at least 8 A to conduct at 1 nS''. Activation RANGE 140-300 mm Hg (vs Martinac''s 40-60) is a range, not a midpoint -> no row.','excised inside-out patch, WT MscS population, 1-s linear saturating ramps, +20 mV pipette, five representative patches','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',93,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(222,'MAIC:BX:00222',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'3-min rest intervals at 0 mV between pressure applications; recovery assayed by repeated activation','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,180000.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'3',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','giant E. coli spheroplasts in a triple-mutant (mscL-/mscS-/mscK-) background expressing WT MscS','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES titrated to pH 7.4 with KOH (symmetrical; NaCl variant where indicated)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES titrated to pH 7.4 with KOH (symmetrical)',20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00017','A 3-min interval between stimuli under low positive or zero applied voltage generally allowed the population to fully recover.; The complete return from the inactivated (refractory) to the closed state (I→C) takes at least 3 min.','Results (Fig 1 legend) + Discussion (gating-cycle summary)','medium','复合 quote 披露（F-004 政策，2026-08-31 补注）：evidence_quote 为原文多处 span 并置（composite 登记册在录）；span 级证据与裁决见 literature/raw/quote_corroboration_manual.json，登记册 tools/literature-mining/configs/composite_quote_registry.json。REPORTED UNIT IS MINUTES (3 min = 180000 ms): unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x60000 to ms at load. paper''s own stated lower bound on the complete I→C recovery duration (''takes at least 3 min'') — a completion bound, not a fitted exponential constant; rowed as tau_deact with value_relation ''>'' per the Shapovalov-2003 >= 20 s precedent. The faster closed-state return under tension is separate (substates/O→S→I at extreme voltages). [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, WT MscS population, return from inactivated (refractory) to closed state at low positive or zero applied voltage',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',93,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(223,'MAIC:BX:00223',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'programmed pressure stimuli from an HSPC-1 clamp: saturating 1-s test ramps (midpoint calibration), 30-s conditioning steps, 60-s inactivating steps + test pulses','T50',NULL,NULL,7.8,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'7.8','mN/m','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','PB113 (mscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT / A98S / L111S MscS; native MscL kept as internal midpoint gauge','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 + 400 mM sucrose','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00018','(C) Positions of activation curves for A98S (γ 0. 5 = 5.8 mN/m), WT (γ 0. 5 = 7.8 mN/m), and L111S (γ 0. 5 = 13.4 mN/m), and the tension dependence of the inactivation rate of WT MscS (data from Fig. 3 E ) on the tension scale.','Fig 4 C legend (activation-curve positions)','medium','tension midpoints are gauge-calibrated: WT gamma0.5 = 7.8 mN/m is the ANCHOR ''as recently measured in whole spheroplast experiments (Belyy et al., 2010b)'' (source prints ''mN/cm'' — a typo for mN/m); A98S/L111S derive from the native-MscL internal-gauge midpoint ratios (A98S 0.75x WT, L111S 1.72x WT) x that anchor -> confidence medium, values as-stated in the Fig 4 C legend. delta_p50 Y-flag: only the 0.75x / 1.72x ratios are stated -> no delta_p50 rows (relative-unit rule); absolute endpoints rowed here. tau_inact + tau_deact Y-flags: inactivation and recovery are quantified as tension-dependent RATE constants from three-state (O→C_A→I) fits of current traces (''the inactivation rate becomes appreciable at tensions near 5 mN/m'', ''The slope of the decreasing recovery rate...'') — rates, not time constants; 1/k forbidden -> no tau rows (the ~5 mN/m statement is an onset-of-rate observation, preserved here). ENERGY/AREA parameters archived (no home): ΔA_C→B = 6.1 ± 1.5 nm2 (n = 3); ΔA_B→I = 2.5 ± 0.1 nm2 (n = 3); total inactivation expansion 8.5 ± 1.6 nm2; alternate 5.5 mN/m-anchor values 8.6 ± 2.2 / 3.5 ± 0.2 / 12.1 nm2; opening-transition area cited as 13-15 nm2. Patch-specific 1-s-ramp midpoints in figure legends (153 mmHg Fig 1 A; 140 mmHg Fig 3 B; 125 mmHg Fig 3 D) are per-patch calibration values, not aggregated p50s -> notes only. Intro-cited: WT inactivation ''∼30 s'' kinetics (Boer et al. 2011); MscS opening at 5-8 mN/m; MscL 10-14 mN/m.','excised inside-out patch, PB113 spheroplast, WT MscS, activation-curve position from 1-s ramps, MscL-gauge-calibrated tension (Fig 4 C)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',94,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(224,'MAIC:BX:00224',5,NULL,NULL,47,'programmed pressure stimuli from an HSPC-1 clamp: saturating 1-s test ramps (midpoint calibration), 30-s conditioning steps, 60-s inactivating steps + test pulses','T50',NULL,NULL,5.8,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'5.8','mN/m','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','PB113 (mscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT / A98S / L111S MscS; native MscL kept as internal midpoint gauge','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 + 400 mM sucrose','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00019','(C) Positions of activation curves for A98S (γ 0. 5 = 5.8 mN/m), WT (γ 0. 5 = 7.8 mN/m), and L111S (γ 0. 5 = 13.4 mN/m), and the tension dependence of the inactivation rate of WT MscS (data from Fig. 3 E ) on the tension scale.','Fig 4 C legend (activation-curve positions)','medium','tension midpoints are gauge-calibrated: WT gamma0.5 = 7.8 mN/m is the ANCHOR ''as recently measured in whole spheroplast experiments (Belyy et al., 2010b)'' (source prints ''mN/cm'' — a typo for mN/m); A98S/L111S derive from the native-MscL internal-gauge midpoint ratios (A98S 0.75x WT, L111S 1.72x WT) x that anchor -> confidence medium, values as-stated in the Fig 4 C legend. delta_p50 Y-flag: only the 0.75x / 1.72x ratios are stated -> no delta_p50 rows (relative-unit rule); absolute endpoints rowed here. tau_inact + tau_deact Y-flags: inactivation and recovery are quantified as tension-dependent RATE constants from three-state (O→C_A→I) fits of current traces (''the inactivation rate becomes appreciable at tensions near 5 mN/m'', ''The slope of the decreasing recovery rate...'') — rates, not time constants; 1/k forbidden -> no tau rows (the ~5 mN/m statement is an onset-of-rate observation, preserved here). ENERGY/AREA parameters archived (no home): ΔA_C→B = 6.1 ± 1.5 nm2 (n = 3); ΔA_B→I = 2.5 ± 0.1 nm2 (n = 3); total inactivation expansion 8.5 ± 1.6 nm2; alternate 5.5 mN/m-anchor values 8.6 ± 2.2 / 3.5 ± 0.2 / 12.1 nm2; opening-transition area cited as 13-15 nm2. Patch-specific 1-s-ramp midpoints in figure legends (153 mmHg Fig 1 A; 140 mmHg Fig 3 B; 125 mmHg Fig 3 D) are per-patch calibration values, not aggregated p50s -> notes only. Intro-cited: WT inactivation ''∼30 s'' kinetics (Boer et al. 2011); MscS opening at 5-8 mN/m; MscL 10-14 mN/m. A98S is the soft gain-of-function mutant that ''lacks inactivation completely'' — qualitative, no numeric inactivation row. Midpoint derivation + shared flags: see the WT row of this paper.','excised inside-out patch, PB113 spheroplast, A98S mutant (soft, gain-of-function), activation-curve position from 1-s ramps, MscL-gauge-calibrated tension (Fig 4 C)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',94,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(225,'MAIC:BX:00225',5,NULL,NULL,48,'programmed pressure stimuli from an HSPC-1 clamp: saturating 1-s test ramps (midpoint calibration), 30-s conditioning steps, 60-s inactivating steps + test pulses','T50',NULL,NULL,13.4,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13.4','mN/m','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','PB113 (mscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT / A98S / L111S MscS; native MscL kept as internal midpoint gauge','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 + 400 mM sucrose','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetrical)',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00020','(C) Positions of activation curves for A98S (γ 0. 5 = 5.8 mN/m), WT (γ 0. 5 = 7.8 mN/m), and L111S (γ 0. 5 = 13.4 mN/m), and the tension dependence of the inactivation rate of WT MscS (data from Fig. 3 E ) on the tension scale.','Fig 4 C legend (activation-curve positions)','medium','tension midpoints are gauge-calibrated: WT gamma0.5 = 7.8 mN/m is the ANCHOR ''as recently measured in whole spheroplast experiments (Belyy et al., 2010b)'' (source prints ''mN/cm'' — a typo for mN/m); A98S/L111S derive from the native-MscL internal-gauge midpoint ratios (A98S 0.75x WT, L111S 1.72x WT) x that anchor -> confidence medium, values as-stated in the Fig 4 C legend. delta_p50 Y-flag: only the 0.75x / 1.72x ratios are stated -> no delta_p50 rows (relative-unit rule); absolute endpoints rowed here. tau_inact + tau_deact Y-flags: inactivation and recovery are quantified as tension-dependent RATE constants from three-state (O→C_A→I) fits of current traces (''the inactivation rate becomes appreciable at tensions near 5 mN/m'', ''The slope of the decreasing recovery rate...'') — rates, not time constants; 1/k forbidden -> no tau rows (the ~5 mN/m statement is an onset-of-rate observation, preserved here). ENERGY/AREA parameters archived (no home): ΔA_C→B = 6.1 ± 1.5 nm2 (n = 3); ΔA_B→I = 2.5 ± 0.1 nm2 (n = 3); total inactivation expansion 8.5 ± 1.6 nm2; alternate 5.5 mN/m-anchor values 8.6 ± 2.2 / 3.5 ± 0.2 / 12.1 nm2; opening-transition area cited as 13-15 nm2. Patch-specific 1-s-ramp midpoints in figure legends (153 mmHg Fig 1 A; 140 mmHg Fig 3 B; 125 mmHg Fig 3 D) are per-patch calibration values, not aggregated p50s -> notes only. Intro-cited: WT inactivation ''∼30 s'' kinetics (Boer et al. 2011); MscS opening at 5-8 mN/m; MscL 10-14 mN/m. L111S is the stiff loss-of-function mutant that ''inactivates silently before reaching the threshold for opening'' — its own inactivation-rate determination was abandoned (''the extremely high threshold for this mutant made the patches prohibitively unstable''). Midpoint derivation + shared flags: see the WT row of this paper.','excised inside-out patch, PB113 spheroplast, L111S mutant (stiff, loss-of-function), activation-curve position from 1-s ramps, MscL-gauge-calibrated tension (Fig 4 C)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',94,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(226,'MAIC:BX:00226',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.2-s pressure steps of increasing amplitude (machine-limited onset ~5 mm Hg/ms); monoexponential approximations of the opening segments','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b; G113A / D62N mutants in the inactivation experiments)','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00021','After reaching the tension threshold of ~5 mN/m ( Fig.3A-C ), MscS population activates with a characteristic time of 1-3 ms, and the active fraction steeply grows with tension.','Results (Fig 3, A-C; population opening kinetics)','medium','population-level characteristic activation time (machine-limited onset: ''the slow onset of pressure may thus underestimate the intrinsic rate of MscS opening''), explicitly attributed to the MscS population -> rowable tau_act. Reported as the RANGE 1-3 ms: lower bound stored as value with value_relation ''~'', full interval in error_type=range (TRPV4 range convention). threshold Y-flag: the paper''s own threshold numbers are ONSETS/saturation, not Boltzmann midpoints -> no p50/t50 rows (onset ruling): tension threshold of ~5 mN/m (quote of the tau_act row); ''saturation is reached at ~8 mN/m (Fig. 3C)''; ''The threshold of about 45 mm Hg for that particular patch is reached within 8 ms''; ''the first super-threshold step activates ~15% of channel population within 2 ms''; ''reach 90% of activity within 5 ms''; ''activating at 8-10 mN/m'' (model section). Per-patch p0.5 was determined with 1-s ramps but no aggregate value is stated; the tension conversion anchor gamma0.5 = 7.8 mN/m is prior work (Belyy 2010, ref 12) -> not rowed. tau_inact Y-flag: inactivation quantified as population FRACTIONS under fixed-duration stimuli, not exponential constants -> no row (''WT shows only 15% of maximum conductance with a 60 s ramp, so approximately 85% of the WT channel population is inactivated''; ''a 15 s constant-pressure stimulation thus is capable of driving about 50% of the WT population to the inactivated state''; ''In the case of the fast-inactivating D62N, 90% of the channels inactivate with a 5 s saturating ramp''; G113A ''less than 10% inactivation during 15-60 s stimulation''; D62N silent inactivation ''~80% of the population is inactivated''). conductance flag: benchmark CSV deliberately downgraded the verify-layer Y to N (1 nS is intro-cited ''(9;12;13)''; own data are population currents) -> downgrade respected, NO conductance row. ENERGY/AREA archived (no home): ΔE = 14.5 kT and ΔA = 10.5 nm2 (Boltzmann fit, Fig 3 legend); ΔE ≈ 18 kT and ΔA = 10.5 nm2 (n = 3); ΔA_C→B = 0.5 nm2; ΔA_O→B = 4.3 nm2. Opening-rate slope ''the apparent initial rate is in the order of ms^-1'' and the cited QuB ''opening rate grows exponentially 12.7 times per 1 mN/m'' (ref 33) are rates -> no tau_act-from-rate row.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, population response to pressure steps (10-15 ms rise) just above the ~5 mN/m tension threshold',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',95,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(227,'MAIC:BX:00227',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'tension dropped from super-threshold to 3 mN/m; population current relaxation fitted to obtain the characteristic closing time','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'60','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS (pB10b; G113A / D62N mutants in the inactivation experiments)','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00022','At 3 mN/m the population relaxes from the fully open to the closed state with a characteristic time of ~60 ms ( Fig. 3D,E ).','Results (Fig 3, D and E)','medium','closure (O→C) characteristic time at the stated 3 mN/m residual tension — deactivation, not inactivation. Companion zero-tension extrapolation is qualitative (''it predicts that MscS can close within a millisecond'') -> not rowed. Tension context: ''if a residual tension in the bacterial membrane persists after the shock, then it should be below 3 mN/m''. See the tau_act row of this paper for the threshold/inactivation/conductance flag coverage.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, relaxation from fully open to closed at 3 mN/m after tension drop',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',95,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(228,'MAIC:BX:00228',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'preprogrammed steps/ramps of negative pressure (suction) from a modified HSPC-1 clamp; midpoints gauged against co-expressed native EcMscL (PB113) known to half-activate at 12 mN/m','T50',NULL,NULL,5.6,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'5.6','mN/m','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing P. aeruginosa PaMscS-1 (PA14_57110) or PaMscS-2 (PA14_65040) from pB10d','E. coli giant spheroplast (P. aeruginosa ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00023','Based on p MscS /p MscL ratios of 0.47 and 0.51, the tension midpoints for PaMscS-1 and PaMscS-2 in this particular setting were determined to be 5.6 and 6.1 mN/m.','Results (Fig 7; tension-midpoint determination section)','medium','midpoint derivation: pMscS/pMscL ratios 0.47 ± 0.01 (n = 4) / 0.51 ± 0.01 (n = 4) against the co-recorded EcMscL wave ''known to half-activate at 12 mN/m'' (literature anchor, Sukharev 1999 lineage) -> the mN/m values are the paper''s own stated absolutes but ratio-anchored; confidence medium (''in this particular setting''). The ratios themselves are not rowed (relative-unit rule). Companion context: ''The activating tension for PaMsc-1, therefore, is slightly lower than that for EC MscS previously estimated between 6.5 (Sukharev, 2002) and 7.8 (Belyy et al., 2010) mN/m'' — prior-work comparison, not rowed.','excised inside-out patch, PaMscS-1 (P. aeruginosa PA14_57110) expressed in PB113 E. coli spheroplasts, activation midpoint from pressure ramps, EcMscL-gauged tension (Fig 7)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',96,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(229,'MAIC:BX:00229',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'preprogrammed steps/ramps of negative pressure (suction) from a modified HSPC-1 clamp; midpoints gauged against co-expressed native EcMscL (PB113) known to half-activate at 12 mN/m','T50',NULL,NULL,6.1,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'6.1','mN/m','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing P. aeruginosa PaMscS-1 (PA14_57110) or PaMscS-2 (PA14_65040) from pB10d','E. coli giant spheroplast (P. aeruginosa ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00024','Based on p MscS /p MscL ratios of 0.47 and 0.51, the tension midpoints for PaMscS-1 and PaMscS-2 in this particular setting were determined to be 5.6 and 6.1 mN/m.','Results (Fig 7; tension-midpoint determination section)','medium','midpoint derivation: pMscS/pMscL ratios 0.47 ± 0.01 (n = 4) / 0.51 ± 0.01 (n = 4) against the co-recorded EcMscL wave ''known to half-activate at 12 mN/m'' (literature anchor, Sukharev 1999 lineage) -> the mN/m values are the paper''s own stated absolutes but ratio-anchored; confidence medium (''in this particular setting''). The ratios themselves are not rowed (relative-unit rule). Companion context: ''The activating tension for PaMsc-1, therefore, is slightly lower than that for EC MscS previously estimated between 6.5 (Sukharev, 2002) and 7.8 (Belyy et al., 2010) mN/m'' — prior-work comparison, not rowed.','excised inside-out patch, PaMscS-2 (P. aeruginosa PA14_65040) expressed in PB113 E. coli spheroplasts, activation midpoint from pressure ramps, EcMscL-gauged tension (Fig 7)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',96,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(230,'MAIC:BX:00230',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'preprogrammed steps/ramps of negative pressure (suction) from a modified HSPC-1 clamp; midpoints gauged against co-expressed native EcMscL (PB113) known to half-activate at 12 mN/m | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.02','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,960.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.96',NULL,'SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing P. aeruginosa PaMscS-1 (PA14_57110) or PaMscS-2 (PA14_65040) from pB10d','E. coli giant spheroplast (P. aeruginosa ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00025','The summary of experimentally determined parameters for the two PaMscS channels in comparison to EC MscS Channel ΔE ΔA P 0.5MscS /P 0.5MscL Conductance Selectivity P CI /P K Inactivation Recovery time kT nm 2 nS % s ; PaMscS-1 | 17.1 ± 0.5 ( n = 16) | 11.0 ± 0.5 ( n = 16) | 0.47 ± 0.01 ( n = 4) | 0.96 ± 0.02 ( n = 3) | ∼1.5 ( n = 3) | 40 ± 8 ( n = 10) | 30 ± 6 ( n = 4) ; PaMscS-2 | 15 ± 2 ( n = 3) | 10 ± 1 ( n = 3) | 0.51 ± 0.01 ( n = 4) | 0.55 ± 0.02 ( n = 3) | ∼4.4 ( n = 3) | 64 ± 3 ( n = 7) | 200 ± 70 ( n = 3); PaMscS-1 has a conductance of ∼1 nS, which is similar to its single EC orthologue, EcMscS. On the other hand, PaMscS-2 has a relatively low conductance of 0.55 nS.','Results + Table 1 (summary of experimentally determined parameters)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). Table 1 value (0.96 ± 0.02 nS, n = 3 for PaMscS-1; 0.55 ± 0.02 nS, n = 3 for PaMscS-2); the running text rounds PaMscS-1 to ''∼1 nS''. Ortholog species in condition_key (P. aeruginosa). Paralog PaMscL conductance 2.1 nS EXCLUDED (MscL-type; ''PaMscL has a conductance of 2.1 nS, which was 30% less than EcMscL''). EC MscS ''~1-1.1'' nS in the same table cites Sukharev 2002 -> intro-cited, no row. [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (4 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, PaMscS-1 expressed in MJF641 E. coli spheroplasts, I-V slope under symmetric 200 mM KCl (Fig 6 / Table 1)','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',96,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(231,'MAIC:BX:00231',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'preprogrammed steps/ramps of negative pressure (suction) from a modified HSPC-1 clamp; midpoints gauged against co-expressed native EcMscL (PB113) known to half-activate at 12 mN/m | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.02','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,550.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.55',NULL,'SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing P. aeruginosa PaMscS-1 (PA14_57110) or PaMscS-2 (PA14_65040) from pB10d','E. coli giant spheroplast (P. aeruginosa ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00026','The summary of experimentally determined parameters for the two PaMscS channels in comparison to EC MscS Channel ΔE ΔA P 0.5MscS /P 0.5MscL Conductance Selectivity P CI /P K Inactivation Recovery time kT nm 2 nS % s ; PaMscS-1 | 17.1 ± 0.5 ( n = 16) | 11.0 ± 0.5 ( n = 16) | 0.47 ± 0.01 ( n = 4) | 0.96 ± 0.02 ( n = 3) | ∼1.5 ( n = 3) | 40 ± 8 ( n = 10) | 30 ± 6 ( n = 4) ; PaMscS-2 | 15 ± 2 ( n = 3) | 10 ± 1 ( n = 3) | 0.51 ± 0.01 ( n = 4) | 0.55 ± 0.02 ( n = 3) | ∼4.4 ( n = 3) | 64 ± 3 ( n = 7) | 200 ± 70 ( n = 3); PaMscS-1 has a conductance of ∼1 nS, which is similar to its single EC orthologue, EcMscS. On the other hand, PaMscS-2 has a relatively low conductance of 0.55 nS.','Results + Table 1 (summary of experimentally determined parameters)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). Table 1 value (0.96 ± 0.02 nS, n = 3 for PaMscS-1; 0.55 ± 0.02 nS, n = 3 for PaMscS-2); the running text rounds PaMscS-1 to ''∼1 nS''. Ortholog species in condition_key (P. aeruginosa). Paralog PaMscL conductance 2.1 nS EXCLUDED (MscL-type; ''PaMscL has a conductance of 2.1 nS, which was 30% less than EcMscL''). EC MscS ''~1-1.1'' nS in the same table cites Sukharev 2002 -> intro-cited, no row. [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (4 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, PaMscS-2 expressed in MJF641 E. coli spheroplasts, I-V slope under symmetric 200 mM KCl (Fig 6 / Table 1)','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',96,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(232,'MAIC:BX:00232',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'conditioning pressure dropped to zero after partial inactivation; recovery monitored with a train of short test pulses; exponential fit | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 6','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30000.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'30',NULL,'SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing P. aeruginosa PaMscS-1 (PA14_57110) or PaMscS-2 (PA14_65040) from pB10d','E. coli giant spheroplast (P. aeruginosa ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00027','The characteristic times (τ) of recovery were 30 ± 6 s for PaMscS-1 and 200 ± 60 s for PaMscS-2 (0.5 and 3.4 min, respectively).','Results (Fig 8, C and D; Table 1 Recovery-time column)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS SECONDS: unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to ms at load. recovery from inactivation explicitly attributed to the channel -> rowable tau_deact (MscS adaptation ruling). n from Table 1 (PaMscS-1 n = 4; PaMscS-2 n = 3). Full-recovery bounds kept in note: ''The time required for full recovery after complete inactivation of PaMscS-1 was ∼5 min, whereas full recovery of PaMscS-2 took over 10 min.'' Inactivation EXTENT (Table 1: PaMscS-1 40 ± 8%, n = 10; PaMscS-2 64 ± 3%, n = 7; text 30 ± 5% / 60 ± 3%) is a population fraction with no parameter_kind home -> not rowed. ΔE/ΔA archived (no home): PaMscS-1 17.1 ± 0.5 kT / 11.0 ± 0.5 nm2 (n = 16); PaMscS-2 15 ± 2 kT / 10.0 ± 1 nm2.','excised inside-out patch, PaMscS-1 expressed in MJF641 E. coli spheroplasts, recovery after partial inactivation (10-s conditioning step at p1/2), train of test pulses (Fig 8)','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',96,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(233,'MAIC:BX:00233',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'conditioning pressure dropped to zero after partial inactivation; recovery monitored with a train of short test pulses; exponential fit | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 60','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,200000.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'200',NULL,'SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing P. aeruginosa PaMscS-1 (PA14_57110) or PaMscS-2 (PA14_65040) from pB10d','E. coli giant spheroplast (P. aeruginosa ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00028','The characteristic times (τ) of recovery were 30 ± 6 s for PaMscS-1 and 200 ± 60 s for PaMscS-2 (0.5 and 3.4 min, respectively).','Results (Fig 8, C and D; Table 1 Recovery-time column)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS SECONDS: unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to ms at load. recovery from inactivation explicitly attributed to the channel -> rowable tau_deact (MscS adaptation ruling). n from Table 1 (PaMscS-1 n = 4; PaMscS-2 n = 3). Table 1 prints this value as 200 ± 70 (n = 3) — text/table error-term discrepancy declared; text value rowed. Full-recovery bounds kept in note: ''The time required for full recovery after complete inactivation of PaMscS-1 was ∼5 min, whereas full recovery of PaMscS-2 took over 10 min.'' Inactivation EXTENT (Table 1: PaMscS-1 40 ± 8%, n = 10; PaMscS-2 64 ± 3%, n = 7; text 30 ± 5% / 60 ± 3%) is a population fraction with no parameter_kind home -> not rowed. ΔE/ΔA archived (no home): PaMscS-1 17.1 ± 0.5 kT / 11.0 ± 0.5 nm2 (n = 16); PaMscS-2 15 ± 2 kT / 10.0 ± 1 nm2.','excised inside-out patch, PaMscS-2 expressed in MJF641 E. coli spheroplasts, recovery after partial inactivation (10-s conditioning step at p1/2), train of test pulses (Fig 8)','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',96,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(234,'MAIC:BX:00234',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'preprogrammed steps/ramps of negative pressure (suction) from a modified HSPC-1 clamp; midpoints gauged against co-expressed native EcMscL (PB113) known to half-activate at 12 mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.5',NULL,'SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing P. aeruginosa PaMscS-1 (PA14_57110) or PaMscS-2 (PA14_65040) from pB10d','E. coli giant spheroplast (P. aeruginosa ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.2,'asymmetric KCl (gradient condition) in 10 mM CaCl2 / 90 mM MgCl2 / 10 mM HEPES pH 7.2 base','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00029','Based on the Goldman equation, the E rev shift for PaMscS-1 in response to 1:5 (pipette/bath) gradient of KCl (relative to symmetric conditions) of -6.1 mV predicts the permeability ratio P CI /P K of 1.5. For PaMscS-2, the E rev shift of 23 mV (5:1 pipette/bath gradient) predicts P CI /P K of 4.4.; In an asymmetric solution containing 5:1 gradient of KCI, the reversal potentials of both PaMscS channels shifted toward the equilibrium potential for CI − , indicating that PaMscS-1 and PaMscS-2 favor anions over cations with P CI /P K ∼1.5 and 4.4, respectively.','Results (Ionic selectivity; Fig 6 legend)','medium','复合 quote 披露（F-004 政策，2026-08-31 补注）：evidence_quote 为原文多处 span 并置（composite 登记册在录）；span 级证据与裁决见 literature/raw/quote_corroboration_manual.json，登记册 tools/literature-mining/configs/composite_quote_registry.json。P_Cl/P_K from Goldman-equation analysis of the E_rev shift under the stated KCl gradient — both channels are anion-preferring. schema_gap: no ion-selectivity ratio column in the DB (reversal_potential_mv only a partial proxy). Source typo declared: one Results span prints ''KCI''/''CI −'' for KCl/Cl−; the Fig 6 legend span spells KCl correctly. Table 1 lists ''∼1.5 (n = 3)'' / ''∼4.4 (n = 3)''. [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, PaMscS-1 expressed in MJF641 E. coli spheroplasts, asymmetric 1:5 (pipette/bath) KCl gradient, Goldman analysis of E_rev shift','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',96,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(235,'MAIC:BX:00235',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'preprogrammed steps/ramps of negative pressure (suction) from a modified HSPC-1 clamp; midpoints gauged against co-expressed native EcMscL (PB113) known to half-activate at 12 mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,4.4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'4.4',NULL,'SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing P. aeruginosa PaMscS-1 (PA14_57110) or PaMscS-2 (PA14_65040) from pB10d','E. coli giant spheroplast (P. aeruginosa ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.2,'asymmetric KCl (gradient condition) in 10 mM CaCl2 / 90 mM MgCl2 / 10 mM HEPES pH 7.2 base','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00030','Based on the Goldman equation, the E rev shift for PaMscS-1 in response to 1:5 (pipette/bath) gradient of KCl (relative to symmetric conditions) of -6.1 mV predicts the permeability ratio P CI /P K of 1.5. For PaMscS-2, the E rev shift of 23 mV (5:1 pipette/bath gradient) predicts P CI /P K of 4.4.; In an asymmetric solution containing 5:1 gradient of KCI, the reversal potentials of both PaMscS channels shifted toward the equilibrium potential for CI − , indicating that PaMscS-1 and PaMscS-2 favor anions over cations with P CI /P K ∼1.5 and 4.4, respectively.','Results (Ionic selectivity; Fig 6 legend)','medium','复合 quote 披露（F-004 政策，2026-08-31 补注）：evidence_quote 为原文多处 span 并置（composite 登记册在录）；span 级证据与裁决见 literature/raw/quote_corroboration_manual.json，登记册 tools/literature-mining/configs/composite_quote_registry.json。P_Cl/P_K from Goldman-equation analysis of the E_rev shift under the stated KCl gradient — both channels are anion-preferring. schema_gap: no ion-selectivity ratio column in the DB (reversal_potential_mv only a partial proxy). Source typo declared: one Results span prints ''KCI''/''CI −'' for KCl/Cl−; the Fig 6 legend span spells KCl correctly. Table 1 lists ''∼1.5 (n = 3)'' / ''∼4.4 (n = 3)''. [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, PaMscS-2 expressed in MJF641 E. coli spheroplasts, asymmetric 5:1 (pipette/bath) KCl gradient (inverted), Goldman analysis of E_rev shift','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',96,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(236,'MAIC:BX:00236',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'preprogrammed steps/ramps of negative pressure (suction) from a modified HSPC-1 clamp; midpoints gauged against co-expressed native EcMscL (PB113) known to half-activate at 12 mN/m','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-6.1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-6.1','mV','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing P. aeruginosa PaMscS-1 (PA14_57110) or PaMscS-2 (PA14_65040) from pB10d','E. coli giant spheroplast (P. aeruginosa ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.2,'asymmetric KCl (gradient condition) in 10 mM CaCl2 / 90 mM MgCl2 / 10 mM HEPES pH 7.2 base','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00031','Based on the Goldman equation, the E rev shift for PaMscS-1 in response to 1:5 (pipette/bath) gradient of KCl (relative to symmetric conditions) of -6.1 mV predicts the permeability ratio P CI /P K of 1.5. For PaMscS-2, the E rev shift of 23 mV (5:1 pipette/bath gradient) predicts P CI /P K of 4.4.','Results (Ionic selectivity; Fig 6 legend)','medium','ΔE_rev SHIFT, NOT an absolute E_rev (extraction-review D-2: do not ingest into reversal_potential_mv as an absolute zero-current potential) — shift relative to symmetric conditions, used by the paper to derive the P_Cl/P_K rows. shift is NEGATIVE (toward E_Cl) for the 1:5 gradient — sign as printed in the source.','excised inside-out patch, PaMscS-1 expressed in MJF641 E. coli spheroplasts, E_rev shift relative to symmetric 200 mM KCl (1:5 (pipette/bath) KCl gradient)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',96,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(237,'MAIC:BX:00237',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'preprogrammed steps/ramps of negative pressure (suction) from a modified HSPC-1 clamp; midpoints gauged against co-expressed native EcMscL (PB113) known to half-activate at 12 mN/m','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,23.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'23','mV','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing P. aeruginosa PaMscS-1 (PA14_57110) or PaMscS-2 (PA14_65040) from pB10d','E. coli giant spheroplast (P. aeruginosa ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.2,'asymmetric KCl (gradient condition) in 10 mM CaCl2 / 90 mM MgCl2 / 10 mM HEPES pH 7.2 base','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00032','Based on the Goldman equation, the E rev shift for PaMscS-1 in response to 1:5 (pipette/bath) gradient of KCl (relative to symmetric conditions) of -6.1 mV predicts the permeability ratio P CI /P K of 1.5. For PaMscS-2, the E rev shift of 23 mV (5:1 pipette/bath gradient) predicts P CI /P K of 4.4.','Results (Ionic selectivity; Fig 6 legend)','medium','ΔE_rev SHIFT, NOT an absolute E_rev (extraction-review D-2: do not ingest into reversal_potential_mv as an absolute zero-current potential) — shift relative to symmetric conditions, used by the paper to derive the P_Cl/P_K rows. sign not printed in the source for this value; gradient was inverted because ''no channel activity was observed in the opposite configuration''.','excised inside-out patch, PaMscS-2 expressed in MJF641 E. coli spheroplasts, E_rev shift relative to symmetric 200 mM KCl (5:1 (pipette/bath) KCl gradient (inverted configuration))',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',96,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(238,'MAIC:BX:00238',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure (suction) applied to the patch pipette on liposome-reconstituted channels; MscMJ traces recorded at +50 and -50 mV pipette potential','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,270.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'270','pS','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified recombinant MscMJ (Methanococcus jannaschii) reconstituted into azolectin liposomes',NULL,NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00033','The conductance of MscMJLR estimated from the current–voltage plot (Figure 4 B) was ∼2 nS, significantly larger than the 270 pS of MscMJ.','Results (conductance comparison; Fig 4 B / Table I)','medium','270 pS is stated in this paper''s own Results comparison and listed in Table I as 0.27 nS; Table I credits the original MscMJ measurement to the companion study (Kloda and Martinac, 2001a) — provenance declared, confidence medium. Unit IS pS as printed (normal pS handling; the paralog MscMJLR nS values are NOT rowed). Ortholog species in condition_key (M. jannaschii). This paper''s own MscMJ recordings: Fig 4 C traces at +50/-50 mV activated by 55 and 35 mmHg suction (stimulus levels for the shown traces, onset-type values -> not rowed as midpoints); Fig 5 B / 5 D panels adapted from the companion. PARALOG ARCHIVE (MscMJLR = archaeal MscL-LIKE ortholog; cross-family data retained in notes/quotes only, NOT rowed per the paired-channel ruling): p 1/2 = 29.2 ± 2.0 mmHg (mean ± SE, n = 5); 1/α = 1.7 ± 0.2 mmHg per e-fold (n = 5); conductance 1.70 ± 0.03 nS at -40 mV (n = 7) and 2.20 ± 0.05 nS at +40 mV (n = 6), ''~2 nS'', outward rectification; E_rev shift 17.6 ± 1.2 mV (n = 4) with P_K/P_Cl ≈ 5; ΔG0 ≈ 18 kT; Hille-model pore ∼27 Å; activation pressures ''between 25 and 100 mmHg'' (range); blocked by 0.1 mM gadolinium (no IC50 stated). MscMJ-side values that are COMPANION-PAPER cites (Table I ''Reference'' column = Kloda and Martinac, 2001a; Fig 5 B and D ''adapted from Kloda and Martinac (2001a)'') -> intro-cited, not rowed: p 1/2 57 mmHg, 1/α 11 mmHg, ΔG0 5 kT, P_K/P_Cl ≈ 6, E_rev shift ≈ 18 mV; the E. coli MscS Table-I row (36 mmHg / 5 / 7 kT / 0.97 (+ve) and 0.65 (-ve) nS; Martinac et al. 1987 + unpublished) is likewise compiled prior work -> no row. threshold + ion_selectivity Y-flags therefore yield no further rows (own-data values are MscMJLR=paralog; MscMJ values are companion cites); the 270 pS conductance row below is the task-directed mscs-side row.','liposome-reconstituted purified MscMJ (M. jannaschii), symmetric 200 mM KCl, single-channel currents at ±50 mV pipette potential (Fig 4 C)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',97,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(239,'MAIC:BX:00239',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure up to -80 mmHg (activation ramps) or constant -40 mmHg (I-V); two-pulse voltage protocol for inactivation; 3-min intervals between pulse sets','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1160.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.16',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,6.0,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 6.0 + 300 mM sucrose (symmetric); 300 mM KCl bath / 100 mM KCl pipette (asymmetric)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 6.0',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00034','The current-voltage relation, recorded at a constant pressure of -40 mmHg, shows a slope conductance of ∼1.16 nS in symmetric solutions (200 mM KCl, pH 6.0) and a slope conductance of ∼1.19 nS in asymmetric solutions (100 mM KCl pipette/300 mM KCl bath, pH 6.0). Under these conditions the reversal potential of MscS is ∼2 mV.','Fig 2 legend (A)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). symmetric-solution slope conductance. wet-lab experimental values from the Vásquez/Perozo patch-clamp portion (Fig 2); the MD-side conductances are simulation outputs and are NOT rowed. tau_inact Y-flag: single-exponential decay constants tau(V) exist (Fig 3 D, ''Decay time constant τ obtained from fitting a single exponential to the macroscopic records'') but appear only as a PLOT — no numeric tau in text (''the voltage dependence of inactivation observed here arises at voltages larger than ±40 mV'') -> no tau row. threshold Y-flag: onset-type values only (''revealed MscS activity when a gentle pressure (such as -40 mmHg) was applied''; macroscopic currents ''elicited by an increase in negative pressure up to -80 mmHg''); Fig 3 B midpoints P1/2-vs-voltage are voltage-INDEPENDENT and figure-only -> no p50 row. Running-text E_rev prints +2.2 mV for the same asymmetric condition (same quote rowed below as the GHK span); the Fig 2 legend''s ''∼2 mV'' is rowed per the task directive. Source glyph: the paper prints ''P Cl+ / P K−'' (apparent subscript-sign typo for P_Cl/P_K) — transcribed as printed. Intro-cited values NOT rowed: the abstract/intro ''∼1 nS'' conductance and the ''previously reported ratio of ∼1.48''.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, I-V at constant -40 mmHg, symmetric 200 mM KCl, pH 6.0 (slope of the constant-pressure I-V)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',98,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(240,'MAIC:BX:00240',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure up to -80 mmHg (activation ramps) or constant -40 mmHg (I-V); two-pulse voltage protocol for inactivation; 3-min intervals between pulse sets','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1190.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.19',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,6.0,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 6.0 + 300 mM sucrose (symmetric); 300 mM KCl bath / 100 mM KCl pipette (asymmetric)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 6.0',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00035','The current-voltage relation, recorded at a constant pressure of -40 mmHg, shows a slope conductance of ∼1.16 nS in symmetric solutions (200 mM KCl, pH 6.0) and a slope conductance of ∼1.19 nS in asymmetric solutions (100 mM KCl pipette/300 mM KCl bath, pH 6.0). Under these conditions the reversal potential of MscS is ∼2 mV.','Fig 2 legend (A)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). asymmetric-solution slope conductance — coincidentally the same numeral as the GHK P_Cl/P_K ratio rowed below; distinct quantities, both as printed. wet-lab experimental values from the Vásquez/Perozo patch-clamp portion (Fig 2); the MD-side conductances are simulation outputs and are NOT rowed. tau_inact Y-flag: single-exponential decay constants tau(V) exist (Fig 3 D, ''Decay time constant τ obtained from fitting a single exponential to the macroscopic records'') but appear only as a PLOT — no numeric tau in text (''the voltage dependence of inactivation observed here arises at voltages larger than ±40 mV'') -> no tau row. threshold Y-flag: onset-type values only (''revealed MscS activity when a gentle pressure (such as -40 mmHg) was applied''; macroscopic currents ''elicited by an increase in negative pressure up to -80 mmHg''); Fig 3 B midpoints P1/2-vs-voltage are voltage-INDEPENDENT and figure-only -> no p50 row. Running-text E_rev prints +2.2 mV for the same asymmetric condition (same quote rowed below as the GHK span); the Fig 2 legend''s ''∼2 mV'' is rowed per the task directive. Source glyph: the paper prints ''P Cl+ / P K−'' (apparent subscript-sign typo for P_Cl/P_K) — transcribed as printed. Intro-cited values NOT rowed: the abstract/intro ''∼1 nS'' conductance and the ''previously reported ratio of ∼1.48''.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, I-V at constant -40 mmHg, asymmetric 100 mM KCl pipette / 300 mM KCl bath, pH 6.0 (slope of the constant-pressure I-V)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',98,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(241,'MAIC:BX:00241',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure up to -80 mmHg (activation ramps) or constant -40 mmHg (I-V); two-pulse voltage protocol for inactivation; 3-min intervals between pulse sets','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,2.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2','mV','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,6.0,'300 mM KCl bath / 100 mM KCl pipette (other salts as symmetric), pH 6.0','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 6.0',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00036','The current-voltage relation, recorded at a constant pressure of -40 mmHg, shows a slope conductance of ∼1.16 nS in symmetric solutions (200 mM KCl, pH 6.0) and a slope conductance of ∼1.19 nS in asymmetric solutions (100 mM KCl pipette/300 mM KCl bath, pH 6.0). Under these conditions the reversal potential of MscS is ∼2 mV.','Fig 2 legend (A)','medium','Fig 2 legend value ''∼2 mV'' rowed as-directed; the running text prints +2.2 mV for the same measurement (span included in the GHK quote below). Sign as printed in the legend (no sign). wet-lab experimental values from the Vásquez/Perozo patch-clamp portion (Fig 2); the MD-side conductances are simulation outputs and are NOT rowed. tau_inact Y-flag: single-exponential decay constants tau(V) exist (Fig 3 D, ''Decay time constant τ obtained from fitting a single exponential to the macroscopic records'') but appear only as a PLOT — no numeric tau in text (''the voltage dependence of inactivation observed here arises at voltages larger than ±40 mV'') -> no tau row. threshold Y-flag: onset-type values only (''revealed MscS activity when a gentle pressure (such as -40 mmHg) was applied''; macroscopic currents ''elicited by an increase in negative pressure up to -80 mmHg''); Fig 3 B midpoints P1/2-vs-voltage are voltage-INDEPENDENT and figure-only -> no p50 row. Running-text E_rev prints +2.2 mV for the same asymmetric condition (same quote rowed below as the GHK span); the Fig 2 legend''s ''∼2 mV'' is rowed per the task directive. Source glyph: the paper prints ''P Cl+ / P K−'' (apparent subscript-sign typo for P_Cl/P_K) — transcribed as printed. Intro-cited values NOT rowed: the abstract/intro ''∼1 nS'' conductance and the ''previously reported ratio of ∼1.48''.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, I-V at constant -40 mmHg, asymmetric 100 mM KCl pipette / 300 mM KCl bath',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',98,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(242,'MAIC:BX:00242',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure up to -80 mmHg (activation ramps) or constant -40 mmHg (I-V); two-pulse voltage protocol for inactivation; 3-min intervals between pulse sets',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.19,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.19',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,6.0,'300 mM KCl bath / 100 mM KCl pipette (other salts as symmetric), pH 6.0','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 6.0',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00037','Under asymmetric conditions, the reversal potential is estimated to be +2.2 mV, which is small compared to the theoretical reversal potential for a completely selective anion channel (+28.4 mV according to the Nernst equation). Using the GHK equation (see Materials and Methods), the selectivity of the channel is estimated to be P Cl+ / P K− = 1.19, slightly smaller than the previously reported ratio of ∼1.48 ( 10 ). Thus, MscS seems to be only very slightly selective for anions.','Results (current-voltage relation and selectivity; Fig 2)','medium','own experimental E_rev analyzed with the GHK equation; schema_gap (no ion-selectivity ratio column; reversal_potential_mv only a partial proxy). The comparison ''∼1.48 (10)'' is a prior-work ratio -> not rowed. wet-lab experimental values from the Vásquez/Perozo patch-clamp portion (Fig 2); the MD-side conductances are simulation outputs and are NOT rowed. tau_inact Y-flag: single-exponential decay constants tau(V) exist (Fig 3 D, ''Decay time constant τ obtained from fitting a single exponential to the macroscopic records'') but appear only as a PLOT — no numeric tau in text (''the voltage dependence of inactivation observed here arises at voltages larger than ±40 mV'') -> no tau row. threshold Y-flag: onset-type values only (''revealed MscS activity when a gentle pressure (such as -40 mmHg) was applied''; macroscopic currents ''elicited by an increase in negative pressure up to -80 mmHg''); Fig 3 B midpoints P1/2-vs-voltage are voltage-INDEPENDENT and figure-only -> no p50 row. Running-text E_rev prints +2.2 mV for the same asymmetric condition (same quote rowed below as the GHK span); the Fig 2 legend''s ''∼2 mV'' is rowed per the task directive. Source glyph: the paper prints ''P Cl+ / P K−'' (apparent subscript-sign typo for P_Cl/P_K) — transcribed as printed. Intro-cited values NOT rowed: the abstract/intro ''∼1 nS'' conductance and the ''previously reported ratio of ∼1.48''.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, asymmetric 100/300 mM KCl, Goldman-Hodgkin-Katz analysis of the measured reversal potential',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',98,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(243,'MAIC:BX:00243',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 clamp: 1-s triangular ramps (midpoints), pulse-step (closing kinetics), pulse-step-pulse protocols (10-s conditioning steps near p0.5, recovery trains); Ficoll 400 / PEG 3350 perfused to the cytoplasmic side | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.4','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1400.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.4',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465-derived / PB113 (mscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT or mutant MscS (pB10d); PB113 with native WT MscL used as the internal tension gauge for mutant gamma0.5 determination','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES + 400 mM sucrose, pH 7.4 (Ficoll/PEG added wt/vol as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00038','WT showed full activation with 1-s ramps, its closure within a 10-s period took place at tensions near the midpoint, and it moderately inactivated during a 5-s step and recovered with a characteristic τ of 1.4 ± 0.4 s ( n = 10; see also Table S1).','Results (Fig 4, A and B; Fig 6; Table S1)','high','REPORTED UNIT IS SECONDS: unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to ms at load. REAL fitted recovery constant, explicitly attributed to WT MscS -> rowable tau_deact (MscS adaptation ruling). Fig 4 text prints the WT value once as ''1.4 + 0.4 s (n = 10)'' (glyph variant) and the Fig 6 legend as ''1.4 ± 0.4 s'' — ± form rowed. inactivation EXTENT not tau: ''WT MscS shows its maximal inactivation of roughly 40-50% of channels upon exposure to a 10-s step of tension of ∼8 mN/m'' (extent at 10-s/5%-Ficoll 80-90%; G168D <15%/<20%; G113A ∼40%) -> no tau_inact row. Calibration anchors NOT rowed for this paper: WT MscS gamma0.5 = 7.8 mN/m and MscL gamma0.5 = 13 mN/m are ''the previously established midpoint tensions ... (Belyy et al., 2010b)'' — methods-cited; the 7.8 mN/m measurement is rowed from Belyy 2010 itself (this batch); MscL 13 mN/m is paralog-side. RATE constants not converted (1/k forbidden): intrinsic closing rates 2,430 ± 270 s^-1 (n = 6) WT vs 107 ± 24 s^-1 (n = 6) G168D; tension slopes -1.54 ± 0.16 and -2.0 ± 0.17 s^-1/(mN/m). N117V closure ''with a τ of ∼0.1 s at tensions close to 90% of saturating tension'' — single-condition closure constant kept in note (the mutant-recovery constants are the fitted population values rowed). ENERGY/AREA archived: effective in-plane area of the TM barrel ''estimated from the inactivation and recovery kinetics as ∼8 nm2'' (cites Kamaraju et al., 2011). Ficoll raises the activation midpoint (counteracts tension; cytoplasmic crowding pressure) -> modulator_role ''antagonist'' is the closest enum. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, WT MscS, pulse-step-pulse protocol (saturating pulse, conditioning step, recovery train of saturating test pulses)','10','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',99,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(244,'MAIC:BX:00244',5,NULL,NULL,49,'HSPC-1 clamp: 1-s triangular ramps (midpoints), pulse-step (closing kinetics), pulse-step-pulse protocols (10-s conditioning steps near p0.5, recovery trains); Ficoll 400 / PEG 3350 perfused to the cytoplasmic side | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.02','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,500.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.5',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465-derived / PB113 (mscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT or mutant MscS (pB10d); PB113 with native WT MscL used as the internal tension gauge for mutant gamma0.5 determination','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES + 400 mM sucrose, pH 7.4 (Ficoll/PEG added wt/vol as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00039','The N117V and N167V MscS mutants showed more inactivation than WT MscS after the conditioning step, yet both mutants recovered faster, with a characteristic time of recovery (τ) of 0.5 ± 0.02 s ( n = 3) for N117V and 0.6 ± 0.2 s ( n = 3) for N167V.','Results (Fig 6 legend; N117V/N167V recovery)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS SECONDS: unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to ms at load. REAL fitted recovery constant, explicitly attributed to N117V mutant -> rowable tau_deact (MscS adaptation ruling). recovered three times faster than WT.Fig 4 text prints the WT value once as ''1.4 + 0.4 s (n = 10)'' (glyph variant) and the Fig 6 legend as ''1.4 ± 0.4 s'' — ± form rowed. inactivation EXTENT not tau: ''WT MscS shows its maximal inactivation of roughly 40-50% of channels upon exposure to a 10-s step of tension of ∼8 mN/m'' (extent at 10-s/5%-Ficoll 80-90%; G168D <15%/<20%; G113A ∼40%) -> no tau_inact row. Calibration anchors NOT rowed for this paper: WT MscS gamma0.5 = 7.8 mN/m and MscL gamma0.5 = 13 mN/m are ''the previously established midpoint tensions ... (Belyy et al., 2010b)'' — methods-cited; the 7.8 mN/m measurement is rowed from Belyy 2010 itself (this batch); MscL 13 mN/m is paralog-side. RATE constants not converted (1/k forbidden): intrinsic closing rates 2,430 ± 270 s^-1 (n = 6) WT vs 107 ± 24 s^-1 (n = 6) G168D; tension slopes -1.54 ± 0.16 and -2.0 ± 0.17 s^-1/(mN/m). N117V closure ''with a τ of ∼0.1 s at tensions close to 90% of saturating tension'' — single-condition closure constant kept in note (the mutant-recovery constants are the fitted population values rowed). ENERGY/AREA archived: effective in-plane area of the TM barrel ''estimated from the inactivation and recovery kinetics as ∼8 nm2'' (cites Kamaraju et al., 2011). Ficoll raises the activation midpoint (counteracts tension; cytoplasmic crowding pressure) -> modulator_role ''antagonist'' is the closest enum.','excised inside-out patch, N117V mutant, pulse-step-pulse protocol (saturating pulse, conditioning step, recovery train of saturating test pulses)','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',99,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
