010b)'' — methods-cited; the 7.8 mN/m measurement is rowed from Belyy 2010 itself (this batch); MscL 13 mN/m is paralog-side. RATE constants not converted (1/k forbidden): intrinsic closing rates 2,430 ± 270 s^-1 (n = 6) WT vs 107 ± 24 s^-1 (n = 6) G168D; tension slopes -1.54 ± 0.16 and -2.0 ± 0.17 s^-1/(mN/m). N117V closure ''with a τ of ∼0.1 s at tensions close to 90% of saturating tension'' — single-condition closure constant kept in note (the mutant-recovery constants are the fitted population values rowed). ENERGY/AREA archived: effective in-plane area of the TM barrel ''estimated from the inactivation and recovery kinetics as ∼8 nm2'' (cites Kamaraju et al., 2011). Ficoll raises the activation midpoint (counteracts tension; cytoplasmic crowding pressure) -> modulator_role ''antagonist'' is the closest enum.','excised inside-out patch, N167V mutant, pulse-step-pulse protocol (saturating pulse, conditioning step, recovery train of saturating test pulses)','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',99,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(246,'MAIC:BX:00246',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 clamp: 1-s triangular ramps (midpoints), pulse-step (closing kinetics), pulse-step-pulse protocols (10-s conditioning steps near p0.5, recovery trains); Ficoll 400 / PEG 3350 perfused to the cytoplasmic side','T50',NULL,NULL,13.0,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13','mN/m','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465-derived / PB113 (mscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT or mutant MscS (pB10d); PB113 with native WT MscL used as the internal tension gauge for mutant gamma0.5 determination','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES + 400 mM sucrose, pH 7.4 (Ficoll/PEG added wt/vol as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00041','As indicated by measurements in the PB113 mscL -positive strain, both valine mutants activated at much higher tension than WT (∼13 mN/m).','Results (The TM3b-β domain interface; Fig 6)','medium','ONE value stated for BOTH valine mutants (no per-mutant numbers) -> single row, constructs documented in condition_key, variant fields blank. Gauge-derived: ''From the ratio of pressure midpoints and γ 0.5 for MscL, we calculated γ 0.5 for MscS'' (Methods; MscL anchor 13 mN/m, Belyy 2010b lineage) -> confidence medium, value as-stated. Approximate (∼) activation-curve position. inactivation EXTENT not tau: ''WT MscS shows its maximal inactivation of roughly 40-50% of channels upon exposure to a 10-s step of tension of ∼8 mN/m'' (extent at 10-s/5%-Ficoll 80-90%; G168D <15%/<20%; G113A ∼40%) -> no tau_inact row. Calibration anchors NOT rowed for this paper: WT MscS gamma0.5 = 7.8 mN/m and MscL gamma0.5 = 13 mN/m are ''the previously established midpoint tensions ... (Belyy et al., 2010b)'' — methods-cited; the 7.8 mN/m measurement is rowed from Belyy 2010 itself (this batch); MscL 13 mN/m is paralog-side. RATE constants not converted (1/k forbidden): intrinsic closing rates 2,430 ± 270 s^-1 (n = 6) WT vs 107 ± 24 s^-1 (n = 6) G168D; tension slopes -1.54 ± 0.16 and -2.0 ± 0.17 s^-1/(mN/m). N117V closure ''with a τ of ∼0.1 s at tensions close to 90% of saturating tension'' — single-condition closure constant kept in note (the mutant-recovery constants are the fitted population values rowed). ENERGY/AREA archived: effective in-plane area of the TM barrel ''estimated from the inactivation and recovery kinetics as ∼8 nm2'' (cites Kamaraju et al., 2011). Ficoll raises the activation midpoint (counteracts tension; cytoplasmic crowding pressure) -> modulator_role ''antagonist'' is the closest enum.','excised inside-out patch, N117V / N167V MscS expressed in PB113 (mscL+) spheroplasts, activation midpoint from pressure ramps, native-MscL-gauge-calibrated tension',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',99,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(247,'MAIC:BX:00247',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 clamp: 1-s triangular ramps (midpoints), pulse-step (closing kinetics), pulse-step-pulse protocols (10-s conditioning steps near p0.5, recovery trains); Ficoll 400 / PEG 3350 perfused to the cytoplasmic side | MODULATOR: Ficoll 400 (antagonist) 5 % wt/vol',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,10.0,'%',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10','%','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465-derived / PB113 (mscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT or mutant MscS (pB10d); PB113 with native WT MscL used as the internal tension gauge for mutant gamma0.5 determination','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES + 400 mM sucrose, pH 7.4 (Ficoll/PEG added wt/vol as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00042','Ramp responses measured in the presence of 5% wt/vol Ficoll 400 showed a 10 ± 6% ( n = 10) shift of the activation curve midpoint toward higher pressures for WT MscS, as measured on the ascending limb of the ramp ( Fig. 4 A , red trace). The midpoint on the descending limb also shifted toward higher pressures (22% ± 10%, n = 10), signifying stabilization of the resting state compared with the open state.','Results (G168D mutation affects...; Fig 4 A)','medium','paper''s own explicit % midpoint shift; delta_p50_* is pressure-unit-only and the magnitude is a percentage -> threshold_fold_shift schema_gap (unit ''%'' as reported). Magnitude rowed positive; direction (''toward higher pressures'') stated in the label and quote. Ficoll is a crowding agent acting on the cytoplasmic cage, not a ligand — ''antagonist'' is the closest enum for the threshold-raising effect. 10% Ficoll drives complete WT inactivation (extent, not rowed). inactivation EXTENT not tau: ''WT MscS shows its maximal inactivation of roughly 40-50% of channels upon exposure to a 10-s step of tension of ∼8 mN/m'' (extent at 10-s/5%-Ficoll 80-90%; G168D <15%/<20%; G113A ∼40%) -> no tau_inact row. Calibration anchors NOT rowed for this paper: WT MscS gamma0.5 = 7.8 mN/m and MscL gamma0.5 = 13 mN/m are ''the previously established midpoint tensions ... (Belyy et al., 2010b)'' — methods-cited; the 7.8 mN/m measurement is rowed from Belyy 2010 itself (this batch); MscL 13 mN/m is paralog-side. RATE constants not converted (1/k forbidden): intrinsic closing rates 2,430 ± 270 s^-1 (n = 6) WT vs 107 ± 24 s^-1 (n = 6) G168D; tension slopes -1.54 ± 0.16 and -2.0 ± 0.17 s^-1/(mN/m). N117V closure ''with a τ of ∼0.1 s at tensions close to 90% of saturating tension'' — single-condition closure constant kept in note (the mutant-recovery constants are the fitted population values rowed). ENERGY/AREA archived: effective in-plane area of the TM barrel ''estimated from the inactivation and recovery kinetics as ∼8 nm2'' (cites Kamaraju et al., 2011). Ficoll raises the activation midpoint (counteracts tension; cytoplasmic crowding pressure) -> modulator_role ''antagonist'' is the closest enum.','excised inside-out patch, WT MscS, 5% wt/vol Ficoll 400 on the cytoplasmic side vs 0% control, ascending limb of 1-s ramps','10','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',99,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
