 of roughly 40-50% of channels upon exposure to a 10-s step of tension of ∼8 mN/m'' (extent at 10-s/5%-Ficoll 80-90%; G168D <15%/<20%; G113A ∼40%) -> no tau_inact row. Calibration anchors NOT rowed for this paper: WT MscS gamma0.5 = 7.8 mN/m and MscL gamma0.5 = 13 mN/m are ''the previously established midpoint tensions ... (Belyy et al., 2010b)'' — methods-cited; the 7.8 mN/m measurement is rowed from Belyy 2010 itself (this batch); MscL 13 mN/m is paralog-side. RATE constants not converted (1/k forbidden): intrinsic closing rates 2,430 ± 270 s^-1 (n = 6) WT vs 107 ± 24 s^-1 (n = 6) G168D; tension slopes -1.54 ± 0.16 and -2.0 ± 0.17 s^-1/(mN/m). N117V closure ''with a τ of ∼0.1 s at tensions close to 90% of saturating tension'' — single-condition closure constant kept in note (the mutant-recovery constants are the fitted population values rowed). ENERGY/AREA archived: effective in-plane area of the TM barrel ''estimated from the inactivation and recovery kinetics as ∼8 nm2'' (cites Kamaraju et al., 2011). Ficoll raises the activation midpoint (counteracts tension; cytoplasmic crowding pressure) -> modulator_role ''antagonist'' is the closest enum.','excised inside-out patch, WT MscS, 5% wt/vol Ficoll 400 on the cytoplasmic side vs 0% control, descending limb of 1-s ramps','10','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',99,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(249,'MAIC:BX:00249',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 clamp: 1-s ramps (midpoints), 25-30 s pressure steps with 0.25-s test-pulse trains (inactivation/recovery); 3-min intervals; TFE (0.5-5 vol%) applied to the bath (cytoplasmic side) by perfusion or to the pipette (periplasmic side) by backfill','P50',120.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'120','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing MscS-His6 (pB10b-derived); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetric; + TFE vol% as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (sucrose plug when TFE-backfilled)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00044','Using a typical size of patch pipettes, the midpoint pressure of activation ( p 1/2 ) varied in the range between 120 and 170 mm Hg; however, within each patch, sequential sweeps grouped tightly around a single midpoint with <2% deviation around the mean ( 26 ).','Results (Dose-response curves; Fig 2/Fig 3 text)','medium','population spread of per-patch midpoints (no single mean stated): lower bound stored as value with value_relation ''~'', full interval in error_type=range (TRPV4 range convention). Within-patch midpoints are tight (<2%). RATIO thresholds not rowed (relative-unit rule): bath 2 vol% midpoint ratio 1.13 ± 0.08 (n = 4); pipette 5 vol% ratio 0.93 ± 0.04 (n = 3). Biochemical TFE titration (10-15 vol% complete monomer dissociation in gels) is not channel gating -> no rows. ''full recovery taking ∼3 min'' is stated as PREVIOUS experiments (Akitake 2005 lineage) -> not rowed here (the pilot rows the 3-min bound from Akitake 2005 itself). Washout ''returned 80-100% of the inactivated population'' is an extent -> no row. TFE is a low-dielectric cosolvent partitioning into the bilayer — role enums approximate the threshold-direction effect only (rightward/raising = ''antagonist'', leftward/lowering = ''potentiator''). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, 1-s ramps, control (no TFE), across-patch population range',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',100,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(250,'MAIC:BX:00250',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 clamp: 1-s ramps (midpoints), 25-30 s pressure steps with 0.25-s test-pulse trains (inactivation/recovery); 3-min intervals; TFE (0.5-5 vol%) applied to the bath (cytoplasmic side) by perfusion or to the pipette (periplasmic side) by backfill | MODULATOR: 2,2,2-Trifluoroethanol (TFE) (antagonist) 1.25 vol % (0.5-2 range)','P50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,10.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing MscS-His6 (pB10b-derived); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetric; + TFE vol% as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (sucrose plug when TFE-backfilled)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00045','Perfusion of TFE from the bath (cytoplasmic side of the membrane) even at low concentrations (0.5–2 vol %) invariably shifted p 1/2 to the right by ∼10–40 mm Hg ( Fig. 3, A – C ). The peak ratio of midpoints for 2 vol % TFE in the bath, relative to control, was 1.13 ± 0.08 ( n = 4).','Results (Effects of TFE on MscS gating; Figs 2 and 3)','medium','absolute mmHg endpoints stated -> delta_p50 row (task rule). concentration range stated (0.5-2 vol%) — midpoint of the stated range stored in the modulator concentration field with the range declared in the unit string (review consistency fix: same midpoint convention as the 3-5 vol% row).RATIO thresholds not rowed (relative-unit rule): bath 2 vol% midpoint ratio 1.13 ± 0.08 (n = 4); pipette 5 vol% ratio 0.93 ± 0.04 (n = 3). Biochemical TFE titration (10-15 vol% complete monomer dissociation in gels) is not channel gating -> no rows. ''full recovery taking ∼3 min'' is stated as PREVIOUS experiments (Akitake 2005 lineage) -> not rowed here (the pilot rows the 3-min bound from Akitake 2005 itself). Washout ''returned 80-100% of the inactivated population'' is an extent -> no row. TFE is a low-dielectric cosolvent partitioning into the bilayer — role enums approximate the threshold-direction effect only (rightward/raising = ''antagonist'', leftward/lowering = ''potentiator'').','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, bath (cytoplasmic) TFE 0.5-2 vol%, rightward shift, vs same-patch TFE-free control',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',100,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(251,'MAIC:BX:00251',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 clamp: 1-s ramps (midpoints), 25-30 s pressure steps with 0.25-s test-pulse trains (inactivation/recovery); 3-min intervals; TFE (0.5-5 vol%) applied to the bath (cytoplasmic side) by perfusion or to the pipette (periplasmic side) by backfill | MODULATOR: 2,2,2-Trifluoroethanol (TFE) (potentiator) 1 vol %','P50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'5','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing MscS-His6 (pB10b-derived); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetric; + TFE vol% as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (sucrose plug when TFE-backfilled)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00046','Patches exposed to 1 vol % TFE from the pipette (periplasmic side of the membrane) displayed a slight (∼5 mm Hg) leftward shift of the dose-response curves without any significant effect on G max . ... When the concentration of TFE was increased to 3–5 vol %, larger decreases in p 1/2 (leftward shifts) of ∼20 mm Hg were observed.','Results (Effects of TFE on MscS gating; Fig 2)','medium','absolute mmHg endpoints stated -> delta_p50 row (task rule). MAGNITUDE rowed (5); direction ''leftward'' (p1/2-decreasing, negative delta) stated in the label and quote — no signed value printed in the source.RATIO thresholds not rowed (relative-unit rule): bath 2 vol% midpoint ratio 1.13 ± 0.08 (n = 4); pipette 5 vol% ratio 0.93 ± 0.04 (n = 3). Biochemical TFE titration (10-15 vol% complete monomer dissociation in gels) is not channel gating -> no rows. ''full recovery taking ∼3 min'' is stated as PREVIOUS experiments (Akitake 2005 lineage) -> not rowed here (the pilot rows the 3-min bound from Akitake 2005 itself). Washout ''returned 80-100% of the inactivated population'' is an extent -> no row. TFE is a low-dielectric cosolvent partitioning into the bilayer — role enums approximate the threshold-direction effect only (rightward/raising = ''antagonist'', leftward/lowering = ''potentiator''). [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, pipette (periplasmic) TFE 1 vol%, leftward shift, vs same-patch TFE-free control',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',100,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(252,'MAIC:BX:00252',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 clamp: 1-s ramps (midpoints), 25-30 s pressure steps with 0.25-s test-pulse trains (inactivation/recovery); 3-min intervals; TFE (0.5-5 vol%) applied to the bath (cytoplasmic side) by perfusion or to the pipette (periplasmic side) by backfill | MODULATOR: 2,2,2-Trifluoroethanol (TFE) (potentiator) 4 vol % (3-5 range)','P50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,20.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'20','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing MscS-His6 (pB10b-derived); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetric; + TFE vol% as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (sucrose plug when TFE-backfilled)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00047','Patches exposed to 1 vol % TFE from the pipette (periplasmic side of the membrane) displayed a slight (∼5 mm Hg) leftward shift of the dose-response curves without any significant effect on G max . ... When the concentration of TFE was increased to 3–5 vol %, larger decreases in p 1/2 (leftward shifts) of ∼20 mm Hg were observed.','Results (Effects of TFE on MscS gating; Fig 2)','medium','absolute mmHg endpoints stated -> delta_p50 row (task rule). MAGNITUDE rowed (20); direction ''leftward'' as above. 3-5 vol% range stated — midpoint of the stated range stored in the concentration field with the range declared in the unit string.RATIO thresholds not rowed (relative-unit rule): bath 2 vol% midpoint ratio 1.13 ± 0.08 (n = 4); pipette 5 vol% ratio 0.93 ± 0.04 (n = 3). Biochemical TFE titration (10-15 vol% complete monomer dissociation in gels) is not channel gating -> no rows. ''full recovery taking ∼3 min'' is stated as PREVIOUS experiments (Akitake 2005 lineage) -> not rowed here (the pilot rows the 3-min bound from Akitake 2005 itself). Washout ''returned 80-100% of the inactivated population'' is an extent -> no row. TFE is a low-dielectric cosolvent partitioning into the bilayer — role enums approximate the threshold-direction effect only (rightward/raising = ''antagonist'', leftward/lowering = ''potentiator''). [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, pipette (periplasmic) TFE 3-5 vol%, leftward shift, vs same-patch TFE-free control',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',100,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(253,'MAIC:BX:00253',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'25-s step of subsaturating pressure (160 mm Hg); single-exponential fit of the decaying current','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,2800.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2.8',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing MscS-His6 (pB10b-derived); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetric; + TFE vol% as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (sucrose plug when TFE-backfilled)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00048','Responses to a step of subsaturating pressure (160 mm Hg) recorded on the same patch before ( shaded ) and after TFE perfusion ( solid ). ... The current decay time ( τ i ) decreased from 2.8 s in control to 0.25 s, with TFE illustrating a higher rate of inactivation.','Fig 5 legend (B) + Results (inactivation)','medium','复合 quote 披露（F-004 政策，2026-08-31 补注）：evidence_quote 为原文多处 span 并置（composite 登记册在录）；span 级证据与裁决见 literature/raw/quote_corroboration_manual.json，登记册 tools/literature-mining/configs/composite_quote_registry.json。REPORTED UNIT IS SECONDS: unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to ms at load. REAL fitted single-exponential decay constants (same patch, before/after TFE — the Fig 5 protocol used 3 vol% TFE on the cytoplasmic side) -> rowable tau_inact for both conditions. TFE speeds inactivation ~11-fold. RATIO thresholds not rowed (relative-unit rule): bath 2 vol% midpoint ratio 1.13 ± 0.08 (n = 4); pipette 5 vol% ratio 0.93 ± 0.04 (n = 3). Biochemical TFE titration (10-15 vol% complete monomer dissociation in gels) is not channel gating -> no rows. ''full recovery taking ∼3 min'' is stated as PREVIOUS experiments (Akitake 2005 lineage) -> not rowed here (the pilot rows the 3-min bound from Akitake 2005 itself). Washout ''returned 80-100% of the inactivated population'' is an extent -> no row. TFE is a low-dielectric cosolvent partitioning into the bilayer — role enums approximate the threshold-direction effect only (rightward/raising = ''antagonist'', leftward/lowering = ''potentiator''). [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, 25-s subsaturating pressure step (160 mm Hg), single-exponential decay fit, control (TFE-free)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',100,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(254,'MAIC:BX:00254',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'25-s step of subsaturating pressure (160 mm Hg); single-exponential fit of the decaying current | MODULATOR: 2,2,2-Trifluoroethanol (TFE) (antagonist) 3 vol %','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,250.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.25',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing MscS-His6 (pB10b-derived); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetric; + TFE vol% as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (sucrose plug when TFE-backfilled)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00049','Responses to a step of subsaturating pressure (160 mm Hg) recorded on the same patch before ( shaded ) and after TFE perfusion ( solid ). ... The current decay time ( τ i ) decreased from 2.8 s in control to 0.25 s, with TFE illustrating a higher rate of inactivation.','Fig 5 legend (B) + Results (inactivation)','medium','复合 quote 披露（F-004 政策，2026-08-31 补注）：evidence_quote 为原文多处 span 并置（composite 登记册在录）；span 级证据与裁决见 literature/raw/quote_corroboration_manual.json，登记册 tools/literature-mining/configs/composite_quote_registry.json。REPORTED UNIT IS SECONDS: unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to ms at load. REAL fitted single-exponential decay constants (same patch, before/after TFE — the Fig 5 protocol used 3 vol% TFE on the cytoplasmic side) -> rowable tau_inact for both conditions. TFE speeds inactivation ~11-fold. RATIO thresholds not rowed (relative-unit rule): bath 2 vol% midpoint ratio 1.13 ± 0.08 (n = 4); pipette 5 vol% ratio 0.93 ± 0.04 (n = 3). Biochemical TFE titration (10-15 vol% complete monomer dissociation in gels) is not channel gating -> no rows. ''full recovery taking ∼3 min'' is stated as PREVIOUS experiments (Akitake 2005 lineage) -> not rowed here (the pilot rows the 3-min bound from Akitake 2005 itself). Washout ''returned 80-100% of the inactivated population'' is an extent -> no row. TFE is a low-dielectric cosolvent partitioning into the bilayer — role enums approximate the threshold-direction effect only (rightward/raising = ''antagonist'', leftward/lowering = ''potentiator''). [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, 25-s subsaturating pressure step (160 mm Hg), single-exponential decay fit, after cytoplasmic perfusion of 3 vol% TFE',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',100,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(255,'MAIC:BX:00255',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'30-s intermediate pressure step, then test pulses spaced 1/10/30/60 s; bi-exponential fit of peak-current recovery','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1800.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.8',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing MscS-His6 (pB10b-derived); MscS-only patches','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetric; + TFE vol% as indicated)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (sucrose plug when TFE-backfilled)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00050','Recovery appears to be a multiexponential process with at least two components ( τ 1 r and τ 2 r ). We observed a relatively fast component in the beginning ( τ 1 r = 1.8 s, ∼85–90% G max ), followed by a much slower recovery to the initial G max ( τ 2 r = 18.9 s).','Results + Fig 6 legend (A)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS SECONDS: unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to ms at load. control recovery is multiexponential with at least two components; only the DOMINANT fast component is rowed (extraction-review D-1: two same-condition tau_deact rows 10x apart invite mis-averaging). The slow component is ARCHIVED here, not rowed: τ2r = 18.9 s (''completion of recovery to the initial Gmax''); a possible third longer component is also declared (''a third component with a longer characteristic time but smaller contribution may exist''). These are recovery-fit components, not open-dwell taus. TFE lengthens recovery qualitatively (no numeric tau under TFE) -> no TFE-condition tau_deact row. RATIO thresholds not rowed (relative-unit rule): bath 2 vol% midpoint ratio 1.13 ± 0.08 (n = 4); pipette 5 vol% ratio 0.93 ± 0.04 (n = 3). Biochemical TFE titration (10-15 vol% complete monomer dissociation in gels) is not channel gating -> no rows. ''full recovery taking ∼3 min'' is stated as PREVIOUS experiments (Akitake 2005 lineage) -> not rowed here (the pilot rows the 3-min bound from Akitake 2005 itself). Washout ''returned 80-100% of the inactivated population'' is an extent -> no row. TFE is a low-dielectric cosolvent partitioning into the bilayer — role enums approximate the threshold-direction effect only (rightward/raising = ''antagonist'', leftward/lowering = ''potentiator'').','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, train of 0.25-s saturating test pulses after a 30-s inactivating step, two-exponential recovery fit, fast component (∼85–90% of Gmax), control (no TFE)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',100,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(256,'MAIC:BX:00256',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pressure ramps with negative pressure; decay-rate and open-dwell analysis in Clampfit 10.3; sampling 30303 Hz, 5 kHz lowpass | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.08 (sd)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1320.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.32',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF429 (mscS-/mscK-, MscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT or mutant MscS (pB10d, C-terminal 6-His); native MscL retained as internal pressure standard','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.5,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.5','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.5 (symmetrical)',-20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00051','The conductance of the wildtype channel was determined to be 1.32±0.08 nS.; Table 1 ## Kinetic values for wildtype channel and mutants. Pressure Threshold Ratio (P S /P L ) Conductance (nS) Rate of Inactivation (sec) Open Dwell Time (msec) WT 0.69±0.03 1.32±0.08 ND 1 ND 2 L118F 0.56±0.02 1.34±0.06 ND 1 ND 2 F127E 0.54±0.07 1.33±0.04 ND 1 ND 2 A120S 0.67±0.01 1.30±0.02 2.1±1.5 ND 2 F127T 0.59±0.03 1.36±0.08 3.0±1.8 ND 2 S114I 0.65±0.02 0.96±0.08 1.4±0.1 1.4±1.7 S114T 0.61±0.03 1.34±0.04 1.9±0.5 2.1±3.6 L123F 0.73±0.03 1.25±0.04 ND 1 0.8±0.9 F127K 0.77±0.03 1.33±0.04 0.6±0.2 2.0±2.9 All values have been calculated from at least 4 independent patches from at least two preps and the error is the standard deviation.','Results (Kinetic Analysis of Point Mutations; Table 1)','high','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). own-data WT conductance (Table 1 column ''Conductance (nS)''); error is the standard deviation, values from ≥4 independent patches / ≥2 preps. ''Rate of Inactivation (sec)'' table column: values are in SECONDS (0.6-3.0) while the header and text consistently say ''rate'' (''inactivation rates that are less than 4 seconds'') — dimensionally ambiguous (a rate would be s^-1); per the task rule the paper''s own wording is ambiguous -> NO tau_inact rows, values archived here: A120S 2.1±1.5, F127T 3.0±1.8, S114I 1.4±0.1, S114T 1.9±0.5, F127K 0.6±0.2 (WT and three mutants ND). Open Dwell Time column (msec) NEVER rowed (dwell components). P_S/P_L threshold ratios (WT 0.69±0.03; L118F 0.56±0.02; F127E 0.54±0.07; A120S 0.67±0.01; F127T 0.59±0.03; S114I 0.65±0.02; S114T 0.61±0.03; L123F 0.73±0.03; F127K 0.77±0.03) are MscL-referenced ratios -> no p50 rows (ratio rule). delta_p50 Y-flag: ''L118F showed a very slight but significant difference from wildtype ... gating at a statistically lower pressure thresholds'' — ratio-only statement -> no row. Mutant conductances (Table 1 ''Conductance (nS)'' column) ARE rowed as 8 separate mutant rows (extraction-review G-3: own-data absolute values, core DB use case); they cluster at 1.25-1.36 nS with S114I 0.96±0.08 nS the outlier. [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (Results sentence + rendered Table 1 content; Table 1 in archive in order, quote rendering artifacts block literal grep; classified 2026-08-31, r2)','excised inside-out patch, MJF429 spheroplast WT MscS, single-channel openings on negative-pressure ramps, symmetric 200 mM KCl, -20 mV',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',101,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(257,'MAIC:BX:00257',5,NULL,NULL,51,'pressure ramps with negative pressure; decay-rate and open-dwell analysis in Clampfit 10.3; sampling 30303 Hz, 5 kHz lowpass | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.06 (sd)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1340.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.34',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF429 (mscS-/mscK-, MscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT or mutant MscS (pB10d, C-terminal 6-His); native MscL retained as internal pressure standard','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.5,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.5','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.5 (symmetrical)',-20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00052','Table 1 ## Kinetic values for wildtype channel and mutants. Pressure Threshold Ratio (P S /P L ) Conductance (nS) Rate of Inactivation (sec) Open Dwell Time (msec) WT 0.69±0.03 1.32±0.08 ND 1 ND 2 L118F 0.56±0.02 1.34±0.06 ND 1 ND 2 F127E 0.54±0.07 1.33±0.04 ND 1 ND 2 A120S 0.67±0.01 1.30±0.02 2.1±1.5 ND 2 F127T 0.59±0.03 1.36±0.08 3.0±1.8 ND 2 S114I 0.65±0.02 0.96±0.08 1.4±0.1 1.4±1.7 S114T 0.61±0.03 1.34±0.04 1.9±0.5 2.1±3.6 L123F 0.73±0.03 1.25±0.04 ND 1 0.8±0.9 F127K 0.77±0.03 1.33±0.04 0.6±0.2 2.0±2.9 All values have been calculated from at least 4 independent patches from at least two preps and the error is the standard deviation.','Table 1 (Kinetic values for wildtype channel and mutants)','high','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). own-data L118F mutant conductance (Table 1 ''Conductance (nS)'' column); error is the standard deviation (table footer), ≥4 independent patches / ≥2 preps. Same-table P_S/P_L ratio / inactivation-time / open-dwell columns NOT rowed (ratio rule / ambiguous-header rule / dwell rule — see batch notes). ''Rate of Inactivation (sec)'' table column: values are in SECONDS (0.6-3.0) while the header and text consistently say ''rate'' (''inactivation rates that are less than 4 seconds'') — dimensionally ambiguous (a rate would be s^-1); per the task rule the paper''s own wording is ambiguous -> NO tau_inact rows, values archived here: A120S 2.1±1.5, F127T 3.0±1.8, S114I 1.4±0.1, S114T 1.9±0.5, F127K 0.6±0.2 (WT and three mutants ND). Open Dwell Time column (msec) NEVER rowed (dwell components). P_S/P_L threshold ratios (WT 0.69±0.03; L118F 0.56±0.02; F127E 0.54±0.07; A120S 0.67±0.01; F127T 0.59±0.03; S114I 0.65±0.02; S114T 0.61±0.03; L123F 0.73±0.03; F127K 0.77±0.03) are MscL-referenced ratios -> no p50 rows (ratio rule). delta_p50 Y-flag: ''L118F showed a very slight but significant difference from wildtype ... gating at a statistically lower pressure thresholds'' — ratio-only statement -> no row. Mutant conductances (Table 1 ''Conductance (nS)'' column) ARE rowed as 8 separate mutant rows (extraction-review G-3: own-data absolute values, core DB use case); they cluster at 1.25-1.36 nS with S114I 0.96±0.08 nS the outlier.','excised inside-out patch, MJF429 spheroplast L118F MscS mutant, single-channel openings on negative-pressure ramps, symmetric 200 mM KCl, -20 mV',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',101,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(258,'MAIC:BX:00258',5,NULL,NULL,52,'pressure ramps with negative pressure; decay-rate and open-dwell analysis in Clampfit 10.3; sampling 30303 Hz, 5 kHz lowpass | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.04 (sd)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1330.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.33',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF429 (mscS-/mscK-, MscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT or mutant MscS (pB10d, C-terminal 6-His); native MscL retained as internal pressure standard','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.5,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.5','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.5 (symmetrical)',-20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00053','Table 1 ## Kinetic values for wildtype channel and mutants. Pressure Threshold Ratio (P S /P L ) Conductance (nS) Rate of Inactivation (sec) Open Dwell Time (msec) WT 0.69±0.03 1.32±0.08 ND 1 ND 2 L118F 0.56±0.02 1.34±0.06 ND 1 ND 2 F127E 0.54±0.07 1.33±0.04 ND 1 ND 2 A120S 0.67±0.01 1.30±0.02 2.1±1.5 ND 2 F127T 0.59±0.03 1.36±0.08 3.0±1.8 ND 2 S114I 0.65±0.02 0.96±0.08 1.4±0.1 1.4±1.7 S114T 0.61±0.03 1.34±0.04 1.9±0.5 2.1±3.6 L123F 0.73±0.03 1.25±0.04 ND 1 0.8±0.9 F127K 0.77±0.03 1.33±0.04 0.6±0.2 2.0±2.9 All values have been calculated from at least 4 independent patches from at least two preps and the error is the standard deviation.','Table 1 (Kinetic values for wildtype channel and mutants)','high','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). own-data F127E mutant conductance (Table 1 ''Conductance (nS)'' column); error is the standard deviation (table footer), ≥4 independent patches / ≥2 preps. Same-table P_S/P_L ratio / inactivation-time / open-dwell columns NOT rowed (ratio rule / ambiguous-header rule / dwell rule — see batch notes). ''Rate of Inactivation (sec)'' table column: values are in SECONDS (0.6-3.0) while the header and text consistently say ''rate'' (''inactivation rates that are less than 4 seconds'') — dimensionally ambiguous (a rate would be s^-1); per the task rule the paper''s own wording is ambiguous -> NO tau_inact rows, values archived here: A120S 2.1±1.5, F127T 3.0±1.8, S114I 1.4±0.1, S114T 1.9±0.5, F127K 0.6±0.2 (WT and three mutants ND). Open Dwell Time column (msec) NEVER rowed (dwell components). P_S/P_L threshold ratios (WT 0.69±0.03; L118F 0.56±0.02; F127E 0.54±0.07; A120S 0.67±0.01; F127T 0.59±0.03; S114I 0.65±0.02; S114T 0.61±0.03; L123F 0.73±0.03; F127K 0.77±0.03) are MscL-referenced ratios -> no p50 rows (ratio rule). delta_p50 Y-flag: ''L118F showed a very slight but significant difference from wildtype ... gating at a statistically lower pressure thresholds'' — ratio-only statement -> no row. Mutant conductances (Table 1 ''Conductance (nS)'' column) ARE rowed as 8 separate mutant rows (extraction-review G-3: own-data absolute values, core DB use case); they cluster at 1.25-1.36 nS with S114I 0.96±0.08 nS the outlier.','excised inside-out patch, MJF429 spheroplast F127E MscS mutant, single-channel openings on negative-pressure ramps, symmetric 200 mM KCl, -20 mV',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',101,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
