INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(264,'MAIC:BX:00264',5,NULL,NULL,58,'pressure ramps with negative pressure; decay-rate and open-dwell analysis in Clampfit 10.3; sampling 30303 Hz, 5 kHz lowpass | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.04 (sd)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1330.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.33',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF429 (mscS-/mscK-, MscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT or mutant MscS (pB10d, C-terminal 6-His); native MscL retained as internal pressure standard','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.5,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.5','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.5 (symmetrical)',-20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00059','Table 1 ## Kinetic values for wildtype channel and mutants. Pressure Threshold Ratio (P S /P L ) Conductance (nS) Rate of Inactivation (sec) Open Dwell Time (msec) WT 0.69±0.03 1.32±0.08 ND 1 ND 2 L118F 0.56±0.02 1.34±0.06 ND 1 ND 2 F127E 0.54±0.07 1.33±0.04 ND 1 ND 2 A120S 0.67±0.01 1.30±0.02 2.1±1.5 ND 2 F127T 0.59±0.03 1.36±0.08 3.0±1.8 ND 2 S114I 0.65±0.02 0.96±0.08 1.4±0.1 1.4±1.7 S114T 0.61±0.03 1.34±0.04 1.9±0.5 2.1±3.6 L123F 0.73±0.03 1.25±0.04 ND 1 0.8±0.9 F127K 0.77±0.03 1.33±0.04 0.6±0.2 2.0±2.9 All values have been calculated from at least 4 independent patches from at least two preps and the error is the standard deviation.','Table 1 (Kinetic values for wildtype channel and mutants)','high','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). own-data F127K mutant conductance (Table 1 ''Conductance (nS)'' column); error is the standard deviation (table footer), ≥4 independent patches / ≥2 preps. Same-table P_S/P_L ratio / inactivation-time / open-dwell columns NOT rowed (ratio rule / ambiguous-header rule / dwell rule — see batch notes). ''Rate of Inactivation (sec)'' table column: values are in SECONDS (0.6-3.0) while the header and text consistently say ''rate'' (''inactivation rates that are less than 4 seconds'') — dimensionally ambiguous (a rate would be s^-1); per the task rule the paper''s own wording is ambiguous -> NO tau_inact rows, values archived here: A120S 2.1±1.5, F127T 3.0±1.8, S114I 1.4±0.1, S114T 1.9±0.5, F127K 0.6±0.2 (WT and three mutants ND). Open Dwell Time column (msec) NEVER rowed (dwell components). P_S/P_L threshold ratios (WT 0.69±0.03; L118F 0.56±0.02; F127E 0.54±0.07; A120S 0.67±0.01; F127T 0.59±0.03; S114I 0.65±0.02; S114T 0.61±0.03; L123F 0.73±0.03; F127K 0.77±0.03) are MscL-referenced ratios -> no p50 rows (ratio rule). delta_p50 Y-flag: ''L118F showed a very slight but significant difference from wildtype ... gating at a statistically lower pressure thresholds'' — ratio-only statement -> no row. Mutant conductances (Table 1 ''Conductance (nS)'' column) ARE rowed as 8 separate mutant rows (extraction-review G-3: own-data absolute values, core DB use case); they cluster at 1.25-1.36 nS with S114I 0.96±0.08 nS the outlier.','excised inside-out patch, MJF429 spheroplast F127K MscS mutant, single-channel openings on negative-pressure ramps, symmetric 200 mM KCl, -20 mV',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',101,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(265,'MAIC:BX:00265',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 clamp: 500-ms ramps to score MscS/MscL midpoints before and after 59-s conditioning stimuli; whole-spheroplast recordings with simultaneous patch imaging for the tension calibration','T50',NULL,NULL,7.8,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'7.8','mN/m','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OTHER','E. coli giant spheroplasts (whole-spheroplast mode) with WT MscS; patch curvature imaged for the pressure-to-tension conversion','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl + symmetric salts (spheroplast recording buffer)','200 mM KCl + symmetric salts',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00060','The fit of the averaged curve to the Boltzmann-type equation (see Materials and methods) produces the values of ΔE = 1.17 × 10 −19 J (28 kT) and ΔA = 14.7 nm 2 (solid black line). The combined fit indicated average midpoint γ 0.5 = 7.8 mN/m.','Fig legend (whole-spheroplast MscS activation curve)','medium','direct own-data whole-spheroplast midpoint (the value later used as the 7.8 mN/m calibration anchor by Kamaraju 2011 / Rowe 2014 / Dave 2021); tension from Laplace + imaged patch curvature. recording_mode OTHER: ''whole spheroplast mode'' has no enum member (intact spheroplast + imaging, not a ruptured whole-cell). The ΔE/ΔA values in the same quote are archived, not rowed. PARALOG (MscL-side) numerics excluded everywhere: adaptation tau 1.89 s; midpoint shift 10-20 mmHg; whole-spheroplast MscL V23T recordings; MscL densities. conductance Y-flag: ''unitary MscS currents (10 pA at -30 mV) appear three times smaller than in excised patches (30 pA)'' — current AMPLITUDES, not a conductance -> no row. ENERGY/AREA archived (no parameter_kind home): ΔE = 28 kT, ΔA = 14.7 nm2 (whole-spheroplast Boltzmann fit); ''the slope corresponding to ∼15-nm2 in-plane expansion''. The adaptation mode-shift is a membrane-mechanics-driven displacement of the activation curve, distinct from MscS inactivation — rowed as tau_inact because it is the fitted time constant of the loss of mechanosensitivity under tension.','whole-spheroplast recording of WT MscS with simultaneous patch imaging, Boltzmann fit of the averaged activation curve (native spheroplast membrane)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',102,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(266,'MAIC:BX:00266',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'midpoints scored with identical 500-ms ramps before/after conditioning stimuli of increasing duration; exponential fit of midpoint shift vs duration','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,2000.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2.0',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','PB113 (mscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts co-expressing WT MscS and WT MscL (two-wave patches)','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl + symmetric salts (spheroplast recording buffer)','200 mM KCl + symmetric salts',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00061','Fitted with single-exponential functions, this dataset yielded remarkably similar characteristic times (τ = 1.89 s for MscL and 2.00 s for MscS).','Results (Fig 2 C legend)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS SECONDS: unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to ms at load. REAL single-exponential time constant of the MscS adaptation/mode-shift (rightward displacement of the activation curve under repeated stimulation), explicitly attributed to MscS — the MscL value in the same sentence (1.89 s) is paralog-side and NOT rowed. Rowed as tau_inact as the closest tau kind (slow loss of mechanosensitivity); it is NOT the classic open->inactivated current decay. PARALOG (MscL-side) numerics excluded everywhere: adaptation tau 1.89 s; midpoint shift 10-20 mmHg; whole-spheroplast MscL V23T recordings; MscL densities. conductance Y-flag: ''unitary MscS currents (10 pA at -30 mV) appear three times smaller than in excised patches (30 pA)'' — current AMPLITUDES, not a conductance -> no row. ENERGY/AREA archived (no parameter_kind home): ΔE = 28 kT, ΔA = 14.7 nm2 (whole-spheroplast Boltzmann fit); ''the slope corresponding to ∼15-nm2 in-plane expansion''. The adaptation mode-shift is a membrane-mechanics-driven displacement of the activation curve, distinct from MscS inactivation — rowed as tau_inact because it is the fitted time constant of the loss of mechanosensitivity under tension.','excised inside-out patch, WT MscS, midpoint-vs-conditioning-duration series (500-ms ramps bracketing 59-s preconditioning stimuli), single-exponential fit',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',102,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(267,'MAIC:BX:00267',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'adaptation induced by pressure steps of varying length/magnitude, then released; midpoint re-scored','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,200.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'200','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','PB113 (mscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts co-expressing WT MscS and WT MscL (two-wave patches)','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl + symmetric salts (spheroplast recording buffer)','200 mM KCl + symmetric salts',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00062','Our observations show that in the absence of pressure, adaptation reverses with a characteristic time of ∼200 ms to several seconds, depending on both the length and magnitude of the adaptation-inducing pressure step.','Discussion (adaptation reversal)','medium','lower bound of the stated range (''∼200 ms to several seconds'') stored as value with value_relation ''~''; the upper end (''several seconds'') is not numeric -> no error_high invented. Dependent on the preceding conditioning step. PARALOG (MscL-side) numerics excluded everywhere: adaptation tau 1.89 s; midpoint shift 10-20 mmHg; whole-spheroplast MscL V23T recordings; MscL densities. conductance Y-flag: ''unitary MscS currents (10 pA at -30 mV) appear three times smaller than in excised patches (30 pA)'' — current AMPLITUDES, not a conductance -> no row. ENERGY/AREA archived (no parameter_kind home): ΔE = 28 kT, ΔA = 14.7 nm2 (whole-spheroplast Boltzmann fit); ''the slope corresponding to ∼15-nm2 in-plane expansion''. The adaptation mode-shift is a membrane-mechanics-driven displacement of the activation curve, distinct from MscS inactivation — rowed as tau_inact because it is the fitted time constant of the loss of mechanosensitivity under tension.','excised inside-out patch, WT MscS, return of the activation midpoint to the naive position after pressure release (zero tension)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',102,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(268,'MAIC:BX:00268',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 clamp: 500-ms ramps to score MscS/MscL midpoints before and after 59-s conditioning stimuli; whole-spheroplast recordings with simultaneous patch imaging for the tension calibration','P50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,15.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','PB113 (mscL+) E. coli giant spheroplasts co-expressing WT MscS and WT MscL (two-wave patches)','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl + symmetric salts (spheroplast recording buffer)','200 mM KCl + symmetric salts',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00063','In six independent patches, the midpoint shift of MscS varied between 15 and 25 mmHg after a 59-s preconditioning stimulus, whereas the midpoint shift of MscL varied between 10 and 20 mmHg.','Results (Fig 2 legend)','medium','across-patch range 15-25 mmHg: lower bound stored as value with value_relation ''~'', full interval in error_type=range, n = 6 patches. Direction is ''toward higher tension'' (right shift) per the surrounding text. The MscL 10-20 mmHg counterpart is paralog-side -> not rowed. PARALOG (MscL-side) numerics excluded everywhere: adaptation tau 1.89 s; midpoint shift 10-20 mmHg; whole-spheroplast MscL V23T recordings; MscL densities. conductance Y-flag: ''unitary MscS currents (10 pA at -30 mV) appear three times smaller than in excised patches (30 pA)'' — current AMPLITUDES, not a conductance -> no row. ENERGY/AREA archived (no parameter_kind home): ΔE = 28 kT, ΔA = 14.7 nm2 (whole-spheroplast Boltzmann fit); ''the slope corresponding to ∼15-nm2 in-plane expansion''. The adaptation mode-shift is a membrane-mechanics-driven displacement of the activation curve, distinct from MscS inactivation — rowed as tau_inact because it is the fitted time constant of the loss of mechanosensitivity under tension.','excised inside-out patch, WT MscS, midpoint shift after a 59-s preconditioning stimulus vs naive, six independent patches','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',102,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(269,'MAIC:BX:00269',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pressure application on excised patches; I-V from holding potentials -50 mV to +50 mV (10-mV steps) in symmetric then asymmetric KCl','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-9.5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-9.5','mV','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF429 (mscS-/mscK-, MscL+) E. coli protoplasts expressing WT or mutant MscS (pMscSH6); native MscL retained as the pressure standard','E. coli protoplast / giant spheroplast',NULL,7.1,'200 mM KCl (symmetric) or 600 mM KCl (asymmetric), 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.1 ± 0.1','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.1 ± 0.1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00064','TABLE 1 Reversal potentials for MscS mutant channels Channel E rev (mV) Wild-type -9.5 R88S -11.3 T93R -11.0 G101D -8.0 G113A -10.0 G113D -12.4 G113M -10.0 G113R -9.3 The mean reversal potential ( E rev ) was determined from the current-voltage plots recorded for each mutant. None of the mutant reversal potentials were significantly different from that of wild-typ','Table 1 (Reversal potentials for MscS mutant channels)','high','own-data Table 1 WT E_rev under the 200/600 mM KCl gradient; anion preference (negative E_rev toward E_Cl). n from the WT P_L:P_S series (n = 15 patches). ATTRIBUTION rulings: ''The conductance of each mutant tested here was similar to the mean of 1.25 nS reported previously for wild-type MscS (13)'' — the 1.25 nS is a previously-reported (intro-cited) value -> NEVER rowed. The ∼750 pS level is the paper''s OWN observation for the G113P mutant (flickery open state, cannot reach full conductance) -> rowed below. P_L:P_S ratio tables NOT rows (MscL-referenced ratios; ratio rule): WT 1.62 ± 0.03 (n = 15), G113D 1.31 ± 0.03 (n = 7), G113R 1.43 ± 0.03 (n = 8), R88S 1.39 ± 0.03 (n = 5), G113A 1.45 ± 0.04 (n = 8), G113P 1.33 ± 0.03 (n = 5); delta_p50 Y-flag covered by these ratio-only statements -> no rows. Mutant E_revs (R88S -11.3, T93R -11.0, G101D -8.0, G113A -10.0, G113D -12.4, G113M -10.0, G113R -9.3) are all not significantly different from WT -> archived here, WT rowed only (task directive). tau_inact flag: ''The mean open dwell time for MscS-Ec channels is ∼150 ms (13)'' is an intro-cited DWELL time (ref 13) -> no tau row; own desensitization analysis is qualitative. G113D ''∼10% decrease in conductance'' is a relative statement -> no row. PORE geometry archived: ''The MscS channel pore attains a diameter calculated to be ∼14-16 Å in the open conformation''.','excised inside-out patch, MJF429 protoplast WT MscS, I-V under asymmetric KCl (200 mM pipette / 600 mM bath), zero-current intercept','15','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',103,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(270,'MAIC:BX:00270',5,NULL,NULL,59,'pressure application on excised patches; I-V from holding potentials -50 mV to +50 mV (10-mV steps) in symmetric then asymmetric KCl','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,750.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'750','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF429 (mscS-/mscK-, MscL+) E. coli protoplasts expressing WT or mutant MscS (pMscSH6); native MscL retained as the pressure standard','E. coli protoplast / giant spheroplast',NULL,7.1,'200 mM KCl (symmetric) or 600 mM KCl (asymmetric), 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.1 ± 0.1','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.1 ± 0.1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00065','Further, these mutant channels commonly opened to a single-channel conductance level of only ∼750 pS and appeared unable to achieve the fully open state because open dwell times were not sufficiently long to capture measurable larger conductance levels with our recording system.','Results (mutants at Gly 113; Fig 6)','medium','OWN observation for the G113P hinge mutant — the channel ''appeared unable to achieve the fully open state'', opening to a ∼750 pS level only (a substate, not the full conductance; declared in the label). Unit pS as printed. ATTRIBUTION rulings: ''The conductance of each mutant tested here was similar to the mean of 1.25 nS reported previously for wild-type MscS (13)'' — the 1.25 nS is a previously-reported (intro-cited) value -> NEVER rowed. The ∼750 pS level is the paper''s OWN observation for the G113P mutant (flickery open state, cannot reach full conductance) -> rowed below. P_L:P_S ratio tables NOT rows (MscL-referenced ratios; ratio rule): WT 1.62 ± 0.03 (n = 15), G113D 1.31 ± 0.03 (n = 7), G113R 1.43 ± 0.03 (n = 8), R88S 1.39 ± 0.03 (n = 5), G113A 1.45 ± 0.04 (n = 8), G113P 1.33 ± 0.03 (n = 5); delta_p50 Y-flag covered by these ratio-only statements -> no rows. Mutant E_revs (R88S -11.3, T93R -11.0, G101D -8.0, G113A -10.0, G113D -12.4, G113M -10.0, G113R -9.3) are all not significantly different from WT -> archived here, WT rowed only (task directive). tau_inact flag: ''The mean open dwell time for MscS-Ec channels is ∼150 ms (13)'' is an intro-cited DWELL time (ref 13) -> no tau row; own desensitization analysis is qualitative. G113D ''∼10% decrease in conductance'' is a relative statement -> no row. PORE geometry archived: ''The MscS channel pore attains a diameter calculated to be ∼14-16 Å in the open conformation''.','excised inside-out patch, MJF429 protoplast G113P MscS, single-channel openings under sustained pressure, symmetric 200 mM KCl',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',103,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(271,'MAIC:BX:00271',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 high-speed pressure clamp; 1-s saturating ramps for midpoints, slow ramps for single-channel events; trehalose (0.5-1 M) applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) side | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.1','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1000.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.0',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','giant spheroplasts of V. cholerae N16961 (native channels) and E. coli AW405 controls; excised patches','V. cholerae giant spheroplast (MscS-like + MscL-like native channels)',NULL,NULL,'symmetric recording buffer (200 mM KCl base) + trehalose as indicated','symmetric recording buffer (200 mM KCl base)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00066','From multiple traces taken at different voltages, we created I-V plots and determined slope conductances at hyperpolarizing voltages (pipette positive) for single MscS-like (1.0 ± 0.1 nS) and MscL-like channels (2.6 ± 0.1 nS, or 2.9 nS after Rs correction) of V. cholerae ( Fig. 3 ).','Results (single-channel conductances; Fig 3)','high','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). V. cholerae ortholog (species in condition_key). Error type not stated. The MscL-like 2.6 ± 0.1 nS (2.9 Rs-corrected) in the same sentence is paralog-side -> NOT rowed. ORTHOLOG species in condition_key (VcMscS = V. cholerae MscS-like). TASK-NOTE DISCREPANCY declared: the extraction task listed ''24±4%/11±2% trehalose fold-shifts'' — those exact numerals are the MscL-LIKE (paralog) shifts in the source sentence; the MscS-side values are 24 ± 16% (V. cholerae) and 12 ± 5% (E. coli), rowed here, while the MscL-side 24±4%/11±2% are excluded with this note. p0.5 ratio 0.48 ± 0.04 (V. cholerae) / 0.60 ± 0.05 (E. coli) and the MscL-gauge calibration (EcMscL ≈ 12 mN/m) are ratio/referenced quantities -> no rows. Channel DENSITIES archived (no parameter_kind home): V. cholerae 1.2 ± 0.7 MscS-like and 11 ± 4 MscL-like channels/µm2; E. coli 3.6 ± 1.8 / 4.3 ± 2.2; patch radii 1.37 ± 0.3 µm. MscL-side conductance 2.6 ± 0.1 nS (2.9 nS Rs-corrected) is paralog -> not rowed. iv_relation: ''characteristic inward rectification and subconductive states at depolarizing voltages'' — kept in this note rather than an iv_relation row (rectifying terminology refers to the single-channel I-V shape; task directive rows conductance only).','excised inside-out patch, V. cholerae giant spheroplast native MscS-like (VcMscS) channels, I-V slope at hyperpolarizing voltages (pipette positive)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',104,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(272,'MAIC:BX:00272',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 high-speed pressure clamp; 1-s saturating ramps for midpoints, slow ramps for single-channel events; trehalose (0.5-1 M) applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) side','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,2000.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','giant spheroplasts of V. cholerae N16961 (native channels) and E. coli AW405 controls; excised patches','V. cholerae giant spheroplast (MscS-like + MscL-like native channels)',NULL,NULL,'symmetric recording buffer (200 mM KCl base) + trehalose as indicated','symmetric recording buffer (200 mM KCl base)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00067','The Vibrio MscS-like channels exhibit characteristic inward rectification and subconductive states at depolarizing voltages; they also adapt and inactivate at subsaturating tensions and recover within 2 s upon tension release, just like E. coli MscS.','Abstract / Results (adaptation and recovery of Vibrio MscS-like channels)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS SECONDS: unit column left blank because the tau_* storage vocabulary fixes ms; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to ms at load. ''recover within 2 s upon tension release, just like E. coli MscS'' — completion bound, rowed with value_relation ''<'' (same convention as the pilot''s 3-min lower bound, opposite direction); no fitted constant stated. ORTHOLOG species in condition_key (VcMscS = V. cholerae MscS-like). TASK-NOTE DISCREPANCY declared: the extraction task listed ''24±4%/11±2% trehalose fold-shifts'' — those exact numerals are the MscL-LIKE (paralog) shifts in the source sentence; the MscS-side values are 24 ± 16% (V. cholerae) and 12 ± 5% (E. coli), rowed here, while the MscL-side 24±4%/11±2% are excluded with this note. p0.5 ratio 0.48 ± 0.04 (V. cholerae) / 0.60 ± 0.05 (E. coli) and the MscL-gauge calibration (EcMscL ≈ 12 mN/m) are ratio/referenced quantities -> no rows. Channel DENSITIES archived (no parameter_kind home): V. cholerae 1.2 ± 0.7 MscS-like and 11 ± 4 MscL-like channels/µm2; E. coli 3.6 ± 1.8 / 4.3 ± 2.2; patch radii 1.37 ± 0.3 µm. MscL-side conductance 2.6 ± 0.1 nS (2.9 nS Rs-corrected) is paralog -> not rowed. iv_relation: ''characteristic inward rectification and subconductive states at depolarizing voltages'' — kept in this note rather than an iv_relation row (rectifying terminology refers to the single-channel I-V shape; task directive rows conductance only). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, V. cholerae native MscS-like (VcMscS) channels, adaptation/inactivation at subsaturating tensions then tension release',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',104,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(273,'MAIC:BX:00273',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 high-speed pressure clamp; 1-s saturating ramps for midpoints, slow ramps for single-channel events; trehalose (0.5-1 M) applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) side | MODULATOR: trehalose (antagonist) 1 M',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,24.0,'%',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'24','%','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','giant spheroplasts of V. cholerae N16961 (native channels) and E. coli AW405 controls; excised patches','V. cholerae giant spheroplast (MscS-like + MscL-like native channels)',NULL,NULL,'symmetric recording buffer (200 mM KCl base) + trehalose as indicated','symmetric recording buffer (200 mM KCl base)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00068','In four independent experiments, the average shift of MscS activation midpoint in the presence of 1 M trehalose was 24 ± 16% for V. cholerae and 12 ± 5% for E. coli . Shifts of MscL-like channels were 24 ± 4% and 11 ± 2% for V. cholerae and E. coli , respectively.','Results (Both MscS-like and MscL-like channels are modulated by compatible osmolytes; Fig 6)','medium','paper''s own explicit % midpoint shift (n = 4); magnitude rowed positive, direction ''right-shift of the activation curve'' stated in the label and the Fig 6 text. Trehalose is a compatible osmolyte/crowder -> ''antagonist'' as the closest enum for the threshold-raising effect. ORTHOLOG species in condition_key (VcMscS = V. cholerae MscS-like). TASK-NOTE DISCREPANCY declared: the extraction task listed ''24±4%/11±2% trehalose fold-shifts'' — those exact numerals are the MscL-LIKE (paralog) shifts in the source sentence; the MscS-side values are 24 ± 16% (V. cholerae) and 12 ± 5% (E. coli), rowed here, while the MscL-side 24±4%/11±2% are excluded with this note. p0.5 ratio 0.48 ± 0.04 (V. cholerae) / 0.60 ± 0.05 (E. coli) and the MscL-gauge calibration (EcMscL ≈ 12 mN/m) are ratio/referenced quantities -> no rows. Channel DENSITIES archived (no parameter_kind home): V. cholerae 1.2 ± 0.7 MscS-like and 11 ± 4 MscL-like channels/µm2; E. coli 3.6 ± 1.8 / 4.3 ± 2.2; patch radii 1.37 ± 0.3 µm. MscL-side conductance 2.6 ± 0.1 nS (2.9 nS Rs-corrected) is paralog -> not rowed. iv_relation: ''characteristic inward rectification and subconductive states at depolarizing voltages'' — kept in this note rather than an iv_relation row (rectifying terminology refers to the single-channel I-V shape; task directive rows conductance only).','excised inside-out patch, V. cholerae (VcMscS) native MscS-like channels, 1 M trehalose on the cytoplasmic side vs control, midpoint shift','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',104,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
