o/referenced quantities -> no rows. Channel DENSITIES archived (no parameter_kind home): V. cholerae 1.2 ± 0.7 MscS-like and 11 ± 4 MscL-like channels/µm2; E. coli 3.6 ± 1.8 / 4.3 ± 2.2; patch radii 1.37 ± 0.3 µm. MscL-side conductance 2.6 ± 0.1 nS (2.9 nS Rs-corrected) is paralog -> not rowed. iv_relation: ''characteristic inward rectification and subconductive states at depolarizing voltages'' — kept in this note rather than an iv_relation row (rectifying terminology refers to the single-channel I-V shape; task directive rows conductance only).','excised inside-out patch, E. coli (EcMscS) native MscS-like channels, 1 M trehalose on the cytoplasmic side vs control, midpoint shift','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',104,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(275,'MAIC:BX:00275',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pneumatic suction pulses (e.g. 215 mm Hg) at constant +15 mV pipette voltage; cosolvents (ficoll 400, dextran, glucose, PEGs) applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) or periplasmic (pipette) side at matched osmolarity (760 mOsm/kg H2O, sorbitol-adjusted)','P50',207.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'207','mm Hg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','E. coli MJF379 (Frag1 kefA::kan, MscS+ MscL+) giant spheroplasts; recordings focused on the MscS population','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.2,'150 mM KCl, 400 mM sorbitol, 4 mM CaCl2, 5 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (+ cosolvent as indicated)','150 mM KCl, 400 mM sorbitol, 4 mM CaCl2, 5 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2',15.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00070','The experimental points were fitted to Boltzmann curves, and the midpoints of the Boltzmann curves in control and in solutions with 2% and 5% ficoll were 207, 230, and 244 mm Hg, respectively.','Results (Effect of ficoll on MscS single-channel currents; Fig 2 D)','high','single set of fitted midpoints from the Fig 2 D Po(gamma) analysis (representative experiment series). tau_inact Y-flag: the paper quantifies inactivation by the time constant ''defined as the inverse of the inactivation rate'' and reports effects as faster/slower (rates/plots); the ONLY numeric taus in text are from ONE double-pulse experiment (''in the control, τ 1 and τ 2 were 0.27 s and 0.26 s, and in the presence of glucose 0.20 s and 0.10 s'') with the paper itself noting ''in other experiments a similar effect was not observed'' -> single-experiment, non-reproduced values archived here, NOT rowed (task directive: rates/no-aggregate -> no tau row). conductance flag: single-channel currents shown but no numeric conductance in text (''We did not observe a reduction of the channel conductance'' qualitative) -> no row. Per-trace PEG midpoint pairs (180/190 for PEG 200; 169/220 for PEG 6000) are single-experiment Boltzmann midpoints -> the aggregated SHIFT rows are rowed instead (endpoints kept in the quote). Cosolvents are preferentially-excluded crowders raising the midpoint -> ''antagonist'' as the closest enum; glucose/dextran/PEG also act via chamber penetration (size-dependent), noted.','excised inside-out patch, MJF379 spheroplast WT MscS, Po-vs-suction Boltzmann fit, control (no cosolvent)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',105,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(276,'MAIC:BX:00276',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pneumatic suction pulses (e.g. 215 mm Hg) at constant +15 mV pipette voltage; cosolvents (ficoll 400, dextran, glucose, PEGs) applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) or periplasmic (pipette) side at matched osmolarity (760 mOsm/kg H2O, sorbitol-adjusted) | MODULATOR: ficoll 400 (antagonist) 2 % w/v','P50',230.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'230','mm Hg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','E. coli MJF379 (Frag1 kefA::kan, MscS+ MscL+) giant spheroplasts; recordings focused on the MscS population','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.2,'150 mM KCl, 400 mM sorbitol, 4 mM CaCl2, 5 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (+ cosolvent as indicated)','150 mM KCl, 400 mM sorbitol, 4 mM CaCl2, 5 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2',15.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00071','The experimental points were fitted to Boltzmann curves, and the midpoints of the Boltzmann curves in control and in solutions with 2% and 5% ficoll were 207, 230, and 244 mm Hg, respectively.','Results (Effect of ficoll on MscS single-channel currents; Fig 2 D)','medium','cosolvent-condition midpoint from the same Fig 2 D Boltzmann fits; ficoll raises the midpoint (preferential exclusion / crowding pressure on the cytoplasmic chamber) -> ''antagonist'' as the closest enum. tau_inact Y-flag: the paper quantifies inactivation by the time constant ''defined as the inverse of the inactivation rate'' and reports effects as faster/slower (rates/plots); the ONLY numeric taus in text are from ONE double-pulse experiment (''in the control, τ 1 and τ 2 were 0.27 s and 0.26 s, and in the presence of glucose 0.20 s and 0.10 s'') with the paper itself noting ''in other experiments a similar effect was not observed'' -> single-experiment, non-reproduced values archived here, NOT rowed (task directive: rates/no-aggregate -> no tau row). conductance flag: single-channel currents shown but no numeric conductance in text (''We did not observe a reduction of the channel conductance'' qualitative) -> no row. Per-trace PEG midpoint pairs (180/190 for PEG 200; 169/220 for PEG 6000) are single-experiment Boltzmann midpoints -> the aggregated SHIFT rows are rowed instead (endpoints kept in the quote). Cosolvents are preferentially-excluded crowders raising the midpoint -> ''antagonist'' as the closest enum; glucose/dextran/PEG also act via chamber penetration (size-dependent), noted.','excised inside-out patch, MJF379 spheroplast WT MscS, Po-vs-suction Boltzmann fit, 2% ficoll on the cytoplasmic side',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',105,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
