INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(279,'MAIC:BX:00279',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pneumatic suction pulses (e.g. 215 mm Hg) at constant +15 mV pipette voltage; cosolvents (ficoll 400, dextran, glucose, PEGs) applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) or periplasmic (pipette) side at matched osmolarity (760 mOsm/kg H2O, sorbitol-adjusted) | MODULATOR: PEG 200 (antagonist) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 4.5','P50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,7.9,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'7.9','mm Hg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','E. coli MJF379 (Frag1 kefA::kan, MscS+ MscL+) giant spheroplasts; recordings focused on the MscS population','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.2,'150 mM KCl, 400 mM sorbitol, 4 mM CaCl2, 5 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (+ cosolvent as indicated)','150 mM KCl, 400 mM sorbitol, 4 mM CaCl2, 5 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2',15.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00074','The data points were fitted with Boltzmann curves, and the midpoints of the curves in the control and in the presence of PEG were 180 and 190 mm Hg for PEG 200 ( Fig. 5 D ) and 169 and 220 mm Hg for PEG 6000 ( Fig. 5 E ). The average shift of the midpoint of the Boltzmann curve was 7.9 ± 4.5 and 61.7 ± 10.4 mm Hg in the presence of PEG 200 and PEG 6000, respectively ( n = 3, in both cases).','Results (Effects of PEGs...; Fig 5, D and E)','medium','absolute mmHg endpoints with n -> delta_p50 rows (magnitude positive; direction ''toward higher pressures'' stated in label/quote). PEG concentrations not restated in this sentence (30 mOsm matched fractions) -> modulator_concentration left blank for the PEG rows. tau_inact Y-flag: the paper quantifies inactivation by the time constant ''defined as the inverse of the inactivation rate'' and reports effects as faster/slower (rates/plots); the ONLY numeric taus in text are from ONE double-pulse experiment (''in the control, τ 1 and τ 2 were 0.27 s and 0.26 s, and in the presence of glucose 0.20 s and 0.10 s'') with the paper itself noting ''in other experiments a similar effect was not observed'' -> single-experiment, non-reproduced values archived here, NOT rowed (task directive: rates/no-aggregate -> no tau row). conductance flag: single-channel currents shown but no numeric conductance in text (''We did not observe a reduction of the channel conductance'' qualitative) -> no row. Per-trace PEG midpoint pairs (180/190 for PEG 200; 169/220 for PEG 6000) are single-experiment Boltzmann midpoints -> the aggregated SHIFT rows are rowed instead (endpoints kept in the quote). Cosolvents are preferentially-excluded crowders raising the midpoint -> ''antagonist'' as the closest enum; glucose/dextran/PEG also act via chamber penetration (size-dependent), noted.','excised inside-out patch, MJF379 spheroplast WT MscS, PEG 200 (cytoplasmic) vs control, average midpoint shift','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',105,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
