INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(281,'MAIC:BX:00281',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pneumatic suction pulses (e.g. 215 mm Hg) at constant +15 mV pipette voltage; cosolvents (ficoll 400, dextran, glucose, PEGs) applied to the cytoplasmic (bath) or periplasmic (pipette) side at matched osmolarity (760 mOsm/kg H2O, sorbitol-adjusted) | MODULATOR: dextran (MW 35,000) (antagonist) 4.57 % w/v | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2.8','P50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,12.4,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12.4','mm Hg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','E. coli MJF379 (Frag1 kefA::kan, MscS+ MscL+) giant spheroplasts; recordings focused on the MscS population','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.2,'150 mM KCl, 400 mM sorbitol, 4 mM CaCl2, 5 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (+ cosolvent as indicated)','150 mM KCl, 400 mM sorbitol, 4 mM CaCl2, 5 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2',15.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00076','The channel open probabilities, P o , at different pressures were fitted to Boltzmann curves. After the channels were exposed to dextran or glucose, the curves were shifted toward higher pressures. The average change of their position was 12.4 ± 2.8 ( n = 4) and 14.3 ± 7 mm Hg ( n = 3) in 4.57% dextran and in 10 mM glucose, respectively.','Results (Effects of dextran and glucose; Fig 7)','medium','absolute mmHg endpoints with n -> delta_p50 rows (magnitude positive; direction ''toward higher pressures'' stated in label/quote). PEG concentrations not restated in this sentence (30 mOsm matched fractions) -> modulator_concentration left blank for the PEG rows. tau_inact Y-flag: the paper quantifies inactivation by the time constant ''defined as the inverse of the inactivation rate'' and reports effects as faster/slower (rates/plots); the ONLY numeric taus in text are from ONE double-pulse experiment (''in the control, τ 1 and τ 2 were 0.27 s and 0.26 s, and in the presence of glucose 0.20 s and 0.10 s'') with the paper itself noting ''in other experiments a similar effect was not observed'' -> single-experiment, non-reproduced values archived here, NOT rowed (task directive: rates/no-aggregate -> no tau row). conductance flag: single-channel currents shown but no numeric conductance in text (''We did not observe a reduction of the channel conductance'' qualitative) -> no row. Per-trace PEG midpoint pairs (180/190 for PEG 200; 169/220 for PEG 6000) are single-experiment Boltzmann midpoints -> the aggregated SHIFT rows are rowed instead (endpoints kept in the quote). Cosolvents are preferentially-excluded crowders raising the midpoint -> ''antagonist'' as the closest enum; glucose/dextran/PEG also act via chamber penetration (size-dependent), noted.','excised inside-out patch, MJF379 spheroplast WT MscS, 4.57% dextran (cytoplasmic) vs control, average midpoint shift','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',105,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
