lf noting ''in other experiments a similar effect was not observed'' -> single-experiment, non-reproduced values archived here, NOT rowed (task directive: rates/no-aggregate -> no tau row). conductance flag: single-channel currents shown but no numeric conductance in text (''We did not observe a reduction of the channel conductance'' qualitative) -> no row. Per-trace PEG midpoint pairs (180/190 for PEG 200; 169/220 for PEG 6000) are single-experiment Boltzmann midpoints -> the aggregated SHIFT rows are rowed instead (endpoints kept in the quote). Cosolvents are preferentially-excluded crowders raising the midpoint -> ''antagonist'' as the closest enum; glucose/dextran/PEG also act via chamber penetration (size-dependent), noted.','excised inside-out patch, MJF379 spheroplast WT MscS, 10 mM glucose (cytoplasmic) vs control, average midpoint shift','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',105,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(283,'MAIC:BX:00283',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0 to -200 mmHg pressure ramps at +30 or -30 mV pipette voltage; single-channel steps at ±40 mV; patch radius 1.3 ± 0.2 µm imaged for the Laplace tension conversion | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 20','P50',145.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'145','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (Δ7, channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing TcMscS (pQE80, N-terminal 6-His) or EcMscS control','E. coli giant spheroplast (T. cruzi ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 + 400 mM sucrose (symmetric base)','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00078','EcMscS showed its half-activation pressure at 90 ± 3 mmHg ( Figure 2F , black symbols; n = 54). TcMscS had its pressure midpoint at 145 ± 20 mmHg ( Figure 2F , blue symbols; n = 11). These measurements were done with standard-size pipettes, producing patches of 1.3 ± 0.2 μm radius (r) when an activating pressure gradient is applied.; Given that EcMscS activates in E. coli spheroplasts at 7.8 mN/m ( Belyy et al., 2010 ), we concluded that the midpoint of TcMscS activation is 12.6 mN/m.','Results (Electrophysiological properties of TcMscS; Fig 2F)','medium','ORTHOLOG species in condition_key (TcMscS, T. cruzi). As-reported pressure form rowed per the task rule (pick one form); the derived 12.6 mN/m tension (EcMscS-anchored) is carried in the quote and archived in the note. Error type not stated. as-reported form chosen: the PRESSURE midpoint (145 ± 20 mmHg) is rowed; the 12.6 mN/m tension equivalent is a DERIVED value (''Given that EcMscS activates ... at 7.8 mN/m (Belyy et al., 2010), we concluded ... 12.6 mN/m'') anchored on the literature EcMscS tension -> archived in this note, not rowed. The EcMscS 90 ± 3 mmHg (n = 54) control is the paper''s own E. coli MscS measurement (mscs-side, not paralog) -> rowed. Conductance restated in the text as ''the 400 pS unitary conductance in symmetric 200 mM KCl'' (same 0.40 nS) — one row (the ± error form). Ca-gluconate condition: current ''dropped to 0.9 ± 0.5 pA (n = 3), translating into a 30 pS conductance'' -> archived here (rounded translation, different electrolyte; task rows the KCl conductance). EcMscS conductances 0.5 nS (100 mM CaCl2) / 1.1 nS (KCl) are cited comparisons (Cox 2013 / literature) -> not rowed. Source glyph: the methods print ''KCI/MgCI2'' for KCl/MgCl2 in one span (rendering artifact, not quoted). [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (4 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, MJF641 spheroplast expressing TcMscS, Po-vs-pressure Boltzmann midpoint (Fig 2F)','11','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',106,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(284,'MAIC:BX:00284',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0 to -200 mmHg pressure ramps at +30 or -30 mV pipette voltage; single-channel steps at ±40 mV; patch radius 1.3 ± 0.2 µm imaged for the Laplace tension conversion | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 3','P50',90.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'90','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (Δ7, channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing TcMscS (pQE80, N-terminal 6-His) or EcMscS control','E. coli giant spheroplast (T. cruzi ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 + 400 mM sucrose (symmetric base)','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00079','EcMscS showed its half-activation pressure at 90 ± 3 mmHg ( Figure 2F , black symbols; n = 54). TcMscS had its pressure midpoint at 145 ± 20 mmHg ( Figure 2F , blue symbols; n = 11). These measurements were done with standard-size pipettes, producing patches of 1.3 ± 0.2 μm radius (r) when an activating pressure gradient is applied.','Results (Electrophysiological properties of TcMscS; Fig 2F)','high','own-data E. coli MscS control series (n = 54 patches) recorded in the same system — mscs-side (same gene), not paralog; also serves as the internal reference for the TcMscS midpoint. as-reported form chosen: the PRESSURE midpoint (145 ± 20 mmHg) is rowed; the 12.6 mN/m tension equivalent is a DERIVED value (''Given that EcMscS activates ... at 7.8 mN/m (Belyy et al., 2010), we concluded ... 12.6 mN/m'') anchored on the literature EcMscS tension -> archived in this note, not rowed. The EcMscS 90 ± 3 mmHg (n = 54) control is the paper''s own E. coli MscS measurement (mscs-side, not paralog) -> rowed. Conductance restated in the text as ''the 400 pS unitary conductance in symmetric 200 mM KCl'' (same 0.40 nS) — one row (the ± error form). Ca-gluconate condition: current ''dropped to 0.9 ± 0.5 pA (n = 3), translating into a 30 pS conductance'' -> archived here (rounded translation, different electrolyte; task rows the KCl conductance). EcMscS conductances 0.5 nS (100 mM CaCl2) / 1.1 nS (KCl) are cited comparisons (Cox 2013 / literature) -> not rowed. Source glyph: the methods print ''KCI/MgCI2'' for KCl/MgCl2 in one span (rendering artifact, not quoted). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','excised inside-out patch, MJF641 spheroplast expressing EcMscS (control), Po-vs-pressure Boltzmann midpoint (Fig 2F)','54','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',106,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(285,'MAIC:BX:00285',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0 to -200 mmHg pressure ramps at +30 or -30 mV pipette voltage; single-channel steps at ±40 mV; patch radius 1.3 ± 0.2 µm imaged for the Laplace tension conversion | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.02','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,400.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.4',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (Δ7, channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing TcMscS (pQE80, N-terminal 6-His) or EcMscS control','E. coli giant spheroplast (T. cruzi ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 + 400 mM sucrose (symmetric base)','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00080','The current amplitude of 12 pA translates to 0.40 ± 0.02 nS conductance (n = 11). The I-V curve for TcMscS obtained under symmetric electrolyte conditions (200 mM KCl) is linear ( Figure 2B , black symbols)','Results (Electrophysiological properties of TcMscS; Fig 2, A and B)','high','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). linear I-V under symmetric KCl (ortholog species in condition_key). as-reported form chosen: the PRESSURE midpoint (145 ± 20 mmHg) is rowed; the 12.6 mN/m tension equivalent is a DERIVED value (''Given that EcMscS activates ... at 7.8 mN/m (Belyy et al., 2010), we concluded ... 12.6 mN/m'') anchored on the literature EcMscS tension -> archived in this note, not rowed. The EcMscS 90 ± 3 mmHg (n = 54) control is the paper''s own E. coli MscS measurement (mscs-side, not paralog) -> rowed. Conductance restated in the text as ''the 400 pS unitary conductance in symmetric 200 mM KCl'' (same 0.40 nS) — one row (the ± error form). Ca-gluconate condition: current ''dropped to 0.9 ± 0.5 pA (n = 3), translating into a 30 pS conductance'' -> archived here (rounded translation, different electrolyte; task rows the KCl conductance). EcMscS conductances 0.5 nS (100 mM CaCl2) / 1.1 nS (KCl) are cited comparisons (Cox 2013 / literature) -> not rowed. Source glyph: the methods print ''KCI/MgCI2'' for KCl/MgCl2 in one span (rendering artifact, not quoted).','excised inside-out patch, MJF641 spheroplast expressing TcMscS, single-channel I-V slope under symmetric 200 mM KCl','11','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',106,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(286,'MAIC:BX:00286',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0 to -200 mmHg pressure ramps at +30 or -30 mV pipette voltage; single-channel steps at ±40 mV; patch radius 1.3 ± 0.2 µm imaged for the Laplace tension conversion | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.4','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-4.3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-4.3','mV','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (Δ7, channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing TcMscS (pQE80, N-terminal 6-His) or EcMscS control','E. coli giant spheroplast (T. cruzi ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.4,'425 mM KCl in the bath (200 mM KCl pipette), other salts as symmetric base','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00081','After a perfusion of buffer containing 425 mM KCl in the bath ( Figure 2B , red symbols), the I-V curve changes its slope and the x-intercept reproducibly shifts to -4.3 ± 0.4 mV (n = 4). According to the Goldman equation, under a given ionic gradient, the reversal potential of -4.3 mV corresponds to a P Cl- /P K+ of 1.6, signifying that the channel passes about 3 Cl - per 2 K + ions, that is, it shows a slight anionic preference.','Results (Electrophysiological properties of TcMscS; Fig 2B)','high','negative shift toward E_Cl — slight anionic preference. as-reported form chosen: the PRESSURE midpoint (145 ± 20 mmHg) is rowed; the 12.6 mN/m tension equivalent is a DERIVED value (''Given that EcMscS activates ... at 7.8 mN/m (Belyy et al., 2010), we concluded ... 12.6 mN/m'') anchored on the literature EcMscS tension -> archived in this note, not rowed. The EcMscS 90 ± 3 mmHg (n = 54) control is the paper''s own E. coli MscS measurement (mscs-side, not paralog) -> rowed. Conductance restated in the text as ''the 400 pS unitary conductance in symmetric 200 mM KCl'' (same 0.40 nS) — one row (the ± error form). Ca-gluconate condition: current ''dropped to 0.9 ± 0.5 pA (n = 3), translating into a 30 pS conductance'' -> archived here (rounded translation, different electrolyte; task rows the KCl conductance). EcMscS conductances 0.5 nS (100 mM CaCl2) / 1.1 nS (KCl) are cited comparisons (Cox 2013 / literature) -> not rowed. Source glyph: the methods print ''KCI/MgCI2'' for KCl/MgCl2 in one span (rendering artifact, not quoted).','excised inside-out patch, MJF641 spheroplast expressing TcMscS, I-V x-intercept under asymmetric KCl (200 mM pipette / 425 mM bath)','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',106,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(287,'MAIC:BX:00287',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0 to -200 mmHg pressure ramps at +30 or -30 mV pipette voltage; single-channel steps at ±40 mV; patch radius 1.3 ± 0.2 µm imaged for the Laplace tension conversion',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.6',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF641 (Δ7, channel-free) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing TcMscS (pQE80, N-terminal 6-His) or EcMscS control','E. coli giant spheroplast (T. cruzi ortholog expressed)',NULL,7.4,'425 mM KCl in the bath (200 mM KCl pipette), other salts as symmetric base','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00082','After a perfusion of buffer containing 425 mM KCl in the bath ( Figure 2B , red symbols), the I-V curve changes its slope and the x-intercept reproducibly shifts to -4.3 ± 0.4 mV (n = 4). According to the Goldman equation, under a given ionic gradient, the reversal potential of -4.3 mV corresponds to a P Cl- /P K+ of 1.6, signifying that the channel passes about 3 Cl - per 2 K + ions, that is, it shows a slight anionic preference.','Results (Electrophysiological properties of TcMscS; Fig 2B)','medium','schema_gap: no ion-selectivity ratio column in the DB. ''passes about 3 Cl- per 2 K+ ions'' is the paper''s restatement of the same ratio -> not a separate row. as-reported form chosen: the PRESSURE midpoint (145 ± 20 mmHg) is rowed; the 12.6 mN/m tension equivalent is a DERIVED value (''Given that EcMscS activates ... at 7.8 mN/m (Belyy et al., 2010), we concluded ... 12.6 mN/m'') anchored on the literature EcMscS tension -> archived in this note, not rowed. The EcMscS 90 ± 3 mmHg (n = 54) control is the paper''s own E. coli MscS measurement (mscs-side, not paralog) -> rowed. Conductance restated in the text as ''the 400 pS unitary conductance in symmetric 200 mM KCl'' (same 0.40 nS) — one row (the ± error form). Ca-gluconate condition: current ''dropped to 0.9 ± 0.5 pA (n = 3), translating into a 30 pS conductance'' -> archived here (rounded translation, different electrolyte; task rows the KCl conductance). EcMscS conductances 0.5 nS (100 mM CaCl2) / 1.1 nS (KCl) are cited comparisons (Cox 2013 / literature) -> not rowed. Source glyph: the methods print ''KCI/MgCI2'' for KCl/MgCl2 in one span (rendering artifact, not quoted).','excised inside-out patch, MJF641 spheroplast expressing TcMscS, asymmetric 200/425 mM KCl, Goldman-equation analysis of the -4.3 mV E_rev','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',106,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(288,'MAIC:BX:00288',5,NULL,NULL,60,'pressure ramps on excised inside-out patches at -20 mV; MscL openings in the same patch used as the threshold reference | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.02','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1640.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.64',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF429 / MJF612 E. coli protoplast-spheroplasts expressing WT (MscSYFF background) or Trp mutant MscS; native MscL retained as the pressure reference; DOPC reconstitution used for a subset','E. coli protoplast / spheroplast',NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES (pH not captured in cache)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES (symmetrical)',-20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00083','However, if the pressure on the patch was increased ( P L : P S = 1.17–1.49), stable openings that were ∼50% larger than that of the WT [1.64 ± 0.02 nS ( n = 5) ( Figure 5 D)] were observed, and these exhibited a stability similar to that of MscS ( Figure 5 A).','Results (A unique property was observed with V99W; Fig 5 D)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). V99W two-conductance-state phenotype: the ROWED value is the high-pressure stable state (∼50% larger than WT); the low-pressure flickery state conducts at the MscSYFF-like ∼1.1 nS (attribution-ambiguous reference value, NOT rowed — see batch notes). P_L:P_S ranges in the quote are threshold ratios, not rowed. ATTRIBUTION ruling on the ~1.1 nS: two mentions — the Table 1 footnote ''WT indicates that the channel gives rise to a stable open state typical of MscS with a conductance ∼1.1 nS'' (a general characterization of the typical WT level) and the bracketed MscSYFF value ''∼1.1 ± 0.01 nS (n = 5)'' used as the low-pressure reference — the MscSYFF properties were ''previously reported'' (ref 20), making the bracket''s provenance ambiguous -> NOT rowed (attribution-ambiguous per the task check). Table 1 P_L:P_S ratio columns NOT rows (ratio rule): YFF 1.36 ± 0.06, M47W 1.30 ± 0.08, S95W 1.02 ± 0.04, A103W 1.31 ± 0.18, V107W 1.28 ± 0.24, A102W 1.04 ± 0.04, G113W 1.66 ± 0.19, V99W 1.8-2.4 / 1.17-1.49 (two pressure ranges), R88W 1.04 ± 0.03, plus nd entries. delta_p50 Y-flag: MscSYFF ''required a tension ∼50% higher than that of the wild type'' — cited from the previous report (ref 20) AND a percentage -> no row; V99W low-pressure P_L:P_S 1.8-2.4 is ratio-only -> no row. ''high conductance may be explained by a π-π'' — qualitative. V99W two-state phenotype documented in the row condition; ~50%-larger-than-WT is the same 1.64 nS statement (not a separate row).','excised inside-out patch, V99W MscS, stable openings at increased pressure (P_L:P_S 1.17-1.49 range), symmetric 200 mM KCl, -20 mV','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',107,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(289,'MAIC:BX:00289',5,NULL,NULL,61,'pressure ramps on excised inside-out patches at -20 mV; MscL openings in the same patch used as the threshold reference','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1200.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.2',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF429 / MJF612 E. coli protoplast-spheroplasts expressing WT (MscSYFF background) or Trp mutant MscS; native MscL retained as the pressure reference; DOPC reconstitution used for a subset','E. coli protoplast / spheroplast',NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES (pH not captured in cache)','200 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, 10 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES (symmetrical)',-20.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00084','In the double mutant, V99W/F80A, only stable conductances of WT magnitude (∼23 pA, ∼1.2 nS) were observed (bottom).','Fig 5 legend (A, bottom panel; V99W/F80A compensating double mutant)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). extraction-review G-3 addition: own-data Fig 5 legend value (∼-prefixed, no error term, no n in the legend) -> value_relation ''~'', medium confidence. The double mutant removes the V99W high-conductance state (F80 volume compensation) and restores WT-magnitude stable openings. ATTRIBUTION ruling on the ~1.1 nS: two mentions — the Table 1 footnote ''WT indicates that the channel gives rise to a stable open state typical of MscS with a conductance ∼1.1 nS'' (a general characterization of the typical WT level) and the bracketed MscSYFF value ''∼1.1 ± 0.01 nS (n = 5)'' used as the low-pressure reference — the MscSYFF properties were ''previously reported'' (ref 20), making the bracket''s provenance ambiguous -> NOT rowed (attribution-ambiguous per the task check). Table 1 P_L:P_S ratio columns NOT rows (ratio rule): YFF 1.36 ± 0.06, M47W 1.30 ± 0.08, S95W 1.02 ± 0.04, A103W 1.31 ± 0.18, V107W 1.28 ± 0.24, A102W 1.04 ± 0.04, G113W 1.66 ± 0.19, V99W 1.8-2.4 / 1.17-1.49 (two pressure ranges), R88W 1.04 ± 0.03, plus nd entries. delta_p50 Y-flag: MscSYFF ''required a tension ∼50% higher than that of the wild type'' — cited from the previous report (ref 20) AND a percentage -> no row; V99W low-pressure P_L:P_S 1.8-2.4 is ratio-only -> no row. ''high conductance may be explained by a π-π'' — qualitative. V99W two-state phenotype documented in the row condition; ~50%-larger-than-WT is the same 1.64 nS statement (not a separate row).','excised inside-out patch, V99W/F80A double-mutant MscS, stable openings only (WT magnitude), symmetric 200 mM KCl, -20 mV',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',107,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(290,'MAIC:BX:00290',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'short triangle stimulation ramps (HSPS-1); pipette bubble number BN 6.5-7 (BN 5 for small patches); +40 mV pipette potential for the midpoint series | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 5.5','P50',-27.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-27.0','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocytes injected with pOO2-MscS cRNA (de-vitellinized, 3-7 d); excised inside-out patches in symmetric complete ND96','Xenopus laevis oocyte',NULL,7.4,'complete ND96: 96 mM NaCl, 2 mM KCl, 1.8 mM CaCl2, 1 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetrical; bath also 300 mM sucrose for spheroplast records)','complete ND96: 96 mM NaCl, 2 mM KCl, 1.8 mM CaCl2, 1 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00085','Opening and closing curves fitted with a Boltzmann distribution function ( Fig. 4 A , red and blue, respectively) indicated an average activation midpoint pressure of -27.0 ± 5.5 mmHg and inactivation midpoint pressure of -32.6 ± 6.4 mmHg ( n = 7 patches) when measured with a pipette of BN 7 ( Fig. 4 A ).','Results (Activation and inactivation behavior; Fig 4 A)','medium','novel expression system (Xenopus oocyte, ND96 — lower ionic strength than spheroplast buffers); suction printed negative, value as-reported. onset-rule correction: the task note called -19.1 ± 5.1 mmHg a ''midpoint'', but the source explicitly defines it as the activation THRESHOLD (''the pressure at which the first stable channel opening is detected''); the Boltzmann midpoints are -27.0 ± 5.5 (opening branch) and -32.6 ± 6.4 (closing branch) -> the midpoints are rowed, the thresholds (-19.1 ± 5.1 / -15.8 ± 5.3) are archived here per the onset-thresholds-are-not-midpoints rule. ''inactivation midpoint pressure'' is the closing branch of the hysteresis loop (closing-fit midpoint), rowed with that declared. Ratios not rowed: activation/inactivation midpoint ratio 0.89 ± 0.14; threshold ratio 1.48 ± 0.50. BN 5 single-patch example (-39.7/-50.1 opening, -27.4/-34.8 closing) -> per-patch, not rowed. tau_inact flag: ''slow and reversible inactivation (with current decaying over a 10-s interval)'' — descriptive only, no fitted constant -> no row. PORE geometry archived: TEA+ (~8 Å) permeates; ''a pore diameter of at least 10-15 Å in the open state'' (MD/crystal cites). Intro-cited conductances NOT rowed: ''∼1.2 nS in giant spheroplasts ... (Akitake et al., 2005; Edwards et al., 2005; Sotomayor et al., 2007)'' and ''∼0.5 nS in liposomes (Sukharev, 2002; Vásquez et al., 2007)''; the conductance ratio 1.6 (positive/negative) vs 2.0 (Sukharev 2002, cited) is a ratio -> note only. Expression system is novel (oocyte) — recording_mode INSIDE_OUT per ''All the traces presented in this report except for that shown in Fig. 1 A were obtained from inside-out (excised) patches''.','excised inside-out patch, Xenopus oocyte expressing EcMscS, triangle ramp Boltzmann fits, opening branch (activation midpoint), BN 7 pipette','7','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',108,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
