. Ratios not rowed: activation/inactivation midpoint ratio 0.89 ± 0.14; threshold ratio 1.48 ± 0.50. BN 5 single-patch example (-39.7/-50.1 opening, -27.4/-34.8 closing) -> per-patch, not rowed. tau_inact flag: ''slow and reversible inactivation (with current decaying over a 10-s interval)'' — descriptive only, no fitted constant -> no row. PORE geometry archived: TEA+ (~8 Å) permeates; ''a pore diameter of at least 10-15 Å in the open state'' (MD/crystal cites). Intro-cited conductances NOT rowed: ''∼1.2 nS in giant spheroplasts ... (Akitake et al., 2005; Edwards et al., 2005; Sotomayor et al., 2007)'' and ''∼0.5 nS in liposomes (Sukharev, 2002; Vásquez et al., 2007)''; the conductance ratio 1.6 (positive/negative) vs 2.0 (Sukharev 2002, cited) is a ratio -> note only. Expression system is novel (oocyte) — recording_mode INSIDE_OUT per ''All the traces presented in this report except for that shown in Fig. 1 A were obtained from inside-out (excised) patches''.','excised inside-out patch, Xenopus oocyte expressing EcMscS, triangle ramp Boltzmann fits, closing branch (''inactivation midpoint'' of the hysteresis loop), BN 7 pipette','7','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',108,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(292,'MAIC:BX:00292',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'short triangle stimulation ramps (HSPS-1); pipette bubble number BN 6.5-7 (BN 5 for small patches); +40 mV pipette potential for the midpoint series | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 3','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,351.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'351','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocytes injected with pOO2-MscS cRNA (de-vitellinized, 3-7 d); excised inside-out patches in symmetric complete ND96','Xenopus laevis oocyte',NULL,7.4,'complete ND96: 96 mM NaCl, 2 mM KCl, 1.8 mM CaCl2, 1 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (symmetrical; bath also 300 mM sucrose for spheroplast records)','complete ND96: 96 mM NaCl, 2 mM KCl, 1.8 mM CaCl2, 1 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00087','At positive pipette potentials, the single-channel conductance for MscS derived from the slope of the current-voltage curve was 351 ± 3 pS, whereas at negative pipette potentials, the slope of the current-voltage curve was 218 ± 2 pS.','Results (current-voltage relationship; Fig 3 A)','high','unit IS pS as printed (normal pS handling). The voltage asymmetry (351/218 pS, ratio 1.6) reflects the MscS rectification in the oocyte environment; direction noted, no iv_relation row (task directive). onset-rule correction: the task note called -19.1 ± 5.1 mmHg a ''midpoint'', but the source explicitly defines it as the activation THRESHOLD (''the pressure at which the first stable channel opening is detected''); the Boltzmann midpoints are -27.0 ± 5.5 (opening branch) and -32.6 ± 6.4 (closing branch) -> the midpoints are rowed, the thresholds (-19.1 ± 5.1 / -15.8 ± 5.3) are archived here per the onset-thresholds-are-not-midpoints rule. ''inactivation midpoint pressure'' is the closing branch of the hysteresis loop (closing-fit midpoint), rowed with that declared. Ratios not rowed: activation/inactivation midpoint ratio 0.89 ± 0.14; threshold ratio 1.48 ± 0.50. BN 5 single-patch example (-39.7/-50.1 opening, -27.4/-34.8 closing) -> per-patch, not rowed. tau_inact flag: ''slow and reversible inactivation (with current decaying over a 10-s interval)'' — descriptive only, no fitted constant -> no row. PORE geometry archived: TEA+ (~8 Å) permeates; ''a pore diameter of at least 10-15 Å in the open state'' (MD/crystal cites). Intro-cited conductances NOT rowed: ''∼1.2 nS in giant spheroplasts ... (Akitake et al., 2005; Edwards et al., 2005; Sotomayor et al., 2007)'' and ''∼0.5 nS in liposomes (Sukharev, 2002; Vásquez et al., 2007)''; the conductance ratio 1.6 (positive/negative) vs 2.0 (Sukharev 2002, cited) is a ratio -> note only. Expression system is novel (oocyte) — recording_mode INSIDE_OUT per ''All the traces presented in this report except for that shown in Fig. 1 A were obtained from inside-out (excised) patches''.','excised inside-out patch, Xenopus oocyte expressing EcMscS, I-V slope at positive pipette potentials, symmetric ND96',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',108,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
