wed: activation/inactivation midpoint ratio 0.89 ± 0.14; threshold ratio 1.48 ± 0.50. BN 5 single-patch example (-39.7/-50.1 opening, -27.4/-34.8 closing) -> per-patch, not rowed. tau_inact flag: ''slow and reversible inactivation (with current decaying over a 10-s interval)'' — descriptive only, no fitted constant -> no row. PORE geometry archived: TEA+ (~8 Å) permeates; ''a pore diameter of at least 10-15 Å in the open state'' (MD/crystal cites). Intro-cited conductances NOT rowed: ''∼1.2 nS in giant spheroplasts ... (Akitake et al., 2005; Edwards et al., 2005; Sotomayor et al., 2007)'' and ''∼0.5 nS in liposomes (Sukharev, 2002; Vásquez et al., 2007)''; the conductance ratio 1.6 (positive/negative) vs 2.0 (Sukharev 2002, cited) is a ratio -> note only. Expression system is novel (oocyte) — recording_mode INSIDE_OUT per ''All the traces presented in this report except for that shown in Fig. 1 A were obtained from inside-out (excised) patches''.','excised inside-out patch, Xenopus oocyte expressing EcMscS, I-V slope at negative pipette potentials, symmetric ND96',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',108,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(294,'MAIC:BX:00294',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'excised inside-out patches at +30 mV (pipette); ramps/steps via HSPC-1-type clamp; pulse-step-pulse protocols for inactivation | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 17','P50',-89.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-89','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','E. coli giant spheroplasts: Frag1 (WT parental), MJF367 (ΔmscL, native MscS+), and plasmid-expressed WT/G168D/G113A MscS (pB10d) in channel-free backgrounds','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES + 400 mM sucrose, pH 7.4','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00089','Number of channels and gating pressures (in mm Hg) from patch-clamp measurements | Strain | Frag1 | MJF367 | MJF451 | PB113 | Number of MscS | 38 ±13 | 70 ±34 | | | Number of MscL | 69 ±18 | | 57 ±5 | 47 ±17 | MscS threshold pressure (mm Hg) | -78 ±15 | -62 ±13 | | | MscL threshold pressure (mm Hg) | -142 ±27 | | -121 ±35 | -118 ±14 | MscS midpoint pressure (mm Hg) | -89 ±17 | -76 ±12 | | | MscL midpoint pressure (mm Hg) | -163 ±28 | | -132 ±27 | -145 ±15 | MscS saturation pressure (mm Hg) | -107 ±17 | -91 ±15 | | | MscL saturation pressure (mm Hg) | -195 ±26 | | -165 ±29 | -199 ±28 | Full table of patch-clamp channel numbers and gating pressures (N ≥ 3).','Supplemental Table S2 (patch-clamp gating pressures; N ≥ 3; docx text extracted from the EPMC supplementary zip — quote begins at the table header, analyst prefix removed per the verbatim-quote rule)','high','own-data native-MscS population midpoint (N ≥ 3 patches; error type not stated). Suction printed negative in the table, value as-reported. The two strains are distinct conditions (WT background vs ΔmscL upregulation context). Suppl Table S2 (fetched THIS batch from the EPMC supplementaryFiles zip, cached at .scratch/mscs_fulltext/PMC10082366_TableS2.txt) MscS-side rows: midpoints rowed (below); THRESHOLD pressures (-78 ±15 Frag1 / -62 ±13 MJF367) are onset values -> archived, not rowed (onset rule); SATURATION pressures (-107 ±17 / -91 ±15) are saturation levels -> archived. MscL-side Table S2 columns are PARALOG -> all excluded (thresholds -142 ±27 / -121 ±35 / -118 ±14; midpoints -163 ±28 / -132 ±27 / -145 ±15; saturations -195 ±26 / -165 ±29 / -199 ±28; MscL counts). Channel counts per patch (38 ±13 / 70 ±34 MscS) and patch radii (1.4 ±0.1 µm, areas 11-15 µm2) archived. tau_inact flag: inactivation degree measured by pulse-step-pulse but ''numeric values in figures only'' (verify-layer ruling; Fig S6) -> no row. tau_deact flag: ''the channel recovers to the resting state within 1-3 s'' appears in the INTRODUCTION as a general MscS property (citations follow in the adjacent sentence) -> intro-tier statement, not rowed (Kamaraju-2011 ~30 s precedent). conductance flag: all ~1 nS statements are literature-cited; own data are population recordings -> no row (verify-layer r1-M2 downgrade respected). WT ''7.2 mN/m'' is the literature value (Belyy 2010b) cited for comparison -> not rowed for this paper.','excised inside-out patch, E. coli Frag1 giant spheroplast (wild-type parental strain (native MscS/MscL/MscK)), population activation midpoint from pressure ramps (Suppl Table S2)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',109,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
