 .scratch/mscs_fulltext/PMC10082366_TableS2.txt) MscS-side rows: midpoints rowed (below); THRESHOLD pressures (-78 ±15 Frag1 / -62 ±13 MJF367) are onset values -> archived, not rowed (onset rule); SATURATION pressures (-107 ±17 / -91 ±15) are saturation levels -> archived. MscL-side Table S2 columns are PARALOG -> all excluded (thresholds -142 ±27 / -121 ±35 / -118 ±14; midpoints -163 ±28 / -132 ±27 / -145 ±15; saturations -195 ±26 / -165 ±29 / -199 ±28; MscL counts). Channel counts per patch (38 ±13 / 70 ±34 MscS) and patch radii (1.4 ±0.1 µm, areas 11-15 µm2) archived. tau_inact flag: inactivation degree measured by pulse-step-pulse but ''numeric values in figures only'' (verify-layer ruling; Fig S6) -> no row. tau_deact flag: ''the channel recovers to the resting state within 1-3 s'' appears in the INTRODUCTION as a general MscS property (citations follow in the adjacent sentence) -> intro-tier statement, not rowed (Kamaraju-2011 ~30 s precedent). conductance flag: all ~1 nS statements are literature-cited; own data are population recordings -> no row (verify-layer r1-M2 downgrade respected). WT ''7.2 mN/m'' is the literature value (Belyy 2010b) cited for comparison -> not rowed for this paper.','excised inside-out patch, E. coli MJF367 giant spheroplast (ΔmscL background (native MscS, MscS-only channel complement)), population activation midpoint from pressure ramps (Suppl Table S2)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',109,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(296,'MAIC:BX:00296',5,NULL,NULL,62,'excised inside-out patches at +30 mV (pipette); ramps/steps via HSPC-1-type clamp; pulse-step-pulse protocols for inactivation | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.1','T50',NULL,NULL,6.4,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'6.4','mN/m','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','E. coli giant spheroplasts: Frag1 (WT parental), MJF367 (ΔmscL, native MscS+), and plasmid-expressed WT/G168D/G113A MscS (pB10d) in channel-free backgrounds','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.4,'200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES + 400 mM sucrose, pH 7.4','200 mM KCl, 50 mM MgCl2, 5 mM CaCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.4',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00091','The midpoint ratio for G168D is 0.54 ± 0.01 and the tension is 6.4 ± 0.1 mN/m, which is similar to the literature values for WT MscS at 0.6 for the midpoint ratio and 7.2 mN/m for the tension ( Belyy et al., 2010b ).','Results (G168D MscS is insensitive to voltage section; Fig 8 context)','medium','gauge-derived absolute (midpoint ratio 0.54 ± 0.01 x the native-MscL 12 mN/m anchor) — rowed as the paper''s own stated tension with the derivation declared, confidence medium (Çetiner/Kamaraju-2011 convention). The WT comparison values (ratio 0.6 / 7.2 mN/m) are Belyy 2010b literature cites -> not rowed for this paper. Suppl Table S2 (fetched THIS batch from the EPMC supplementaryFiles zip, cached at .scratch/mscs_fulltext/PMC10082366_TableS2.txt) MscS-side rows: midpoints rowed (below); THRESHOLD pressures (-78 ±15 Frag1 / -62 ±13 MJF367) are onset values -> archived, not rowed (onset rule); SATURATION pressures (-107 ±17 / -91 ±15) are saturation levels -> archived. MscL-side Table S2 columns are PARALOG -> all excluded (thresholds -142 ±27 / -121 ±35 / -118 ±14; midpoints -163 ±28 / -132 ±27 / -145 ±15; saturations -195 ±26 / -165 ±29 / -199 ±28; MscL counts). Channel counts per patch (38 ±13 / 70 ±34 MscS) and patch radii (1.4 ±0.1 µm, areas 11-15 µm2) archived. tau_inact flag: inactivation degree measured by pulse-step-pulse but ''numeric values in figures only'' (verify-layer ruling; Fig S6) -> no row. tau_deact flag: ''the channel recovers to the resting state within 1-3 s'' appears in the INTRODUCTION as a general MscS property (citations follow in the adjacent sentence) -> intro-tier statement, not rowed (Kamaraju-2011 ~30 s precedent). conductance flag: all ~1 nS statements are literature-cited; own data are population recordings -> no row (verify-layer r1-M2 downgrade respected). WT ''7.2 mN/m'' is the literature value (Belyy 2010b) cited for comparison -> not rowed for this paper.','excised inside-out patch, PB113 (mscL+) spheroplast expressing G168D MscS from pB10d, midpoint ratio vs native MscL gauge (12 mN/m)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',109,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(297,'MAIC:BX:00297',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pressure applied to liposome patches; patch curvature determined by video imaging to convert pressure to tension; Po(gamma) recorded with descending pressure series | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.1','T50',NULL,NULL,5.5,'dyn/cm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'5.5','dyne/cm','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified 31-kDa MscS-6His protein (octylglucoside + lipids) reconstituted into soybean asolectin liposomes',NULL,NULL,NULL,'not stated in abstract','not stated in abstract',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00092','Po(gamma) curves had the midpoint at 5.5 +/- 0.1 dyne/cm and gave estimates for the energy of opening DeltaG = 11.4 +/- 0.5 kT, and the transition-related area change DeltaA = 8.4 +/- 0.4 nm(2) when fitted with a two-state Boltzmann model.','Abstract (Po(gamma) midpoint sentence)','medium','purified-protein reconstitution landmark (MscS sufficiency); unit dyne/cm as printed (= mN/m; unit_db uses the legal TensionUnit member). The DeltaG/DeltaA values in the same sentence are ENERGY/AREA parameters -> archived in the batch note, not rowed. ABSTRACT-tier access (PMC1302147 page carries abstract + references only; body is a captcha-blocked scanned PDF) — abstract access_basis, quote from the abstract only. unit ''dyne/cm'' as printed = mN/m (legal TensionUnit value, declared). ENERGY/AREA archived (no parameter_kind home): DeltaG = 11.4 ± 0.5 kT; DeltaA = 8.4 ± 0.4 nm2. Activation pressures ''20-60 mm Hg'' in liposomes are a range/onset tier -> no p50 row. conductance flag: ''the single-channel conductance is proportional to the buffer conductivity'' — no numeric in the abstract -> no row. ion_selectivity flag: ''the same asymmetric I-V curve and slight anionic preference as in situ'' — qualitative -> no row. Subunit-stoichiometry notes (hexamer call from cross-linking) were later corrected to a heptamer — context only.','purified MscS reconstituted into soybean asolectin liposomes, Po-vs-tension two-state Boltzmann fit (video-imaged patch curvature)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',110,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(298,'MAIC:BX:00298',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure (suction) ramps/steps on liposome patches; I-V from single-channel events at multiple voltages | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2.0 (sem)','P50',-35.26,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-35.26','mmHg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified MscSP (Silicibacter pomeroyi) and purified E. coli MscS/MscL reconstituted or coreconstituted into azolectin liposomes; MscSP also expressed in MJF465 E. coli giant spheroplasts','azolectin liposome (reconstituted channels)',NULL,NULL,'250 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, liposome recording solution (symmetrical)','250 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00093','Table 1. Midpoint activation pressure of reconstituted MscS, MscSP, and MscL channels in liposome patches Midpoint activation pressure MscS n MscSP n MscL n (mmHg) (mmHg) (mmHg) -35.26 ± 2.00 5 -54.63 ± 2.72 ∗ 7 -71.42 ±2.22 ∗ † 5 ... All values are represented as mean ± SE.','Table 1 (midpoint activation pressure of reconstituted channels) + Results (Fig 4)','high','own-data fitted midpoints (mean ± SE, n = patches); suction printed negative, value as-reported. ORTHOLOG species in condition_key (MscSP = Silicibacter pomeroyi, marine alpha-proteobacterium). Table 1 midpoint pressures are ABSOLUTE fitted values -> rowed (MscS and MscSP; MscL -71.42 ± 2.22 is paralog-side -> excluded); the activation RANGES are onset tier -> archived: liposomes ''activated by negative pressure ... in the range of -20 to -30 mmHg'' (MscSP), spheroplasts ''-100 and -130 mm Hg''; the spheroplast MscS literature range ''-30 and -70 mm Hg (19)'' is a prior-work cite. Table 2 ratios NOT rows: midpoint activation ratio MscL/MscS 2.03, MscL/MscSP 1.31; threshold ratios MscL/MscS 2.00 ± 0.12 (n = 4), MscL/MscSP 1.28 ± 0.08 (n = 7). EcMscS comparative conductances (0.82/1.37 nS) were measured in the same study/liposome system (''was measured to be''); the trailing ''(1)'' cite attaches to the two-thirds rectification remark -> rowed with the ambiguity declared, confidence medium. ''MscSP channels strongly rectify'' + substates — rectification noted, no iv_relation row (task directive). MscSP lacks inactivation (unlike EcMscS) -> no tau rows. Error type: mean ± SE per Table 1 footer. [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','azolectin liposome-reconstituted E. coli MscS (reconstituted), Boltzmann midpoint of the activation curve (Table 1)','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',111,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(299,'MAIC:BX:00299',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure (suction) ramps/steps on liposome patches; I-V from single-channel events at multiple voltages | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2.72 (sem)','P50',-54.63,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-54.63','mmHg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified MscSP (Silicibacter pomeroyi) and purified E. coli MscS/MscL reconstituted or coreconstituted into azolectin liposomes; MscSP also expressed in MJF465 E. coli giant spheroplasts','azolectin liposome (reconstituted channels)',NULL,NULL,'250 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, liposome recording solution (symmetrical)','250 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00094','Table 1. Midpoint activation pressure of reconstituted MscS, MscSP, and MscL channels in liposome patches Midpoint activation pressure MscS n MscSP n MscL n (mmHg) (mmHg) (mmHg) -35.26 ± 2.00 5 -54.63 ± 2.72 ∗ 7 -71.42 ±2.22 ∗ † 5 ... All values are represented as mean ± SE.','Table 1 (midpoint activation pressure of reconstituted channels) + Results (Fig 4)','high','own-data fitted midpoints (mean ± SE, n = patches); suction printed negative, value as-reported. ORTHOLOG species in condition_key. ORTHOLOG species in condition_key (MscSP = Silicibacter pomeroyi, marine alpha-proteobacterium). Table 1 midpoint pressures are ABSOLUTE fitted values -> rowed (MscS and MscSP; MscL -71.42 ± 2.22 is paralog-side -> excluded); the activation RANGES are onset tier -> archived: liposomes ''activated by negative pressure ... in the range of -20 to -30 mmHg'' (MscSP), spheroplasts ''-100 and -130 mm Hg''; the spheroplast MscS literature range ''-30 and -70 mm Hg (19)'' is a prior-work cite. Table 2 ratios NOT rows: midpoint activation ratio MscL/MscS 2.03, MscL/MscSP 1.31; threshold ratios MscL/MscS 2.00 ± 0.12 (n = 4), MscL/MscSP 1.28 ± 0.08 (n = 7). EcMscS comparative conductances (0.82/1.37 nS) were measured in the same study/liposome system (''was measured to be''); the trailing ''(1)'' cite attaches to the two-thirds rectification remark -> rowed with the ambiguity declared, confidence medium. ''MscSP channels strongly rectify'' + substates — rectification noted, no iv_relation row (task directive). MscSP lacks inactivation (unlike EcMscS) -> no tau rows. Error type: mean ± SE per Table 1 footer. [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','azolectin liposome-reconstituted MscSP (Silicibacter pomeroyi ortholog, reconstituted), Boltzmann midpoint of the activation curve (Table 1)','7','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',111,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(300,'MAIC:BX:00300',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure (suction) ramps/steps on liposome patches; I-V from single-channel events at multiple voltages | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 8.9','P50',171.9,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'171.9','mm Hg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MscSP (Silicibacter pomeroyi ortholog) expressed in MJF465 E. coli giant spheroplasts (in addition to the liposome reconstitution series)','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,NULL,'250 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, liposome recording solution (symmetrical)','250 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00095','MscSP activated at higher tension in membrane patches of giant spheroplasts characterized by 8.7 ± 0.8 mm Hg (1/ α ) per e-fold change in the channel activity and midpoint activation pressure p 1/2 of 171.9 ± 8.9 mm Hg, compared with 1/ α  = - 4.6 ± 0.5 mm Hg in liposome patches and midpoint of activation pressure of p 1/2  = -54.6 ± 2.7 ( Fig. 4 and Table 1 ).','Results (spheroplast midpoint sentence; Fig 4)','high','own-data spheroplast-side fitted midpoint (extraction-review G-1 addition; the sentence gives no n — error as printed, type not stated). Printed POSITIVE (171.9) whereas the liposome midpoints print negative suction — sign as-reported per condition, not normalized. Slope reciprocals in the same sentence have no parameter_kind home -> archived here: 1/α = 8.7 ± 0.8 mm Hg per e-fold (spheroplasts), 1/α = -4.6 ± 0.5 mm Hg (liposomes). ORTHOLOG species in condition_key (MscSP = Silicibacter pomeroyi, marine alpha-proteobacterium). Table 1 midpoint pressures are ABSOLUTE fitted values -> rowed (MscS and MscSP; MscL -71.42 ± 2.22 is paralog-side -> excluded); the activation RANGES are onset tier -> archived: liposomes ''activated by negative pressure ... in the range of -20 to -30 mmHg'' (MscSP), spheroplasts ''-100 and -130 mm Hg''; the spheroplast MscS literature range ''-30 and -70 mm Hg (19)'' is a prior-work cite. Table 2 ratios NOT rows: midpoint activation ratio MscL/MscS 2.03, MscL/MscSP 1.31; threshold ratios MscL/MscS 2.00 ± 0.12 (n = 4), MscL/MscSP 1.28 ± 0.08 (n = 7). EcMscS comparative conductances (0.82/1.37 nS) were measured in the same study/liposome system (''was measured to be''); the trailing ''(1)'' cite attaches to the two-thirds rectification remark -> rowed with the ambiguity declared, confidence medium. ''MscSP channels strongly rectify'' + substates — rectification noted, no iv_relation row (task directive). MscSP lacks inactivation (unlike EcMscS) -> no tau rows. Error type: mean ± SE per Table 1 footer.','giant spheroplast (MJF465) expressing MscSP (Silicibacter pomeroyi ortholog), Boltzmann midpoint of the activation curve (Fig 4) — a distinct recording condition from the liposome Table 1 midpoints',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',111,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(301,'MAIC:BX:00301',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure (suction) ramps/steps on liposome patches; I-V from single-channel events at multiple voltages | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.03','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1040.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.04',NULL,'SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified MscSP (Silicibacter pomeroyi) and purified E. coli MscS/MscL reconstituted or coreconstituted into azolectin liposomes; MscSP also expressed in MJF465 E. coli giant spheroplasts','azolectin liposome (reconstituted channels)',NULL,NULL,'250 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2, liposome recording solution (symmetrical)','250 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl2 (symmetrical)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00096','Its unitary conductance at positive voltages is 1.04 ± 0.03 nS ( n = 8) and 0.61 ± 0.02 nS ( n = 8) at negative voltages in symmetric 250 mM KCl, 90 mM MgCl 2 liposome recording solution (see Materials and Methods ).','Results (unitary conductance; Fig 6)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). ORTHOLOG species in condition_key. ORTHOLOG species in condition_key (MscSP = Silicibacter pomeroyi, marine alpha-proteobacterium). Table 1 midpoint pressures are ABSOLUTE fitted values -> rowed (MscS and MscSP; MscL -71.42 ± 2.22 is paralog-side -> excluded); the activation RANGES are onset tier -> archived: liposomes ''activated by negative pressure ... in the range of -20 to -30 mmHg'' (MscSP), spheroplasts ''-100 and -130 mm Hg''; the spheroplast MscS literature range ''-30 and -70 mm Hg (19)'' is a prior-work cite. Table 2 ratios NOT rows: midpoint activation ratio MscL/MscS 2.03, MscL/MscSP 1.31; threshold ratios MscL/MscS 2.00 ± 0.12 (n = 4), MscL/MscSP 1.28 ± 0.08 (n = 7). EcMscS comparative conductances (0.82/1.37 nS) were measured in the same study/liposome system (''was measured to be''); the trailing ''(1)'' cite attaches to the two-thirds rectification remark -> rowed with the ambiguity declared, confidence medium. ''MscSP channels strongly rectify'' + substates — rectification noted, no iv_relation row (task directive). MscSP lacks inactivation (unlike EcMscS) -> no tau rows. Error type: mean ± SE per Table 1 footer.','azolectin liposome-reconstituted MscSP (Silicibacter pomeroyi), single-channel I-V slope at positive voltages, symmetric 250 mM KCl / 90 mM MgCl2','8','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',111,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
