 and -70 mm Hg (19)'' is a prior-work cite. Table 2 ratios NOT rows: midpoint activation ratio MscL/MscS 2.03, MscL/MscSP 1.31; threshold ratios MscL/MscS 2.00 ± 0.12 (n = 4), MscL/MscSP 1.28 ± 0.08 (n = 7). EcMscS comparative conductances (0.82/1.37 nS) were measured in the same study/liposome system (''was measured to be''); the trailing ''(1)'' cite attaches to the two-thirds rectification remark -> rowed with the ambiguity declared, confidence medium. ''MscSP channels strongly rectify'' + substates — rectification noted, no iv_relation row (task directive). MscSP lacks inactivation (unlike EcMscS) -> no tau rows. Error type: mean ± SE per Table 1 footer.','azolectin liposome-reconstituted E. coli MscS (comparative), single-channel I-V slope at negative pipette voltages, symmetric 250 mM KCl / 90 mM MgCl2',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',111,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(305,'MAIC:BX:00305',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'patch-clamp with negative pressure (suction) on spheroplast and liposome patches; identical channel activities in all three preparations','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1000.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1',NULL,'SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OTHER','E. coli (strain AW740) giant spheroplasts, native-membrane-vesicle/asolectin liposome fusions, and octylglucoside-solubilized extract reassembled into asolectin liposomes','E. coli (giant spheroplast / reconstituted liposome)',NULL,NULL,'200 mM KCl (conductance reference condition)','200 mM KCl',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00100','MSC activities were similar in all three preparations, consisting of a large nonselective MSC of 3-nS conductance (in 200 mM KCl) that was activated by high negative pressures, and a small weakly anion-selective MSC of 1 nS activated by lower negative pressures.','Abstract (two-MSC characterization sentence)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). pre-molecular-identification era value: ''small ... MSC of 1 nS'' = the channel later identified as MscS (yggB); rowed with the attribution note. No error term or n in the abstract. The 3-nS large MSC in the same sentence is MscL-side (paralog) -> not rowed. ABSTRACT-tier access (PMC1225713 page abstract only). ATTRIBUTION ruling (task-directed): the ~1-nS small weakly anion-selective MSC at LOWER negative pressures is the MscS-side channel (later cloned as yggB/mscS) -> rowed with this note; the 3-nS large nonselective MSC at high pressures is the MscL-side channel (paralog) -> EXCLUDED. ''Both channels appeared more sensitive to suction in liposomes than in spheroplasts'' — directional, no numerics -> no threshold rows. Native molecular-mass estimates (60-80 kDa large MSC, 200-400 kDa small MSC) are biochemical, not gating -> archived. No error/n stated for the 1 nS.','E. coli AW740 patch-clamp (giant spheroplasts and reconstituted asolectin liposomes), small weakly anion-selective MSC, 200 mM KCl',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',112,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(306,'MAIC:BX:00306',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HSPC-1 clamp; single-channel openings on 1-s subsaturating ramps and ensemble currents under 50-ms voltage pulses (-200 to +200 mV) at saturating pressure','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1200.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.2',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','MJF465 (mscS-/mscL-/mscK-) E. coli giant spheroplasts expressing WT MscS or D3N/D8N/R88Q/K169Q mutants (pB10b)','E. coli giant spheroplast',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical; 0.5 or 1.5 M KCl variants for the high-salt I-V)','200 mM KCl, 10 mM CaCl2, 40 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00101','Escherichia coli MscS acting as a tension-activated osmolyte release valve shows a nonsaturable conductance (1.2 nS in a 39 mS/cm electrolyte) and weak preference for anions.','Abstract (nonsaturable conductance sentence)','medium','REPORTED UNIT IS NANOSIEMENS (nS): unit column left blank because the conductance storage vocabulary fixes pS; value kept as-reported — convert x1000 to pS at load (do NOT read as pS). electrolyte-normalized statement (39 mS/cm = the measured 200 mM KCl recording buffer); ''nonsaturable'' = conductance grows with salt concentration. Rounding variants in the same paper (1 nS Discussion / 1 ± 0.1 nS Fig 2 D box) noted. EXPERIMENTAL value rowed (wet-lab ephys + MD paper; task rule): the abstract 1.2 nS at 39 mS/cm bulk conductivity (= the standard 200 mM KCl buffer, measured 110.4 mS/m); the Discussion restates the same limit as ''open-state conductance (1 nS in a 39 mS/cm buffer)'' and the Fig 2 D experimental box as ''G = 1 ± 0.1 nS'' — same condition, coarser rounding; abstract value rowed. SIMULATION outputs NOT rowed: 4.3 nS barrel slope (1.5 M KCl, cage-corrected), simulated I-V curves. K169 rectification: ''Among the charged residues surrounding the pore, only K169 was found to contribute noticeably in the rectification'' — a SIMULATION attribution with the experimental ''selectivity and rectification were in agreement'', no explicit LINEAR/OUTWARD/INWARD statement for the experimental I-V -> no iv_relation row (task rule: only if explicit). PORE GEOMETRY / AREA archived: open-state model ''a pore 1.6 nm wide''; experimental-parameter box ΔA = 12 ± 1.2 nm2 (with ∼10% accuracy); ''~8 waters per Cl-'' electroosmotic coupling. Simulation tensions (10-50 dyne/cm) are NOT experimental thresholds. K169Q/D3N/D8N/R88Q mutant I-Vs are figure-only -> no numeric mutant rows.','excised inside-out patch, MJF465 spheroplast WT MscS, single-channel + ensemble I-V in symmetric 200 mM KCl buffer (39 mS/cm)',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',113,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(307,'MAIC:BX:00307',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative-pressure ramps on liposome patches at +30 mV pipette potential; patch-shape confocal imaging for the tension calculation; cholesterol 5-30% and LPC 5 µM applied as indicated | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.1 (sem)','T50',NULL,NULL,6.2,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'6.2','mN/m','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified E. coli MscS and MscL coreconstituted into azolectin (99.9%) + rhodamine-PE (0.1%) liposomes (cholesterol/PE/PC variants as indicated)','azolectin liposome (coreconstituted MscS + MscL)',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical; liposome recording solution)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00102','Boltzmann curves for MscS and MscL. The midpoint tension for MscS and MscL is 6.2 ± 0.1 and 12.0 ± 0.3 mN/m, respectively (mean ± SEM; n = 4).','Results (Fig 1 E; Boltzmann midpoint tensions)','high','purified-channel coreconstitution system (both channels in one liposome, tension from confocal patch imaging). The MscL 12.0 ± 0.3 mN/m in the same sentence is paralog-side -> not rowed. MscS-side rows only: midpoint tension 6.2 ± 0.1 mN/m (n = 4, azolectin coreconstituted liposomes, confocal tension calibration) + the two explicit MscS threshold changes (cholesterol +126%, LPC -75%). PARALOG (MscL-side) excluded: midpoint tension 12.0 ± 0.3 mN/m; cholesterol +27%; LPC -57%; TR (MscL/MscS threshold ratio) changes. ''Activation threshold'' here = first-opening threshold (onset tier): the % CHANGES are rowed as threshold_fold_shift (schema_gap) with the onset definition declared; no absolute-threshold rows. The no-LPC time-control drift (''The activation threshold before application of LPC decreased over that interval 15% for MscS and 10% for MscL'') is a patch-creep control, not a modulator effect -> not rowed (archived here). Cholesterol concentration in the Fig 3 comparison is azolectin:cholesterol 70%:30% (''the addition of 5-30% cholesterol'' range in text) -> 30% stored with the range declared. LPC = lysophosphatidylcholine, 5 µM to the bath -> ''potentiator'' as the closest enum for the threshold-lowering effect (spontaneous activity after ~10 min); cholesterol stiffens/thickens -> ''antagonist''. FLIM-FRET MscS-MscL clustering raises the MscS threshold — quantified in figures only -> no row. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','azolectin liposomes with coreconstituted E. coli MscS + MscL, Boltzmann fit of Po-vs-tension (confocal patch-shape imaging), +30 mV','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',114,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(308,'MAIC:BX:00308',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative-pressure ramps on liposome patches at +30 mV pipette potential; patch-shape confocal imaging for the tension calculation; cholesterol 5-30% and LPC 5 µM applied as indicated | MODULATOR: cholesterol (antagonist) 30 % (azolectin:cholesterol 70:30; 5-30% range tested)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,126.0,'%',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'126','%','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified E. coli MscS and MscL coreconstituted into azolectin (99.9%) + rhodamine-PE (0.1%) liposomes (cholesterol/PE/PC variants as indicated)','azolectin liposome (coreconstituted MscS + MscL)',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical; liposome recording solution)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00103','Higher membrane tension was required to activate both channels in the presence of cholesterol. The relative increase in activation threshold of MscS was much higher (126%) compared with MscL (27%) ( Fig. 3 B ) indicating a much stronger effect of cholesterol on MscS.','Results (Fig 3 B cholesterol / Fig 4 C LPC)','medium','paper''s own explicit % change of the MscS first-opening (onset) threshold; no absolute mmHg endpoints for these comparisons -> threshold_fold_shift schema_gap (unit ''%'' as reported). MscL counterparts (27% / 57%) are paralog-side -> excluded. cholesterol raises the MscS first-opening threshold (bilayer thickness/stiffness/pressure-profile effect) -> ''antagonist'' as the closest enum. MscS-side rows only: midpoint tension 6.2 ± 0.1 mN/m (n = 4, azolectin coreconstituted liposomes, confocal tension calibration) + the two explicit MscS threshold changes (cholesterol +126%, LPC -75%). PARALOG (MscL-side) excluded: midpoint tension 12.0 ± 0.3 mN/m; cholesterol +27%; LPC -57%; TR (MscL/MscS threshold ratio) changes. ''Activation threshold'' here = first-opening threshold (onset tier): the % CHANGES are rowed as threshold_fold_shift (schema_gap) with the onset definition declared; no absolute-threshold rows. The no-LPC time-control drift (''The activation threshold before application of LPC decreased over that interval 15% for MscS and 10% for MscL'') is a patch-creep control, not a modulator effect -> not rowed (archived here). Cholesterol concentration in the Fig 3 comparison is azolectin:cholesterol 70%:30% (''the addition of 5-30% cholesterol'' range in text) -> 30% stored with the range declared. LPC = lysophosphatidylcholine, 5 µM to the bath -> ''potentiator'' as the closest enum for the threshold-lowering effect (spontaneous activity after ~10 min); cholesterol stiffens/thickens -> ''antagonist''. FLIM-FRET MscS-MscL clustering raises the MscS threshold — quantified in figures only -> no row.','azolectin:cholesterol (70%:30%) liposomes vs azolectin (100%), coreconstituted MscS',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',114,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(309,'MAIC:BX:00309',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative-pressure ramps on liposome patches at +30 mV pipette potential; patch-shape confocal imaging for the tension calculation; cholesterol 5-30% and LPC 5 µM applied as indicated | MODULATOR: lysophosphatidylcholine (LPC) (potentiator) 5 µM',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,75.0,'%',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'75','%','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified E. coli MscS and MscL coreconstituted into azolectin (99.9%) + rhodamine-PE (0.1%) liposomes (cholesterol/PE/PC variants as indicated)','azolectin liposome (coreconstituted MscS + MscL)',NULL,7.2,'200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2 (symmetrical; liposome recording solution)','200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, 5 mM HEPES, pH 7.2',30.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MSCS-EX-00104','Again, we applied a pressure ramp and noticed a 75% reduction in the activation threshold of MscS and 57% in the activation threshold of MscL ( Fig. 4 C ), resulting in a significant increase in the MscL/MscS TR ( Fig. 4 D ).','Results (Fig 3 B cholesterol / Fig 4 C LPC)','medium','paper''s own explicit % change of the MscS first-opening (onset) threshold; no absolute mmHg endpoints for these comparisons -> threshold_fold_shift schema_gap (unit ''%'' as reported). MscL counterparts (27% / 57%) are paralog-side -> excluded. LPC (5 µM, bath) LOWERS the MscS threshold and eventually causes spontaneous activity -> ''potentiator'' as the closest enum; magnitude rowed positive with the reduction direction in the label/quote. MscS-side rows only: midpoint tension 6.2 ± 0.1 mN/m (n = 4, azolectin coreconstituted liposomes, confocal tension calibration) + the two explicit MscS threshold changes (cholesterol +126%, LPC -75%). PARALOG (MscL-side) excluded: midpoint tension 12.0 ± 0.3 mN/m; cholesterol +27%; LPC -57%; TR (MscL/MscS threshold ratio) changes. ''Activation threshold'' here = first-opening threshold (onset tier): the % CHANGES are rowed as threshold_fold_shift (schema_gap) with the onset definition declared; no absolute-threshold rows. The no-LPC time-control drift (''The activation threshold before application of LPC decreased over that interval 15% for MscS and 10% for MscL'') is a patch-creep control, not a modulator effect -> not rowed (archived here). Cholesterol concentration in the Fig 3 comparison is azolectin:cholesterol 70%:30% (''the addition of 5-30% cholesterol'' range in text) -> 30% stored with the range declared. LPC = lysophosphatidylcholine, 5 µM to the bath -> ''potentiator'' as the closest enum for the threshold-lowering effect (spontaneous activity after ~10 min); cholesterol stiffens/thickens -> ''antagonist''. FLIM-FRET MscS-MscL clustering raises the MscS threshold — quantified in figures only -> no row.','5 µM LPC applied to the bath vs 10-min no-LPC interval, coreconstituted MscS',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',114,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(310,'MAIC:BX:00310',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'mechanical indentation with a fire-polished glass pipette (3-4 µm tip) positioned at 80 degrees to the cell, driven by a Clampex-controlled piezoelectric microstage; 1 µm/ms ramp, 150-ms stimuli, series of 0.5 or 1 µm increments every 10-20 s; threshold = minimum indentation from probe-cell contact to first channel response | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.9 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,8.6,'um',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'8.6','µm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','HEK-P1KO (Piezo1-knockout HEK293T) transiently transfected with the indicated channel (Arabidopsis OSCA1.1/1.2/1.8/2.3/3.1/4.1, DmTMEM63, MmTMEM63A/B/C, HsTMEM63A; 600 ng/ml per clone, recorded 24-48 h after transfection)','HEK-P1KO (HEK293T Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,7.3,'133 NaCl, 3 KCl, 2.5 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, 10 HEPES, 10 glucose, pH 7.3 (NaOH), 300 mmol/kg (iso-osmotic)','133 CsCl, 1 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, 5 EGTA, 10 HEPES, 4 MgATP, 0.4 Na2GTP, pH 7.3 (CsOH)',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00001','OSCA1.1 and OSCA1.2 whole-cell MA currents had an apparent activation threshold of 8.6 ± 0.9 µm and 6.3 ± 0.7 µm, and inactivated (channel closure in continued presence of stimulus) with a time constant of 10.0 ± 1.3 ms and 10.4 ± 1.7 ms, respectively ( Figure 1B and Table 1 ).','Results (poke thresholds; Fig 1, A and B; Table 1)','high','SEMANTICS: the paper''s poke ''apparent activation threshold'' is the MINIMUM indentation from probe-cell contact to first channel response (methods definition), not a Boltzmann 50% midpoint; mapped to the x50 slot per the round ruling (poke indentation -> x50). n from Table 1. MURTHY ARCHIVE (not rowed): OSCA2.3 / OSCA3.1 / OSCA4.1 Table-1 rows are PARALOG-SUBCLADE (round config: OSCA2.x/3.x = paralog) or no-activity mock-level (OSCA4.1 13.3±2.0 pA poke / 1.2±0.05 pA stretch; OSCA2.3 stretch Imax 31.3±11 pA, tau_act 18.8±3.2, tau_inact 110±70, P50 59.7±3.8, conductance n.d.; OSCA3.1 poke 9.7±1.4 pA, stretch Imax 306±47, tau_act 5.6±1.4, tau_inact 18.5±2.5, P50 44.5±3.2, conductance 24.9±3.4 pS) — OSCA1.8 IS OSCA1-subclade (core, rowed). MmTMEM63C row = mock-level currents (4.5±0.9 pA poke / 4.73±0.8 pA stretch; no P50/tau) -> no rows. MmPIEZO1 (3045±875 pA poke etc., P50 24.0±3.6, conductance 27.3±0.3 pS from Saotome et al. 2018) = out-of-family comparison, never rowed. All Imax columns are currents (pA), no parameter_kind home. Gd3+ (60 µM in the pipette) blocks OSCA1.1/1.2 maximal currents by 80%/72% and MmTMEM63A by 75% — percent block, no Hill fit -> no ic50 rows. MmTMEM63A ion-substitution I-V (Control/NMDG-Cl/KCl/Cs-Meth) is qualitative (no E_rev/ratio numbers) -> no ion_selectivity row for TMEM63s. Hyperosmotic (300->620 mmol/kg) whole-cell currents: osmotic gradient without X50/EC50 -> never rowed (round N-standard). Yuan 2014''s smaller conductance values are cited prior work, not rowed. Text-vs-Table error variants: P50 text -58.5±3.7 vs table 58.5±2.4; stretch inact text 24±3.4 / 24.6±4.8 vs table 24.0±3.0 / 24.6±4.7 — table rowed (carries n), variants declared.','AtOSCA1.1_HEK-P1KO_poke_fire-polished-probe_3-4um-tip_minimum-indentation_-80mV_Table1','9','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',131,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
