% — percent block, no Hill fit -> no ic50 rows. MmTMEM63A ion-substitution I-V (Control/NMDG-Cl/KCl/Cs-Meth) is qualitative (no E_rev/ratio numbers) -> no ion_selectivity row for TMEM63s. Hyperosmotic (300->620 mmol/kg) whole-cell currents: osmotic gradient without X50/EC50 -> never rowed (round N-standard). Yuan 2014''s smaller conductance values are cited prior work, not rowed. Text-vs-Table error variants: P50 text -58.5±3.7 vs table 58.5±2.4; stretch inact text 24±3.4 / 24.6±4.8 vs table 24.0±3.0 / 24.6±4.7 — table rowed (carries n), variants declared.','HsTMEM63A_HEK-P1KO_cell-attached_stretch_HSPC_Boltzmann-P50_-80mV_Table1','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',131,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(338,'MAIC:BX:00338',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure (as high as 100-120 mmHg) applied to patches excised from proteoliposomes in symmetrical 200 mM KCl; single-channel slope conductance from I-V linear regression | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 13 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,346.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'346','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified OSCA1.2(-EGFP) reconstituted into liposomes (direct force-from-lipids demonstration; inside-out patches on proteoliposomes)','proteoliposome (purified OSCA1.2 protein)',NULL,7.0,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM MOPS, pH 7.0 (KOH)','200 mM KCl, 5 mM MOPS, pH 7.0 (KOH)',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00029','At the single-channel level, the stretch-activated currents exhibited sub-conductance states, were voltage-dependent, and had a conductance of 346 ± 13 pS in 200 mM KCl solution, which matched the single-channel conductance measured from OSCA1.2-expressing cells (304 ± 9 pS) under the same ionic concentration ( Figure 3—figure supplement 1 and Figure 3G,H ).','Results (proteoliposome single channels; Fig 3, G and H; Fig 3—figure supplement 1)','high','DERIVATION DECLARED: slope conductance from I-V (linear regression / single-point amplitude at -80 mV assuming 0 pA at 0 mV, methods); subconductance states present. purified OSCA1.2(-EGFP) in soybean liposomes, inside-out patches, symmetrical 200 mM KCl — the paper''s direct force-from-lipids demonstration (no cellular components); N = 8 proteoliposome patches. MURTHY ARCHIVE (not rowed): OSCA2.3 / OSCA3.1 / OSCA4.1 Table-1 rows are PARALOG-SUBCLADE (round config: OSCA2.x/3.x = paralog) or no-activity mock-level (OSCA4.1 13.3±2.0 pA poke / 1.2±0.05 pA stretch; OSCA2.3 stretch Imax 31.3±11 pA, tau_act 18.8±3.2, tau_inact 110±70, P50 59.7±3.8, conductance n.d.; OSCA3.1 poke 9.7±1.4 pA, stretch Imax 306±47, tau_act 5.6±1.4, tau_inact 18.5±2.5, P50 44.5±3.2, conductance 24.9±3.4 pS) — OSCA1.8 IS OSCA1-subclade (core, rowed). MmTMEM63C row = mock-level currents (4.5±0.9 pA poke / 4.73±0.8 pA stretch; no P50/tau) -> no rows. MmPIEZO1 (3045±875 pA poke etc., P50 24.0±3.6, conductance 27.3±0.3 pS from Saotome et al. 2018) = out-of-family comparison, never rowed. All Imax columns are currents (pA), no parameter_kind home. Gd3+ (60 µM in the pipette) blocks OSCA1.1/1.2 maximal currents by 80%/72% and MmTMEM63A by 75% — percent block, no Hill fit -> no ic50 rows. MmTMEM63A ion-substitution I-V (Control/NMDG-Cl/KCl/Cs-Meth) is qualitative (no E_rev/ratio numbers) -> no ion_selectivity row for TMEM63s. Hyperosmotic (300->620 mmol/kg) whole-cell currents: osmotic gradient without X50/EC50 -> never rowed (round N-standard). Yuan 2014''s smaller conductance values are cited prior work, not rowed. Text-vs-Table error variants: P50 text -58.5±3.7 vs table 58.5±2.4; stretch inact text 24±3.4 / 24.6±4.8 vs table 24.0±3.0 / 24.6±4.7 — table rowed (carries n), variants declared.','AtOSCA1.2_proteoliposome_inside-out_stretch_200mM-KCl_single-channel_Fig3G-H','8','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',131,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(339,'MAIC:BX:00339',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure (as high as 100-120 mmHg) applied to patches excised from proteoliposomes in symmetrical 200 mM KCl; single-channel slope conductance from I-V linear regression | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 9 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,304.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'304','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified OSCA1.2(-EGFP) reconstituted into liposomes (direct force-from-lipids demonstration; inside-out patches on proteoliposomes)','proteoliposome (purified OSCA1.2 protein)',NULL,7.0,'200 mM KCl, 5 mM MOPS, pH 7.0 (KOH)','200 mM KCl, 5 mM MOPS, pH 7.0 (KOH)',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00030','At the single-channel level, the stretch-activated currents exhibited sub-conductance states, were voltage-dependent, and had a conductance of 346 ± 13 pS in 200 mM KCl solution, which matched the single-channel conductance measured from OSCA1.2-expressing cells (304 ± 9 pS) under the same ionic concentration ( Figure 3—figure supplement 1 and Figure 3G,H ).','Results (proteoliposome single channels; Fig 3, G and H; Fig 3—figure supplement 1)','high','DERIVATION DECLARED: slope conductance from I-V (linear regression / single-point amplitude at -80 mV assuming 0 pA at 0 mV, methods); subconductance states present. matched cell-attached measurement under the SAME 200 mM KCl ionic condition (304 ± 9 pS vs 346 ± 13 pS in liposomes — ''matched'' per the source sentence); N = 6 cells. MURTHY ARCHIVE (not rowed): OSCA2.3 / OSCA3.1 / OSCA4.1 Table-1 rows are PARALOG-SUBCLADE (round config: OSCA2.x/3.x = paralog) or no-activity mock-level (OSCA4.1 13.3±2.0 pA poke / 1.2±0.05 pA stretch; OSCA2.3 stretch Imax 31.3±11 pA, tau_act 18.8±3.2, tau_inact 110±70, P50 59.7±3.8, conductance n.d.; OSCA3.1 poke 9.7±1.4 pA, stretch Imax 306±47, tau_act 5.6±1.4, tau_inact 18.5±2.5, P50 44.5±3.2, conductance 24.9±3.4 pS) — OSCA1.8 IS OSCA1-subclade (core, rowed). MmTMEM63C row = mock-level currents (4.5±0.9 pA poke / 4.73±0.8 pA stretch; no P50/tau) -> no rows. MmPIEZO1 (3045±875 pA poke etc., P50 24.0±3.6, conductance 27.3±0.3 pS from Saotome et al. 2018) = out-of-family comparison, never rowed. All Imax columns are currents (pA), no parameter_kind home. Gd3+ (60 µM in the pipette) blocks OSCA1.1/1.2 maximal currents by 80%/72% and MmTMEM63A by 75% — percent block, no Hill fit -> no ic50 rows. MmTMEM63A ion-substitution I-V (Control/NMDG-Cl/KCl/Cs-Meth) is qualitative (no E_rev/ratio numbers) -> no ion_selectivity row for TMEM63s. Hyperosmotic (300->620 mmol/kg) whole-cell currents: osmotic gradient without X50/EC50 -> never rowed (round N-standard). Yuan 2014''s smaller conductance values are cited prior work, not rowed. Text-vs-Table error variants: P50 text -58.5±3.7 vs table 58.5±2.4; stretch inact text 24±3.4 / 24.6±4.8 vs table 24.0±3.0 / 24.6±4.7 — table rowed (carries n), variants declared.','AtOSCA1.2_HEK-P1KO_cell-attached_stretch_200mM-KCl_single-channel_Fig3G-H_Fig3-fig-supp1','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',131,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(340,'MAIC:BX:00340',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents in excised outside-out patches under asymmetrical NaCl; positive pressure pulses in the outside-out configuration (HSPC-1)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.21,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.21',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OUTSIDE_OUT','HEK-P1KO transiently transfected with Arabidopsis OSCA1.1 or OSCA1.2','HEK-P1KO (HEK293T Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,7.3,'30 NaCl, 10 HEPES, 225 sucrose, pH 7.3 (NaOH) (extracellular)','150 NaCl, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (NaOH) (intracellular)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00031','Characterization of the stretch-activated currents in asymmetrical NaCl solutions revealed that OSCA1.1 and OSCA1.2 evoked non-selective cation currents with some chloride permeability (OSCA1.1: P Cl /P Na = 0.21 ± 0.06; OSCA1.2: P Cl /P Na = 0.17 ± 0.01) ( Figure 1H ).','Results (ion selectivity; Fig 1H)','high','SCHEMA GAP: no DB home for this parameter class (see data/extraction_schema.md schema-gap register). ion_selectivity_ratio has no DB column (reversal_potential_mv is only a partial proxy). GHK-derived from E_rev in asymmetrical NaCl (30 mM out / 150 mM in + sucrose); dimensionless as-reported; both channels are non-selective cation channels with residual Cl- permeability. MURTHY ARCHIVE (not rowed): OSCA2.3 / OSCA3.1 / OSCA4.1 Table-1 rows are PARALOG-SUBCLADE (round config: OSCA2.x/3.x = paralog) or no-activity mock-level (OSCA4.1 13.3±2.0 pA poke / 1.2±0.05 pA stretch; OSCA2.3 stretch Imax 31.3±11 pA, tau_act 18.8±3.2, tau_inact 110±70, P50 59.7±3.8, conductance n.d.; OSCA3.1 poke 9.7±1.4 pA, stretch Imax 306±47, tau_act 5.6±1.4, tau_inact 18.5±2.5, P50 44.5±3.2, conductance 24.9±3.4 pS) — OSCA1.8 IS OSCA1-subclade (core, rowed). MmTMEM63C row = mock-level currents (4.5±0.9 pA poke / 4.73±0.8 pA stretch; no P50/tau) -> no rows. MmPIEZO1 (3045±875 pA poke etc., P50 24.0±3.6, conductance 27.3±0.3 pS from Saotome et al. 2018) = out-of-family comparison, never rowed. All Imax columns are currents (pA), no parameter_kind home. Gd3+ (60 µM in the pipette) blocks OSCA1.1/1.2 maximal currents by 80%/72% and MmTMEM63A by 75% — percent block, no Hill fit -> no ic50 rows. MmTMEM63A ion-substitution I-V (Control/NMDG-Cl/KCl/Cs-Meth) is qualitative (no E_rev/ratio numbers) -> no ion_selectivity row for TMEM63s. Hyperosmotic (300->620 mmol/kg) whole-cell currents: osmotic gradient without X50/EC50 -> never rowed (round N-standard). Yuan 2014''s smaller conductance values are cited prior work, not rowed. Text-vs-Table error variants: P50 text -58.5±3.7 vs table 58.5±2.4; stretch inact text 24±3.4 / 24.6±4.8 vs table 24.0±3.0 / 24.6±4.7 — table rowed (carries n), variants declared. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','AtOSCA1.1_HEK-P1KO_outside-out_stretch_asymmetrical-NaCl_PCl-PNa_Fig1H',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',131,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
