ance row; the verify layer''s conductance flag is N). Responder fractions 8/33 T63a+/+ (~25%) vs 1/29 T63a-/- = KO validation context, archived. Mechanical-indentation two-photon Ca2+ imaging values (1.79 ± 0.6 soma/process ratio, 8.0 ± 1.19 s spread) are imaging metrics. Myelin geometry metrics (internode lengths, g ratios) are phenotype, not channel parameters. Error convention: results text = mean ± SD (STAR Methods statistical analysis). The source prints the inactivation error separator as ''+ 45.59'' — read as the ± of the sentence pair, declared.','mTMEM63A_OL-primary-native_cell-attached_HSPC_1s-pulses_-60mV_tau_inact_Fig2F-J',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',133,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(353,'MAIC:BX:00353',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'extracellular osmolarity stepped from 300 to 170 mOsm/L (mannitol-free hypotonic Na-gluconate solution) with simultaneous GCaMP6f Ca2+ monitoring; 100-ms voltage ramps -80 to +80 mV every 1 s; isotonic solution restored when currents at -70 mV reached ~500 pA | STIMULUS: 170 mOsm/L',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,6580.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'6.58','s','HYPOTONIC',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','Neuro-2a (N2a) mouse neuroblastoma cells transfected with mouse TMEM63B-P2A-GCaMP6f (mouse Tmem63b amplified from mouse brain cDNAs)','N2a (mouse neuroblastoma)',NULL,7.4,'80 Na-gluconate, 1 Ca-gluconate, 10 HEPES, pH 7.4 (NaOH), 300 mOsm/L isotonic (with 130 mM mannitol) stepped to 170 mOsm/L hypotonic (mannitol-free)','80 K-gluconate, 10 HEPES, 130 mannitol, pH 7.4, 300 mOsm/L',-70.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00044','The currents possessed the characteristics of slow activation (6.58 ± 0.36 s; n = 133; between ~20% and 80% activation at -70 mV; Figure 2B) and rapid deactivation (1.29 ± 0.06 s between ~20% and 80% deactivation; Figure 2B). The activation times were likely underestimated because the maximal activation had not been reached in most cells of our recordings.','Results (TMEM63B is a hypo-osmolarity-activated cation channel; Figure 2B)','high','SCHEMA GAP: no DB home for this parameter class (see data/extraction_schema.md schema-gap register). UNIT HAZARD (round ruling 3): the verify layer''s tau_act/tau_deact flags resolve HERE — these whole-cell 20-80% rise/fall TIMES are in SECONDS as-reported (never converted; x1000-to-ms hazard: 6.58 s = 6580 ms, do NOT load into tau_*_ms). The validator fixes tau_* to ms and the schema-gap register defines macroscopic_rise_time precisely for second-scale whole-cell current kinetics (''NOT single-channel exponential tau''), so both values row as macroscopic_rise_time (schema_gap); they are 20-80% times, not exponential taus. The deactivation row reuses the kind (the schema has no macroscopic fall-time member; fall-time analog, declared). n = 133 attaches to the activation measurement only. Activation ''likely underestimated'' per the source. DU ARCHIVE (not rowed): substituted-cation E_rev endpoints (-5.6 ± 1.0 mV K+ n=13; -20.0 ± 1.7 Cs+ n=9; -13.0 ± 2.8 Mg2+ n=7; -20.8 ± 1.5 Ca2+ n=13; 3.3 ± 3.2 Ba2+ n=7) are the GHK derivation basis of the ROWED Px/PK ratios — not rowed separately (double representation). Percent block at single concentrations (100 µM RR 82.7% ± 3.4% n=17; 1 mM La3+ 96.7% ± 0.6% n=12) archived; the ROWED quantities are the paper''s own IC50 fits. NMDG+ substitution abolishes currents (qualitative). Osmotic dose-dependence (300 -> 200/240 mOsm responder fractions) is gradient-only without X50/EC50 -> threshold flag yields NO row (round N-standard ruling). Hyperosmotic 600 mOsm responses (~5% cells) qualitative. Native OHC side: inward currents increased by ~70 pA, blocked by 1 mM La3+, absent in Tmem63b-/- — no channel-parameter numerics. Error convention: means ± SEM (STAR Methods). [F-004:undetermined] junction not certifiable offline (no fulltext corpus (abstract-only fallback); classified 2026-08-31)','mTMEM63B_N2a_whole-cell_hypotonic-170mOsML_20-80pct-activation-time_-70mV_Fig2B','133','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',134,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
