c_rise_time (schema_gap); they are 20-80% times, not exponential taus. The deactivation row reuses the kind (the schema has no macroscopic fall-time member; fall-time analog, declared). n = 133 attaches to the activation measurement only. Activation ''likely underestimated'' per the source. DU ARCHIVE (not rowed): substituted-cation E_rev endpoints (-5.6 ± 1.0 mV K+ n=13; -20.0 ± 1.7 Cs+ n=9; -13.0 ± 2.8 Mg2+ n=7; -20.8 ± 1.5 Ca2+ n=13; 3.3 ± 3.2 Ba2+ n=7) are the GHK derivation basis of the ROWED Px/PK ratios — not rowed separately (double representation). Percent block at single concentrations (100 µM RR 82.7% ± 3.4% n=17; 1 mM La3+ 96.7% ± 0.6% n=12) archived; the ROWED quantities are the paper''s own IC50 fits. NMDG+ substitution abolishes currents (qualitative). Osmotic dose-dependence (300 -> 200/240 mOsm responder fractions) is gradient-only without X50/EC50 -> threshold flag yields NO row (round N-standard ruling). Hyperosmotic 600 mOsm responses (~5% cells) qualitative. Native OHC side: inward currents increased by ~70 pA, blocked by 1 mM La3+, absent in Tmem63b-/- — no channel-parameter numerics. Error convention: means ± SEM (STAR Methods). [F-004:undetermined] junction not certifiable offline (no fulltext corpus (abstract-only fallback); classified 2026-08-31)','mTMEM63B_N2a_whole-cell_hypotonic-170mOsML_20-80pct-deactivation-time_-70mV_Fig2B',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',134,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(355,'MAIC:BX:00355',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'extracellular osmolarity stepped from 300 to 170 mOsm/L (mannitol-free hypotonic Na-gluconate solution) with simultaneous GCaMP6f Ca2+ monitoring; 100-ms voltage ramps -80 to +80 mV every 1 s; isotonic solution restored when currents at -70 mV reached ~500 pA | STIMULUS: 170 mOsm/L | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.8 (sem)','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-6.9,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-6.9','mV','HYPOTONIC',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','Neuro-2a (N2a) mouse neuroblastoma cells transfected with mouse TMEM63B-P2A-GCaMP6f (mouse Tmem63b amplified from mouse brain cDNAs)','N2a (mouse neuroblastoma)',NULL,7.4,'80 Na-gluconate, 1 Ca-gluconate, 10 HEPES, pH 7.4 (NaOH), 300 mOsm/L isotonic (with 130 mM mannitol) stepped to 170 mOsm/L hypotonic (mannitol-free)','80 K-gluconate, 10 HEPES, 130 mannitol, pH 7.4, 300 mOsm/L',-70.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00046','The reversal potential of the osmosensitive currents averaged -6.9 ± 0.8 mV (n = 22).','Results (TMEM63B is a hypo-osmolarity-activated cation channel; Figure 2)','high','absolute E_rev of the Na-gluconate-based osmosensitive current (not a shift); basis of the substituted-cation Px/PK series. DU ARCHIVE (not rowed): substituted-cation E_rev endpoints (-5.6 ± 1.0 mV K+ n=13; -20.0 ± 1.7 Cs+ n=9; -13.0 ± 2.8 Mg2+ n=7; -20.8 ± 1.5 Ca2+ n=13; 3.3 ± 3.2 Ba2+ n=7) are the GHK derivation basis of the ROWED Px/PK ratios — not rowed separately (double representation). Percent block at single concentrations (100 µM RR 82.7% ± 3.4% n=17; 1 mM La3+ 96.7% ± 0.6% n=12) archived; the ROWED quantities are the paper''s own IC50 fits. NMDG+ substitution abolishes currents (qualitative). Osmotic dose-dependence (300 -> 200/240 mOsm responder fractions) is gradient-only without X50/EC50 -> threshold flag yields NO row (round N-standard ruling). Hyperosmotic 600 mOsm responses (~5% cells) qualitative. Native OHC side: inward currents increased by ~70 pA, blocked by 1 mM La3+, absent in Tmem63b-/- — no channel-parameter numerics. Error convention: means ± SEM (STAR Methods).','mTMEM63B_N2a_whole-cell_hypotonic-170mOsML_Erev_ramp--80-to-+80mV_Fig2A','22','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',134,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(356,'MAIC:BX:00356',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'extracellular osmolarity stepped from 300 to 170 mOsm/L (mannitol-free hypotonic Na-gluconate solution) with simultaneous GCaMP6f Ca2+ monitoring; 100-ms voltage ramps -80 to +80 mV every 1 s; isotonic solution restored when currents at -70 mV reached ~500 pA | STIMULUS: 170 mOsm/L',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.96,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.96',NULL,'HYPOTONIC',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','Neuro-2a (N2a) mouse neuroblastoma cells transfected with mouse TMEM63B-P2A-GCaMP6f (mouse Tmem63b amplified from mouse brain cDNAs)','N2a (mouse neuroblastoma)',NULL,7.4,'80 Na-gluconate, 1 Ca-gluconate, 10 HEPES, pH 7.4 (NaOH), 300 mOsm/L isotonic (with 130 mM mannitol) stepped to 170 mOsm/L hypotonic (mannitol-free)','80 K-gluconate, 10 HEPES, 130 mannitol, pH 7.4, 300 mOsm/L',-70.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00047','The permeability of monovalent cations relative to K+ (Px/PK) was K+ (1.00) ~Na+ (0.96) > Cs+ (0.58) and of divalent cations was Ba2+ (1.80) > Mg2+ (0.71) > Ca2+ (0.45), respectively (Figure 2F).','Results (ionic selectivity; Figures 2, D-2F)','high','SCHEMA GAP: no DB home for this parameter class (see data/extraction_schema.md schema-gap register). ion_selectivity_ratio has no DB column. GHK-derived from the substituted-cation E_rev shifts (divalent cations at half the Na+ concentration, osmolarity maintained with mannitol); dimensionless, no error terms stated. K+ (1.00) is the normalization reference, not a measurement -> not rowed. E_rev determined from 7 to 22 cells per cation (per-cation ns archived with the endpoint E_revs). DU ARCHIVE (not rowed): substituted-cation E_rev endpoints (-5.6 ± 1.0 mV K+ n=13; -20.0 ± 1.7 Cs+ n=9; -13.0 ± 2.8 Mg2+ n=7; -20.8 ± 1.5 Ca2+ n=13; 3.3 ± 3.2 Ba2+ n=7) are the GHK derivation basis of the ROWED Px/PK ratios — not rowed separately (double representation). Percent block at single concentrations (100 µM RR 82.7% ± 3.4% n=17; 1 mM La3+ 96.7% ± 0.6% n=12) archived; the ROWED quantities are the paper''s own IC50 fits. NMDG+ substitution abolishes currents (qualitative). Osmotic dose-dependence (300 -> 200/240 mOsm responder fractions) is gradient-only without X50/EC50 -> threshold flag yields NO row (round N-standard ruling). Hyperosmotic 600 mOsm responses (~5% cells) qualitative. Native OHC side: inward currents increased by ~70 pA, blocked by 1 mM La3+, absent in Tmem63b-/- — no channel-parameter numerics. Error convention: means ± SEM (STAR Methods).','mTMEM63B_N2a_whole-cell_hypotonic-cation-substitution_P-Na+-over-K_GHK_Fig2F',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',134,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
