INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(365,'MAIC:BX:00365',7,NULL,NULL,66,'conventional pressure clamp: High-Speed Pressure Clamp-1 (ALA Scientific) negative pressure applied to the patch pipette, -50 to -200 mmHg in -25 mmHg steps; pipettes fire-polished to 10-15 MOhm (14 MOhm matched condition), sampled 10 kHz / filtered 2 kHz; normalized currents fitted with the Boltzmann equation','P50',-200.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-200','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293T-P1KO cells transfected with AtOSCA1.1-CGFP (wild type) or the indicated mutant (recorded 24-36 h after transfection)','HEK293T-P1KO (Piezo1 knockout)',22.0,NULL,'(native membrane environment; solutions per the referenced method)','(per the referenced method)',-60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00058','While P393A at M3 and P511A at M6 slightly reduce channel mechanosensitivity to the half-activation pressures of -174 ± 5 mmHg and -152 ± 10 mmHg, respectively, P443A at M4 and G480A at M5 largely lead to a loss-of-function phenotype as both of their half-activation pressures are beyond -200 mmHg (Fig. 7a, b ).; b Normalized negative pressure activated currents were fitted with the Boltzmann equation. The half-activation pressure is -136 ± 6 mmHg for wildtype OSCA1.1 (black, circle), -174 ± 5 mmHg for OSCA1.1-P393A (red, square), -152 ± 10 mmHg for OSCA1.1-P511A (blue, rhombic), and beyond -200 mmHg for both OSCA1.1-P443A (pink, square) and OSCA1.1-G480A (green, triangle) in HEK293-P1KO cells under the same pipette condition of 14 MΩ.','Results (flexible kink residues; Fig 7, a and b); Fig 7b legend','high','复合 quote 披露（F-004 政策，2026-08-31 补注）：evidence_quote 为原文多处 span 并置（composite 登记册在录）；span 级证据与裁决见 literature/raw/quote_corroboration_manual.json，登记册 tools/literature-mining/configs/composite_quote_registry.json。QUANTIFIED BOUND, not a fitted value: ''half-activation pressures are beyond -200 mmHg'' (loss-of-function phenotype; P50 more negative than -200 mmHg) -> value_relation ''<'' with the as-printed -200 bound; no error term. n = 3 independent cells, mean ± SEM (legend). delta_p50: the paper states shifts only qualitatively -> no delta_p50 rows; compare against the rowed WT endpoint. SHAN ARCHIVE (not rowed): conductance Y-flag -> the paper''s ''single-channel conductance ... is -10 ± 1 pA'' (WT and F516A, -60 mV) and the lyso-PC-activated ''~-6 pA'' F516A current are UNITARY CURRENTS in pA, not pS conductance -> NO conductance rows (round ruling 4; pS-vs-pA hazard declared). delta_p50 Y-flag -> no numeric shift magnitude is stated anywhere (''slightly lower'', ''slightly reduce'') -> mutant ENDPOINT rows only; arithmetic deltas forbidden. Cryo-EM kink angles (M3a 75 deg, M4a 34 deg, M5a 79 deg, M6a 46 deg; lyso-PC M6b movement ~54 deg) are structural descriptors, no parameter_kind home. Low expression of F516A -> smaller microscopic currents (qualitative). [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','AtOSCA1.1-P443A_HEK293T-P1KO_cell-attached_HSPC_-50-to--200mmHg_Boltzmann-P50_-60mV_Fig7b','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',135,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
