6.3±1.8 pA TMEM63A/B liposome; 171.6±25.5 / 120.8±33.2 pA 5Mu / 63A-IL2; 2.6±0.2 pA empty liposomes) are currents. delta_p50 Y-flag -> no numeric mmHg shift stated (''substantially higher P50'') -> endpoint rows only; arithmetic forbidden. ion_selectivity ''unclear'' -> qualitative acidic-neck pore inference (E571/D584 -> K mutants only reduce currents) -> no row. Gd3+ reduces TMEM63A Imax by 76% (percent, no fit) -> no row. Single-channel open-dwell times (OSCA1.2 3.5±0.3 ms; 5Mu 1.8±0.2 ms) have no tau_* home (open-state lifetimes, not activation/inactivation) -> archived. OSCA1.2-E531K concatemer unitary currents (11 / 3 / 7 pA) archived. MD-simulation ''~120 pS as expected for OSCA1.2'' is a simulation expectation, not a measurement.','AtOSCA1.2_proteoliposome-D&R_excised-patch_HSPC_300ms-pulses_Boltzmann-P50_-80mV_Fig4D',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',136,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(376,'MAIC:BX:00376',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents in cell-attached patches: stepwise 300-ms negative pressure pulses (10-mmHg increments, 2 s between stimuli) via a high-speed pressure clamp (HSPC-1, ALA Scientific); patch potential held at -80 mV; P50 from Boltzmann fits of I-P curves | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 4.1','P50',-109.8,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-109.8','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293T cells transiently transfected with human TMEM63A or TMEM63B (or Arabidopsis OSCA1.2 / its monomeric mutants); macroscopic and single-channel currents recorded 4-12 h after seeding (24-48 h post transfection)','HEK293T',NULL,7.3,'(per the referenced HEK293T protocol)','130 NaCl, 5 KCl, 10 HEPES, 10 TEA-Cl, 1 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, pH 7.3 (NaOH); 3-5 MOhm',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00069','Notably, compared to OSCA1.2, OSCA1.2 5Mu showed a substantially higher P 50 (-109.8 ± 4.1 mmHg, Figure 5K ), suggesting that switching from a dimer to monomer leads to high-threshold mechanosensitivity. Similarly, monomeric OSCA1.2 63A IL2 expression also induced high-threshold (P 50 = -133.1 ± 7.7 mmHg) stretch-activated currents (I max = 120.8 ± 33.2 pA) ( Figure 5I – 5K ).','Results (monomeric OSCA1.2 mutants; Figures 5, I-5K)','high','monomeric OSCA1.2 5Mu (five point mutations in the IL2 dimerization interface). IL2-interface quintuple mutant that renders OSCA1.2 monomeric; no single HGVS (multi-residue construct) -> variant_hgvs_short blank, construct in the key. delta_p50 flag: the dimer->monomer shift vs the rowed dimeric AtOSCA1.2 HEK endpoint (-85.9 ± 5.2) is NOT stated as a number -> no delta row (arithmetic forbidden). ZHENG ARCHIVE (not rowed): TMEM63A/B unitary conductance UNRESOLVED (''not able to resolve single-channel currents of TMEM63s, which were probably too small to be detected''; proteoliposome: ''No single-channel current was resolved'') -> no TMEM63 conductance rows (round ruling 4). The rowed 129±3 / 133 / 126±5 / 57±5 pS values are AtOSCA1.2-subclade (SELF-subclade -> rowable per the round ruling; gene checked per quote). Imax values (310.2±85.1 pA OSCA1.2 HEK; 155.4±20.9 pA liposome; 18.7±3.1 / 16.3±1.8 pA TMEM63A/B liposome; 171.6±25.5 / 120.8±33.2 pA 5Mu / 63A-IL2; 2.6±0.2 pA empty liposomes) are currents. delta_p50 Y-flag -> no numeric mmHg shift stated (''substantially higher P50'') -> endpoint rows only; arithmetic forbidden. ion_selectivity ''unclear'' -> qualitative acidic-neck pore inference (E571/D584 -> K mutants only reduce currents) -> no row. Gd3+ reduces TMEM63A Imax by 76% (percent, no fit) -> no row. Single-channel open-dwell times (OSCA1.2 3.5±0.3 ms; 5Mu 1.8±0.2 ms) have no tau_* home (open-state lifetimes, not activation/inactivation) -> archived. OSCA1.2-E531K concatemer unitary currents (11 / 3 / 7 pA) archived. MD-simulation ''~120 pS as expected for OSCA1.2'' is a simulation expectation, not a measurement.','AtOSCA1.2-5Mu_HEK293T_cell-attached_HSPC_300ms-pulses_Boltzmann-P50_-80mV_Fig5K',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',136,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(377,'MAIC:BX:00377',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents in cell-attached patches: stepwise 300-ms negative pressure pulses (10-mmHg increments, 2 s between stimuli) via a high-speed pressure clamp (HSPC-1, ALA Scientific); patch potential held at -80 mV; P50 from Boltzmann fits of I-P curves | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 7.7','P50',-133.1,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-133.1','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293T cells transiently transfected with human TMEM63A or TMEM63B (or Arabidopsis OSCA1.2 / its monomeric mutants); macroscopic and single-channel currents recorded 4-12 h after seeding (24-48 h post transfection)','HEK293T',NULL,7.3,'(per the referenced HEK293T protocol)','130 NaCl, 5 KCl, 10 HEPES, 10 TEA-Cl, 1 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, pH 7.3 (NaOH); 3-5 MOhm',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00070','Notably, compared to OSCA1.2, OSCA1.2 5Mu showed a substantially higher P 50 (-109.8 ± 4.1 mmHg, Figure 5K ), suggesting that switching from a dimer to monomer leads to high-threshold mechanosensitivity. Similarly, monomeric OSCA1.2 63A IL2 expression also induced high-threshold (P 50 = -133.1 ± 7.7 mmHg) stretch-activated currents (I max = 120.8 ± 33.2 pA) ( Figure 5I – 5K ).','Results (monomeric OSCA1.2 mutants; Figures 5, I-5K)','high','monomeric OSCA1.2 63A IL2 chimera (OSCA1.2 backbone with the TMEM63A IL2 domain). CHIMERA: OSCA1.2 backbone + human TMEM63A IL2 — AtOSCA1.2-subclade row (pore/backbone gene), chimera declared; unlike 5Mu it shows little inactivation. delta_p50 flag: the dimer->monomer shift vs the rowed dimeric AtOSCA1.2 HEK endpoint (-85.9 ± 5.2) is NOT stated as a number -> no delta row (arithmetic forbidden). ZHENG ARCHIVE (not rowed): TMEM63A/B unitary conductance UNRESOLVED (''not able to resolve single-channel currents of TMEM63s, which were probably too small to be detected''; proteoliposome: ''No single-channel current was resolved'') -> no TMEM63 conductance rows (round ruling 4). The rowed 129±3 / 133 / 126±5 / 57±5 pS values are AtOSCA1.2-subclade (SELF-subclade -> rowable per the round ruling; gene checked per quote). Imax values (310.2±85.1 pA OSCA1.2 HEK; 155.4±20.9 pA liposome; 18.7±3.1 / 16.3±1.8 pA TMEM63A/B liposome; 171.6±25.5 / 120.8±33.2 pA 5Mu / 63A-IL2; 2.6±0.2 pA empty liposomes) are currents. delta_p50 Y-flag -> no numeric mmHg shift stated (''substantially higher P50'') -> endpoint rows only; arithmetic forbidden. ion_selectivity ''unclear'' -> qualitative acidic-neck pore inference (E571/D584 -> K mutants only reduce currents) -> no row. Gd3+ reduces TMEM63A Imax by 76% (percent, no fit) -> no row. Single-channel open-dwell times (OSCA1.2 3.5±0.3 ms; 5Mu 1.8±0.2 ms) have no tau_* home (open-state lifetimes, not activation/inactivation) -> archived. OSCA1.2-E531K concatemer unitary currents (11 / 3 / 7 pA) archived. MD-simulation ''~120 pS as expected for OSCA1.2'' is a simulation expectation, not a measurement.','AtOSCA1.2-63A-IL2_HEK293T_cell-attached_HSPC_300ms-pulses_Boltzmann-P50_-80mV_Fig5K',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',136,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(378,'MAIC:BX:00378',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents in cell-attached patches: stepwise 300-ms negative pressure pulses (10-mmHg increments, 2 s between stimuli) via a high-speed pressure clamp (HSPC-1, ALA Scientific); patch potential held at -80 mV; P50 from Boltzmann fits of I-P curves | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 3 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,129.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'129','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293T cells transiently transfected with human TMEM63A or TMEM63B (or Arabidopsis OSCA1.2 / its monomeric mutants); macroscopic and single-channel currents recorded 4-12 h after seeding (24-48 h post transfection)','HEK293T',NULL,7.3,'(per the referenced HEK293T protocol)','130 NaCl, 5 KCl, 10 HEPES, 10 TEA-Cl, 1 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, pH 7.3 (NaOH); 3-5 MOhm',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00071','In HEK293T cells, OSCA1.2 induced two types of stretch-activated unitary currents, a dominant fully open current with a conductance of 129 ± 3 pS, and a transient smaller current with approximately half amplitude ( Figure 5L and 5M ).','Results (single-channel behavior; Figures 5, L and 5M)','high','pS actual conductance (ruling 4 satisfied: these are stated conductances, not pA currents). SELF-subclade check: every one of these values belongs to the AtOSCA1.2 (or OSCA1.2-mutant/chimera) construct — the round ruling explicitly makes them rowable AtOSCA1.2 rows. dominant fully open level; a transient approximately half-amplitude level (sub-conductance / single-pore interpretation) is archived without a value. ZHENG ARCHIVE (not rowed): TMEM63A/B unitary conductance UNRESOLVED (''not able to resolve single-channel currents of TMEM63s, which were probably too small to be detected''; proteoliposome: ''No single-channel current was resolved'') -> no TMEM63 conductance rows (round ruling 4). The rowed 129±3 / 133 / 126±5 / 57±5 pS values are AtOSCA1.2-subclade (SELF-subclade -> rowable per the round ruling; gene checked per quote). Imax values (310.2±85.1 pA OSCA1.2 HEK; 155.4±20.9 pA liposome; 18.7±3.1 / 16.3±1.8 pA TMEM63A/B liposome; 171.6±25.5 / 120.8±33.2 pA 5Mu / 63A-IL2; 2.6±0.2 pA empty liposomes) are currents. delta_p50 Y-flag -> no numeric mmHg shift stated (''substantially higher P50'') -> endpoint rows only; arithmetic forbidden. ion_selectivity ''unclear'' -> qualitative acidic-neck pore inference (E571/D584 -> K mutants only reduce currents) -> no row. Gd3+ reduces TMEM63A Imax by 76% (percent, no fit) -> no row. Single-channel open-dwell times (OSCA1.2 3.5±0.3 ms; 5Mu 1.8±0.2 ms) have no tau_* home (open-state lifetimes, not activation/inactivation) -> archived. OSCA1.2-E531K concatemer unitary currents (11 / 3 / 7 pA) archived. MD-simulation ''~120 pS as expected for OSCA1.2'' is a simulation expectation, not a measurement.','AtOSCA1.2_HEK293T_cell-attached_single-channel_-80mV_Fig5L-M',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',136,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(379,'MAIC:BX:00379',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'patch on visible unilamellar proteoliposome membranes; stepwise 300-ms negative pressure pulses (HSPC-1, 10-mmHg increments), patch potential -80 mV','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,133.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'133','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified TMEM63A / TMEM63B / OSCA1.2 protein reconstituted into liposomes by the dehydration-rehydration (D&R) method; excised-patch recordings on unilamellar proteoliposomes','proteoliposome (purified TMEM63A/B or OSCA1.2 protein)',NULL,7.3,'140 KCl, 10 HEPES, 1 MgCl2, 10 glucose, pH 7.3 (KOH)','130 NaCl, 5 KCl, 10 HEPES, 10 TEA-Cl, 1 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, pH 7.3 (NaOH)',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00072','Single-channel current recordings revealed a conductance of 133 pS ( Figure S1I ), consistent with measurements from HEK293T cells.','Results (proteoliposome single channels; Figure S1I)','high','pS actual conductance (ruling 4 satisfied: these are stated conductances, not pA currents). SELF-subclade check: every one of these values belongs to the AtOSCA1.2 (or OSCA1.2-mutant/chimera) construct — the round ruling explicitly makes them rowable AtOSCA1.2 rows. no error term stated for the liposome value; ''consistent with measurements from HEK293T cells''. ZHENG ARCHIVE (not rowed): TMEM63A/B unitary conductance UNRESOLVED (''not able to resolve single-channel currents of TMEM63s, which were probably too small to be detected''; proteoliposome: ''No single-channel current was resolved'') -> no TMEM63 conductance rows (round ruling 4). The rowed 129±3 / 133 / 126±5 / 57±5 pS values are AtOSCA1.2-subclade (SELF-subclade -> rowable per the round ruling; gene checked per quote). Imax values (310.2±85.1 pA OSCA1.2 HEK; 155.4±20.9 pA liposome; 18.7±3.1 / 16.3±1.8 pA TMEM63A/B liposome; 171.6±25.5 / 120.8±33.2 pA 5Mu / 63A-IL2; 2.6±0.2 pA empty liposomes) are currents. delta_p50 Y-flag -> no numeric mmHg shift stated (''substantially higher P50'') -> endpoint rows only; arithmetic forbidden. ion_selectivity ''unclear'' -> qualitative acidic-neck pore inference (E571/D584 -> K mutants only reduce currents) -> no row. Gd3+ reduces TMEM63A Imax by 76% (percent, no fit) -> no row. Single-channel open-dwell times (OSCA1.2 3.5±0.3 ms; 5Mu 1.8±0.2 ms) have no tau_* home (open-state lifetimes, not activation/inactivation) -> archived. OSCA1.2-E531K concatemer unitary currents (11 / 3 / 7 pA) archived. MD-simulation ''~120 pS as expected for OSCA1.2'' is a simulation expectation, not a measurement.','AtOSCA1.2_proteoliposome-D&R_excised-patch_single-channel_-80mV_Fig5L-M_FigS1I',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',136,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(380,'MAIC:BX:00380',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents in cell-attached patches: stepwise 300-ms negative pressure pulses (10-mmHg increments, 2 s between stimuli) via a high-speed pressure clamp (HSPC-1, ALA Scientific); patch potential held at -80 mV; P50 from Boltzmann fits of I-P curves | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 5 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,126.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'126','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293T cells transiently transfected with human TMEM63A or TMEM63B (or Arabidopsis OSCA1.2 / its monomeric mutants); macroscopic and single-channel currents recorded 4-12 h after seeding (24-48 h post transfection)','HEK293T',NULL,7.3,'(per the referenced HEK293T protocol)','130 NaCl, 5 KCl, 10 HEPES, 10 TEA-Cl, 1 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, pH 7.3 (NaOH); 3-5 MOhm',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00073','However, our recordings of monomeric OSCA1.2 5Mu showed a similar fully open current with a conductance of 126 ± 5 pS and a small current of half amplitude ( Figure 5L and 5M ), which indicated that the fully open current observed in OSCA1.2 is from a single-pore and two subunits in OSCA1.2 function in a largely independent manner.','Results (single-channel behavior; Figures 5, L and 5M)','high','pS actual conductance (ruling 4 satisfied: these are stated conductances, not pA currents). SELF-subclade check: every one of these values belongs to the AtOSCA1.2 (or OSCA1.2-mutant/chimera) construct — the round ruling explicitly makes them rowable AtOSCA1.2 rows. monomeric mutant retains a similar fully open conductance -> the full-open level is single-pore, protomers gate independently. ZHENG ARCHIVE (not rowed): TMEM63A/B unitary conductance UNRESOLVED (''not able to resolve single-channel currents of TMEM63s, which were probably too small to be detected''; proteoliposome: ''No single-channel current was resolved'') -> no TMEM63 conductance rows (round ruling 4). The rowed 129±3 / 133 / 126±5 / 57±5 pS values are AtOSCA1.2-subclade (SELF-subclade -> rowable per the round ruling; gene checked per quote). Imax values (310.2±85.1 pA OSCA1.2 HEK; 155.4±20.9 pA liposome; 18.7±3.1 / 16.3±1.8 pA TMEM63A/B liposome; 171.6±25.5 / 120.8±33.2 pA 5Mu / 63A-IL2; 2.6±0.2 pA empty liposomes) are currents. delta_p50 Y-flag -> no numeric mmHg shift stated (''substantially higher P50'') -> endpoint rows only; arithmetic forbidden. ion_selectivity ''unclear'' -> qualitative acidic-neck pore inference (E571/D584 -> K mutants only reduce currents) -> no row. Gd3+ reduces TMEM63A Imax by 76% (percent, no fit) -> no row. Single-channel open-dwell times (OSCA1.2 3.5±0.3 ms; 5Mu 1.8±0.2 ms) have no tau_* home (open-state lifetimes, not activation/inactivation) -> archived. OSCA1.2-E531K concatemer unitary currents (11 / 3 / 7 pA) archived. MD-simulation ''~120 pS as expected for OSCA1.2'' is a simulation expectation, not a measurement.','AtOSCA1.2-5Mu_HEK293T_cell-attached_single-channel_-80mV_Fig5L-M',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',136,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(381,'MAIC:BX:00381',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents in cell-attached patches: stepwise 300-ms negative pressure pulses (10-mmHg increments, 2 s between stimuli) via a high-speed pressure clamp (HSPC-1, ALA Scientific); patch potential held at -80 mV; P50 from Boltzmann fits of I-P curves | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 5 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,57.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'57','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293T cells transiently transfected with human TMEM63A or TMEM63B (or Arabidopsis OSCA1.2 / its monomeric mutants); macroscopic and single-channel currents recorded 4-12 h after seeding (24-48 h post transfection)','HEK293T',NULL,7.3,'(per the referenced HEK293T protocol)','130 NaCl, 5 KCl, 10 HEPES, 10 TEA-Cl, 1 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, pH 7.3 (NaOH); 3-5 MOhm',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00074','Our recordings from monomeric OSCA1.2 63A IL2 only showed currents resembling the assumed sub-conductance currents, with a conductance of 57 ± 5 pS ( Figure 5L and 5M ).','Results (single-channel behavior; Figures 5, L and 5M)','high','pS actual conductance (ruling 4 satisfied: these are stated conductances, not pA currents). SELF-subclade check: every one of these values belongs to the AtOSCA1.2 (or OSCA1.2-mutant/chimera) construct — the round ruling explicitly makes them rowable AtOSCA1.2 rows. chimera shows only the smaller level (partial pore activation per the paper). ZHENG ARCHIVE (not rowed): TMEM63A/B unitary conductance UNRESOLVED (''not able to resolve single-channel currents of TMEM63s, which were probably too small to be detected''; proteoliposome: ''No single-channel current was resolved'') -> no TMEM63 conductance rows (round ruling 4). The rowed 129±3 / 133 / 126±5 / 57±5 pS values are AtOSCA1.2-subclade (SELF-subclade -> rowable per the round ruling; gene checked per quote). Imax values (310.2±85.1 pA OSCA1.2 HEK; 155.4±20.9 pA liposome; 18.7±3.1 / 16.3±1.8 pA TMEM63A/B liposome; 171.6±25.5 / 120.8±33.2 pA 5Mu / 63A-IL2; 2.6±0.2 pA empty liposomes) are currents. delta_p50 Y-flag -> no numeric mmHg shift stated (''substantially higher P50'') -> endpoint rows only; arithmetic forbidden. ion_selectivity ''unclear'' -> qualitative acidic-neck pore inference (E571/D584 -> K mutants only reduce currents) -> no row. Gd3+ reduces TMEM63A Imax by 76% (percent, no fit) -> no row. Single-channel open-dwell times (OSCA1.2 3.5±0.3 ms; 5Mu 1.8±0.2 ms) have no tau_* home (open-state lifetimes, not activation/inactivation) -> archived. OSCA1.2-E531K concatemer unitary currents (11 / 3 / 7 pA) archived. MD-simulation ''~120 pS as expected for OSCA1.2'' is a simulation expectation, not a measurement.','AtOSCA1.2-63A-IL2_HEK293T_cell-attached_single-channel_-80mV_Fig5L-M',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',136,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(382,'MAIC:BX:00382',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure applied to excised outside-out membrane patches via a HSPC device (ALA Scientific); sampled 20 kHz, filtered 1 kHz (low-pass); Multiclamp 200B amplifier + DIGIDATA 1550A / Clampex 10.5 | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 5.37 (sem)','P50',-83.25,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-83.25','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OUTSIDE_OUT','Drosophila S2 cells transfected with DmTMEM63-GFP (pUAST backbone cotransfected with pActin-Gal4, TransIT-Insect; recorded 24-36 h after transfection)','Drosophila S2 (Schneider''s medium + 10% FBS, 25 °C)',25.0,7.2,'140 NaMES (sodium methanesulfonate), 10 HEPES, 320 mOsm, pH 7.2','140 potassium gluconic acid, 10 HEPES, 320 mOsm, pH 7.2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00075','Subsequently, we observed high threshold stretch-activated currents (with a P 50 of -83.25 ± 5.37 mmHg) in S2 cells transfected with Dm TMEM63-GFP (Supplementary Fig. 7b–e ), which is consistent with prior study 38 .','Results (Identification of humidity sensitive OSNs by using a knock-in driver of Tmem63; Supplementary Fig. 7, b–e)','high','CROSS-KINGDOM RULING: Drosophila TMEM63 is an osca-family row (never paralog). Heterologous recombinant DmTMEM63-GFP in S2 cells with an explicit numeric -> confidence high (round ruling 9; heterologous-heavy is the disclosed norm). Negative suction as-printed. SL2 ARCHIVE (not rowed): the paper''s native humidity data (single-sensillum recordings, GCaMP6m antennal-lobe imaging, behavior) carry no channel-parameter numerics. tau_*/conductance/ion flags = N by the verify layer. Error convention: ''All data in bar and line graphs are presented as means ± SEM'' (Statistics and reproducibility) -> error_type=sem. n for the P50 fit is not printed (Supplementary Fig. 7b-e).','DmTMEM63_S2_outside-out_HSPC_negative-pressure_P50_25C_SuppFig7b-e',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',137,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(383,'MAIC:BX:00383',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'voltage-clamp detection of unitary channel fluctuations across the DIB (Dagan 3900A amplifier + pCLAMP 10; filtered 1 kHz, sampled 250 kHz); bilayer formation monitored with a triangular wave protocol; no applied pressure — channel active in the absence of osmotically active solutes | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,284.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'284','pS','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified rice OsOSCA1.2 reconstituted into droplet interface bilayers (DIBs): OsOSCA1.2 proteoliposomes in E. coli polar-extract lipids on the agar-coated head-stage Ag electrode vs POPC/POPS/DOPA (1:1:0.5) liposomes on the reference electrode, droplets in hexadecane; protein/lipid 1:500 (wt/wt)','droplet interface bilayer (purified OsOSCA1.2 protein)',NULL,7.4,'reconstitution buffer 10 mM HEPES, 150 mM KCl, pH 7.4 (cis droplet; symmetrical condition 150:150 mM KCl)','reconstitution buffer 10 mM HEPES, 150 mM KCl, pH 7.4 (trans droplet; asymmetrical condition 15:150 mM KCl)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00076','In symmetrical ionic conditions, the current-to-voltage relation for OsOSCA1.2 was quite linear, yielding a unitary conductance of 284 ± 2 pS and showing no signs of current rectification.','Results (Functional Reconstitution of OsOSCA1.2; SI Appendix, Fig. S1 C–E)','high','CROSS-KINGDOM RULING: rice OsOSCA1.2 = osca-family row. pS actual conductance (ruling 4) from the linear current-to-voltage relation in symmetrical 150:150 mM KCl, recorded with no applied pressure (force-from-lipids-free DIB baseline activity). MAITY ARCHIVE (not rowed): ''between 300 and 350 pS'' is a CITED range of other reconstituted OSCA proteins (Murthy 2018) — prior work, never rowed. E_K+ -54 mV is the activity-corrected Nernst reference used for the ratio derivation, not a channel measurement. The infrequent 50% subconductance state has no value. tsA201 Fura-2 (168/627 mosmol/kg) and Xenopus oocyte TEVC osmotic assays were NEGATIVE (no OsOSCA1.2-dependent currents/Ca2+ changes) -> threshold flag stays N (and osmotic gradients never row regardless, round N-standard). DIB has no dedicated recording_mode enum — RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME used as the closest member with the preparation declared here. Error convention for ± 2 / ± 1 not stated -> error_type blank.','OsOSCA1.2_DIB-reconstituted_symmetrical-150:150mM-KCl_unitary-conductance_SuppFigS1C-E',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',138,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(384,'MAIC:BX:00384',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'voltage-clamp detection of unitary channel fluctuations across the DIB (Dagan 3900A amplifier + pCLAMP 10; filtered 1 kHz, sampled 250 kHz); bilayer formation monitored with a triangular wave protocol; no applied pressure — channel active in the absence of osmotically active solutes','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-26.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-26','mV','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified rice OsOSCA1.2 reconstituted into droplet interface bilayers (DIBs): OsOSCA1.2 proteoliposomes in E. coli polar-extract lipids on the agar-coated head-stage Ag electrode vs POPC/POPS/DOPA (1:1:0.5) liposomes on the reference electrode, droplets in hexadecane; protein/lipid 1:500 (wt/wt)','droplet interface bilayer (purified OsOSCA1.2 protein)',NULL,7.4,'reconstitution buffer 10 mM HEPES, 150 mM KCl, pH 7.4 (cis droplet; symmetrical condition 150:150 mM KCl)','reconstitution buffer 10 mM HEPES, 150 mM KCl, pH 7.4 (trans droplet; asymmetrical condition 15:150 mM KCl)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00077','Under nonsymmetrical ionic conditions ( cis / trans 15:150 mM KCl), with an inwardly directed K + gradient, the inward single-channel currents reversed (E rev ) at about -26 mV, closer to the Nernst potential for K + (E K + : -54 mV after correction for ionic activities), indicating a modest selectivity for K + over Cl - as suggested by the calculated P K + /P Cl - = 5 ± 1 ( SI Appendix , Fig. S1 I ).','Results (Functional Reconstitution of OsOSCA1.2; SI Appendix, Fig. S1I)','high','value_relation ''~'': the source prints ''at about -26 mV'' (no error term). Absolute E_rev under the cis/trans 15:150 mM KCl gradient; basis of the rowed P_K+/P_Cl- ratio. MAITY ARCHIVE (not rowed): ''between 300 and 350 pS'' is a CITED range of other reconstituted OSCA proteins (Murthy 2018) — prior work, never rowed. E_K+ -54 mV is the activity-corrected Nernst reference used for the ratio derivation, not a channel measurement. The infrequent 50% subconductance state has no value. tsA201 Fura-2 (168/627 mosmol/kg) and Xenopus oocyte TEVC osmotic assays were NEGATIVE (no OsOSCA1.2-dependent currents/Ca2+ changes) -> threshold flag stays N (and osmotic gradients never row regardless, round N-standard). DIB has no dedicated recording_mode enum — RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME used as the closest member with the preparation declared here. Error convention for ± 2 / ± 1 not stated -> error_type blank.','OsOSCA1.2_DIB-reconstituted_asymmetrical-15:150mM-KCl_Erev_SuppFigS1I',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',138,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(385,'MAIC:BX:00385',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'voltage-clamp detection of unitary channel fluctuations across the DIB (Dagan 3900A amplifier + pCLAMP 10; filtered 1 kHz, sampled 250 kHz); bilayer formation monitored with a triangular wave protocol; no applied pressure — channel active in the absence of osmotically active solutes',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'5',NULL,'OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME','purified rice OsOSCA1.2 reconstituted into droplet interface bilayers (DIBs): OsOSCA1.2 proteoliposomes in E. coli polar-extract lipids on the agar-coated head-stage Ag electrode vs POPC/POPS/DOPA (1:1:0.5) liposomes on the reference electrode, droplets in hexadecane; protein/lipid 1:500 (wt/wt)','droplet interface bilayer (purified OsOSCA1.2 protein)',NULL,7.4,'reconstitution buffer 10 mM HEPES, 150 mM KCl, pH 7.4 (cis droplet; symmetrical condition 150:150 mM KCl)','reconstitution buffer 10 mM HEPES, 150 mM KCl, pH 7.4 (trans droplet; asymmetrical condition 15:150 mM KCl)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00078','Under nonsymmetrical ionic conditions ( cis / trans 15:150 mM KCl), with an inwardly directed K + gradient, the inward single-channel currents reversed (E rev ) at about -26 mV, closer to the Nernst potential for K + (E K + : -54 mV after correction for ionic activities), indicating a modest selectivity for K + over Cl - as suggested by the calculated P K + /P Cl - = 5 ± 1 ( SI Appendix , Fig. S1 I ).','Results (Functional Reconstitution of OsOSCA1.2; SI Appendix, Fig. S1I)','high','SCHEMA GAP: no DB home for this parameter class (see data/extraction_schema.md schema-gap register). ion_selectivity_ratio has no DB column (reversal_potential_mv is only a partial proxy). Calculated from E_rev (~-26 mV) against the activity-corrected K+ Nernst potential (-54 mV) under the 10-fold KCl gradient; dimensionless as-reported; ''a modest selectivity for K+ over Cl-''. MAITY ARCHIVE (not rowed): ''between 300 and 350 pS'' is a CITED range of other reconstituted OSCA proteins (Murthy 2018) — prior work, never rowed. E_K+ -54 mV is the activity-corrected Nernst reference used for the ratio derivation, not a channel measurement. The infrequent 50% subconductance state has no value. tsA201 Fura-2 (168/627 mosmol/kg) and Xenopus oocyte TEVC osmotic assays were NEGATIVE (no OsOSCA1.2-dependent currents/Ca2+ changes) -> threshold flag stays N (and osmotic gradients never row regardless, round N-standard). DIB has no dedicated recording_mode enum — RECONSTITUTED_PROTEOLIPOSOME used as the closest member with the preparation declared here. Error convention for ± 2 / ± 1 not stated -> error_type blank.','OsOSCA1.2_DIB-reconstituted_asymmetrical-15:150mM-KCl_P-K-over-P-Cl_SuppFigS1I',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',138,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(386,'MAIC:BX:00386',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents in cell-attached patches (Axopatch 200B): 500-ms negative pressure pulses via a Clampex-controlled HSPC-1 (ALA Scientific) in steps of Δ-10 mmHg; filtered 2 kHz, sampled 20 kHz; single-channel currents at -80 mV; amplitude from Gaussian fits of trace histograms (5-10 repeats) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,25.6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'25.6','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK-P1KO (Piezo1-knockout HEK293T) cells transfected with OSCA1.2-EGFP (WT) or OSCA1.2(E531A)-EGFP (Lipofectamine 2000, 600 ng/mL; recorded 24-48 h after transfection)','HEK-P1KO (HEK293T Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,7.3,'140 KCl, 1 MgCl2, 10 glucose, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (KOH) (zero-membrane-potential external)','130 NaCl, 5 KCl, 1 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, 10 TEA-Cl, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (NaOH); 1-3 MOhm',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00079','( E ) Left, maximal current response from individual cells expressing OSCA1.2 (Imax: 487 ± 55 pA, N = 9) or OSCA1.2 (E531A) (Imax: 681 ± 161 pA, N = 9). Right, Inactivation time constant (ms) for individual cells across the two conditions. Bars represent population mean (OSCA1.2: 25.6 ± 2 ms (N = 6); OSCA1.2 (E531A): 17.4 ± 2 ms (N = 9). *p=0.01, Mann Whitney test).','Fig 3 legend, panel E (inactivation time constant; WT vs E531A)','high','figure-legend numerics printed verbatim (ruling 5 satisfied). E531 is the only pore-facing acidic residue conserved in this region across OSCA/TMEM63 — the mutant shows ''modestly faster inactivation kinetics'' (Results). ms as-reported. JOJOA-CRUZ-2018 ARCHIVE (not rowed): Imax values (WT 487 ± 55 pA N=9; E531A 681 ± 161 pA N=9) are CURRENTS (no home, in the tau quote). The main text''s ''decreased the stretch-activated single-channel conductance by 1.6-fold'' is a fold statement (132/82) — the ABSOLUTE values are the rowed ones. MD-simulation conductance predictions absent. threshold/tau_act/ion flags = N by the verify layer (no P50, no activation constant, no E_rev printed). Error convention (SEM vs SD) not stated for the Fig 3E/G values -> error_type blank. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','AtOSCA1.2-WT_HEK-P1KO_cell-attached_HSPC_500ms-pulses_current-inactivation_Fig3E','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',139,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(387,'MAIC:BX:00387',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents in cell-attached patches (Axopatch 200B): 500-ms negative pressure pulses via a Clampex-controlled HSPC-1 (ALA Scientific) in steps of Δ-10 mmHg; filtered 2 kHz, sampled 20 kHz; single-channel currents at -80 mV; amplitude from Gaussian fits of trace histograms (5-10 repeats) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 5','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,132.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'132','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK-P1KO (Piezo1-knockout HEK293T) cells transfected with OSCA1.2-EGFP (WT) or OSCA1.2(E531A)-EGFP (Lipofectamine 2000, 600 ng/mL; recorded 24-48 h after transfection)','HEK-P1KO (HEK293T Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,7.3,'140 KCl, 1 MgCl2, 10 glucose, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (KOH) (zero-membrane-potential external)','130 NaCl, 5 KCl, 1 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, 10 TEA-Cl, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (NaOH); 1-3 MOhm',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00080','( G ) Left, average I-V response curve for stretch-activated single-channel currents from wildtype or mutant channels. Right, channel conductance from individual cells across the two conditions. Bars represent population mean (OSCA1.2: 132 ± 5 ms (N = 6); OSCA1.2 (E531A): 82 ± 1 ms (N = 8). ***p=0.0007, Mann Whitney test).','Fig 3 legend, panel G (channel conductance; WT vs E531A)','medium','CONFIDENCE=medium (extraction-review M-1): the stored unit (pS) is analyst-inferred from the printed ''ms'' glyph — the schema ladder reserves high for printed-unit rows; unit correction declared, never silent. UNIT GLYPH HAZARD (declared, ruling 3 pattern): the Fig 3G legend prints ''132 ± 5 ms'' / ''82 ± 1 ms'' — ''ms'' is dimensionally impossible for the panel''s own quantity (''channel conductance'' from the average I-V response curve; methods define ''Single-channel slope conductance ... calculated from linear regression curve fit