INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(390,'MAIC:BX:00390',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents (SAC) in cell-attached patches; negative pressure via HSPC per Murthy et al. 2018; electrode resistances matched (WT 2.3±0.1 / 2.4±0.1 / 2.1±0.2 MOhm across cohorts); threshold reported in mmHg (Fig 2c/4c bottom panels); Multi-clamp 700A amplifier | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 5 (sem)','P50',-48.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-48','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK-P1KO (Piezo1-knockout HEK293T) cells transiently transfected with OSCA1.2 pIRES2-mCherry (WT) or the indicated mutant (recorded per the Murthy 2018 protocol)','HEK-P1KO (HEK293T Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,NULL,'(high-K+ zeroing external per the Murthy 2018 protocol; Fig 4c data collected within 15 min of high-K+ exposure)','(standard pipette solution per the Murthy 2018 protocol)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00083','Despite differences in the amplitude of macroscopic currents, which could be explained by variation in expression levels, all mutant channels were activated at similar thresholds (WT: -48±5 mmHg (N=25); W75K: -56±11 mmHg (N=3), L80E: -41±6 mmHg (N=5), W75K/L80E: -53±8 mmHg (N=11)) ( Figure 2c , bottom panel).','Results (stretch, amphipathic-helix cohort; Figure 2c, bottom panel)','high','SEMANTICS (ruling 2): the paper''s ''mmHg threshold'' is the negative-pressure threshold for SAC activation in cell-attached patches, mapped to the p50 slot per the round''s pressure-clamp ruling; the separately analysed Boltzmann P50 (Fig 4d) prints no numerics in text. error_type=sem per the legend''s ''mean ± S.E.M.'' convention. wild-type AtOSCA1.2 stretch threshold, main cohort (electrodes 2.3±0.1 MOhm). JOJOA-CRUZ-2024 ARCHIVE (not rowed): OSCA3.1 poke data = PARALOG subclade (never row) — its 13.8±0.9 µm endpoint is context-only; the OSCA1.2WT 10.4±1.2 µm printed in the same sentence duplicates the Fig 2—fig supp 4a ''displacements up to'' protocol endpoint of that small cohort (ambiguous threshold-vs-max semantics) -> not rowed; the rowed WT poke threshold is the Fig 2b cohort (5.3±0.5 µm, N=46). OSCA1.2-OSCA3.1-BLD chimera and OSCA1.2-P77R: no numerics printed in text/legends (panels only). Maximum-displacement protocol endpoints (8.9±0.6 / 12.8±0.7 / 12.4±0.7 / 12.8±0.5 / 9.8±0.8 / 11.8±0.6 / 9.7±1 / 12.1±0.6 / 7.2±1.4 / 6.5±0.6 µm) are stimulus protocol descriptors, not thresholds. Responder fractions (47/51, 3/24, 2/16, 2/24, 1/20, 25/26 ...) and electrode resistances (MOhm) archived. K435I/K536I poke current -365 pA (N=1) is a single-cell current. delta_p50 Y-flag: the poke shift is stated only qualitatively (''a larger displacement ... appeared to be needed''; OSCA3.1-vs-1.2 ''not statistically significant'') -> endpoint rows only, arithmetic deltas forbidden. tau_inact ''unclear'' flag: inactivation time constants exist as FIGURE PANELS ONLY with no numeric in text (''variability ... from moderately fast to extremely slow (data not shown)'') -> no row. En-dash-as-minus glyphs flattened to ''-'' (declared in scraped_via). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','AtOSCA1.2_HEK-P1KO_cell-attached_HSPC_stretch-mmHg-threshold_Fig2c','25','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',140,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
