INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(393,'MAIC:BX:00393',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents (SAC) in cell-attached patches; negative pressure via HSPC per Murthy et al. 2018; electrode resistances matched (WT 2.3±0.1 / 2.4±0.1 / 2.1±0.2 MOhm across cohorts); threshold reported in mmHg (Fig 2c/4c bottom panels); Multi-clamp 700A amplifier | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 8 (sem)','P50',-53.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-53','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK-P1KO (Piezo1-knockout HEK293T) cells transiently transfected with OSCA1.2 pIRES2-mCherry (WT) or the indicated mutant (recorded per the Murthy 2018 protocol)','HEK-P1KO (HEK293T Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,NULL,'(high-K+ zeroing external per the Murthy 2018 protocol; Fig 4c data collected within 15 min of high-K+ exposure)','(standard pipette solution per the Murthy 2018 protocol)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00086','Despite differences in the amplitude of macroscopic currents, which could be explained by variation in expression levels, all mutant channels were activated at similar thresholds (WT: -48±5 mmHg (N=25); W75K: -56±11 mmHg (N=3), L80E: -41±6 mmHg (N=5), W75K/L80E: -53±8 mmHg (N=11)) ( Figure 2c , bottom panel).','Results (stretch, amphipathic-helix cohort; Figure 2c, bottom panel)','high','SEMANTICS (ruling 2): the paper''s ''mmHg threshold'' is the negative-pressure threshold for SAC activation in cell-attached patches, mapped to the p50 slot per the round''s pressure-clamp ruling; the separately analysed Boltzmann P50 (Fig 4d) prints no numerics in text. error_type=sem per the legend''s ''mean ± S.E.M.'' convention. double AH mutant; no single HGVS (two-residue construct) — construct in the key; stretch threshold unchanged while poke is largely abrogated (the paper''s key stimulus-modality dissociation). JOJOA-CRUZ-2024 ARCHIVE (not rowed): OSCA3.1 poke data = PARALOG subclade (never row) — its 13.8±0.9 µm endpoint is context-only; the OSCA1.2WT 10.4±1.2 µm printed in the same sentence duplicates the Fig 2—fig supp 4a ''displacements up to'' protocol endpoint of that small cohort (ambiguous threshold-vs-max semantics) -> not rowed; the rowed WT poke threshold is the Fig 2b cohort (5.3±0.5 µm, N=46). OSCA1.2-OSCA3.1-BLD chimera and OSCA1.2-P77R: no numerics printed in text/legends (panels only). Maximum-displacement protocol endpoints (8.9±0.6 / 12.8±0.7 / 12.4±0.7 / 12.8±0.5 / 9.8±0.8 / 11.8±0.6 / 9.7±1 / 12.1±0.6 / 7.2±1.4 / 6.5±0.6 µm) are stimulus protocol descriptors, not thresholds. Responder fractions (47/51, 3/24, 2/16, 2/24, 1/20, 25/26 ...) and electrode resistances (MOhm) archived. K435I/K536I poke current -365 pA (N=1) is a single-cell current. delta_p50 Y-flag: the poke shift is stated only qualitatively (''a larger displacement ... appeared to be needed''; OSCA3.1-vs-1.2 ''not statistically significant'') -> endpoint rows only, arithmetic deltas forbidden. tau_inact ''unclear'' flag: inactivation time constants exist as FIGURE PANELS ONLY with no numeric in text (''variability ... from moderately fast to extremely slow (data not shown)'') -> no row. En-dash-as-minus glyphs flattened to ''-'' (declared in scraped_via). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','AtOSCA1.2-W75K/L80E_HEK-P1KO_cell-attached_HSPC_stretch-mmHg-threshold_Fig2c','11','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',140,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(394,'MAIC:BX:00394',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents (SAC) in cell-attached patches; negative pressure via HSPC per Murthy et al. 2018; electrode resistances matched (WT 2.3±0.1 / 2.4±0.1 / 2.1±0.2 MOhm across cohorts); threshold reported in mmHg (Fig 2c/4c bottom panels); Multi-clamp 700A amplifier | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 10 (sem)','P50',-43.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-43','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK-P1KO (Piezo1-knockout HEK293T) cells transiently transfected with OSCA1.2 pIRES2-mCherry (WT) or the indicated mutant (recorded per the Murthy 2018 protocol)','HEK-P1KO (HEK293T Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,NULL,'(high-K+ zeroing external per the Murthy 2018 protocol; Fig 4c data collected within 15 min of high-K+ exposure)','(standard pipette solution per the Murthy 2018 protocol)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00087','Furthermore, the mutant could be activated by stretch at similar thresholds to WT (WT: -43±10 mmHg (N=6); K435I/K536I: -60±10 mmHg (N=7); Figure 4c , bottom panel), and similar stretch-response dependence (i.e. similar pressures required to elicit half-maximal currents (P 50 ) and slope; Figure 4d ).','Results (stretch, lipid-interacting-residue cohort; Figure 4c, bottom panel)','high','SEMANTICS (ruling 2): the paper''s ''mmHg threshold'' is the negative-pressure threshold for SAC activation in cell-attached patches, mapped to the p50 slot per the round''s pressure-clamp ruling; the separately analysed Boltzmann P50 (Fig 4d) prints no numerics in text. error_type=sem per the legend''s ''mean ± S.E.M.'' convention. SECOND WT measurement, independent cohort/experiment (high-K+ condition, data collected within 15 min of exposure; electrodes 2.1±0.2 MOhm) — rowed separately from the Fig 2c WT (-48±5, N=25), never pooled. JOJOA-CRUZ-2024 ARCHIVE (not rowed): OSCA3.1 poke data = PARALOG subclade (never row) — its 13.8±0.9 µm endpoint is context-only; the OSCA1.2WT 10.4±1.2 µm printed in the same sentence duplicates the Fig 2—fig supp 4a ''displacements up to'' protocol endpoint of that small cohort (ambiguous threshold-vs-max semantics) -> not rowed; the rowed WT poke threshold is the Fig 2b cohort (5.3±0.5 µm, N=46). OSCA1.2-OSCA3.1-BLD chimera and OSCA1.2-P77R: no numerics printed in text/legends (panels only). Maximum-displacement protocol endpoints (8.9±0.6 / 12.8±0.7 / 12.4±0.7 / 12.8±0.5 / 9.8±0.8 / 11.8±0.6 / 9.7±1 / 12.1±0.6 / 7.2±1.4 / 6.5±0.6 µm) are stimulus protocol descriptors, not thresholds. Responder fractions (47/51, 3/24, 2/16, 2/24, 1/20, 25/26 ...) and electrode resistances (MOhm) archived. K435I/K536I poke current -365 pA (N=1) is a single-cell current. delta_p50 Y-flag: the poke shift is stated only qualitatively (''a larger displacement ... appeared to be needed''; OSCA3.1-vs-1.2 ''not statistically significant'') -> endpoint rows only, arithmetic deltas forbidden. tau_inact ''unclear'' flag: inactivation time constants exist as FIGURE PANELS ONLY with no numeric in text (''variability ... from moderately fast to extremely slow (data not shown)'') -> no row. En-dash-as-minus glyphs flattened to ''-'' (declared in scraped_via). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','AtOSCA1.2_HEK-P1KO_cell-attached_HSPC_stretch-mmHg-threshold_Fig4c_high-K-bath','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',140,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(395,'MAIC:BX:00395',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stretch-activated currents (SAC) in cell-attached patches; negative pressure via HSPC per Murthy et al. 2018; electrode resistances matched (WT 2.3±0.1 / 2.4±0.1 / 2.1±0.2 MOhm across cohorts); threshold reported in mmHg (Fig 2c/4c bottom panels); Multi-clamp 700A amplifier | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 10 (sem)','P50',-60.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-60','mmHg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK-P1KO (Piezo1-knockout HEK293T) cells transiently transfected with OSCA1.2 pIRES2-mCherry (WT) or the indicated mutant (recorded per the Murthy 2018 protocol)','HEK-P1KO (HEK293T Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,NULL,'(high-K+ zeroing external per the Murthy 2018 protocol; Fig 4c data collected within 15 min of high-K+ exposure)','(standard pipette solution per the Murthy 2018 protocol)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00088','Furthermore, the mutant could be activated by stretch at similar thresholds to WT (WT: -43±10 mmHg (N=6); K435I/K536I: -60±10 mmHg (N=7); Figure 4c , bottom panel), and similar stretch-response dependence (i.e. similar pressures required to elicit half-maximal currents (P 50 ) and slope; Figure 4d ).','Results (stretch, lipid-interacting-residue cohort; Figure 4c, bottom panel)','high','SEMANTICS (ruling 2): the paper''s ''mmHg threshold'' is the negative-pressure threshold for SAC activation in cell-attached patches, mapped to the p50 slot per the round''s pressure-clamp ruling; the separately analysed Boltzmann P50 (Fig 4d) prints no numerics in text. error_type=sem per the legend''s ''mean ± S.E.M.'' convention. TM4/TM6b pore-fenestration lysine double mutant (OSCA3.1-like residues); no single HGVS (two-residue construct). The Boltzmann P50 analysis of Fig 4d prints no numerics in text. JOJOA-CRUZ-2024 ARCHIVE (not rowed): OSCA3.1 poke data = PARALOG subclade (never row) — its 13.8±0.9 µm endpoint is context-only; the OSCA1.2WT 10.4±1.2 µm printed in the same sentence duplicates the Fig 2—fig supp 4a ''displacements up to'' protocol endpoint of that small cohort (ambiguous threshold-vs-max semantics) -> not rowed; the rowed WT poke threshold is the Fig 2b cohort (5.3±0.5 µm, N=46). OSCA1.2-OSCA3.1-BLD chimera and OSCA1.2-P77R: no numerics printed in text/legends (panels only). Maximum-displacement protocol endpoints (8.9±0.6 / 12.8±0.7 / 12.4±0.7 / 12.8±0.5 / 9.8±0.8 / 11.8±0.6 / 9.7±1 / 12.1±0.6 / 7.2±1.4 / 6.5±0.6 µm) are stimulus protocol descriptors, not thresholds. Responder fractions (47/51, 3/24, 2/16, 2/24, 1/20, 25/26 ...) and electrode resistances (MOhm) archived. K435I/K536I poke current -365 pA (N=1) is a single-cell current. delta_p50 Y-flag: the poke shift is stated only qualitatively (''a larger displacement ... appeared to be needed''; OSCA3.1-vs-1.2 ''not statistically significant'') -> endpoint rows only, arithmetic deltas forbidden. tau_inact ''unclear'' flag: inactivation time constants exist as FIGURE PANELS ONLY with no numeric in text (''variability ... from moderately fast to extremely slow (data not shown)'') -> no row. En-dash-as-minus glyphs flattened to ''-'' (declared in scraped_via). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','AtOSCA1.2-K435I/K536I_HEK-P1KO_cell-attached_HSPC_stretch-mmHg-threshold_Fig4c_high-K-bath','7','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',140,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(396,'MAIC:BX:00396',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'poke: membrane indentation with a blunt glass probe in whole-cell mode; ''apparent threshold'' = displacement in µm above touching the cell needed to observe currents; maximum displacements up to ~8.9-12.8 µm per cohort (protocol endpoints, archived) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.5 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5.3,'um',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'5.3','µm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','HEK-P1KO cells transiently transfected with OSCA1.2 pIRES2-mCherry (WT) or the indicated mutant (recorded per the Murthy 2018 protocol)','HEK-P1KO (HEK293T Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,NULL,'(per the Murthy 2018 protocol)','(per the Murthy 2018 protocol)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00089','Moreover, in OSCA1.2 W75K/L80E , a larger displacement of the membrane by the probe relative to the WT appeared to be needed to observe currents (‘apparent threshold’; WT: 5.3±0.5 µm (N=46; mean ± S.E.M.), W75K/L80E: 15.3±2.3 µm (N=2), with the none-responsive W75K/L80E cells rupturing at a 13.0±0.5 µm (N=22); Figure 2b , bottom panel).','Results (poke, amphipathic-helix cohort; Figure 2b, bottom panel)','high','SEMANTICS: the paper''s poke ''apparent threshold'' is the probe displacement (µm above touching) needed to first observe currents — mapped to the x50 slot per the round ruling (poke -> x50), same convention as the pilot''s Murthy poke rows. N = 2 for the double mutant (only 2 of 24 cells responded; non-responders ruptured at 13.0±0.5 µm, N=22 — archived bound context). delta_p50 flag: shift stated only qualitatively -> endpoint rows only. JOJOA-CRUZ-2024 ARCHIVE (not rowed): OSCA3.1 poke data = PARALOG subclade (never row) — its 13.8±0.9 µm endpoint is context-only; the OSCA1.2WT 10.4±1.2 µm printed in the same sentence duplicates the Fig 2—fig supp 4a ''displacements up to'' protocol endpoint of that small cohort (ambiguous threshold-vs-max semantics) -> not rowed; the rowed WT poke threshold is the Fig 2b cohort (5.3±0.5 µm, N=46). OSCA1.2-OSCA3.1-BLD chimera and OSCA1.2-P77R: no numerics printed in text/legends (panels only). Maximum-displacement protocol endpoints (8.9±0.6 / 12.8±0.7 / 12.4±0.7 / 12.8±0.5 / 9.8±0.8 / 11.8±0.6 / 9.7±1 / 12.1±0.6 / 7.2±1.4 / 6.5±0.6 µm) are stimulus protocol descriptors, not thresholds. Responder fractions (47/51, 3/24, 2/16, 2/24, 1/20, 25/26 ...) and electrode resistances (MOhm) archived. K435I/K536I poke current -365 pA (N=1) is a single-cell current. delta_p50 Y-flag: the poke shift is stated only qualitatively (''a larger displacement ... appeared to be needed''; OSCA3.1-vs-1.2 ''not statistically significant'') -> endpoint rows only, arithmetic deltas forbidden. tau_inact ''unclear'' flag: inactivation time constants exist as FIGURE PANELS ONLY with no numeric in text (''variability ... from moderately fast to extremely slow (data not shown)'') -> no row. En-dash-as-minus glyphs flattened to ''-'' (declared in scraped_via). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','AtOSCA1.2_HEK-P1KO_poke_blunt-probe_whole-cell_apparent-threshold_Fig2b','46','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',140,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(397,'MAIC:BX:00397',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'poke: membrane indentation with a blunt glass probe in whole-cell mode; ''apparent threshold'' = displacement in µm above touching the cell needed to observe currents; maximum displacements up to ~8.9-12.8 µm per cohort (protocol endpoints, archived) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2.3 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,15.3,'um',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15.3','µm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','HEK-P1KO cells transiently transfected with OSCA1.2 pIRES2-mCherry (WT) or the indicated mutant (recorded per the Murthy 2018 protocol)','HEK-P1KO (HEK293T Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,NULL,'(per the Murthy 2018 protocol)','(per the Murthy 2018 protocol)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00090','Moreover, in OSCA1.2 W75K/L80E , a larger displacement of the membrane by the probe relative to the WT appeared to be needed to observe currents (‘apparent threshold’; WT: 5.3±0.5 µm (N=46; mean ± S.E.M.), W75K/L80E: 15.3±2.3 µm (N=2), with the none-responsive W75K/L80E cells rupturing at a 13.0±0.5 µm (N=22); Figure 2b , bottom panel).','Results (poke, amphipathic-helix cohort; Figure 2b, bottom panel)','high','SEMANTICS: the paper''s poke ''apparent threshold'' is the probe displacement (µm above touching) needed to first observe currents — mapped to the x50 slot per the round ruling (poke -> x50), same convention as the pilot''s Murthy poke rows. N = 2 for the double mutant (only 2 of 24 cells responded; non-responders ruptured at 13.0±0.5 µm, N=22 — archived bound context). delta_p50 flag: shift stated only qualitatively -> endpoint rows only. JOJOA-CRUZ-2024 ARCHIVE (not rowed): OSCA3.1 poke data = PARALOG subclade (never row) — its 13.8±0.9 µm endpoint is context-only; the OSCA1.2WT 10.4±1.2 µm printed in the same sentence duplicates the Fig 2—fig supp 4a ''displacements up to'' protocol endpoint of that small cohort (ambiguous threshold-vs-max semantics) -> not rowed; the rowed WT poke threshold is the Fig 2b cohort (5.3±0.5 µm, N=46). OSCA1.2-OSCA3.1-BLD chimera and OSCA1.2-P77R: no numerics printed in text/legends (panels only). Maximum-displacement protocol endpoints (8.9±0.6 / 12.8±0.7 / 12.4±0.7 / 12.8±0.5 / 9.8±0.8 / 11.8±0.6 / 9.7±1 / 12.1±0.6 / 7.2±1.4 / 6.5±0.6 µm) are stimulus protocol descriptors, not thresholds. Responder fractions (47/51, 3/24, 2/16, 2/24, 1/20, 25/26 ...) and electrode resistances (MOhm) archived. K435I/K536I poke current -365 pA (N=1) is a single-cell current. delta_p50 Y-flag: the poke shift is stated only qualitatively (''a larger displacement ... appeared to be needed''; OSCA3.1-vs-1.2 ''not statistically significant'') -> endpoint rows only, arithmetic deltas forbidden. tau_inact ''unclear'' flag: inactivation time constants exist as FIGURE PANELS ONLY with no numeric in text (''variability ... from moderately fast to extremely slow (data not shown)'') -> no row. En-dash-as-minus glyphs flattened to ''-'' (declared in scraped_via). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','AtOSCA1.2-W75K/L80E_HEK-P1KO_poke_blunt-probe_whole-cell_apparent-threshold_Fig2b','2','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',140,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(398,'MAIC:BX:00398',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cell-attached recordings on S2 cells: 500-ms stepwise protocol with 10-mmHg pressure increments through the recording pipette via a high-speed pressure clamp (HSPC, ALA Scientific); Axopatch 700B, sampled 10 kHz, filtered 0.5 kHz; noise analysis of current fluctuations at -80 mV holding','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.93,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.93','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','Drosophila S2 cells expressing DmTMEM63-GFP (recorded at room temperature; borosilicate pipettes 3-4 MOhm)','Drosophila S2',NULL,7.4,'base solution 140 KCl, 1 MgCl2, 10 glucose, 10 HEPES, pH 7.4 (KOH)','standard pipette solution 133 NaCl, 5 KCl, 1 CaCl2, 1 MgCl2, 10 HEPES, pH 7.4 (NaOH)',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00091','c , Noise analysis of the fluctuations of the Dm TMEM63 currents. The variance of the current traces shown is plotted against the current amplitudes and fitted with σ 2 =i·I-I 2 /N. The obtained fitting parameters were i = -0.154 pA and N = 247 channels. So, the single-channel conductance is 1.93 pS at a holding potential of -80 mV.','Extended Data Fig. 3 legend, panel c (noise analysis; single-channel conductance)','high','DERIVATION DECLARED: non-stationary noise analysis (sigma^2 = i·I - I^2/N; i = -0.154 pA, N = 247 channels) -> 1.93 pS at -80 mV; methods: ''The single-channel conductance was estimated through the non-stationary noise analysis''. pS actual conductance (ruling 4 satisfied — this is a stated pS conductance, not a pA current; the pA unitary current is the fit parameter archived). Legend-text numerics printed verbatim (ruling 5). Cross-kingdom ruling: Drosophila TMEM63 = osca-family row. KAILI ARCHIVE (not rowed): threshold Y-flag -> Extended Data Fig 3b quantifies the P50 of DmTMEM63 (n = 7 cells, Boltzmann fits) but the legend prints NO numeric values (figure-level only; ''substantially higher than that of NompC'' in text — and NompC is out-of-family anyway) -> no row (ruling 5). The unitary i = -0.154 pA and N = 247 are the noise-analysis FIT PARAMETERS (current, not conductance) -> carried in the quote, no separate row. DmTMEM63 ion selectivity is qualitative (permeable to Na+/K+, not NMDG; I-V curves without E_rev/ratio values) -> no row. mTMEM63A (Ms TMEM63A) lysosomal MS currents in N2a cells: KO abolishes / overexpression enlarges — no numeric thresholds/conductances printed (dose-response curves figure-level with ''source data'' pointers only). Lysosome-attached DmTMEM63 recordings (-10 to -80 mmHg at -60 mV; WT n = 6 lysosomes vs Tmem63 mutants) carry no printed parameter values.','DmTMEM63_S2_cell-attached_HSPC_noise-analysis_-80mV_ExtDataFig3c',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',141,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(399,'MAIC:BX:00399',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,'inside-out patches held at constant -50 mmHg (syringe + manometer) and -60 mV, then stepped through a depolarizing voltage protocol (tau_on quantified at +160 mV); pipettes 2-4 MOhm, fire-polished; Axopatch 200B, sampled 10 kHz','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,41.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'41','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','TMEM16F-knockout HEK293T cells expressing eGFP-tagged Arabidopsis OSCA1.2 (WT) or the indicated TM4 lysine mutant (L438K / A439K); recorded at room temperature 18-48 h after transfection','TMEM16F KO HEK293T',NULL,7.3,'140 NaCl, 10 HEPES, 5 EGTA, pH 7.3 (NaOH) (internal face)','140 NaCl, 10 HEPES, 2 MgCl2, pH 7.3 (NaOH) (external face)',-60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OSCA-EX-00092','( g ) Quantification of activation τ on at -50 mmHg and 160 mV for WT (41 ms), L438K (13 ms), and A439K (16 ms) ( Figure 4—source data 1 ). Statistical comparison was conducted with unpaired t -tests with Welch’s correction (***p < 0.001, ****p < 0.0001).','Fig 4 legend, panel g (activation tau_on at -50 mmHg and 160 mV)','high','own-data figure-legend numerics printed verbatim (ruling 5 satisfied). tau_on measured under CONSTANT -50 mmHg suction with a depolarizing step to +160 mV (the paper''s constant-pressure/variable-voltage protocol) — condition declared; no error term printed for the tau_on values (legend prints bare means; SEM applies to the figure''s error bars). Cohort sizes for the same constructs'' inside-out patches (Fig 4e legend): WT n=8, L438K n=8, A439K n=6 — not attached to the tau_on panel -> n left blank. TMEM16-family data in the same paper stay out (not OSCA family). LOWRY ARCHIVE (not rowed): the paper''s own P50-style values quoted in the reviewer-response section (''P50 ~55 mmHg for 1.2 and ~61 mmHg for 63A in 10.7554/eLife.41844 versus ~86 mmHg for 1.2 and -123 mmHg for 63A in 10.1016/j.neuron.2023.07.006'') are LITERATURE CITATIONS -> never rowed (ruling 6). G-V half-maximal voltages (V0.5) have NO parameter_kind home (a voltage-activation midpoint at fixed pressure is not a reversal potential; block_voltage is a pore-blocker metric): OSCA1.2 WT 108.7±5.6 / L438K 66.7±3.7 mV (text) + WT 109 / L438K 67 / A439K 63 mV (Fig 4f legend); mTMEM63A WT 122.3±3.5 -> W472K 95.9±6.3 / S475K 92.1±8.6 / A476K 96.8±4.2 mV at -80 mmHg cell-attached (Fig 6d-f) — all archived with quotes. TMEM16F/TMEM16A data (the paper''s first half) = NON-OSCA superfamily member -> never rowed. Annexin-V PS-scramblase percentages are imaging metrics. Hypotonic 120 mOsm/kg scramblase activation = osmotic gradient without X50/EC50 -> never rowed (round N-standard).','AtOSCA1.2-WT_TMEM16F-KO-HEK293T_inside-out_-50mmHg_tau-on_+160mV_Fig4g',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',142,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
