ependent subconductance) rows of the same table. NON-TMC residual archive (double-KO reverse-polarity channel = an unidentified, tip-link-independent channel; NEVER rowed for tmc): X1 = -165 nm, X2 = -33 nm, I_max 0.66 nA; current-decline taus 2.9 ± 0.3 ms (n = 5) and 3.2 ± 0.1 ms (n = 4, BAPTA); E_rev +6.1 ± 0.5 mV (n = 4); P_Ca/P_Cs 1.9 ± 0.07 (apex) / 1.8 ± 0.04 (base) with Ca-reversal E_rev 10.9 ± 0.6 / 9.9 ± 0.5 mV; unitary 65 pS (5.5 ± 0.2 pA) plus fast flickering; DHS half-block 25 ± 6 µM; Ca2+ half-block K_I 1.2 ± 0.3 mM, Hill 1.1 ± 0.3; FM1-43 reduced current to 0.37 ± 0.09 (5 µM). The 25-pS small slow channel is seen in BOTH wild type and double knockouts (''subconductance state'', onset/decay ~30 ms) — TMC-INDEPENDENT, so the task-note ''conductance ~25 pS'' example is NOT rowed. WT/single-KO P_Ca/P_Cs 3.7-6.3 and E_rev 22-28 mV are companion-paper values (Kim and Fettiplace 2013, 10.1085/jgp.201210913) -> not rowed here. WT Ca2+ half-block K_I 0.9 ± 0.3 mM (Hill 1.0 ± 0.3, own-data control comparison) archived, not rowed. Fig 2 C heterozygote onset dashed fit 16 ms = single-example fit -> archived.','mTmc1_OHC_apex_P4_Tmc2-KO_BAPTA-single-channel_stiff-probe-0.2um_-84mV_Table1','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',145,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
