hive (double-KO reverse-polarity channel = an unidentified, tip-link-independent channel; NEVER rowed for tmc): X1 = -165 nm, X2 = -33 nm, I_max 0.66 nA; current-decline taus 2.9 ± 0.3 ms (n = 5) and 3.2 ± 0.1 ms (n = 4, BAPTA); E_rev +6.1 ± 0.5 mV (n = 4); P_Ca/P_Cs 1.9 ± 0.07 (apex) / 1.8 ± 0.04 (base) with Ca-reversal E_rev 10.9 ± 0.6 / 9.9 ± 0.5 mV; unitary 65 pS (5.5 ± 0.2 pA) plus fast flickering; DHS half-block 25 ± 6 µM; Ca2+ half-block K_I 1.2 ± 0.3 mM, Hill 1.1 ± 0.3; FM1-43 reduced current to 0.37 ± 0.09 (5 µM). The 25-pS small slow channel is seen in BOTH wild type and double knockouts (''subconductance state'', onset/decay ~30 ms) — TMC-INDEPENDENT, so the task-note ''conductance ~25 pS'' example is NOT rowed. WT/single-KO P_Ca/P_Cs 3.7-6.3 and E_rev 22-28 mV are companion-paper values (Kim and Fettiplace 2013, 10.1085/jgp.201210913) -> not rowed here. WT Ca2+ half-block K_I 0.9 ± 0.3 mM (Hill 1.0 ± 0.3, own-data control comparison) archived, not rowed. Fig 2 C heterozygote onset dashed fit 16 ms = single-example fit -> archived.','mTmc1_OHC_base_P2-P3_Tmc2-KO_BAPTA-single-channel_stiff-probe-0.2um_-84mV_Table1','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',145,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(602,'MAIC:BX:00602',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'fluid jet (10-15 µm tip driven by a 25-mm piezo disc) delivering 35-Hz sinusoids or 1-kHz-filtered steps to the hair bundle, bundle motion calibrated on a photodiode pair; single-channel steps via a piezoactuator-driven glass probe (~0.2 µm deflections)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'60','pS','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlea, isolated organ of Corti: outer hair cells P0-P10; Tmc1 dn/dn (exon-14 deletion) and Tmc2 tm1Lex (exon-1 deletion) mutants on CBA/J background; CD-1 / Tmc heterozygote controls','mouse cochlear outer hair cell (apical or basal turn)',NULL,7.4,'150 NaCl, 6 KCl, 1.5 CaCl2, 2 Na-pyruvate, 8 D-glucose, 10 Na-HEPES, pH 7.4 (~315 mOsm/l)','135 CsCl, 3 MgATP, 10 Tris phosphocreatine, 1 EGTA, 10 Cs-HEPES, pH 7.2 (~298 mOsm/l)',-84.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00010','Wild type Apex 5.2 ± 0.1 a , b 62 50 5, P4–P5 Tmc1+/- Apex 5.3 ± 0.1 63 41 4, P4 Tmc1-/- Apex 4.1 ± 0.1 a 49 93 6, P4–P5 Tmc2+/- Apex 5.5 ± 0.3 65 13 4, P4 Tmc2-/- Apex 5.2 ± 0.2 62 14 4, P4 Tmc1-/-Tmc2-/- Apex 5.5 ± 0.1 65 56 4, P5–P6 Tmc1-/-Tmc2-/- Apex 2.1 ± 0.03 c 25 8 3, P6 Wild type Base 8.5 ± 0.2 b , d 101 80 14, P3 Tmc2-/- Base 8.6 ± 0.2 102 37 5, P2–P3 Tmc2+/- Base 8.1 ± 0.2 96 14 4, P2–P3 Tmc1-/- Base 5.0 ± 0.1 d 60 26 5, P2–P3','Table 1 (row Tmc1−/− base; n cells 5, age P2-P3)','medium','Tmc1 knockout channel (TMC2-only): basal conductance most reduced — ''the predominant effect was at the base''. G_channel column carries no error term (Table 1 quotes ± SEM for the I_channel amplitudes only; G is the stated pS value). pS is the native TMC scale (no unit hazard). Native-preparation value whose TMC pore attribution is part of the round''s contested question -> confidence medium. Excluded rows: the double-KO 65 pS (non-TMC residual) and 25 pS (TMC-independent subconductance) rows of the same table. NON-TMC residual archive (double-KO reverse-polarity channel = an unidentified, tip-link-independent channel; NEVER rowed for tmc): X1 = -165 nm, X2 = -33 nm, I_max 0.66 nA; current-decline taus 2.9 ± 0.3 ms (n = 5) and 3.2 ± 0.1 ms (n = 4, BAPTA); E_rev +6.1 ± 0.5 mV (n = 4); P_Ca/P_Cs 1.9 ± 0.07 (apex) / 1.8 ± 0.04 (base) with Ca-reversal E_rev 10.9 ± 0.6 / 9.9 ± 0.5 mV; unitary 65 pS (5.5 ± 0.2 pA) plus fast flickering; DHS half-block 25 ± 6 µM; Ca2+ half-block K_I 1.2 ± 0.3 mM, Hill 1.1 ± 0.3; FM1-43 reduced current to 0.37 ± 0.09 (5 µM). The 25-pS small slow channel is seen in BOTH wild type and double knockouts (''subconductance state'', onset/decay ~30 ms) — TMC-INDEPENDENT, so the task-note ''conductance ~25 pS'' example is NOT rowed. WT/single-KO P_Ca/P_Cs 3.7-6.3 and E_rev 22-28 mV are companion-paper values (Kim and Fettiplace 2013, 10.1085/jgp.201210913) -> not rowed here. WT Ca2+ half-block K_I 0.9 ± 0.3 mM (Hill 1.0 ± 0.3, own-data control comparison) archived, not rowed. Fig 2 C heterozygote onset dashed fit 16 ms = single-example fit -> archived.','mTmc2_OHC_base_P2-P3_Tmc1-KO_BAPTA-single-channel_stiff-probe-0.2um_-84mV_Table1','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',145,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(603,'MAIC:BX:00603',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'fluid jet (10-15 µm tip driven by a 25-mm piezo disc) delivering 35-Hz sinusoids or 1-kHz-filtered steps to the hair bundle, bundle motion calibrated on a photodiode pair; single-channel steps via a piezoactuator-driven glass probe (~0.2 µm deflections) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 1.1','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,4.7,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'4.7','mV','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlea, isolated organ of Corti: outer hair cells P0-P10; Tmc1 dn/dn (exon-14 deletion) and Tmc2 tm1Lex (exon-1 deletion) mutants on CBA/J background; CD-1 / Tmc heterozygote controls','mouse cochlear outer hair cell (apical or basal turn)',NULL,7.4,'150 NaCl, 6 KCl, 1.5 CaCl2, 2 Na-pyruvate, 8 D-glucose, 10 Na-HEPES, pH 7.4 (~315 mOsm/l)','135 CsCl, 3 MgATP, 10 Tris phosphocreatine, 1 EGTA, 10 Cs-HEPES, pH 7.2 (~298 mOsm/l)',-84.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00011','We next examined the ionic permeability of the channels. The current–voltage relationship in extracellular saline containing 1.5 mM Ca 2+ was approximately linear (not depicted) and reversed at +6.1 ± 0.5 mV ( n = 4). This value is not significantly different (P = 0.33) from the reversal potential measured under the same conditions in wild type (mean = 4.7 ± 1.1 mV; n = 5).','Results (ionic permeability section; WT control comparison, n = 5)','medium','own-data WT control value (''the reversal potential measured under the same conditions in wild type (mean = 4.7 ± 1.1 mV; n = 5)'') quoted as the comparison for the non-TMC residual channel''s +6.1 ± 0.5 mV (residual value NOT rowed). Error type not stated for this sentence (paper''s Table 1 convention is mean ± SEM). Absolute E_rev, not a shift. Native MET channel (TMC1+TMC2) -> confidence medium (attribution contested). NON-TMC residual archive (double-KO reverse-polarity channel = an unidentified, tip-link-independent channel; NEVER rowed for tmc): X1 = -165 nm, X2 = -33 nm, I_max 0.66 nA; current-decline taus 2.9 ± 0.3 ms (n = 5) and 3.2 ± 0.1 ms (n = 4, BAPTA); E_rev +6.1 ± 0.5 mV (n = 4); P_Ca/P_Cs 1.9 ± 0.07 (apex) / 1.8 ± 0.04 (base) with Ca-reversal E_rev 10.9 ± 0.6 / 9.9 ± 0.5 mV; unitary 65 pS (5.5 ± 0.2 pA) plus fast flickering; DHS half-block 25 ± 6 µM; Ca2+ half-block K_I 1.2 ± 0.3 mM, Hill 1.1 ± 0.3; FM1-43 reduced current to 0.37 ± 0.09 (5 µM). The 25-pS small slow channel is seen in BOTH wild type and double knockouts (''subconductance state'', onset/decay ~30 ms) — TMC-INDEPENDENT, so the task-note ''conductance ~25 pS'' example is NOT rowed. WT/single-KO P_Ca/P_Cs 3.7-6.3 and E_rev 22-28 mV are companion-paper values (Kim and Fettiplace 2013, 10.1085/jgp.201210913) -> not rowed here. WT Ca2+ half-block K_I 0.9 ± 0.3 mM (Hill 1.0 ± 0.3, own-data control comparison) archived, not rowed. Fig 2 C heterozygote onset dashed fit 16 ms = single-example fit -> archived. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc1+mTmc2_OHC_WT_1.5mM-Ca-perilymph_Erev_I-V_control-comparison','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',145,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(604,'MAIC:BX:00604',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'hair bundles driven by a glass stylus on a piezoelectric stack actuator (rise ~100 µs; 30 nm/V calibration) or by a 40-Hz sinusoidal fluid jet; bundle motion monitored on a photodiode pair; experiments at 21-24°C | MODULATOR: GsMTx-4 (blocker)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,7.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'7','nm','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear hair cells: wild type, Tmc1dn/dn, Tmc1Δ/Δ (exon 8+10 lacZ replacement), Tmc2−/−, Tmc1dn/dn Tmc2−/− and Tmc1Δ/Δ/Tmc2−/− double mutants, Tmc1dn/dn Tmc3−/−; single channels isolated by BAPTA tip-link removal or by partial block with ~5-10 µM GsMTx-4','mouse cochlear outer / inner hair cell (apical or basal turn)',NULL,7.2,'standard extracellular saline (perilymph-like, 1.5 mM Ca2+ unless stated)','135 CsCl, 3 MgATP, 10 Tris phosphocreatine, 1 EGTA, 10 Cs-HEPES, pH 7.2',-84.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00014','In the experiment depicted, there was a reversible shift in X 0.5 of -25 nm compared with a total 10–90% working range of 72 nm for this cell. In other OHCs, there were small positive or negative shifts in X 0.5 in the presence of 1 or 3 µM toxin, ranging from -30 to 34 nm, but the net effect averaged over all of cells was minimal, with the mean shift (±SEM) being 7 ± 11 nm ( n = 7).','Results (GsMTx-4 effect on the I-X relationship; Fig 1 B)','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. mean ± SEM shift averaged over 7 cells — a NULL result (''the net effect averaged over all of cells was minimal''; per-cell shifts ranged -30 to +34 nm; the example cell showed a reversible -25 nm shift against a 72-nm 10-90% working range). Modulator concentration left blank: 1 or 3 µM mixed. DEMOTED to schema_gap: the displacement-midpoint shift is in nm but delta_p50_* is pressure-unit-only in the DB schema. NON-TMC residual archive (Tmc1dn/dn Tmc2−/− reversed-polarity channel; NEVER rowed): X0.5 = -183 nm, Xs = -19 nm, I_max 0.88 nA (Fig 3 C inset); conductances 61 ± 1 pS apex / 58 ± 1 pS base; inactivation ~3 ms (ensembles 2.5-3 ms, examples 2.7 / 2.5 ms); amiloride IC50 58 ± 4 µM (nH 2.3); DHS IC50 168 ± 21 µM (text; Fig 6 D legend 169 ± 21, nH 0.99); curare apparent IC50 1.7 ± 0.2 µM with ~40-43% current remaining at 100-300 µM and a 24-pS curare-substate. threshold Y-flag -> no x50 row (only the residual -183 nm and a single-cell control example X0.5 = 26 nm, Fig 1 B, exist). ion_selectivity Y-flag -> no row: Table 1 P_Ca/P_Cs (WT apex 6.1 ± 0.7 (7) / base 4.6 ± 0.5 (12); Tmc1dn/dn 5.9 ± 0.2 / 6.3 ± 0.2; Tmc2−/− 4.4 ± 0.1 / 3.9 ± 0.2; IHC 5.7 ± 0.4 / 6.6 ± 0.6 / 4.5 ± 0.2; double-mutant 1.9/1.8) is COMPILED (''Data are summarized from Kim and Fettiplace (2013) and Kim et al. (2013)''), as is the ''PCa/PCs ≈ 6 / ≈ 4.5 / ≈ 2'' grouping statement and the >P6 footnote (4.6 ± 0.1, 5.8 ± 0.4). tau_inact Y-flag -> no row: the WT ''fast adaptation, fit with a single time constant of 5 ms'' is a single-figure-example ensemble fit (Fig 2 A); the ~3 ms constants are residual-side. Also archived: Tmc1Δ/Δ single-channel CURRENTS (-4.3 ± 0.1 pA apex n = 13; -5.1 ± 0.1 pA base n = 7) — currents, not conductance; Tmc2−/− IHC current -5.3 ± 0.2 pA; GTP+cAMP-supplemented basal conductance 111 ± 1 pS (n = 6, +~10%, P = 0.0015, intracellular-solution condition); okadaic acid no effect; heterozygote (Tmc1+/dn Tmc2+/−) curare ratios 0.41 ± 0.04 (-84 mV) / 0.95 ± 0.02 (+76 mV); GsMTx4 pooled-fit IC50 0.65 ± 0.1 µM (nH 0.92-0.93, includes the double mutant); FM1-43 block; Tmc3−/− amplitudes 0.94 ± 0.04 nA (P5) / 0.48 ± 0.11 nA (P7).','mTmc1+mTmc2_OHC_WT_GsMTx4-1-3uM_mean-X0.5-shift-vs-control_Fig1B','7','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',146,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
