 of -4.8 ± 0.1 pA ( n = 12; P4–P5) and a conductance of 57 pS, which were not statistically different from the Tmc1dn/dn mutant (P = 0.40).','Results (IHC single channels; Fig 5; Tmc1dn/dn IHC apex)','medium','GENE-ATTRIBUTION NOTE: Tmc1dn/dn is a Tmc1 single mutant on a Tmc2+ background — the functional channel is carried by TMC2 (paper: ''TMC2 contributing little to channel conductance'' refers to the OHC Tmc1dn/dn vs double-mutant comparison), so the gene token is mTmc2 with the genotype in the key. DERIVATION DECLARED: the paper states the mean unitary current and the conductance it ''correspond[s] to'' at -84 mV (from -4.9 ± 0.1 pA) — the stated pS value is rowed. IHC conductance is location-invariant in WT (P = 0.20) in contrast to OHCs; the Tmc1 mutations reduce it ~11% (identical results with the dn deletion and the lacZ-null allele, P = 0.40). Tmc1dn/dn is an exon-14 deletion and Tmc1Δ/Δ an exon-8+10 lacZ replacement — structural alleles, so variant_hgvs_short is left blank (genotype in condition_key). The GsMTx4-method unitary current -5.6 ± 0.2 pA (n = 3) is archived. NON-TMC residual archive (Tmc1dn/dn Tmc2−/− reversed-polarity channel; NEVER rowed): X0.5 = -183 nm, Xs = -19 nm, I_max 0.88 nA (Fig 3 C inset); conductances 61 ± 1 pS apex / 58 ± 1 pS base; inactivation ~3 ms (ensembles 2.5-3 ms, examples 2.7 / 2.5 ms); amiloride IC50 58 ± 4 µM (nH 2.3); DHS IC50 168 ± 21 µM (text; Fig 6 D legend 169 ± 21, nH 0.99); curare apparent IC50 1.7 ± 0.2 µM with ~40-43% current remaining at 100-300 µM and a 24-pS curare-substate. threshold Y-flag -> no x50 row (only the residual -183 nm and a single-cell control example X0.5 = 26 nm, Fig 1 B, exist). ion_selectivity Y-flag -> no row: Table 1 P_Ca/P_Cs (WT apex 6.1 ± 0.7 (7) / base 4.6 ± 0.5 (12); Tmc1dn/dn 5.9 ± 0.2 / 6.3 ± 0.2; Tmc2−/− 4.4 ± 0.1 / 3.9 ± 0.2; IHC 5.7 ± 0.4 / 6.6 ± 0.6 / 4.5 ± 0.2; double-mutant 1.9/1.8) is COMPILED (''Data are summarized from Kim and Fettiplace (2013) and Kim et al. (2013)''), as is the ''PCa/PCs ≈ 6 / ≈ 4.5 / ≈ 2'' grouping statement and the >P6 footnote (4.6 ± 0.1, 5.8 ± 0.4). tau_inact Y-flag -> no row: the WT ''fast adaptation, fit with a single time constant of 5 ms'' is a single-figure-example ensemble fit (Fig 2 A); the ~3 ms constants are residual-side. Also archived: Tmc1Δ/Δ single-channel CURRENTS (-4.3 ± 0.1 pA apex n = 13; -5.1 ± 0.1 pA base n = 7) — currents, not conductance; Tmc2−/− IHC current -5.3 ± 0.2 pA; GTP+cAMP-supplemented basal conductance 111 ± 1 pS (n = 6, +~10%, P = 0.0015, intracellular-solution condition); okadaic acid no effect; heterozygote (Tmc1+/dn Tmc2+/−) curare ratios 0.41 ± 0.04 (-84 mV) / 0.95 ± 0.02 (+76 mV); GsMTx4 pooled-fit IC50 0.65 ± 0.1 µM (nH 0.92-0.93, includes the double mutant); FM1-43 block; Tmc3−/− amplitudes 0.94 ± 0.04 nA (P5) / 0.48 ± 0.11 nA (P7). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc2_IHC_apex_P4-P5_Tmc1dn/dn_Tmc2-carried_BAPTA-or-GsMTx4-isolation_-84mV_single-channel_Fig5','14','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',146,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
