ss page (cache extended with the full STAR Methods this batch); single-channel open-probability-vs-pressure figure data.','hTMC2_HEK293T-Piezo1KO_shUROD_linear-I-V_-60-to-+60mV_8um-stimuli_Fig6A-B-E',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',147,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(622,'MAIC:BX:00622',8,NULL,NULL,101,'fire-polished ~2-µm-tip glass stimulation pipette driven by a piezo controller poking the cell surface, 1-8 µm steps, 300-ms duration, 10-s intervals; I-V by -60 to +60 mV ramps/steps with 8-µm stimuli | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.95 (sem)','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-9.9,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-9.9','mV','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','Piezo1-KO HEK293T cells transiently co-transfected with HA-tagged wild-type full-length human TMC1 or TMC2 plus shUROD (UROD knockdown enables plasma-membrane trafficking); room temperature','HEK293T (Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,7.3,'133 NaCl, 2.5 CaCl2, 3 KCl, 1 MgCl2, 10 D-glucose, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (NaOH), 300-310 mOsm','133 CsCl, 1 MgCl2, 1 CaCl2, 5 EGTA, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (CsOH), 300-310 mOsm',-60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00035','the reversal potentials of human TMC1-T422K and human TMC1-D572N with shUROD in Piezo1-KO HEK293T cells shifted leftward to -9.90 ± 0.95 and -15.45 ± 1.11 mV, respectively (Figures 6C, 6D, 6F, and 6G)','Results (deafness-mutant E_rev; Fig 6, C, D, F and G)','high','heterologous isolated-channel system (Piezo1-KO HEK293T expressing only TMC1/2; no native MET complex ambiguity) -> confidence high per the round ruling. SHIFT-LABEL WARNING (Çetiner precedent): the stated number is the mutant channel''s ABSOLUTE E_rev; its interpretation is a leftward SHIFT relative to the WT hTMC1 row (-0.20 ± 0.56 mV) — the shift magnitude is not stated as a number and no delta row is created. Mutation: the T422K human deafness mutation (mouse Tmc1 p.T416K equivalent); also ''significantly decreased the permeability of the channel to sodium ions''. Archived (not rowed): current densities -17.78 ± 5.73 / -14.65 ± 3.93 pA/pF and amplitudes -215.2 ± 66.28 / -237.1 ± 54.29 pA (current magnitudes, not conductance); responding-cell ratios 65.22% / 80.77%; blocker sensitivity (GdCl3 10 µM, DHS 200 µM, FM1-43 300 µM, GsMTx-4 5 µM) qualitative -> no pharmacology rows; Na+-dependence (NMDG-Cl vs Na-gluconate) qualitative; mouse mutant MmTMC1-H353A / MmTMC2-H406A E_revs 0.99 ± 0.48 / 0.33 ± 1.13 mV -- ROWED as two scale-v1 rework rows (review M2) with the quote re-verified from the Cell Press page (cache extended with the full STAR Methods this batch); single-channel open-probability-vs-pressure figure data.','hTMC1_HEK293T-Piezo1KO_shUROD_T422K_linear-I-V_8um-stimuli_Fig6C-D-F-G',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',147,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(623,'MAIC:BX:00623',8,NULL,NULL,102,'fire-polished ~2-µm-tip glass stimulation pipette driven by a piezo controller poking the cell surface, 1-8 µm steps, 300-ms duration, 10-s intervals; I-V by -60 to +60 mV ramps/steps with 8-µm stimuli | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 1.11 (sem)','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-15.45,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-15.45','mV','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','Piezo1-KO HEK293T cells transiently co-transfected with HA-tagged wild-type full-length human TMC1 or TMC2 plus shUROD (UROD knockdown enables plasma-membrane trafficking); room temperature','HEK293T (Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,7.3,'133 NaCl, 2.5 CaCl2, 3 KCl, 1 MgCl2, 10 D-glucose, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (NaOH), 300-310 mOsm','133 CsCl, 1 MgCl2, 1 CaCl2, 5 EGTA, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (CsOH), 300-310 mOsm',-60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00036','the reversal potentials of human TMC1-T422K and human TMC1-D572N with shUROD in Piezo1-KO HEK293T cells shifted leftward to -9.90 ± 0.95 and -15.45 ± 1.11 mV, respectively (Figures 6C, 6D, 6F, and 6G)','Results (deafness-mutant E_rev; Fig 6, C, D, F and G)','high','heterologous isolated-channel system (Piezo1-KO HEK293T expressing only TMC1/2; no native MET complex ambiguity) -> confidence high per the round ruling. SHIFT-LABEL WARNING (Çetiner precedent): the stated number is the mutant channel''s ABSOLUTE E_rev; its interpretation is a leftward SHIFT relative to the WT hTMC1 row (-0.20 ± 0.56 mV) — the shift magnitude is not stated as a number and no delta row is created. Mutation: the Beethoven (Bth) D572N deafness mutation; also ''significantly decreased the permeability of the channel to sodium ions''. Archived (not rowed): current densities -17.78 ± 5.73 / -14.65 ± 3.93 pA/pF and amplitudes -215.2 ± 66.28 / -237.1 ± 54.29 pA (current magnitudes, not conductance); responding-cell ratios 65.22% / 80.77%; blocker 