INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(624,'MAIC:BX:00624',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stereociliary bundle vibration via a fluid jet (~10 µm tip) or a piezoactuator-driven glass probe; bundle motion monitored on a photodiode; extracellular 1.5 mM Ca2+ saline or endolymph-like 0.04 mM Ca2+','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,29.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'29','nm','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear apical OHCs (P5-P7); Tmc1 point-mutant lines p.T416K, p.D528N, p.W554L (plus prior-work M412K/D569N comparisons) ALL characterized on a Tmc2−/− background -> TMC1-only MET channel; single channels isolated by submicromolar-Ca2+ BAPTA tip-link removal','mouse cochlear outer hair cell (apex)',NULL,7.4,'standard extracellular saline, 1.5 mM Ca2+ (0.04 mM Ca2+ endolymph-like condition as noted); 100 mM CaCl2 + N-methylglucamine/Tris isotonic-Ca2+ saline for Ca-reversal measurements','142 mM CsCl-based intracellular solution (+ MgATP, phosphocreatine, EGTA, HEPES)',-84.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00037','Dashed curves are fits of current I against displacement x to Boltzmann equation: I = I MAX /[1 + exp((x1 – x)/a)], where I MAX = 1.0 nA, a = 9.8 nm, x1 = 29 nm (1.5 Ca 2+ ) and I MAX = 1.43 nA, a = 21 nm, x1 = 6.9 nm (0.04 Ca 2+ ).','Fig 3 B legend (control I-X fits; 1.5 mM Ca2+ (normal saline))','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. representative-cell Boltzmann fit from the Fig 3 I-X panel (x1 = half-activation displacement; companion fit parameters I_MAX 1.0 / 1.43 nA, a = 9.8 / 21 nm). Lowering extracellular Ca2+ shifts x1 and increases I_MAX — the two Ca2+ conditions are the round''s Ca2+-induced shift endpoints (see delta_p50 note). Error-type note: the quoted text values carry no explicit SEM/SD label; figure panels report mean ± SD for bars — error_type left blank. Table 1 mirror values agree except D528N conductance (Table 1 prints 53.3 ± 2.9, text 53.5 ± 2.9 — text value rowed, discrepancy declared) and control P_Ca/P_Cs error (Table 1 4.25 ± 0.35 (N = 8) matches). PRIOR-WORK rows NOT rowed: M412K (86.2 ± 8.2 pS, P_Ca/P_Cs 1.50 ± 0.12; effects previously shown in Beurg et al., 2015a and Corns et al., 2016) and D569N (87.5 ± 4.5 pS, 1.25 ± 0.11, N_MET 46 ± 18; Beurg et al., 2019). Archived non-rows: macroscopic currents (1.18 ± 0.16 nA control etc.) and N_MET channel counts (166 ± 23 / 123 ± 12 / 157 ± 14 / 54-58 ± 13); resting open probabilities P_OR (0.44 ± 0.06 control; 0.22 ± 0.06 T416K; 0.39 ± 0.01 D528N) and low-Ca2+ current ratios (1.54 ± 0.1 etc.) — population fractions, no parameter_kind home; unitary currents (-7.0 pA examples; 7.1 / 4.6 pA D528N) — currents not conductance; ΔE_rev-only statement ''Reversal potential in Tmc1+/+; Tmc2−/− is ∼7 mV positive to that in Tmc1 p.T416K/T416K'' (shift, no absolute endpoints stated) -> no row; GsMTx4/curare FM1-43 qualitative. delta_p50 flag: the Ca2+-induced x1 change (control 29 -> 6.9 nm; T416K 23 -> 23.6 nm, ''no effect on x1'') is NOT stated as a number — endpoints rowed as the x50 rows; no delta row (arithmetic forbidden).','mTmc1_OHC_apex_Tmc2-KO_control_1.5mM-Ca_bundle-vibration_Boltzmann-x1_Fig3A-B',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',148,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
