epancy declared) and control P_Ca/P_Cs error (Table 1 4.25 ± 0.35 (N = 8) matches). PRIOR-WORK rows NOT rowed: M412K (86.2 ± 8.2 pS, P_Ca/P_Cs 1.50 ± 0.12; effects previously shown in Beurg et al., 2015a and Corns et al., 2016) and D569N (87.5 ± 4.5 pS, 1.25 ± 0.11, N_MET 46 ± 18; Beurg et al., 2019). Archived non-rows: macroscopic currents (1.18 ± 0.16 nA control etc.) and N_MET channel counts (166 ± 23 / 123 ± 12 / 157 ± 14 / 54-58 ± 13); resting open probabilities P_OR (0.44 ± 0.06 control; 0.22 ± 0.06 T416K; 0.39 ± 0.01 D528N) and low-Ca2+ current ratios (1.54 ± 0.1 etc.) — population fractions, no parameter_kind home; unitary currents (-7.0 pA examples; 7.1 / 4.6 pA D528N) — currents not conductance; ΔE_rev-only statement ''Reversal potential in Tmc1+/+; Tmc2−/− is ∼7 mV positive to that in Tmc1 p.T416K/T416K'' (shift, no absolute endpoints stated) -> no row; GsMTx4/curare FM1-43 qualitative. delta_p50 flag: the Ca2+-induced x1 change (control 29 -> 6.9 nm; T416K 23 -> 23.6 nm, ''no effect on x1'') is NOT stated as a number — endpoints rowed as the x50 rows; no delta row (arithmetic forbidden). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc1_OHC_apex_Tmc2-KO_T416K-homo_Ca-reversal_GHK_P-Ca-P-Cs_Table1','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',148,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(634,'MAIC:BX:00634',8,NULL,NULL,104,'stereociliary bundle vibration via a fluid jet (~10 µm tip) or a piezoactuator-driven glass probe; bundle motion monitored on a photodiode; extracellular 1.5 mM Ca2+ saline or endolymph-like 0.04 mM Ca2+',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.57,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.57',NULL,'OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear apical OHCs (P5-P7); Tmc1 point-mutant lines p.T416K, p.D528N, p.W554L (plus prior-work M412K/D569N comparisons) ALL characterized on a Tmc2−/− background -> TMC1-only MET channel; single channels isolated by submicromolar-Ca2+ BAPTA tip-link removal','mouse cochlear outer hair cell (apex)',NULL,7.4,'standard extracellular saline, 1.5 mM Ca2+ (0.04 mM Ca2+ endolymph-like condition as noted); 100 mM CaCl2 + N-methylglucamine/Tris isotonic-Ca2+ saline for Ca-reversal measurements','142 mM CsCl-based intracellular solution (+ MgATP, phosphocreatine, EGTA, HEPES)',-84.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00047','Mean conductance values were 84.8 ± 3.1 pS ( N = 5) in the control and 53.5 ± 2.9 pS ( N = 5) in the mutant, a significant difference ( t test, p = 0.001) corresponding to a 37% reduction in conductance relative to the control. The macroscopic MET current was about half the size of the controls (0.55 ± 0.05 nA, N = 11; difference significant, p = 0.001) in apical OHCs and smaller (0.39 ± 0.11 pA, N = 3) in P8 Tmc1 p.D528N/D528N control IHCs than in Tmc1 +/+ controls IHCs (0.59 ± 0.06 pA, N = 5; Fig. 4 C ). The reduced macroscopic current is largely explained by smaller single-channel conductance rather than by a reduced number of channels in the bundle. The Ca 2+ permeability (P Ca /P Cs ; Fig. 7 C , D ) was reduced 7-fold relative to control from 4.25 ± 0.35 ( N = 8) to 0.57 ± 0.04 ( N = 7) in the homozygotes, Tmc1 p.D528N/D528N. We also characterized the heterozygote Tmc1 p.D528N /+; and found an intermediate reduction to 2.00 ± 0.33 ( N = 6), which is about half-way between the wild type and homozygote.','Results (D528N Ca2+ permeability; Fig 7, C and D)','medium','as-reported ratio (dimensionless); schema_gap: no ion-selectivity ratio column in the DB (reversal_potential_mv only a partial proxy). All values on the Tmc2−/− background -> TMC1-only channel; confidence medium (native, attribution contested). 7-fold reduction vs control — the largest of the series (''strongly endorsing its siting within the pore'' per the verify layer). Error-type note: the quoted text values carry no explicit SEM/SD label; figure panels report mean ± SD for bars — error_type left blank. Table 1 mirror values agree except D528N conductance (Table 1 prints 53.3 ± 2.9, text 53.5 ± 2.9 — text value rowed, discrepancy declared) and control P_Ca/P_Cs error (Table 1 4.25 ± 0.35 (N = 8) matches). PRIOR-WORK rows NOT rowed: M412K (86.2 ± 8.2 pS, P_Ca/P_Cs 1.50 ± 0.12; effects previously shown in Beurg et al., 2015a and Corns et al., 2016) and D569N (87.5 ± 4.5 pS, 1.25 ± 0.11, N_MET 46 ± 18; Beurg et al., 2019). Archived non-rows: macroscopic currents (1.18 ± 0.16 nA control etc.) and N_MET channel counts (166 ± 23 / 123 ± 12 / 157 ± 14 / 54-58 ± 13); resting open probabilities P_OR (0.44 ± 0.06 control; 0.22 ± 0.06 T416K; 0.39 ± 0.01 D528N) and low-Ca2+ current ratios (1.54 ± 0.1 etc.) — population fractions, no parameter_kind home; unitary currents (-7.0 pA examples; 7.1 / 4.6 pA D528N) — currents not conductance; ΔE_rev-only statement ''Reversal potential in Tmc1+/+; Tmc2−/− is ∼7 mV positive to that in Tmc1 p.T416K/T416K'' (shift, no absolute endpoints stated) -> no row; GsMTx4/curare FM1-43 qualitative. delta_p50 flag: the Ca2+-induced x1 change (control 29 -> 6.9 nm; T416K 23 -> 23.6 nm, ''no effect on x1'') is NOT stated as a number — endpoints rowed as the x50 rows; no delta row (arithmetic forbidden). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc1_OHC_apex_Tmc2-KO_D528N-homo_Ca-reversal_GHK_P-Ca-P-Cs_Table1','7','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',148,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
