p.D528N /+; and found an intermediate reduction to 2.00 ± 0.33 ( N = 6), which is about half-way between the wild type and homozygote.','Results (D528N heterozygote; Fig 7, C and D)','medium','as-reported ratio (dimensionless); schema_gap: no ion-selectivity ratio column in the DB (reversal_potential_mv only a partial proxy). All values on the Tmc2−/− background -> TMC1-only channel; confidence medium (native, attribution contested). intermediate heterozygote value, ''about half-way between the wild type and homozygote'' (recessive mutation). Error-type note: the quoted text values carry no explicit SEM/SD label; figure panels report mean ± SD for bars — error_type left blank. Table 1 mirror values agree except D528N conductance (Table 1 prints 53.3 ± 2.9, text 53.5 ± 2.9 — text value rowed, discrepancy declared) and control P_Ca/P_Cs error (Table 1 4.25 ± 0.35 (N = 8) matches). PRIOR-WORK rows NOT rowed: M412K (86.2 ± 8.2 pS, P_Ca/P_Cs 1.50 ± 0.12; effects previously shown in Beurg et al., 2015a and Corns et al., 2016) and D569N (87.5 ± 4.5 pS, 1.25 ± 0.11, N_MET 46 ± 18; Beurg et al., 2019). Archived non-rows: macroscopic currents (1.18 ± 0.16 nA control etc.) and N_MET channel counts (166 ± 23 / 123 ± 12 / 157 ± 14 / 54-58 ± 13); resting open probabilities P_OR (0.44 ± 0.06 control; 0.22 ± 0.06 T416K; 0.39 ± 0.01 D528N) and low-Ca2+ current ratios (1.54 ± 0.1 etc.) — population fractions, no parameter_kind home; unitary currents (-7.0 pA examples; 7.1 / 4.6 pA D528N) — currents not conductance; ΔE_rev-only statement ''Reversal potential in Tmc1+/+; Tmc2−/− is ∼7 mV positive to that in Tmc1 p.T416K/T416K'' (shift, no absolute endpoints stated) -> no row; GsMTx4/curare FM1-43 qualitative. delta_p50 flag: the Ca2+-induced x1 change (control 29 -> 6.9 nm; T416K 23 -> 23.6 nm, ''no effect on x1'') is NOT stated as a number — endpoints rowed as the x50 rows; no delta row (arithmetic forbidden). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc1_OHC_apex_Tmc2-KO_D528N-het_Ca-reversal_GHK_P-Ca-P-Cs_Table1','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',148,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(636,'MAIC:BX:00636',8,NULL,NULL,105,'stereociliary bundle vibration via a fluid jet (~10 µm tip) or a piezoactuator-driven glass probe; bundle motion monitored on a photodiode; extracellular 1.5 mM Ca2+ saline or endolymph-like 0.04 mM Ca2+',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,3.59,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'3.59',NULL,'OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear apical OHCs (P5-P7); Tmc1 point-mutant lines p.T416K, p.D528N, p.W554L (plus prior-work M412K/D569N comparisons) ALL characterized on a Tmc2−/− background -> TMC1-only MET channel; single channels isolated by submicromolar-Ca2+ BAPTA tip-link removal','mouse cochlear outer hair cell (apex)',NULL,7.4,'standard extracellular saline, 1.5 mM Ca2+ (0.04 mM Ca2+ endolymph-like condition as noted); 100 mM CaCl2 + N-methylglucamine/Tris isotonic-Ca2+ saline for Ca-reversal measurements','142 mM CsCl-based intracellular solution (+ MgATP, phosphocreatine, EGTA, HEPES)',-84.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00049','In contrast, there was no effect on single channel current ( Fig. 8 C ), the mean unitary conductance being 88.3 ± 4.0 pS ( N = 4), not significantly different from Tmc1 +/+ 84.8 ± 3.1 pS ( N = 5; t test, p = 0.52). Furthermore, there was only a modest change in Ca 2+ permeability with P Ca /P Cs = 3.59 ± 0.27 ( N = 8).','Results (W554L Ca2+ permeability; Fig 8)','medium','as-reported ratio (dimensionless); schema_gap: no ion-selectivity ratio column in the DB (reversal_potential_mv only a partial proxy). All values on the Tmc2−/− background -> TMC1-only channel; confidence medium (native, attribution contested). modest change only. Error-type note: the quoted text values carry no explicit SEM/SD label; figure panels report mean ± SD for bars — error_type left blank. Table 1 mirror values agree except D528N conductance (Table 1 prints 53.3 ± 2.9, text 53.5 ± 2.9 — text value rowed, discrepancy declared) and control P_Ca/P_Cs error (Table 1 4.25 ± 0.35 (N = 8) matches). PRIOR-WORK rows NOT rowed: M412K (86.2 ± 8.2 pS, P_Ca/P_Cs 1.50 ± 0.12; effects previously shown in Beurg et al., 2015a and Corns et al., 2016) and D569N (87.5 ± 4.5 pS, 1.25 ± 0.11, N_MET 46 ± 18; Beurg et al., 2019). Archived non-rows: macroscopic currents (1.18 ± 0.16 nA control etc.) and N_MET channel counts (166 ± 23 / 123 ± 12 / 157 ± 14 / 54-58 ± 13); resting open probabilities P_OR (0.44 ± 0.06 control; 0.22 ± 0.06 T416K; 0.39 ± 0.01 D528N) and low-Ca2+ current ratios (1.54 ± 0.1 etc.) — population fractions, no parameter_kind home; unitary currents (-7.0 pA examples; 7.1 / 4.6 pA D528N) — currents not conductance; ΔE_rev-only statement ''Reversal potential in Tmc1+/+; Tmc2−/− is ∼7 mV positive to that in Tmc1 p.T416K/T416K'' (shift, no absolute endpoints stated) -> no row; GsMTx4/curare FM1-43 qualitative. delta_p50 flag: the Ca2+-induced x1 change (control 29 -> 6.9 nm; T416K 23 -> 23.6 nm, ''no effect on x1'') is NOT stated as a number — endpoints rowed as the x50 rows; no delta row (arithmetic forbidden). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc1_OHC_apex_Tmc2-KO_W554L-homo_Ca-reversal_GHK_P-Ca-P-Cs_Table1','8','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',148,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(637,'MAIC:BX:00637',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'stiff glass probe delivering 15 step bundle deflections from -175 to 1050 nm; whole-cell transduction currents; activation curves fitted per cell with P0 = 1/(1+exp[-Z(X-X0)/kBT]) and averaged (means ± SEM) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 32 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,380.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'380','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — wild-type WT-TMC1 or point mutants (G411A, G518A, G539A, G539I, D528N, R601A, D528N/R601F); rescue paradigm: no native TMC1/TMC2, other MET-complex components present','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,7.4,'standard extracellular solution, pH 7.4 (~310 mOsm/kg)',NULL,-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00053','The fits of the activation curves of virally transduced WT-TMC1 in IHCs of Tmc1/2- DKO animals yielded Z values of 0.027 ± 0.003 pN and X 0 values of 380 ± 32 nm.','Results (WT-TMC1 activation fits; Fig 2 F)','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. the round''s WT reference midpoint; companion Z = 0.027 ± 0.003 pN archived. Rescue-paradigm caveat: the TMC1 variant is the only TMC in the Tmc1/2-DKO IHCs, but native MET-complex partners (tip link, LHFPL5, TMIE, CIB2) are present — attribution follows the round''s contested convention. ARCHIVED (no parameter_kind home): apparent mechanical-sensitivity slope factors Z in pN (WT 0.027 ± 0.003 pN; G411A 0.017 pN — ''reduced force sensitivity''; D528A/D528N/D528E slope reductions; two-state energy interpretations ~0.5 kBT); maximum currents (WT-TMC1 and mutants, pA); resting open probabilities (~6% WT vs ~20% D528N). Conductance Y-flag -> NO row: the nonstationary-noise values are single-channel CURRENTS in pA (WT-TMC1 12.5 ± 2.5 pA; D528N 3.5 ± 0.5 pA; G411A 14 ± 3.5 pA; G518A 12 ± 2.5 pA; G539A 14 ± 2.5 pA; G539I 14 ± 3 pA), not conductances (''Current magnitudes (pA) are NOT conductance''). D528E midpoints are table S2/figure-only (not rowed); D528A DOES have a text value (X 0 = 566 ± 70 nm; ''shifted to the right by nearly 190 nm'') and is rowed as two scale-v1 rework rows appended after the pilot (review F2).','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-WT-TMC1_stiff-probe_-175-to-1050nm_Boltzmann-X0_per-cell-fits-averaged',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',149,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(638,'MAIC:BX:00638',8,NULL,NULL,106,'stiff glass probe delivering 15 step bundle deflections from -175 to 1050 nm; whole-cell transduction currents; activation curves fitted per cell with P0 = 1/(1+exp[-Z(X-X0)/kBT]) and averaged (means ± SEM) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 28 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,507.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'507','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — wild-type WT-TMC1 or point mutants (G411A, G518A, G539A, G539I, D528N, R601A, D528N/R601F); rescue paradigm: no native TMC1/TMC2, other MET-complex components present','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,7.4,'standard extracellular solution, pH 7.4 (~310 mOsm/kg)',NULL,-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00054','However, the activation curves of TMC1-G411A were shifted rightward ( X 0 = 507 ± 28 nm) compared to WT-TMC1 ( X 0 = 380 ± 32 nm) ( Fig. 3C ). The slopes of the curves, represented by the Z values, were also substantially decreased—from 0.027 to 0.017 pN (table S2).','Results (G411A; Fig 3 C and table S2)','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. rightward shift + slope decrease (Z 0.027 -> 0.017 pN); no shift magnitude stated -> no delta row (endpoints only). Rescue-paradigm caveat: the TMC1 variant is the only TMC in the Tmc1/2-DKO IHCs, but native MET-complex partners (tip link, LHFPL5, TMIE, CIB2) are present — attribution follows the round''s contested convention. ARCHIVED (no parameter_kind home): apparent mechanical-sensitivity slope factors Z in pN (WT 0.027 ± 0.003 pN; G411A 0.017 pN — ''reduced force sensitivity''; D528A/D528N/D528E slope reductions; two-state energy interpretations ~0.5 kBT); maximum currents (WT-TMC1 and mutants, pA); resting open probabilities (~6% WT vs ~20% D528N). Conductance Y-flag -> NO row: the nonstationary-noise values are single-channel CURRENTS in pA (WT-TMC1 12.5 ± 2.5 pA; D528N 3.5 ± 0.5 pA; G411A 14 ± 3.5 pA; G518A 12 ± 2.5 pA; G539A 14 ± 2.5 pA; G539I 14 ± 3 pA), not conductances (''Current magnitudes (pA) are NOT conductance''). D528E midpoints are table S2/figure-only (not rowed); D528A DOES have a text value (X 0 = 566 ± 70 nm; ''shifted to the right by nearly 190 nm'') and is rowed as two scale-v1 rework rows appended after the pilot (review F2).','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-G411A_stiff-probe_-175-to-1050nm_Boltzmann-X0_per-cell-fits-averaged',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',149,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(639,'MAIC:BX:00639',8,NULL,NULL,107,'stiff glass probe delivering 15 step bundle deflections from -175 to 1050 nm; whole-cell transduction currents; activation curves fitted per cell with P0 = 1/(1+exp[-Z(X-X0)/kBT]) and averaged (means ± SEM) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 16 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,493.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'493','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — wild-type WT-TMC1 or point mutants (G411A, G518A, G539A, G539I, D528N, R601A, D528N/R601F); rescue paradigm: no native TMC1/TMC2, other MET-complex components present','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,7.4,'standard extracellular solution, pH 7.4 (~310 mOsm/kg)',NULL,-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00055','TMC1-G518A activation curves were shifted to the right by ~110 nm ( X 0 = 493 ± 16 nm) compared to WT-TMC1 ( X 0 = 380 ± 32 nm) ( Fig. 4, C and D , and table S2). From IHCs expressing TMC1-G539A, we also obtained typical maximum currents of 214 ± 38 pA ( n = 14), and the activation curves were shifted rightward by ~140 nm ( X 0 = 518 ± 30 nm) ( Fig. 4C ).','Results (G518A; Fig 4, C and D and table S2)','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. shift magnitude stated separately (''by ~110 nm'') -> delta row below. Rescue-paradigm caveat: the TMC1 variant is the only TMC in the Tmc1/2-DKO IHCs, but native MET-complex partners (tip link, LHFPL5, TMIE, CIB2) are present — attribution follows the round''s contested convention. ARCHIVED (no parameter_kind home): apparent mechanical-sensitivity slope factors Z in pN (WT 0.027 ± 0.003 pN; G411A 0.017 pN — ''reduced force sensitivity''; D528A/D528N/D528E slope reductions; two-state energy interpretations ~0.5 kBT); maximum currents (WT-TMC1 and mutants, pA); resting open probabilities (~6% WT vs ~20% D528N). Conductance Y-flag -> NO row: the nonstationary-noise values are single-channel CURRENTS in pA (WT-TMC1 12.5 ± 2.5 pA; D528N 3.5 ± 0.5 pA; G411A 14 ± 3.5 pA; G518A 12 ± 2.5 pA; G539A 14 ± 2.5 pA; G539I 14 ± 3 pA), not conductances (''Current magnitudes (pA) are NOT conductance''). D528E midpoints are table S2/figure-only (not rowed); D528A DOES have a text value (X 0 = 566 ± 70 nm; ''shifted to the right by nearly 190 nm'') and is rowed as two scale-v1 rework rows appended after the pilot (review F2).','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-G518A_stiff-probe_-175-to-1050nm_Boltzmann-X0_per-cell-fits-averaged',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',149,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
