27 ± 0.003 pN; G411A 0.017 pN — ''reduced force sensitivity''; D528A/D528N/D528E slope reductions; two-state energy interpretations ~0.5 kBT); maximum currents (WT-TMC1 and mutants, pA); resting open probabilities (~6% WT vs ~20% D528N). Conductance Y-flag -> NO row: the nonstationary-noise values are single-channel CURRENTS in pA (WT-TMC1 12.5 ± 2.5 pA; D528N 3.5 ± 0.5 pA; G411A 14 ± 3.5 pA; G518A 12 ± 2.5 pA; G539A 14 ± 2.5 pA; G539I 14 ± 3 pA), not conductances (''Current magnitudes (pA) are NOT conductance''). D528E midpoints are table S2/figure-only (not rowed); D528A DOES have a text value (X 0 = 566 ± 70 nm; ''shifted to the right by nearly 190 nm'') and is rowed as two scale-v1 rework rows appended after the pilot (review F2).','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-G539A_stiff-probe_-175-to-1050nm_Boltzmann-X0_per-cell-fits-averaged',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',149,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
