nergy interpretations ~0.5 kBT); maximum currents (WT-TMC1 and mutants, pA); resting open probabilities (~6% WT vs ~20% D528N). Conductance Y-flag -> NO row: the nonstationary-noise values are single-channel CURRENTS in pA (WT-TMC1 12.5 ± 2.5 pA; D528N 3.5 ± 0.5 pA; G411A 14 ± 3.5 pA; G518A 12 ± 2.5 pA; G539A 14 ± 2.5 pA; G539I 14 ± 3 pA), not conductances (''Current magnitudes (pA) are NOT conductance''). D528E midpoints are table S2/figure-only (not rowed); D528A DOES have a text value (X 0 = 566 ± 70 nm; ''shifted to the right by nearly 190 nm'') and is rowed as two scale-v1 rework rows appended after the pilot (review F2).','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-D528N_stiff-probe_-175-to-1050nm_Boltzmann-X0_per-cell-fits-averaged',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',149,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(643,'MAIC:BX:00643',8,NULL,NULL,110,'stiff glass probe delivering 15 step bundle deflections from -175 to 1050 nm; whole-cell transduction currents; activation curves fitted per cell with P0 = 1/(1+exp[-Z(X-X0)/kBT]) and averaged (means ± SEM) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 25 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,580.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'580','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — wild-type WT-TMC1 or point mutants (G411A, G518A, G539A, G539I, D528N, R601A, D528N/R601F); rescue paradigm: no native TMC1/TMC2, other MET-complex components present','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,7.4,'standard extracellular solution, pH 7.4 (~310 mOsm/kg)',NULL,-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00059','In both WT-TMC1 and TMC1-D528N, mutation of R601 shifted the activation curves rightward, apparently stabilizing the closed state (R601A: X 0 = 580 ± 25 nm; D528N/R601F: X 0 = 510 ± 46 nm) ( Fig. 6, C and D , and table S2).','Results (R601A; Fig 6, C and D and table S2)','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. rightward shift ''apparently stabilizing the closed state''; slope not significantly affected. Rescue-paradigm caveat: the TMC1 variant is the only TMC in the Tmc1/2-DKO IHCs, but native MET-complex partners (tip link, LHFPL5, TMIE, CIB2) are present — attribution follows the round''s contested convention. ARCHIVED (no parameter_kind home): apparent mechanical-sensitivity slope factors Z in pN (WT 0.027 ± 0.003 pN; G411A 0.017 pN — ''reduced force sensitivity''; D528A/D528N/D528E slope reductions; two-