INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(652,'MAIC:BX:00652',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'25-mm piezoelectric disc driving a fluid jet onto the stereociliary bundle (step and sinusoidal stimuli); I-V by voltage ramps for reversal measurements; ''All values are quoted as mean ± SEM''',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,2.98,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2.98',NULL,'OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear apical OHCs (P3-P9): Tmc2−/− (tm1Lex) vs Tmc2+/− littermate controls; at P3-P4 the MET channel is TMC2-dominant (Tmc2−/− -> TMC1-only channel), from ~P6 TMC1 becomes dominant','mouse cochlear outer hair cell (apex)',NULL,7.5,'135 NaCl, 5.8 KCl, 1.3 CaCl2, 0.9 MgCl2, 0.7 NaH2PO4, 5.6 D-glucose, 10 HEPES-NaOH, 2 Na-pyruvate, pH 7.5, 308 mOsm/kg (Eagle''s MEM amino acids/vitamins added); isotonic-Ca2+ external for Ca-reversal measurements','106 L-glutamic acid, 20 CsCl, 10 Na2 phosphocreatine, 3 MgCl2, 1 EGTA-CsOH, 5 Na2ATP, 5 HEPES (pH ~7.3); Ca-reversal pipette: 135 CsCl, 3 MgATP, 10 Tris phosphocreatine, 1 EGTA-CsOH, 10 HEPES-CsOH, pH 7.3',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00068','We also found that during the second postnatal week, the Ca 2+ permeability (see also “Materials and Methods” section for details) of the MET channel was similar in Tmc2 +/- (P Ca /P Cs : P6–P7 3.37 ± 0.17, n = 7; P9 3.10 ± 0.13, n = 4) and Tmc2 -/- (P6–P7 2.98 ± 0.12, n = 6; P9 3.27 ± 0.16, n = 5) OHCs. Despite this similarity at older ages, the Ca 2+ permeability was significantly reduced in Tmc2 -/- P3–P4 OHCs ( Tmc2 +/- : 4.40 ± 0.24, n = 4; Tmc2 -/- : 2.52 ± 0.13, n = 5, P < 0.0005), in agreement with previous findings (Kim and Fettiplace, 2013 ; Pan et al., 2013 ; Beurg et al., 2015 ).','Results (Ca2+ permeability by age; Tmc2-/-, P6-P7, n = 6)','medium','as-reported ratio (dimensionless); schema_gap: no ion-selectivity ratio column in the DB. mean ± SEM (methods). second postnatal week (TMC1-dominant era): values converge between genotypes — rowed as own-data measurements of the same comparison. Native preparation -> confidence medium (attribution contested). conductance Y-flag -> NO row: ''Taking a value of 62 pS as the conductance of the MET channel for both genotypes (Kim et al., 2013)'' — the 62 pS is ADOPTED from Kim 2013 for channel-count inference (156 vs 60 channels), not measured here (intro/cited-value rule). tau flags -> NO rows: no adaptation time constants; the DHS binding time constants (Tmc2+/− τ = 0.45 ms; Tmc2−/− τ = 0.36 ms at 30 µM extracellular DHS) are BLOCKER-BINDING kinetics, not channel adaptation -> archived. ARCHIVED (no parameter_kind home): two-barrier one-binding-site model energies (E1 11.8/11.9 kT; E2 16.3/15.3 kT; binding well Eb -8.04/-9.64 kT; ΔE 4.555/3.452 kT; electrical distances δ1 0.045, δ2 0.955, δb 0.79); DHS entry rates (586/1078/1462/521 molecules/s — rates, never converted to taus); block fractions at 300 µM intracellular DHS (gerbil P7-P8 0.52 ± 0.07 n = 4; mouse P8 0.57 ± 0.02 / 0.57 ± 0.04 n = 7 each — fractions); MET-current amplitude reductions (61% P4, 28% P5, cited-companion context); P_Ca/P_Cs agreement cites (Kim and Fettiplace 2013; Pan et al., 2013; Beurg et al., 2015). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc1_OHC_apex_Tmc2-KO_P6-P7_Ca-reversal_GHK_P-Ca-P-Cs','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',150,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
