t era): values converge between genotypes — rowed as own-data measurements of the same comparison. Native preparation -> confidence medium (attribution contested). conductance Y-flag -> NO row: ''Taking a value of 62 pS as the conductance of the MET channel for both genotypes (Kim et al., 2013)'' — the 62 pS is ADOPTED from Kim 2013 for channel-count inference (156 vs 60 channels), not measured here (intro/cited-value rule). tau flags -> NO rows: no adaptation time constants; the DHS binding time constants (Tmc2+/− τ = 0.45 ms; Tmc2−/− τ = 0.36 ms at 30 µM extracellular DHS) are BLOCKER-BINDING kinetics, not channel adaptation -> archived. ARCHIVED (no parameter_kind home): two-barrier one-binding-site model energies (E1 11.8/11.9 kT; E2 16.3/15.3 kT; binding well Eb -8.04/-9.64 kT; ΔE 4.555/3.452 kT; electrical distances δ1 0.045, δ2 0.955, δb 0.79); DHS entry rates (586/1078/1462/521 molecules/s — rates, never converted to taus); block fractions at 300 µM intracellular DHS (gerbil P7-P8 0.52 ± 0.07 n = 4; mouse P8 0.57 ± 0.02 / 0.57 ± 0.04 n = 7 each — fractions); MET-current amplitude reductions (61% P4, 28% P5, cited-companion context); P_Ca/P_Cs agreement cites (Kim and Fettiplace 2013; Pan et al., 2013; Beurg et al., 2015). [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc1_OHC_apex_Tmc2-KO_P9_Ca-reversal_GHK_P-Ca-P-Cs','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',150,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(654,'MAIC:BX:00654',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'hair-bundle mechanical stimulation (fluid jet) in 1.3 mM extracellular Ca2+; single-channel events in whole-cell mode | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 18','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,101.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'101','pS','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse utricular type II vestibular hair cells; Tmc1Delta/Delta;Tmc2+/Delta (TMC2-expressing), Tmc1+/Delta;Tmc2Delta/Delta (TMC1-expressing) and wild-type controls','mouse utricular type II vestibular hair cell',NULL,NULL,'standard extracellular saline with 1.3 mM Ca2+ (single-channel set)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00074','In type II vestibular hair cells bathed in 1.3 mM Ca 2+ , single-channel conductances from Tmc1 Δ/Δ ; Tmc2 +/Δ mice (mean = 101 ± 18 pS, n=3; Figure 6A ) were about twice the amplitude of those recorded from Tmc1 +/Δ ; Tmc2 Δ/Δ mice (mean = 50 ± 18 pS, n=4; Figure 6B ). In wild-type cells ( Figure 6C ), most single-channel events had large conductances (mean = 114 ± 8 pS, n=3), consistent with our previous data showing that Tmc2 is highly expressed in vestibular hair cells during the first postnatal week','Results (Tmc function in vestibular hair cells; Fig 6, A-C)','medium','gene token = functional channel composition (Tmc1Δ/Δ;Tmc2+/Δ (TMC2-expressing)); ''about twice the amplitude'' TMC2- vs TMC1-expressing. pS native TMC scale. Native preparation -> confidence medium (attribution contested). Archived: cochlear IHC single-channel conductances are a scatter RANGE only (''g ranged between 60 and 330 pS during the first postnatal week'' in 50 uM Ca2+, 44 wild-type cells; Tmc-mutant values tightly clustered — figure-only); adaptation fast/slow taus are figure-panel fit parameters (no numeric taus in text); P_Ca/P_Cs values are Figure 2F only; the M412K ''33%'' effect is a unitary-CURRENT reduction (current percent, not conductance). Verify-layer note: pro-pore attribution. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc2_vestibular-typeII_Tmc1-KO_Tmc2-het_utricle_1.3mM-Ca_single-channel_Fig6','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',151,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(655,'MAIC:BX:00655',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'hair-bundle mechanical stimulation (fluid jet) in 1.3 mM extracellular Ca2+; single-channel events in whole-cell mode | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 18','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,50.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'50','pS','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse utricular type II vestibular hair cells; Tmc1Delta/Delta;Tmc2+/Delta (TMC2-expressing), Tmc1+/Delta;Tmc2Delta/Delta (TMC1-expressing) and wild-type controls','mouse utricular type II vestibular hair cell',NULL,NULL,'standard extracellular saline with 1.3 mM Ca2+ (single-channel set)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00075','In type II vestibular hair cells bathed in 1.3 mM Ca 2+ , single-channel conductances from Tmc1 Δ/Δ ; Tmc2 +/Δ mice (mean = 101 ± 18 pS, n=3; Figure 6A ) were about twice the amplitude of those recorded from Tmc1 +/Δ ; Tmc2 Δ/Δ mice (mean = 50 ± 18 pS, n=4; Figure 6B ). In wild-type cells ( Figure 6C ), most single-channel events had large conductances (mean = 114 ± 8 pS, n=3), consistent with our previous data showing that Tmc2 is highly expressed in vestibular hair cells during the first postnatal week','Results (Tmc function in vestibular hair cells; Fig 6, A-C)','medium','gene token = functional channel composition (Tmc1+/Δ;Tmc2Δ/Δ (TMC1-expressing)); ''about twice the amplitude'' TMC2- vs TMC1-expressing. pS native TMC scale. Native preparation -> confidence medium (attribution contested). Archived: cochlear IHC single-channel conductances are a scatter RANGE only (''g ranged between 60 and 330 pS during the first postnatal week'' in 50 uM Ca2+, 44 wild-type cells; Tmc-mutant values tightly clustered — figure-only); adaptation fast/slow taus are figure-panel fit parameters (no numeric taus in text); P_Ca/P_Cs values are Figure 2F only; the M412K ''33%'' effect is a unitary-CURRENT reduction (current percent, not conductance). Verify-layer note: pro-pore attribution. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc1_vestibular-typeII_Tmc1-het_Tmc2-KO_utricle_1.3mM-Ca_single-channel_Fig6','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',151,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(656,'MAIC:BX:00656',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'hair-bundle mechanical stimulation (fluid jet) in 1.3 mM extracellular Ca2+; single-channel events in whole-cell mode | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 8','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,114.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'114','pS','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse utricular type II vestibular hair cells; Tmc1Delta/Delta;Tmc2+/Delta (TMC2-expressing), Tmc1+/Delta;Tmc2Delta/Delta (TMC1-expressing) and wild-type controls','mouse utricular type II vestibular hair cell',NULL,NULL,'standard extracellular saline with 1.3 mM Ca2+ (single-channel set)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00076','In type II vestibular hair cells bathed in 1.3 mM Ca 2+ , single-channel conductances from Tmc1 Δ/Δ ; Tmc2 +/Δ mice (mean = 101 ± 18 pS, n=3; Figure 6A ) were about twice the amplitude of those recorded from Tmc1 +/Δ ; Tmc2 Δ/Δ mice (mean = 50 ± 18 pS, n=4; Figure 6B ). In wild-type cells ( Figure 6C ), most single-channel events had large conductances (mean = 114 ± 8 pS, n=3), consistent with our previous data showing that Tmc2 is highly expressed in vestibular hair cells during the first postnatal week','Results (Tmc function in vestibular hair cells; Fig 6, A-C)','medium','gene token = functional channel composition (wild type); ''about twice the amplitude'' TMC2- vs TMC1-expressing. pS native TMC scale. Native preparation -> confidence medium (attribution contested). Archived: cochlear IHC single-channel conductances are a scatter RANGE only (''g ranged between 60 and 330 pS during the first postnatal week'' in 50 uM Ca2+, 44 wild-type cells; Tmc-mutant values tightly clustered — figure-only); adaptation fast/slow taus are figure-panel fit parameters (no numeric taus in text); P_Ca/P_Cs values are Figure 2F only; the M412K ''33%'' effect is a unitary-CURRENT reduction (current percent, not conductance). Verify-layer note: pro-pore attribution. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc1+mTmc2_vestibular-typeII_WT_utricle_1.3mM-Ca_single-channel_Fig6','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',151,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(657,'MAIC:BX:00657',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'fluid-jet bundle stimulation at three extracellular Ca2+ concentrations (1.3, 0.1, 0.04 mM); I-X fitted with a second-order Boltzmann','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,122.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'122','nm','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear apical OHCs P6-P7: Tmc1+/+ controls vs Tmc1 Bth/Bth (M412K Beethoven point mutation); functional channel = mutant/WT TMC1 + TMC2','mouse cochlear outer hair cell (apex)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-81.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00077','Apart from x 1 , all other values were identical among the fits ( Tmc1 +/+ : a 1 = 0.018 nm -1 , a 2 = 0.010 nm -1 , x 2 = -26 nm; Tmc1 Bth/Bth : a 1 = 0.027 nm -1 , a 2 = 0.012 nm -1 , x 2 = 8 nm). For x 1 , the values were as follows: in Tmc1 +/+ , 122 nm in 1.3 m m Ca 2+ , -26 nm in 0.1 m m Ca 2+ , -90 nm in 0.04 m m Ca 2+ ; and in Tmc1 Bth/Bth , 80 nm in 1.3 m m Ca 2+ , 8 nm in 0.1 m m Ca 2+ , -177 nm in 0.04 m m Ca 2+ . Note the larger shift in x 1 in Bth mutants compared with that of wild type on increasing Ca 2+ from 0.04 to 0.1 m m ( Tmc1 Bth/Bth , 185 nm; Tmc1 +/+ , 64 nm), although it was reduced when going from 0.1 to 1.3 m m ( Tmc1 Bth/Bth , 72 nm; Tmc1 +/+ , 148 nm)','Results (I-X fits at three Ca2+ concentrations; Fig 4 legend)','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. collected fits over the stated cell groups (I_max values in the quote); x1 = half-activation displacement of the second-order Boltzmann (X50 analog). Archived (rework M5): the macroscopic MT slope conductances DO have absolute values — Fig 2 legend linear-regression slopes: apical 3.0 pA/mV (Tmc1+/+) vs 2.1 pA/mV (Bth/Bth); basal 3.4 pA/mV vs 2.0 pA/mV (the ~30%/~40% reductions of the text) — but pA/mV macroscopic slope units have no parameter_kind home (NOT unitary conductance) -> not rowed, values recorded here; P_Ca/P_Cs values are Fig 2E only (text: ''reduced significantly, p < 0.0001''); M412K pore energetics (E1 11.57->13.47 kT, E2 16.40->20.79 kT, Eb -7.65->-4.21 kT per the verify layer) have no parameter_kind home. Pro-pore attribution paper. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','mTmc1+mTmc2_OHC_apex_Tmc1-WT_P6-P7_1.3mMCa2+_-81mV_second-order-Boltzmann-x1_Fig4',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',152,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
