fpl5+/+ control 58 ± 8 nm) — same experiment, declared on both rows for loader dedup. Pro-pore context (TMC1/2 as pore subunits; the paper''s own thesis is LHFPL5 as the force-transmission element).','mTmc1_OHC_apex_Tmc2-KO_Lhfpl5-KO_P5_single-Boltzmann-XO','4','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',166,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(728,'MAIC:BX:00728',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'sinusoidal fluid jet; bundle motion monitored; I-X fitted with a single Boltzmann (X_O half-saturation)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,84.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'84','nm','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear apical OHCs P5: Lhfpl5+/- vs Lhfpl5-/-, in a wild-type Tmc background and on a Tmc2-/- background','mouse cochlear outer hair cell (apex)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00150','In the wild type, the half-activation, X O , was 39 ± 10 nm (N = 17) in Lhfpl5+/- , whereas it was 123 ± 37 nm (N = 10) in Lhfpl5-/- , showing an 84 nm positive shift in the absence of LHFPL5. With Tmc2-/- mice, X O was 153 ± 13 nm in Lhfpl5-/- (N = 4), a significant positive shift of 95 nm ( t test , P = 0.005).','Results (stated positive shifts; Fig 2)','medium','[pool-external] Pool-external paper (verified outside the OpenAlex pool sweep; T4-03 disclosure). pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. the paper''s own explicitly stated shift magnitudes (direction: positive/rightward — decreased mechanical sensitivity); endpoints rowed as the x50 rows above. DEMOTED to schema_gap: nm displacement shift but delta_p50_* is pressure-unit-only. Archived (rework M6): the single-channel gating force Z IS stated in the text (not figure-only): Z = 0.34 pN in Tmc1+/+;Lhfpl5+/- (10-90% working range 52 nm) and Z more than halved to 0.13 pN in Lhfpl5-/- (working range 123 nm); the Results-section working range 125 ± 18 nm (N = 5) is an operating range, NOT x50; gating-force/stiffness quantities are force-class values with no parameter_kind home (schema-gap archive per the round rules) -> not rowed, values recorded here. CROSS-PAPER NOTE: the Tmc2-/-;Lhfpl5-/- value 153 ± 13 nm (N = 4) is also reported in Fettiplace 2022 (rowed there with the Lhfpl5+/+ control 58 ± 8 nm) — same experiment, declared on both rows for loader dedup. Pro-pore context (TMC1/2 as pore subunits; the paper''s own thesis is LHFPL5 as the force-transmission element).','mTmc1+mTmc2_OHC_apex_Lhfpl5-KO_vs-het_P5_XO-positive-shift',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',166,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(729,'MAIC:BX:00729',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'sinusoidal fluid jet; bundle motion monitored; I-X fitted with a single Boltzmann (X_O half-saturation)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,95.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'95','nm','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear apical OHCs P5: Lhfpl5+/- vs Lhfpl5-/-, in a wild-type Tmc background and on a Tmc2-/- background','mouse cochlear outer hair cell (apex)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00151','In the wild type, the half-activation, X O , was 39 ± 10 nm (N = 17) in Lhfpl5+/- , whereas it was 123 ± 37 nm (N = 10) in Lhfpl5-/- , showing an 84 nm positive shift in the absence of LHFPL5. With Tmc2-/- mice, X O was 153 ± 13 nm in Lhfpl5-/- (N = 4), a significant positive shift of 95 nm ( t test , P = 0.005).','Results (stated positive shifts; Fig 2)','medium','[pool-external] Pool-external paper (verified outside the OpenAlex pool sweep; T4-03 disclosure). pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. the paper''s own explicitly stated shift magnitudes (direction: positive/rightward — decreased mechanical sensitivity); endpoints rowed as the x50 rows above. DEMOTED to schema_gap: nm displacement shift but delta_p50_* is pressure-unit-only. Archived (rework M6): the single-channel gating force Z IS stated in the text (not figure-only): Z = 0.34 pN in Tmc1+/+;Lhfpl5+/- (10-90% working range 52 nm) and Z more than halved to 0.13 pN in Lhfpl5-/- (working range 123 nm); the Results-section working range 125 ± 18 nm (N = 5) is an operating range, NOT x50; gating-force/stiffness quantities are force-class values with no parameter_kind home (schema-gap archive per the round rules) -> not rowed, values recorded here. CROSS-PAPER NOTE: the Tmc2-/-;Lhfpl5-/- value 153 ± 13 nm (N = 4) is also reported in Fettiplace 2022 (rowed there with the Lhfpl5+/+ control 58 ± 8 nm) — same experiment, declared on both rows for loader dedup. Pro-pore context (TMC1/2 as pore subunits; the paper''s own thesis is LHFPL5 as the force-transmission element).','mTmc1_OHC_apex_Tmc2-KO_Lhfpl5-KO_vs-control_P5_XO-positive-shift',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',166,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(730,'MAIC:BX:00730',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'piezo-driven stiff glass probe deflecting IHC bundles; activation curves fitted with a Boltzmann, means ± SEM across cells | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 32 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,380.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'380','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — WT reference or TM1-2-loop variants (Y238L, Y238W, F234A, G235A); rescue paradigm','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00152','The half-activation displacement (X 0 ) was significantly right-shifted in cells expressing Y238L (X 0 = 519 ± 25 nm) or Y238W (X 0 = 590 ± 25 nm) compared to WT (X 0 = 380 ± 32 nm), indicating stabilization of the closed state.','Fig 4 D legend (WT reference curve)','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. CROSS-CHECK: identical to the Akyuz 2022 WT-TMC1 baseline (380 ± 32 nm, pilot TMC-EX rowed) — the same rescue-paradigm reference; declared for loader dedup. Shift magnitudes not stated as numbers -> no delta rows (endpoints only). Archived: slope factors (dx) ''not significantly different across groups'' (no rowing); G235A ''no significant effect'' framing (value rowed); Table S1 holds the full parameter set. Pro-pore paper.','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-WT-TMC1_stiff-probe_Boltzmann-X0',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',167,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(731,'MAIC:BX:00731',8,NULL,NULL,115,'piezo-driven stiff glass probe deflecting IHC bundles; activation curves fitted with a Boltzmann, means ± SEM across cells | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 25 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,519.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'519','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — WT reference or TM1-2-loop variants (Y238L, Y238W, F234A, G235A); rescue paradigm','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00153','The half-activation displacement (X 0 ) was significantly right-shifted in cells expressing Y238L (X 0 = 519 ± 25 nm) or Y238W (X 0 = 590 ± 25 nm) compared to WT (X 0 = 380 ± 32 nm), indicating stabilization of the closed state.','Fig 4 D legend','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. right-shifted, closed-state stabilization. Shift magnitudes not stated as numbers -> no delta rows (endpoints only). Archived: slope factors (dx) ''not significantly different across groups'' (no rowing); G235A ''no significant effect'' framing (value rowed); Table S1 holds the full parameter set. Pro-pore paper.','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-Y238L_stiff-probe_Boltzmann-X0','9','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',167,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(732,'MAIC:BX:00732',8,NULL,NULL,116,'piezo-driven stiff glass probe deflecting IHC bundles; activation curves fitted with a Boltzmann, means ± SEM across cells | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 25 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,590.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'590','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — WT reference or TM1-2-loop variants (Y238L, Y238W, F234A, G235A); rescue paradigm','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00154','The half-activation displacement (X 0 ) was significantly right-shifted in cells expressing Y238L (X 0 = 519 ± 25 nm) or Y238W (X 0 = 590 ± 25 nm) compared to WT (X 0 = 380 ± 32 nm), indicating stabilization of the closed state.','Fig 4 D legend','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. right-shifted, closed-state stabilization. Shift magnitudes not stated as numbers -> no delta rows (endpoints only). Archived: slope factors (dx) ''not significantly different across groups'' (no rowing); G235A ''no significant effect'' framing (value rowed); Table S1 holds the full parameter set. Pro-pore paper.','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-Y238W_stiff-probe_Boltzmann-X0','7','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',167,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(733,'MAIC:BX:00733',8,NULL,NULL,117,'piezo-driven stiff glass probe deflecting IHC bundles; activation curves fitted with a Boltzmann, means ± SEM across cells | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 32 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,526.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'526','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — WT reference or TM1-2-loop variants (Y238L, Y238W, F234A, G235A); rescue paradigm','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00155','Substitution of F234 with alanine (F234A, red), produced a significant rightward shift in the activation curve (X 0 =526 ± 32 nm) relative to WT-TMC1 (black), indicating a stabilization of the closed state. Mutation of the adjacent G235 to alanine (G235A, blue) had no significant effect (X 0 = 376 ± 33 nm).','Fig 5 B legend (TMIE-interface mutant)','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. reduced force sensitivity / closed-state stabilization (TM1-2 loop / TMIE interface). Shift magnitudes not stated as numbers -> no delta rows (endpoints only). Archived: slope factors (dx) ''not significantly different across groups'' (no rowing); G235A ''no significant effect'' framing (value rowed); Table S1 holds the full parameter set. Pro-pore paper.','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-F234A_stiff-probe_Boltzmann-X0',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',167,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(734,'MAIC:BX:00734',8,NULL,NULL,118,'piezo-driven stiff glass probe deflecting IHC bundles; activation curves fitted with a Boltzmann, means ± SEM across cells | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 33 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,376.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'376','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — WT reference or TM1-2-loop variants (Y238L, Y238W, F234A, G235A); rescue paradigm','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00156','Substitution of F234 with alanine (F234A, red), produced a significant rightward shift in the activation curve (X 0 =526 ± 32 nm) relative to WT-TMC1 (black), indicating a stabilization of the closed state. Mutation of the adjacent G235 to alanine (G235A, blue) had no significant effect (X 0 = 376 ± 33 nm).','Fig 5 B legend','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. ''no significant effect'' vs WT (376 ± 33 vs 380 ± 32 nm) — rowed as the paper''s own stated value. Shift magnitudes not stated as numbers -> no delta rows (endpoints only). Archived: slope factors (dx) ''not significantly different across groups'' (no rowing); G235A ''no significant effect'' framing (value rowed); Table S1 holds the full parameter set. Pro-pore paper.','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-G235A_stiff-probe_Boltzmann-X0',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',167,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(735,'MAIC:BX:00735',8,NULL,NULL,113,'stiff glass probe for adaptation kinetics (fluid jet too slow); paired-pulse protocols for adaptation shifts | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.04','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.23,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.23','ms','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear OHCs: Tmc2-/- (TMC1-only), Tmc1-/- (TMC2-only) and Tmc1 +/+;Tmc2-/- controls; Tmc1 p.D569N mutants','mouse cochlear outer hair cell',NULL,NULL,'standard extracellular saline (1.5 mM Ca2+ unless stated)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00157','MET currents in Tmc1 p.D569N mutant mice were smaller than those in Tmc1 +/+ but nevertheless displayed fast adaptation, with a mean time constant of 0.23 ± 0.04 ms ( n = 6) in OHCs and with maximum currents of 0.4–0.5 nA (Fig. 4 A ).','Results (D569N adaptation; Fig 4 A)','medium','REWORK F3 row: same series/structure as the Tmc2-/- 0.16 ms and Tmc1-/- 0.41 ms rows — ''not attributable to TMC2 because they were present in Tmc2-/-''; mutant MET currents ''nevertheless displayed fast adaptation''. Companion dX/A slope 0.79 ± 0.06 (n = 5) archived (adaptation slope, NOT delta_p50). Archived: 58 pS vs 70 pS unitary conductances are CITED from Beurg 2018 (intro-cited-value rule -> not rowed); dX/A adaptation slopes (control 0.61 ± 0.02, n = 5) are adaptation slopes, NOT delta_p50; fluid-jet adaptation comparisons. Neutral-controversy paper (TMC1/2 treated as channel constituents localizing adaptation to the complex).','mTmc1_OHC_Tmc2-KO_D569N-homo_stiff-probe_adaptation-tauA','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',154,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(736,'MAIC:BX:00736',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'fluid-jet bundle stimulation from fire-polished pipettes (~3 µm tip for OHCs, ~6 µm for IHCs); extracellular 0.02 mM Ca2+ for single-channel estimates | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 3.0','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-28.2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-28.2','mV','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native RAT cochlear hair cells (pre-TMC-identification benchmark; channel identity attributed post-hoc as TMC1/2-complex)','rat cochlear inner / outer hair cell (low- and mid-frequency positions)',NULL,NULL,'extracellular saline with 0.02 mM Ca2+ (single-channel set)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00158','To verify that NMG is effectively impermeant, reversal potentials for the MT current were measured in the NMG/1.5 Ca 2+ solution. These were -28.2 ± 3.0 ( n = 5) in IHCs and -27.8 ± 5.1 ( n = 6) in OHCs. The reversal potentials were analyzed in terms of the GHK equation, inserting the appropriate values of P Ca / P Cs determined above. This gave an average permeability of NMG relative to Cs + of 0.1, making NMG at least 50 times less permeable than Ca 2+ .','Results (Ca2+ permeability; NMG impermeability control)','medium','PRE-ATTRIBUTION BASELINE: channel identity unknown at publication; attributed post-hoc as TMC1/2-complex (rat). Quotes transcribed from the cached PMC full-page render (.scratch/tmc_fulltext/10_1523_jneurosci_2188-06_2006.txt), keeping the source''s italic ''m m'' rendering of mM; other glyphs as printed. REWORK M1 row: absolute E_rev in the NMG/1.5 mM Ca2+ bi-ionic solution (verifies NMG is effectively impermeant). IHC vs OHC differ significantly in Ca2+ carriage (I_Ca/I_Total fractions 0.15 ± 0.02 n = 5 IHC vs 0.12 ± 0.02 n = 6 OHC archived — current fractions, no parameter_kind home).','rTmc1+rTmc2_IHC_low-mid-CF_WT_NMG-1.5mM-Ca_Erev','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',157,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(737,'MAIC:BX:00737',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'fluid-jet bundle stimulation from fire-polished pipettes (~3 µm tip for OHCs, ~6 µm for IHCs); extracellular 0.02 mM Ca2+ for single-channel estimates | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 5.1','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-27.8,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-27.8','mV','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native RAT cochlear hair cells (pre-TMC-identification benchmark; channel identity attributed post-hoc as TMC1/2-complex)','rat cochlear inner / outer hair cell (low- and mid-frequency positions)',NULL,NULL,'extracellular saline with 0.02 mM Ca2+ (single-channel set)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00159','To verify that NMG is effectively impermeant, reversal potentials for the MT current were measured in the NMG/1.5 Ca 2+ solution. These were -28.2 ± 3.0 ( n = 5) in IHCs and -27.8 ± 5.1 ( n = 6) in OHCs. The reversal potentials were analyzed in terms of the GHK equation, inserting the appropriate values of P Ca / P Cs determined above. This gave an average permeability of NMG relative to Cs + of 0.1, making NMG at least 50 times less permeable than Ca 2+ .','Results (Ca2+ permeability; NMG impermeability control)','medium','PRE-ATTRIBUTION BASELINE: channel identity unknown at publication; attributed post-hoc as TMC1/2-complex (rat). Quotes transcribed from the cached PMC full-page render (.scratch/tmc_fulltext/10_1523_jneurosci_2188-06_2006.txt), keeping the source''s italic ''m m'' rendering of mM; other glyphs as printed. REWORK M1 row: absolute E_rev in the NMG/1.5 mM Ca2+ bi-ionic solution (verifies NMG is effectively impermeant). IHC vs OHC differ significantly in Ca2+ carriage (I_Ca/I_Total fractions 0.15 ± 0.02 n = 5 IHC vs 0.12 ± 0.02 n = 6 OHC archived — current fractions, no parameter_kind home).','rTmc1+rTmc2_OHC_apical_WT_NMG-1.5mM-Ca_Erev','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',157,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(738,'MAIC:BX:00738',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'fluid-jet bundle stimulation from fire-polished pipettes (~3 µm tip for OHCs, ~6 µm for IHCs); extracellular 0.02 mM Ca2+ for single-channel estimates',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.1',NULL,'OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native RAT cochlear hair cells (pre-TMC-identification benchmark; channel identity attributed post-hoc as TMC1/2-complex)','rat cochlear inner / outer hair cell (low- and mid-frequency positions)',NULL,NULL,'extracellular saline with 0.02 mM Ca2+ (single-channel set)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00160','To verify that NMG is effectively impermeant, reversal potentials for the MT current were measured in the NMG/1.5 Ca 2+ solution. These were -28.2 ± 3.0 ( n = 5) in IHCs and -27.8 ± 5.1 ( n = 6) in OHCs. The reversal potentials were analyzed in terms of the GHK equation, inserting the appropriate values of P Ca / P Cs determined above. This gave an average permeability of NMG relative to Cs + of 0.1, making NMG at least 50 times less permeable than Ca 2+ .','Results (GHK analysis of the NMG reversal potentials)','medium','PRE-ATTRIBUTION BASELINE: channel identity unknown at publication; attributed post-hoc as TMC1/2-complex (rat). Quotes transcribed from the cached PMC full-page render (.scratch/tmc_fulltext/10_1523_jneurosci_2188-06_2006.txt), keeping the source''s italic ''m m'' rendering of mM; other glyphs as printed. REWORK M1 row: ''an average permeability of NMG relative to Cs+ of 0.1'' (GHK analysis) — NMG at least 50 times less permeable than Ca2+; covers the paper''s ion_selectivity flag alongside the archived I_Ca/I_Total fractions. as-reported ratio; schema_gap.','rTmc1+rTmc2_OHC+IHC_WT_P-NMG-P-Cs_GHK',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',157,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(739,'MAIC:BX:00739',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'single-channel events after BAPTA tip-link removal; fluid-jet I-X fits for X_O | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 3','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,85.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'85','pS','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear apical OHCs on Tmc2-/- backgrounds: Tmc1 +/+;Tmc2-/- controls, Tmc1 p.D528N/D528N, Tmc1 p.E520Q, Tmc1 +/+;Tmie-/-;Tmc2-/- and Tmc1 +/+;Lhfpl5-/-;Tmc2-/-; single channels after BAPTA','mouse cochlear outer hair cell (apex)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-84.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00161','this value is smaller than the control value of 85 ± 3 pS ( t test, P = 0.001) in Tmc1 +/+ ;Tmie +/+ ;Tmc2 -/- measured at the same location.','Results (TMIE-null conductance control; Fig 4)','medium','REWORK M4 row: the paper''s OWN same-location control (no citation marker) for the Tmie-/- comparison (63 ± 5 pS row above). CROSS-PAPER BASELINE WARNING: numerically identical to the Beurg 2021 JGP (10.1085/jgp.202112959) apical-OHC events-based 85 ± 3 pS control (same Tmc1 +/+;Tmc2-/- baseline series) — declared for loader dedup. Tmc2-/- background -> TMC1-only channel. Archived: the critique-reported ''148 ± 90 pS in Tmc1+/- and 102 ± 70 pS'' are ANOTHER GROUP''s values (cited) — not rowed; ~40 pS subconductance state; 10-90% working ranges 125 ± 18 nm (Lhfpl5-/-) vs 70 ± 8 nm (control) are operating ranges, NOT x50; unitary CURRENTS 6.8 ± 0.5 pA (control) and macroscopic 28 ± 6 pA (Lhfpl5-/-). Pro-pore for TMC1 with TMIE also pore-implicated.','mTmc1_OHC_apex_Tmc2-KO_Tmie-plus_control_BAPTA-single-channel_-84mV',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',162,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(740,'MAIC:BX:00740',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10-Hz train of 800-nm step bundle deflections by a glass probe to evoke MET currents; paired MET (I_MET) vs background/leak (I_BG) dose-response; external solution 1.3 mM Ca2+',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,6.4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'6.4',NULL,'OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear OHCs: wild type (MET-channel rows); Tmc1-knockout / Tmc2-knockout comparisons for the leak-side analysis (leak values not rowed)','mouse cochlear outer hair cell',NULL,NULL,'standard extracellular saline with 1.3 mM Ca2+',NULL,-70.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00167','Thus, we included an experiment to measure the Ca 2+ permeability of MET channel. The P Na /P Cs is 1.3, while the P Ca /P Cs is 6.4, which is consistent with the report by Kim and Fettiplace, (2013).','Author-response section (eLife peer-review responses; added MET-channel Ca2+-permeability experiment)','medium','PROVENANCE DECLARED (rework F1): the values come from the AUTHOR-RESPONSE section (a reviewer-prompted supplementary experiment included in the published eLife article''s response), not the main Results; ''consistent with the report by Kim and Fettiplace, (2013)''. MET-channel ratios; the leak-channel P_Ca/P_Cs ~0 / P_Na/P_Cs 0.7 (Fig 6 C-D) are leak-side -> not rowed. REWORK NOTE (review F1): initially judged a zero-row paper (all numerics leak-context); REVOKED by the adversarial review — the Fig 5 legend carries own-data Hill fits for the MET-channel side (TMC-dependent, tip-link-gated currents evoked by 800-nm glass-probe bundle steps) and the author-response section adds MET permeability ratios. The MET-side values are rowed (5 ic50 + 2 ion_selectivity_ratio); the LEAK-side IC50 values (DHS 487 µM Hill -0.65; dTC 82 µM -2.80; amiloride 365 µM -1.67; Gd3+ 524 µM -2.49; La3+ 531 µM -5.67) remain NOT rowed (leak-conductance context out of mechano scope), as do the leak currents (I_Leak -51 ± 3 vs -17 ± 2 pA etc.), resting Vm values, and the figure-only permeation series.','mTmc1+mTmc2_OHC_WT_MET-channel_P-Ca-P-Cs_author-response',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',168,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(741,'MAIC:BX:00741',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10-Hz train of 800-nm step bundle deflections by a glass probe to evoke MET currents; paired MET (I_MET) vs background/leak (I_BG) dose-response; external solution 1.3 mM Ca2+',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.3',NULL,'OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','native mouse cochlear OHCs: wild type (MET-channel rows); Tmc1-knockout / Tmc2-knockout comparisons for the leak-side analysis (leak values not rowed)','mouse cochlear outer hair cell',NULL,NULL,'standard extracellular saline with 1.3 mM Ca2+',NULL,-70.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00168','Thus, we included an experiment to measure the Ca 2+ permeability of MET channel. The P Na /P Cs is 1.3, while the P Ca /P Cs is 6.4, which is consistent with the report by Kim and Fettiplace, (2013).','Author-response section (eLife peer-review responses; added MET-channel Ca2+-permeability experiment)','medium','PROVENANCE DECLARED (rework F1): the values come from the AUTHOR-RESPONSE section (a reviewer-prompted supplementary experiment included in the published eLife article''s response), not the main Results; ''consistent with the report by Kim and Fettiplace, (2013)''. MET-channel ratios; the leak-channel P_Ca/P_Cs ~0 / P_Na/P_Cs 0.7 (Fig 6 C-D) are leak-side -> not rowed. REWORK NOTE (review F1): initially judged a zero-row paper (all numerics leak-context); REVOKED by the adversarial review — the Fig 5 legend carries own-data Hill fits for the MET-channel side (TMC-dependent, tip-link-gated currents evoked by 800-nm glass-probe bundle steps) and the author-response section adds MET permeability ratios. The MET-side values are rowed (5 ic50 + 2 ion_selectivity_ratio); the LEAK-side IC50 values (DHS 487 µM Hill -0.65; dTC 82 µM -2.80; amiloride 365 µM -1.67; Gd3+ 524 µM -2.49; La3+ 531 µM -5.67) remain NOT rowed (leak-conductance context out of mechano scope), as do the leak currents (I_Leak -51 ± 3 vs -17 ± 2 pA etc.), resting Vm values, and the figure-only permeation series.','mTmc1+mTmc2_OHC_WT_MET-channel_P-Na-P-Cs_author-response',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',168,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(742,'MAIC:BX:00742',8,NULL,NULL,119,'stiff glass probe delivering 15 step bundle deflections from -175 to 1050 nm; whole-cell transduction currents; activation curves fitted per cell with P0 = 1/(1+exp[-Z(X-X0)/kBT]) and averaged (means ± SEM) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 70 (sem)','X50',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,566.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'566','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — wild-type WT-TMC1 or point mutants (G411A, G518A, G539A, G539I, D528N, R601A, D528N/R601F); rescue paradigm: no native TMC1/TMC2, other MET-complex components present','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,7.4,'standard extracellular solution, pH 7.4 (~310 mOsm/kg)',NULL,-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00169','In addition, the activation curve was shifted to the right by nearly 190 nm (566 ± 70 nm compared to 380 ± 32 nm).','Results (D528A; Fig 5, C and D and table S2)','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. REWORK F2 row: D528A has a text value (previously misclassified as table-only in the pilot notes — wording corrected there); the marked slope change (''40% reduction in the slope'') means the shift partly reflects slope change (''this apparent shift ... can be accounted for by the marked change in the slope; the resting open probability was not altered''). Companion D528E remains table-S2/figure-only (not rowed). Rescue-paradigm caveat: the TMC1 variant is the only TMC in the Tmc1/2-DKO IHCs, but native MET-complex partners (tip link, LHFPL5, TMIE, CIB2) are present — attribution follows the round''s contested convention. ARCHIVED (no parameter_kind home): apparent mechanical-sensitivity slope factors Z in pN (WT 0.027 ± 0.003 pN; G411A 0.017 pN — ''reduced force sensitivity''; D528A/D528N/D528E slope reductions; two-state energy interpretations ~0.5 kBT); maximum currents (WT-TMC1 and mutants, pA); resting open probabilities (~6% WT vs ~20% D528N). Conductance Y-flag -> NO row: the nonstationary-noise values are single-channel CURRENTS in pA (WT-TMC1 12.5 ± 2.5 pA; D528N 3.5 ± 0.5 pA; G411A 14 ± 3.5 pA; G518A 12 ± 2.5 pA; G539A 14 ± 2.5 pA; G539I 14 ± 3 pA), not conductances (''Current magnitudes (pA) are NOT conductance''). D528E midpoints are table S2/figure-only (not rowed); D528A DOES have a text value (X 0 = 566 ± 70 nm; ''shifted to the right by nearly 190 nm'') and is rowed as two scale-v1 rework rows appended after the pilot (review F2).','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-D528A_stiff-probe_-175-to-1050nm_Boltzmann-X0_per-cell-fits-averaged',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',149,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(743,'MAIC:BX:00743',8,NULL,NULL,119,'stiff glass probe delivering 15 step bundle deflections from -175 to 1050 nm; whole-cell transduction currents; activation curves fitted per cell with P0 = 1/(1+exp[-Z(X-X0)/kBT]) and averaged (means ± SEM)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,190.0,'nm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'190','nm','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','inner hair cells of Tmc1/2 double-knockout mice virally transduced (AAV) with mouse TMC1 — wild-type WT-TMC1 or point mutants (G411A, G518A, G539A, G539I, D528N, R601A, D528N/R601F); rescue paradigm: no native TMC1/TMC2, other MET-complex components present','mouse cochlear inner hair cell',NULL,7.4,'standard extracellular solution, pH 7.4 (~310 mOsm/kg)',NULL,-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00170','In addition, the activation curve was shifted to the right by nearly 190 nm (566 ± 70 nm compared to 380 ± 32 nm).','Results (D528A; ''shifted to the right by nearly 190 nm'')','medium','pore identity contested (electrophysiological attribution vs structural skepticism); mechano_gating_contested=true. Stimulus is stereocilia bundle displacement (fluid jet / stiff probe), mapped to the x50 slot — the hair-cell MET stimulus is bundle DISPLACEMENT (nm), not pressure. REWORK F2 row: the paper''s own explicitly stated shift magnitude (''nearly 190 nm''), value_relation ''~''; endpoints rowed (WT 380 ± 32 and D528A 566 ± 70 nm x50 rows). DEMOTED to schema_gap: nm displacement shift but delta_p50_* is pressure-unit-only. Rescue-paradigm caveat: the TMC1 variant is the only TMC in the Tmc1/2-DKO IHCs, but native MET-complex partners (tip link, LHFPL5, TMIE, CIB2) are present — attribution follows the round''s contested convention. ARCHIVED (no parameter_kind home): apparent mechanical-sensitivity slope factors Z in pN (WT 0.027 ± 0.003 pN; G411A 0.017 pN — ''reduced force sensitivity''; D528A/D528N/D528E slope reductions; two-state energy interpretations ~0.5 kBT); maximum currents (WT-TMC1 and mutants, pA); resting open probabilities (~6% WT vs ~20% D528N). Conductance Y-flag -> NO row: the nonstationary-noise values are single-channel CURRENTS in pA (WT-TMC1 12.5 ± 2.5 pA; D528N 3.5 ± 0.5 pA; G411A 14 ± 3.5 pA; G518A 12 ± 2.5 pA; G539A 14 ± 2.5 pA; G539I 14 ± 3 pA), not conductances (''Current magnitudes (pA) are NOT conductance''). D528E midpoints are table S2/figure-only (not rowed); D528A DOES have a text value (X 0 = 566 ± 70 nm; ''shifted to the right by nearly 190 nm'') and is rowed as two scale-v1 rework rows appended after the pilot (review F2).','mTmc1_IHC_Tmc1/2-DKO_AAV-D528A_X0-rightward-shift-vs-WT-rescue_stiff-probe',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',149,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(744,'MAIC:BX:00744',8,NULL,NULL,120,'fire-polished ~2-µm-tip glass stimulation pipette driven by a piezo controller poking the cell surface, 1-8 µm steps, 300-ms duration, 10-s intervals; I-V by -60 to +60 mV ramps/steps with 8-µm stimuli | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.48 (sem)','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.99,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.99','mV','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','Piezo1-KO HEK293T cells transiently co-transfected with HA-tagged wild-type full-length human TMC1 or TMC2 plus shUROD (UROD knockdown enables plasma-membrane trafficking); room temperature','HEK293T (Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,7.3,'133 NaCl, 2.5 CaCl2, 3 KCl, 1 MgCl2, 10 D-glucose, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (NaOH), 300-310 mOsm','133 CsCl, 1 MgCl2, 1 CaCl2, 5 EGTA, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (CsOH), 300-310 mOsm',-60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00171','The current-voltage relationships of mouse TMC1-H353A and TMC2-H406A mechanically activated currents in Piezo1-KO HEK293T cells were linear between -60 and +60 mV, with reversal potentials of 0.99 ± 0.48 and 0.33 ± 1.13 mV (Figures 2G and 2H), respectively.','Results (mouse TMC1-H353A / TMC2-H406A I-V; Fig 2, G and H)','high','heterologous isolated-channel system (Piezo1-KO HEK293T expressing only TMC1/2; no native MET complex ambiguity) -> confidence high per the round ruling. REWORK M2 row: previously archived without a landed quote; the Cell Press page was re-fetched this batch (cache extended with the full STAR Methods) and the sentence landed in extract_quotes_scale-v1.json before rowing. Mouse point-mutant channels (membrane-trafficking mutations in TM3), absolute E_rev, linear I-V. The pilot archive note was corrected to point here. Archived (not rowed): current densities -17.78 ± 5.73 / -14.65 ± 3.93 pA/pF and amplitudes -215.2 ± 66.28 / -237.1 ± 54.29 pA (current magnitudes, not conductance); responding-cell ratios 65.22% / 80.77%; blocker sensitivity (GdCl3 10 µM, DHS 200 µM, FM1-43 300 µM, GsMTx-4 5 µM) qualitative -> no pharmacology rows; Na+-dependence (NMDG-Cl vs Na-gluconate) qualitative; mouse mutant MmTMC1-H353A / MmTMC2-H406A E_revs 0.99 ± 0.48 / 0.33 ± 1.13 mV -- ROWED as two scale-v1 rework rows (review M2) with the quote re-verified from the Cell Press page (cache extended with the full STAR Methods this batch); single-channel open-probability-vs-pressure figure data.','mTmc1_HEK293T-Piezo1KO_H353A_point-mutant_linear-I-V_-60-to-+60mV_Fig2G-H',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',147,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(745,'MAIC:BX:00745',8,NULL,NULL,121,'fire-polished ~2-µm-tip glass stimulation pipette driven by a piezo controller poking the cell surface, 1-8 µm steps, 300-ms duration, 10-s intervals; I-V by -60 to +60 mV ramps/steps with 8-µm stimuli | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 1.13 (sem)','FULL_CARD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.33,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.33','mV','INDENTATION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','Piezo1-KO HEK293T cells transiently co-transfected with HA-tagged wild-type full-length human TMC1 or TMC2 plus shUROD (UROD knockdown enables plasma-membrane trafficking); room temperature','HEK293T (Piezo1 knockout)',NULL,7.3,'133 NaCl, 2.5 CaCl2, 3 KCl, 1 MgCl2, 10 D-glucose, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (NaOH), 300-310 mOsm','133 CsCl, 1 MgCl2, 1 CaCl2, 5 EGTA, 10 HEPES, pH 7.3 (CsOH), 300-310 mOsm',-60.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TMC-EX-00172','The current-voltage relationships of mouse TMC1-H353A and TMC2-H406A mechanically activated currents in Piezo1-KO HEK293T cells were linear between -60 and +60 mV, with reversal potentials of 0.99 ± 0.48 and 0.33 ± 1.13 mV (Figures 2G and 2H), respectively.','Results (mouse TMC1-H353A / TMC2-H406A I-V; Fig 2, G and H)','high','heterologous isolated-channel system (Piezo1-KO HEK293T expressing only TMC1/2; no native MET complex ambiguity) -> confidence high per the round ruling. REWORK M2 row: previously archived without a landed quote; the Cell Press page was re-fetched this batch (cache extended with the full STAR Methods) and the sentence landed in extract_quotes_scale-v1.json before rowing. Mouse point-mutant channels (membrane-trafficking mutations in TM3), absolute E_rev, linear I-V. The pilot archive note was corrected to point here. Archived (not rowed): current densities -17.78 ± 5.73 / -14.65 ± 3.93 pA/pF and amplitudes -215.2 ± 66.28 / -237.1 ± 54.29 pA (current magnitudes, not conductance); responding-cell ratios 65.22% / 80.77%; blocker sensitivity (GdCl3 10 µM, DHS 200 µM, FM1-43 300 µM, GsMTx-4 5 µM) qualitative -> no pharmacology rows; Na+-dependence (NMDG-Cl vs Na-gluconate) qualitative; mouse mutant MmTMC1-H353A / MmTMC2-H406A E_revs 0.99 ± 0.48 / 0.33 ± 1.13 mV -- ROWED as two scale-v1 rework rows (review M2) with the quote re-verified from the Cell Press page (cache extended with the full STAR Methods this batch); single-channel open-probability-vs-pressure figure data.','mTmc2_HEK293T-Piezo1KO_H406A_point-mutant_linear-I-V_-60-to-+60mV_Fig2G-H',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',147,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(746,'MAIC:BX:00746',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'single-channel recordings during 10-ms ultrasound (1.2 W/cm2 at 5 MHz) or pressure (-30 mmHg) steps','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,73.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'73.0','pS','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocyte (injected cRNA, H. sapiens TRAAK Q9NYG8-1)',NULL,25.0,NULL,'140 mM KCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, 1 mM EGTA, pH 7.1 (KOH)','14 mM KCl, 126 mM NaCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (KOH)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00001','Single channels were confirmed to be TRAAK by their K+ selectivity, single-channel conductance of ∼73 pS at positive potentials; The single-channel current elicited by ultrasound (blue) and pressure (purple) versus voltage (n = 5 patches). The linear fits from 20 mV to 80 mV and the derived conductance is shown.','Results, single-channel paragraph (Fig 3, A-C; fits in Fig 3B)','high','复合 quote 披露（F-004 政策，2026-08-30 补注）：evidence_quote 为两段原文 span 以 '';'' 并置——前段 Results 正文句（''∼73 pS'' 数值载体），后段 Fig 3 图注句（I-V 拟合 20-80 mV 的图注依据，装配披露此前仅见于 evidence_location，F-004 要求入 note）。原文 ''∼73 pS''（约等号），value_relation=~。Fig 3B 拟合范围 20-80 mV（正电位），n=5 patches；flickery 行为含亚电导态，73 pS 为全电导。25 °C（Methods）。开放概率（1.9±0.7%、6.3±3.3%、26±9.7%）与 dwell time 全套（短开 0.79±0.06/1.22±0.15/0.93±0.20 ms；长开 3.20±0.72/3.01±0.94/5.9±2.53 ms；短闭 0.78±0.14/0.96±0.16/1.40±0.52 ms；长闭 193.10±62.17/22.61±10.37/39.23±11.52 ms）无 parameter_kind home，不 row（开放概率百分比/dwell time 裁决）. [F-004:composite] multi-span assembly (2 fragments all verbatim in archived corpus; assembled quote not contiguous in source; classified 2026-08-31)','traak_conductance_inside-out_oocyte_positive-potentials','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(747,'MAIC:BX:00747',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10-ms ultrasound step at 5 MHz (macroscopic current at V test = 0 mV) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.02 (sem)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.23,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.23','ms','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocyte (injected cRNA, H. sapiens TRAAK Q9NYG8-1)',NULL,25.0,NULL,'140 mM KCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, 1 mM EGTA, pH 7.1 (KOH)','14 mM KCl, 126 mM NaCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (KOH)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00002','Ultrasound activates TRAAK currents approximately four times faster than pressure (𝜏activation, ultrasound = 0.23 ± 0.02 ms, 𝜏activation, pressure = 0.91 ± 0.07 ms (mean ± SEM, n = 15 and 12 records, respectively, from 3 patches from 3 cells) (Fig. 1F)','Results, kinetics paragraph (Fig 1 E and F)','high','宏观电流激活时间常数（V test = 0 mV）。stimulus_type=OTHER：超声刺激不在词表内（原文 ultrasound step, 5 MHz）。n=15 records 来自 3 patches/3 cells；论文指出超声 τ 更接近本征动力学（压力 τ 被压力钳装置 1.3 ms 时间常数滤波）。','traak_tau_act_ultrasound_oocyte_0mV','15','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(748,'MAIC:BX:00748',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure step via HSPC (macroscopic current at V test = 0 mV) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.07 (sem)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.91,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.91','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocyte (injected cRNA, H. sapiens TRAAK Q9NYG8-1)',NULL,25.0,NULL,'140 mM KCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, 1 mM EGTA, pH 7.1 (KOH)','14 mM KCl, 126 mM NaCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (KOH)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00003','Ultrasound activates TRAAK currents approximately four times faster than pressure (𝜏activation, ultrasound = 0.23 ± 0.02 ms, 𝜏activation, pressure = 0.91 ± 0.07 ms (mean ± SEM, n = 15 and 12 records, respectively, from 3 patches from 3 cells) (Fig. 1F)','Results, kinetics paragraph (Fig 1 E and F)','high','宏观电流激活时间常数。n=12 records 来自 3 patches/3 cells；论文注明压力激活 τ 受压力钳装置滤波（装置上升时间常数 1.3 ms）。','traak_tau_act_pressure_oocyte_0mV','12','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(749,'MAIC:BX:00749',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'current decay upon removal of 10-ms ultrasound step at 5 MHz (V test = 0 mV) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.02 (sem)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.28,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.28','ms','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocyte (injected cRNA, H. sapiens TRAAK Q9NYG8-1)',NULL,25.0,NULL,'140 mM KCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, 1 mM EGTA, pH 7.1 (KOH)','14 mM KCl, 126 mM NaCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (KOH)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00004','Ultrasound-activated currents similarly decay faster than pressure-activated currents upon stimulus removal (𝜏close, ultrasound = 0.28 ± 0.02, 𝜏close, pressure = 1.21 ± 0.06 (n = 15 and 12 records, respectively, from 3 patches from 3 cells)','Results, kinetics paragraph (Fig 1 E and F)','high','原文 ''𝜏 close, ultrasound = 0.28 ± 0.02'' 数值旁未重复单位，按同句 𝜏 activation 的 ms 上下文与 Fig 1F 纵轴记 unit=ms。tau_deact 语义 = 刺激移除后的关闭/衰减 τ（原文 ''decay faster ... upon stimulus removal''）。n=15 records，3 patches/3 cells。stimulus_type=OTHER（超声不在词表）。','traak_tau_deact_ultrasound_oocyte_0mV','15','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(750,'MAIC:BX:00750',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'current decay upon removal of negative pressure step (V test = 0 mV) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.06 (sem)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.21,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.21','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocyte (injected cRNA, H. sapiens TRAAK Q9NYG8-1)',NULL,25.0,NULL,'140 mM KCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, 1 mM EGTA, pH 7.1 (KOH)','14 mM KCl, 126 mM NaCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (KOH)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00005','Ultrasound-activated currents similarly decay faster than pressure-activated currents upon stimulus removal (𝜏close, ultrasound = 0.28 ± 0.02, 𝜏close, pressure = 1.21 ± 0.06 (n = 15 and 12 records, respectively, from 3 patches from 3 cells)','Results, kinetics paragraph (Fig 1 E and F)','high','τ_close 数值旁原文未重复单位（同句 τ activation 为 ms），unit=ms 按上下文。n=12 records，3 patches/3 cells。','traak_tau_deact_pressure_oocyte_0mV','12','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(751,'MAIC:BX:00751',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10-ms ultrasound step at 5 MHz, 0.34 W/cm2 (V test = 0 mV) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.04 (sem)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.32,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.32','ms','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','purified M. musculus TRAAK (Pichia pastoris) reconstituted into soybean PC proteoliposomes',NULL,25.0,NULL,'5 mM HEPES, 200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, pH 7.2 (KOH)','5 mM HEPES, 20 mM KCl, 180 mM NaCl, pH 7.2 (NaOH)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00006','As observed in patches from Xenopus oocytes, ultrasound activation and subsequent channel closure proceeded at faster rates than those observed with pressure (Fig. 5 E and F, 𝜏activation, ultrasound = 0.32 ± 0.04 ms, 𝜏activation, pressure = 1.24 ± 0.10 ms, 𝜏close, ultrasound = 0.37 ± 0.06 ms, 𝜏close, pressure = 1.10 ± 0.14 ms [mean ± SEM, n = 17 records for ultrasound and n = 14 records for pressure from 2 proteoliposomes]).','Results, proteoliposome paragraph (Fig 5 E and F)','high','纯化重构体系（无细胞成分）的激活 τ，证明超声经脂膜双分子层直接激活。n=17 records 来自 2 proteoliposomes。stimulus_type=OTHER（超声）。0.34 W/cm² 为该系列实验刺激功率（Fig 5A）。','traak_tau_act_ultrasound_proteoliposome_0mV','17','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(752,'MAIC:BX:00752',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure step (-30 mmHg; V test = 0 mV) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.1 (sem)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.24,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.24','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','purified M. musculus TRAAK (Pichia pastoris) reconstituted into soybean PC proteoliposomes',NULL,25.0,NULL,'5 mM HEPES, 200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, pH 7.2 (KOH)','5 mM HEPES, 20 mM KCl, 180 mM NaCl, pH 7.2 (NaOH)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00007','As observed in patches from Xenopus oocytes, ultrasound activation and subsequent channel closure proceeded at faster rates than those observed with pressure (Fig. 5 E and F, 𝜏activation, ultrasound = 0.32 ± 0.04 ms, 𝜏activation, pressure = 1.24 ± 0.10 ms, 𝜏close, ultrasound = 0.37 ± 0.06 ms, 𝜏close, pressure = 1.10 ± 0.14 ms [mean ± SEM, n = 17 records for ultrasound and n = 14 records for pressure from 2 proteoliposomes]).','Results, proteoliposome paragraph (Fig 5 E and F)','high','纯化重构体系；与 oocyte 的 τ activation,pressure（0.91 ms）有统计学差异（P=0.012），超声/close 项无差异。n=14 records，2 proteoliposomes。','traak_tau_act_pressure_proteoliposome_0mV','14','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(753,'MAIC:BX:00753',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'current decay upon removal of 10-ms ultrasound step (V test = 0 mV) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.06 (sem)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.37,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0.37','ms','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','purified M. musculus TRAAK (Pichia pastoris) reconstituted into soybean PC proteoliposomes',NULL,25.0,NULL,'5 mM HEPES, 200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, pH 7.2 (KOH)','5 mM HEPES, 20 mM KCl, 180 mM NaCl, pH 7.2 (NaOH)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00008','As observed in patches from Xenopus oocytes, ultrasound activation and subsequent channel closure proceeded at faster rates than those observed with pressure (Fig. 5 E and F, 𝜏activation, ultrasound = 0.32 ± 0.04 ms, 𝜏activation, pressure = 1.24 ± 0.10 ms, 𝜏close, ultrasound = 0.37 ± 0.06 ms, 𝜏close, pressure = 1.10 ± 0.14 ms [mean ± SEM, n = 17 records for ultrasound and n = 14 records for pressure from 2 proteoliposomes]).','Results, proteoliposome paragraph (Fig 5 E and F)','high','τ_close（刺激移除后衰减）。n=17 records，2 proteoliposomes。','traak_tau_deact_ultrasound_proteoliposome_0mV','17','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(754,'MAIC:BX:00754',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'current decay upon removal of negative pressure step (V test = 0 mV) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.14 (sem)','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.1','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','purified M. musculus TRAAK (Pichia pastoris) reconstituted into soybean PC proteoliposomes',NULL,25.0,NULL,'5 mM HEPES, 200 mM KCl, 40 mM MgCl2, pH 7.2 (KOH)','5 mM HEPES, 20 mM KCl, 180 mM NaCl, pH 7.2 (NaOH)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00009','As observed in patches from Xenopus oocytes, ultrasound activation and subsequent channel closure proceeded at faster rates than those observed with pressure (Fig. 5 E and F, 𝜏activation, ultrasound = 0.32 ± 0.04 ms, 𝜏activation, pressure = 1.24 ± 0.10 ms, 𝜏close, ultrasound = 0.37 ± 0.06 ms, 𝜏close, pressure = 1.10 ± 0.14 ms [mean ± SEM, n = 17 records for ultrasound and n = 14 records for pressure from 2 proteoliposomes]).','Results, proteoliposome paragraph (Fig 5 E and F)','high','τ_close。n=14 records，2 proteoliposomes。','traak_tau_deact_pressure_proteoliposome_0mV','14','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(755,'MAIC:BX:00755',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10-ms ultrasound step, 0.5 W/cm2 at 5 MHz | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2 (sem)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-55.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-55.0','mV','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocyte (co-injected TRAAK + TRPV1 cRNA)',NULL,25.0,NULL,'140 mM KCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, 1 mM EGTA, pH 7.1 (KOH)','14 mM KCl, 126 mM NaCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (KOH)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00010','Ultrasound and pressure stimulation resulted in hyperpolarizing shifts of the reversal potential toward EK+ (from -43 ± 1 mV to -55 ± 2 mV and -52 ± 2 mV, respectively [mean ± SEM, n = 3 patches]) (Fig. 2 E and F), consistent with activation of K+-selective TRAAK channels.',NULL,'medium','TRAAK+TRPV1 共表达 patch 的混合电流 Erev：超声激活后由 -43±1 mV（基础）超极化移向 E_K+（-59 mV 计算值），证明激活成分为 K+ 选择性 TRAAK。混合表达背景扣 confidence（非 TRAAK 单表达）。基础态 -43±1 mV 与热激活（TRPV1 主导）-27±8 mV 不 row（非 TRAAK 激活态）。','traak_erev_ultrasound_trpv1-coexpression','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(756,'MAIC:BX:00756',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10-ms negative pressure step, -35 mmHg | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2 (sem)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-52.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-52.0','mV','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocyte (co-injected TRAAK + TRPV1 cRNA)',NULL,25.0,NULL,'140 mM KCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, 1 mM EGTA, pH 7.1 (KOH)','14 mM KCl, 126 mM NaCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (KOH)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00011','Ultrasound and pressure stimulation resulted in hyperpolarizing shifts of the reversal potential toward EK+ (from -43 ± 1 mV to -55 ± 2 mV and -52 ± 2 mV, respectively [mean ± SEM, n = 3 patches]) (Fig. 2 E and F), consistent with activation of K+-selective TRAAK channels.',NULL,'medium','同上共表达背景；压力激活电流 Erev -52±2 mV，移向 E_K+ 证明 K+ 选择性 TRAAK 激活。混合表达背景扣 confidence。 | ARCHIVE（不 row 理由）：① threshold Y-flag 无行——超声功率-响应中点 0.80±0.05 W/cm2（oocyte, n=6 patches, Boltzmann 拟合）与 0.78±0.04 W/cm2（proteoliposome, n=7）为拟合中点但单位 W/cm2 无 p50/t50/x50 词表 home（PressureUnit 仅压力、TensionUnit 仅张力），归档不 row；10-90% 激活范围 0.3-1.1 / 0.2-1.25 W/cm2 同理。② 最大激活倍数 21.9±5.2-fold（n=6）为固定刺激倍数不 row。③ 神经元全细胞数据（3.6 W/cm2 激活，峰值 407.40±50.77 pA；Erev -77.70±1.44/-71.20±9.74/-75.45±1.49 mV）为 pA 幅度/全细胞混合电流，不 row。④ 亚电导幅度 ~1.25/~2.5 pA 不 row（pA 非 pS 电导）。⑤ 0.15/0.8 ms 刺激达 ~50%/~95% 最大电流（持续时间-响应）无 home。⑥ TRPV1 对照值（capsaicin 6.5±1.1-fold 等）非 TRAAK。⑦ E_K+=-59 mV 为 Nernst 计算值非测量。⑧ TASK2 超声无反应为阴性对照。','traak_erev_pressure_trpv1-coexpression','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',179,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(757,'MAIC:BX:00757',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure step via open-loop pressure system | STIMULUS: -66 mm Hg','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,38.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'38.0','pS','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','COS-7 stable TRAAK cell line',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EXT with 150 mM KCl replacing 150 mM NaCl (KCl-rich, cell-attached bath)','150 mM NaCl, 5 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 1 mM CaCl2, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.4 (EXT)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00012','channel activity is absent at atmospheric pressure but three TRAAK 38-picosiemens channels readily and reversibly open during the application of a -66 mm Hg pressure','Results, cell-attached stretch paragraph (Fig 3, A and B)','high','TRAAK 机械门控首鉴定论文的单通道电导；原文拼写 ''38-picosiemens channels''（数值 38），unit 规范记 pS。0 mV 静息 NPo 0.05±0.03（n=6）与 fold 激活（AA 4.8±0.4、TNP 6.7±1.1）无 kind home 不 row。温度未注明。','traak_conductance_cell-attached_cos_0mV',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',180,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(758,'MAIC:BX:00758',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MODULATOR: arachidonic acid (agonist) 10 µM | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-83.7,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-83.7','mV',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHOLE_CELL','COS-7 stable TRAAK cell line',NULL,NULL,NULL,'150 mM NaCl, 5 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 1 mM CaCl2, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.4 (EXT)','150 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 5 mM EGTA, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.2 (INT)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00013','The reversal potential of the current activated by AA reverses at -83.7 ± 0.7 mV (n = 12), which is the predicted value for E K+','Results, whole-cell AA/TNP paragraph (Fig 2A)','high','AA（10 µM，Fig 2B legend）激活的全细胞电流 Erev，与预测 E_K+ 一致（K+ 选择性）。error_type 原文未标注（无 SEM/SD 说明）留空。I-V 为 -80 mV 保持电位下 800-ms 电压斜坡。','traak_erev_aa_whole-cell_cos','12','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',180,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(759,'MAIC:BX:00759',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure activation (-33 mm Hg in Fig 4B ramp), 800-ms voltage ramp',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-80.0','mV','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','COS-7 stable TRAAK cell line',NULL,NULL,NULL,'150 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 5 mM EGTA, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.2 (INT, intracellular face)','150 mM NaCl, 5 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 1 mM CaCl2, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.4 (EXT)',-80.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00014','The I-V curve performed with a voltage ramp protocol in physiological K+ conditions is outwardly rectifying and reverses at -80 mV, the predicted value for the equilibrium potential for K+','Results, inside-out paragraph (Fig 4B)','medium','无误差/n 报告，confidence=medium。保持电位 -80 mV 为斜坡起点（Fig 4B legend）。仅负压（非正压）激活 inside-out TRAAK（方向性证据）。','traak_erev_pressure_inside-out_cos',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',180,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(760,'MAIC:BX:00760',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure steps via high-speed pressure servo (every 3-5 s) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 3.4','P50',-65.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-65.0','mm Hg','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'COS cells (transfected TRAAK)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'150 mM NaCl, 5 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 1 mM CaCl2, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.4 (physiological K+ gradient)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00016','The average P1/2 value determined by fitting pressure-effect curves with a Boltzmann function (see Fig. 6D) was -65.0 ± 3.4 mm Hg (significantly different from TREK-1; P < 0.01) and the slope factor k was 8.1 ± 0.5 (n = 15)','Results, TRAAK paragraph (Fig 2A; Boltzmann fits in SI Fig 6D)','high','Boltzmann 拟合的 TRAAK 压力半激活 P1/2（n=15）；原文单位拼写 ''mm Hg''（带空格）as-reported，DB 归一 mmHg。原文未明示 TRAAK P1/2 拟合所用 patch 模式（cell-attached 与 inside-out 均在文中使用；对应 TREK-1 段为 inside-out），recording_mode 留空。error_type 原文未标注。温度未注明。1 mmHg = 133 Pa. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','traak_p50_boltzmann_cos','15','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',181,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(761,'MAIC:BX:00761',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure steps via high-speed pressure servo (every 3-5 s) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.5',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,8.1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'8.1',NULL,'PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'COS cells (transfected TRAAK)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'150 mM NaCl, 5 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 1 mM CaCl2, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.4 (physiological K+ gradient)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00017','The average P1/2 value determined by fitting pressure-effect curves with a Boltzmann function (see Fig. 6D) was -65.0 ± 3.4 mm Hg (significantly different from TREK-1; P < 0.01) and the slope factor k was 8.1 ± 0.5 (n = 15)','Results, TRAAK paragraph (Fig 2A; Boltzmann fits in SI Fig 6D)','high','与 P1/2 同一拟合的斜率因子 k（无单位标注；按 I=iN/(1+e^k(P-P1/2)) 形式 k 携带 mmHg^-1，schema hill_slope 为无量纲——as-reported unit 留空，勿与 Sorum 2024 的 mN/m slope factor 约定混用）。error_type 未标注. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','traak_hill-slope_boltzmann_cos','15','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',181,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(762,'MAIC:BX:00762',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'sustained -50 mmHg pressure step via high-speed pressure servo | STIMULUS: -50 mmHg | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 1.5','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,24.2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'24.2','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','COS cells (transfected TRAAK)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'150 mM NaCl, 5 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 1 mM CaCl2, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.4 (physiological K+ gradient)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00018','Currents from TRAAK channels behaved similarly to those from TREK-1 in both cell-attached (τ = 24.2 ± 1.5 ms at -50 mmHg; n = 16) and after excision (τ = 27.1 ± 1.5 ms at -50 mmHg; n = 26)','Results, TRAAK paragraph (Fig 2A)','high','持续压力刺激中的单指数脱敏 τ → tau_inact（刺激未撤除，非 tau_deact；延续 trek-1 轮对同论文 TREK-1 46/76 ms 的裁决）。error_type 未标注。温度未注明. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','traak_tau_inact_cell-attached_-50mmhg','16','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',181,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(763,'MAIC:BX:00763',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'sustained -50 mmHg pressure step via high-speed pressure servo | STIMULUS: -50 mmHg | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 1.5','KINETICS_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,27.1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'27.1','ms','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','COS cells (transfected TRAAK)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'150 mM NaCl, 5 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 1 mM CaCl2, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.4 (physiological K+ gradient)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00019','Currents from TRAAK channels behaved similarly to those from TREK-1 in both cell-attached (τ = 24.2 ± 1.5 ms at -50 mmHg; n = 16) and after excision (τ = 27.1 ± 1.5 ms at -50 mmHg; n = 26)','Results, TRAAK paragraph (Fig 2A)','high','excision 后脱敏 τ（n=26），与 cell-attached 无显著差异（脱敏为通道自身属性；blebs 实验佐证，Fig 9 SI）。error_type 未标注。 | ARCHIVE（不 row 理由）：① delta_p50 flag unclear 无行——pH_i/AA/E306A/CPZ 仅方向性描述 P1/2 位移（''shifting P1/2 toward lower pressures''），无量化 delta-P1/2 mmHg 值。② tau_deact N——''closed immediately when the pressure returned to zero''，恢复需 ≈1 s 非拟合 τ。③ paralog 值全部归档：TREK-1 P1/2 -53.1±3.5/k 10.1±0.69/τ 46±4.2（ca）/76±6.7（io）/56.9±11.1（latrunculin）/35.2±4.1（nocodazole）/60.8±3.8（-80 mV）/72.8±7.7（+80 mV）/ΔC100 τ 22.4±3.1 ms；TREK-2 P1/2 -49.9±5.0/k 18.3±1.3（trek-1/trek-2 轮已提取其 WT 行）。④ TREK-1 电流幅度 365±184/1448±314/346±85/1751±349 pA 为 pA 幅度不 row。⑤ 面积变化 ΔA ≈2 nm2（abstract）/＞1.8 nm2、速率敏感度 k23^1=-0.06/mmHg、seal adhesion 2-3 mN/m 无 parameter_kind home。⑥ 单通道脱敏表现为开放率下降、unitary 电流不变（Fig 2E，定性）. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','traak_tau_inact_inside-out_-50mmhg','26','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',181,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(764,'MAIC:BX:00764',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pressure steps with simultaneous patch imaging; tension via Young-Laplace T = ΔPr/2 (EGFP-CAAX, 120 Hz) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.2 (sem)','T50',NULL,NULL,4.4,'mN/m',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'4.4','mN/m','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocyte (injected cRNA, H. sapiens TRAAK Q9NYG8-2)',NULL,25.0,NULL,'150 mM KCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 1 mM EGTA, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.1 (KOH)','15 mM KCl, 135 mM NaCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (KOH)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00020','TRAAK was activated over a broad range of tension with a midpoint T50 = 4.4 ± 0.2 mN/m, slope factor 1.7 ± 0.2 mN/m, and 10-90% activation range 0.6-8.2 mN/m (mean ± SEM, n = 12 patches)','Results, tension-response paragraph (Fig 2, B and E)','high','0 mV 记录、10 倍 K+ 梯度；n=12 patches（来自 5 个细胞）。10-90% 激活范围 0.6-8.2 mN/m 无词表 home 不 row。TRAAK 为三 K2P 中张力最敏感者（TREK-1 6.4±0.2、TREK-2 5.8±0.1 mN/m 为 paralog，trek-1/trek-2 轮已提取，不 row）。','traak_t50_tension_oocyte_10fold-K-gradient','12','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',182,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(765,'MAIC:BX:00765',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pressure steps with simultaneous patch imaging; tension via Young-Laplace T = ΔPr/2 (EGFP-CAAX, 120 Hz) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 0.2 (sem)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1.7,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1.7','mN/m','PRESSURE_CLAMP',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','Xenopus laevis oocyte (injected cRNA, H. sapiens TRAAK Q9NYG8-2)',NULL,25.0,NULL,'150 mM KCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 1 mM EGTA, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.1 (KOH)','15 mM KCl, 135 mM NaCl, 2 mM MgCl2, 10 mM HEPES, pH 7.4 (KOH)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00021','TRAAK was activated over a broad range of tension with a midpoint T50 = 4.4 ± 0.2 mN/m, slope factor 1.7 ± 0.2 mN/m, and 10-90% activation range 0.6-8.2 mN/m (mean ± SEM, n = 12 patches)','Results, tension-response paragraph (Fig 2, B and E)','high','slope factor（Boltzmann 张力-响应拟合斜率因子，单位 mN/m，as-reported）——与 Honoré 2006 的无量纲指数 k 是两种不同约定，勿混用（延续 trek-2 轮裁决）。n=12 patches（5 cells）。 | ARCHIVE（不 row 理由）：① conductance Y-flag 无行——''single-channel currents of ~1-2 pA under these conditions'' 为 pA 单通道电流幅度非 pS 电导（裁决：pA 不 row）。② 压力激活最大倍数 41.2±14.2-fold（n=12）为固定刺激倍数不 row。③ 超声（3.5 MHz）功率中点 1.8±0.07 W/cm2、2.25 MHz 0.38±0.01 W/cm2（n=17/6 patches）为拟合中点但 W/cm2 无 p50 词表 home，归档；超声激活倍数 16.2±4.2/19.3±4.2-fold 不 row。④ ΔA=2.4 nm2、ΔG=10.5×10^-21 J（2.6 kBT）无 parameter_kind home。⑤ TREK-1 T50 6.4±0.2/slope 2.3±0.2、TREK-2 5.8±0.1/slope 1.4±0.1、MscS T50 3.7±0.2/slope 1.1±0.2/14.6±4.0-fold 为 paralog/细菌通道不 row。⑥ 最低可测张力 0.36 mN/m、basal tension ~0.5-4 mN/m（引 Opsahl & Webb）、讨论中 threshold ~1 mN/m 为估计/方法学约束不 row。⑦ 讨论 TRAAK 与平面双分子层研究（0.8-5.7 mN/m）一致性为引文。','traak_hill-slope_tension_oocyte_10fold-K-gradient','12','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',182,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(766,'MAIC:BX:00766',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'negative pressure steps (-66 mm Hg applications) via open-loop pressure system; Boltzmann fit of pressure-effect relationship | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 2','P50',-46.0,'mmHg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'-46.0','mm Hg','SUCTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','COS cells (DEAE-dextran transient, murine TRAAK, pIRES-CD8)',NULL,NULL,7.2,'150 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 5 mM EGTA, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.2 (INT, intracellular face)','150 mM NaCl, 5 mM KCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 1 mM CaCl2, 10 mM Hepes, pH 7.4 (EXT)',0.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00022','Unlike TREK-1, TRAAK, the other stretch- and AA-sensitive member of the 4TMS/2P K+ channel family (P 0.5 = -46 ± 2 at pH 7.2; n = 7) is quite insensitive to intracellular acidosis; TRAAK is significantly (p< 0.05) less sensitive to stretch (P 0.5 = -46 ± 2 mm Hg)','Results, TRAAK pH-insensitivity paragraph (Fig 6, A and D) + Discussion','high','复合 quote 披露（F-004 政策，2026-08-31 勘误补注）：evidence_quote 为原文多处 span 并置（composite 登记册在录，basis = note-disclosed——本层无该行人工裁决记录，jbc.274.38.26691 归档 abstract-only、span 不可离线复核）；登记册 tools/literature-mining/configs/composite_quote_registry.json。TREK-1 主场论文中内藏的 TRAAK 压力 P50（Boltzmann 拟合，pH_i 7.2，n=7）：Results 段数值无单位，Discussion 重述带 ''mm Hg''——两 span 以 '';'' 拼接，unit 取 mm Hg。0 mV/inside-out 上下文取自 Fig 6A legend。TRAAK 对 pH_i 7.2→5.0 不敏感（Fig 6D，无数值）。error_type 未标注。温度未注明。 | ARCHIVE（不 row 理由）：① TREK-1 全部数值为 paralog——P0.5 -36.8±2.1 mmHg（pH_i 7.2, n=13, inside-out）/Discussion -36±2、HCO3- 激活 5.5±0.5-fold（n=29）、pH 半效 pH_i 6.0/5.9、Δ46/Δ89/Δ100/Δ103/Δ113 突变体系（Δ103 曲线右移 ~60 mmHg）、E_K=-80 mV/TREK-1 HCO3 与 CO2 电流 Erev。② TRAAK/TREK-1 chimera（TRAAK core Gly-255 + TREK-1 C-ter Gly-293~Thr-368）P0.5 -40±3（pH 7.2, n=7）/-32±5（pH 6.0, n=4）/-26±3（pH 5.0, n=4）与 HCO3 激活 3.8±0.4（n=10）为嵌合体构造非 TRAAK 野生型，归档（延续 TRAAK 轮 paralog/chimera 裁决）。③ TRAAK HCO3- 无效（0.9±0.1, n=17）为阴性 fold 结果。④ intro/discussion 引述文献值（100 pS at +50 mV 对称 K+、94/143 pS、-12~-18 mmHg）为转引不 row. [F-004:undetermined] junction not certifiable offline (no fulltext corpus (abstract-only fallback); classified 2026-08-31)','traak_p05_inside-out_cos_phi7.2','7','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',183,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(767,'MAIC:BX:00767',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'voltage clamp, single-channel I-V -90 to +160 mV in 20 mV steps; slope fitted 0-160 mV | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 3.7','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45.5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'45.5','pS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'INSIDE_OUT','COS cells, transient transfection (pIREScd8-TRAAK)','COS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00023','The slope conductance measured between 0 and 160 mV is 45.5 6 3.7 pS (n 5 10).','Results (COS-cell expression paragraph); Fig 5E-F','high','MinerU OCR: ''6''=±, ''5''==; 即 45.5 ± 3.7 pS (n = 10)。TRAAK 首次克隆论文的单通道斜率电导（AA 门控，尚无机械门控数据）。Fig 5F 图注另记 n=8，正文以 n=10 为准。','COS transient pIREScd8-TRAAK, inside-out, I-V slope 0-160 mV','10','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',184,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(768,'MAIC:BX:00768',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cell-attached single-channel at -40 mV (150 mM KCl) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 16','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,92.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'92.0','pS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','COS-7 (transfected)','COS-7',NULL,NULL,'150 mM KCl','150 mM KCl',-40.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00024','The single-channel conductances of the three K+ channels in DRG neurones were 104 ± 8 pS, 110 ± 7 pS, and 95 ± 18 pS at -40 mV similar to those of cloned TREK-1 (108 ± 7 pS), TREK-2 (113 ± 4 pS) and TRAAK (92 ± 16 pS), respectively, expressed in COS-7 cells.','Results (Thermosensitivity ... expressed in dorsal root ganglion neurones)','high','cloned TRAAK 在 COS-7 的单通道电导（作为 DRG native 的对照给出）。温度与 n 未在该值处明示（同文单通道在 24-37°C 测定；TRAAK 因极短开放幅度可变，温升系列中难以精测），误差类型未标注。','COS-7 transfected TRAAK, cell-attached, -40 mV',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',185,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(769,'MAIC:BX:00769',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cell-attached/inside-out single-channel at -40 mV | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 18','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,95.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'95.0','pS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','native','rat dorsal root ganglion (DRG) neuron',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,-40.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00025','The single-channel conductances of the three K+ channels in DRG neurones were 104 ± 8 pS, 110 ± 7 pS, and 95 ± 18 pS at -40 mV similar to those of cloned TREK-1 (108 ± 7 pS), TREK-2 (113 ± 4 pS) and TRAAK (92 ± 16 pS), respectively, expressed in COS-7 cells.','Results (Thermosensitivity ... DRG section); Fig 8','medium','DRG 原生 92-pS 通道经药理/物性匹配鉴定为 TRAAK（被碱液 pH 8.8、花生四烯酸与负压激活），非分子鉴定，confidence=medium。模式（cell-attached 或 inside-out）与温度（24/37°C）未逐一明示。','native DRG neuron TRAAK-like, -40 mV',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',185,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(770,'MAIC:BX:00770',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'continuous perfusion with heated solution, progressive heating 24°C→37°C',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,31.0,NULL,NULL,'31.0','degC','OTHER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','COS-7 (transfected)','COS-7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00026','The threshold for activation of TREK-1 and TRAAK were 25 ± 1°C and 31 ± 2°C, respectively.','Results; Fig 3B','medium','原文单位 ''°C''，按 TRAAK 轮裁决记 degC。非机械阈值：阈值为统计判据（该温度平均通道活性显著高于 24°C，见 TREK-2 段判据说明），非 Boltzmann 拟合中点，故按任务指示 row + schema_gap_flag=Y（thermal_threshold 无 DB 列）。TREK-1 的 25±1°C 为 paralog 值，归档不 row。','COS-7 transfected TRAAK, cell-attached, 24→37°C progressive heating',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',185,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(771,'MAIC:BX:00771',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cell-attached single-channel, [K+]in/[K+]out ~1, voltage steps to ±80 mV | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 5 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,93.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'93.0','pS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','native','rat trigeminal Aβ-afferent node of Ranvier axon',NULL,NULL,'symmetric K+ ([K+]in/[K+]out ~1)','symmetric K+ ([K+]in/[K+]out ~1)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00027','identified a major type of unitary IKleak currents with a large single channel conductance of 93 ± 5 pS at 80 mV and 118 ± 6 pS at -80 mV (n = 15), and weak inward rectification','Results; Fig 1G','medium','native nodal 单通道的分子身份为 TREK-1/TRAAK 混合（作者：''most likely formed as heteromeric TREK-1/TRAAK channels but the presence of homomeric TREK-1 and homomeric TRAAK cannot be excluded''），含 TRAAK 成分故 row，confidence=medium。Mean ± SEM（Fig 1 图注）。','native nodal K2P (trigeminal Aβ NR), cell-attached, +80 mV','15','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',186,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(772,'MAIC:BX:00772',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cell-attached single-channel, [K+]in/[K+]out ~1, voltage steps to ±80 mV | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 6 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,118.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'118.0','pS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','native','rat trigeminal Aβ-afferent node of Ranvier axon',NULL,NULL,'symmetric K+ ([K+]in/[K+]out ~1)','symmetric K+ ([K+]in/[K+]out ~1)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00028','identified a major type of unitary IKleak currents with a large single channel conductance of 93 ± 5 pS at 80 mV and 118 ± 6 pS at -80 mV (n = 15), and weak inward rectification','Results; Fig 1G','medium','同 +80 mV 行：native nodal TREK-1/TRAAK 混合身份（heteromer 最可能、不排除 homomer），含 TRAAK 成分故 row。Mean ± SEM。','native nodal K2P (trigeminal Aβ NR), cell-attached, -80 mV','15','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',186,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(773,'MAIC:BX:00773',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cell-attached single-channel I-V, transmembrane voltages to ±80 mV | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 12 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,100.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'100.0','pS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293 (transfected, TRAAK/mCherry)','HEK293',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00029','We also expressed TRAAK in HEK239 cells, which resulted in homomeric TRAAK channels with single channel conductance of 100 ± 12 pS (n = 6) at 80 mV and 67 ± 12 pS (n = 6) at -80 mV','Results; Fig 3E, F & H','high','原文 ''HEK239'' 为笔误（即 HEK293），quote 保留原词。Mean ± SEM（Fig 1 图注通用标注）。','HEK293 TRAAK homomer, cell-attached, +80 mV','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',186,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(774,'MAIC:BX:00774',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cell-attached single-channel I-V, transmembrane voltages to ±80 mV | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 12 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,67.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'67.0','pS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293 (transfected, TRAAK/mCherry)','HEK293',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00030','We also expressed TRAAK in HEK239 cells, which resulted in homomeric TRAAK channels with single channel conductance of 100 ± 12 pS (n = 6) at 80 mV and 67 ± 12 pS (n = 6) at -80 mV','Results; Fig 3E, F & H','high','原文 ''HEK239'' 为笔误（即 HEK293），quote 保留原词。Mean ± SEM。','HEK293 TRAAK homomer, cell-attached, -80 mV','6','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',186,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(775,'MAIC:BX:00775',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cell-attached single-channel I-V, transmembrane voltages to ±80 mV | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 7 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,87.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'87.0','pS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293 (cotransfected TREK-1/EGFP + TRAAK/mCherry)','HEK293',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00031','In contrast, when TREK-1 and TRAAK channels were co-expressed, a new type of unitary currents appeared which had single channel conductance of 87 ± 7 pS (n = 5) at 80 mV and 125 ± 6 pS (n = 8) at -80 mV','Results; Fig 3E, G & H','medium','heterodimer 构造（TREK-1/TRAAK 共表达异源二聚体，TRAAK 相关构造，按 TRAAK 轮裁决可 row）；电导与 native nodal K2P 相似，为 nodal 通道身份的对照。','HEK293 TREK-1+TRAAK coexpression heteromer, +80 mV','5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',186,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(776,'MAIC:BX:00776',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cell-attached single-channel I-V, transmembrane voltages to ±80 mV | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 6 (sem)','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,125.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'125.0','pS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293 (cotransfected TREK-1/EGFP + TRAAK/mCherry)','HEK293',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00032','In contrast, when TREK-1 and TRAAK channels were co-expressed, a new type of unitary currents appeared which had single channel conductance of 87 ± 7 pS (n = 5) at 80 mV and 125 ± 6 pS (n = 8) at -80 mV','Results; Fig 3E, G & H','medium','heterodimer 构造（TREK-1/TRAAK 共表达异源二聚体），+80 mV 行同。','HEK293 TREK-1+TRAAK coexpression heteromer, -80 mV','8','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',186,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "biophysics_experiment" VALUES(777,'MAIC:BX:00777',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cell-attached single-channel, pipette potentials +100 to -100 mV (symmetrical 150 mM KCl) | ERROR-AS-REPORTED: 3.2','CONDUCTANCE_ONLY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,65.4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'65.4','pS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'CELL_ATTACHED','HEK293 (transfected)','HEK293',NULL,7.3,'150 mM KCl, 1 mM MgCl2, 5 mM EGTA, 10 mM HEPES (symmetric)','150 mM KCl, 1 mM MgCl2, 5 mM EGTA, 10 mM HEPES',100.0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRAAK-00033','Unitary conductances of TRAAK and Td-TREK1/TRAAK are 65.4 ± 3.2 pS and 80.7 ± 1.9 pS at +100 mV and 110.9 ± 1.5 pS and 98.7 ± 3.9 pS at -100 mV, respectively (n = 10).','Results (Heterodimers of TREK/TRAAK Subunits...); Fig 5B','high','±100 mV 为 pipette 电位（cell-attached）。误差类型（SEM/SD）在 Fig 5 处未明示，留空。','HEK293 TRAAK homomer, cell-attached, +100 mV','10','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',187,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
