INSERT INTO "unmapped_measurement" VALUES(1,'MAIC:UM:00001',4,'pressure_threshold',8.0,'nN/um2','KEEP: in-situ stress midpoint (adjudicated 2026-08-21: reserve p50 for patch-clamp midpoints)','ASIC-00019','P ½ values were 15 ± 4 nN/μm 2 ( n = 3) and 8 ± 1 nN/μm 2 ( n = 17) in e1515 and wild-type animals, respectively.','Results, "Missense mutations in mec-10 and mec-4 decrease MRC amplitude" (supplemental Fig. 3C values quoted in text)','high','stimulus_type as-printed: mechanical (touch; pressure step via calibrated probe). recording_mode as-printed: in vivo whole-cell voltage clamp (touch receptor neuron). Native mechanoreceptor current (MRC) recorded in vivo from the PLM touch receptor neuron of C. elegans; current flows through the MEC-4/MEC-10(/MEC-2/MEC-6/UNC-24) DEG/ENaC transduction-channel complex. Channel attribution is genetic (mutant epistasis: mec-4 null animals lack MRCs while mec-10 deletion retains them; O''Hagan et al. 2005), so mechano_gating_contested=true on these native rows. Fitted mechanical midpoint of the normalized MRC pressure–response curve (probe calibrated per O''Hagan et al. 2005); rowed per the fitted-mechanical-midpoint ruling. | MAIN-AGENT RULING (re-applied after agent rewrite): kind p50->pressure_threshold (schema_gap) — stress-unit midpoint nN/um2 has no p50-family home; symmetric with the Chen-2016 ruling.','pressure_threshold_MRC_pressure_wt_celegans_plm_invivo','17','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',70,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "unmapped_measurement" VALUES(2,'MAIC:UM:00002',4,'pressure_threshold',15.0,'nN/um2','KEEP: in-situ stress midpoint (adjudicated 2026-08-21: reserve p50 for patch-clamp midpoints)','ASIC-00020','P ½ values were 15 ± 4 nN/μm 2 ( n = 3) and 8 ± 1 nN/μm 2 ( n = 17) in e1515 and wild-type animals, respectively.','Results, "Missense mutations in mec-10 and mec-4 decrease MRC amplitude" (supplemental Fig. 3C values quoted in text)','high','stimulus_type as-printed: mechanical (touch; pressure step via calibrated probe). recording_mode as-printed: in vivo whole-cell voltage clamp (touch receptor neuron). Native mechanoreceptor current (MRC) recorded in vivo from the PLM touch receptor neuron of C. elegans; current flows through the MEC-4/MEC-10(/MEC-2/MEC-6/UNC-24) DEG/ENaC transduction-channel complex. Channel attribution is genetic (mutant epistasis: mec-4 null animals lack MRCs while mec-10 deletion retains them; O''Hagan et al. 2005), so mechano_gating_contested=true on these native rows. Right-shifted pressure–response in e1515 (N-terminal S105F); u332 curves indistinguishable from wild type (no u332 P½ row). | MAIN-AGENT RULING (re-applied after agent rewrite): kind p50->pressure_threshold (schema_gap) — stress-unit midpoint nN/um2 has no p50-family home; symmetric with the Chen-2016 ruling.','pressure_threshold_MRC_pressure_mec-10_e1515_celegans_plm_invivo','3','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',70,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "unmapped_measurement" VALUES(3,'MAIC:UM:00003',4,'block_voltage',0.26,NULL,'KEEP: Woodhull electrical distance delta (dimensionless)','ASIC-00121','Insert shows voltage dependence of amiloride blockade for DELM-1. Data were fitted using a Woodhull model ( Woodhull, 1973 ) (δ = 0.26, n = 7).','Results (Fig. 7E legend, inset); running text: ''Amiloride block was voltage dependent (δ = 0.26, Fig. 7 E , inset)''','medium','stimulus_type as-printed: voltage steps + blocker. recording_mode as-printed: two-electrode voltage clamp. 无量纲 Woodhull 电距离 δ（阻塞剂进入孔道的电场分数）→ 归入 block_voltage（电压依赖性阻断参数）。kind 映射为判断性选择（词表中最贴近的家），如审查改判可移 archive。','block_voltage_woodhull-delta_amiloride_DELM-1_xenopus-oocyte','7','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',84,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "unmapped_measurement" VALUES(4,'MAIC:UM:00004',4,'pressure_threshold',4.5,'nN/um2','KEEP: in-situ stress midpoint (adjudicated 2026-08-21: reserve p50 for patch-clamp midpoints)','ASIC-00136','In addition, the half-maximal pressure (P1//2) for the mechanoreceptor current (MRC) differed slightly between poml-1 and wild-type TRNs (poml-1 P1/2 = 7.7 ± 0.8 nN/μm2 vs. wild-type P1/2 = 4.5 ± 0.7 nN/μm2, mean ± SD; Supplemental Figure S4D), but poml-1 mutations did not affect MRC peak amplitude or kinetics (Supplemental Figure S4E).','Results, ''MEC-6 and POML-1 are important for MEC-4 production and localization'' (values from Supplemental Fig. S4D)','high','Round ruling (new precedent): native channel-level fitted mechanical midpoint in stress units -> pressure_threshold. indentation-stimulus Boltzmann stress midpoint; stress-unit schema gap (p50=mmHg/t50=mN/m/x50=um have no stress home) — flagged schema_gap. mean ± SD. Native MEC-4/MEC-10 transduction complex in its own membrane (WT animals); round''s unique channel-level mechanical threshold in stress units. As-printed source typography ''P1//2'' in the quote is the XML rendering of P1/2. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','celegans_trn_native_mrc_indentation_p1-2_wt',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',90,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "unmapped_measurement" VALUES(5,'MAIC:UM:00005',4,'pressure_threshold',7.7,'nN/um2','KEEP: in-situ stress midpoint (adjudicated 2026-08-21: reserve p50 for patch-clamp midpoints)','ASIC-00137','In addition, the half-maximal pressure (P1//2) for the mechanoreceptor current (MRC) differed slightly between poml-1 and wild-type TRNs (poml-1 P1/2 = 7.7 ± 0.8 nN/μm2 vs. wild-type P1/2 = 4.5 ± 0.7 nN/μm2, mean ± SD; Supplemental Figure S4D), but poml-1 mutations did not affect MRC peak amplitude or kinetics (Supplemental Figure S4E).','Results, ''MEC-6 and POML-1 are important for MEC-4 production and localization'' (values from Supplemental Fig. S4D)','high','Round ruling: poml-1 value is a threshold SHIFT context rowed as its own pressure_threshold row (condition_key poml-1), not delta_p50 (delta_p50''s unit_db is mmHg-only). indentation-stimulus Boltzmann stress midpoint; stress-unit schema gap (p50=mmHg/t50=mN/m/x50=um have no stress home) — flagged schema_gap. mean ± SD; ~1.7x elevation vs WT with unchanged MRC peak amplitude/kinetics — consistent with reduced MEC-4 expression, not a changed channel. mechano_gating_contested: shift attributed via poml-1 null background (chaperone epistasis on MEC-4 expression level), channel complex itself WT MEC-4/MEC-10. [F-004:verbatim-semi] '';'' junction(s) confirmed in archived corpus (classified 2026-08-31)','celegans_trn_native_mrc_indentation_p1-2_poml-1-null',NULL,'LITERATURE','2026-11-08',90,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "unmapped_measurement" VALUES(6,'MAIC:UM:00006',6,'pressure_threshold',9.98,'mN/m','KEEP: proteoliposome first-opening tension threshold (not a midpoint; t50 column owns tension midpoints)','MSCL-EX-00090','In contrast, we found that Q65R increased the sensitivity of the channel to applied tension when reconstituted in azolectin liposomes, by reducing its activation threshold and thus making it easier to open (membrane tension required for the first channel opening: Q65R = 7.80 ± 0.19 mN/m, WT = 9.98 ± 0.30 mN/m (Fig. 4).','Results (lipid-dependent Q65E/Q65R sensitivity; Fig 4)','high','[supplemental_verified] [pool-external] 2026-11-07 landscape scan (PR #134) -> pool-external verification (data/mscl/literature/raw/pool_external_verified.json); supplemental-verified entry, in_benchmark=N. First-response detection threshold (tension for FIRST channel opening), NOT a Boltzmann midpoint -> pressure_threshold schema_gap (layer ruling: onset/first-opening values are never p50/t50). Tension computed by the paper via Laplace''s law from patch fluorometry (rhodamine-PE), not a direct stimulus readout — declared. n from Fig 4 legend (''n > 5 per mutant''). mean ± s.e.m. (figure legend). DURU ARCHIVE (not rowed): tau_act ''unclear'' — kinetics are central to the title but no tau/time-constant value in main text; MD ''kinetics'' are trajectory-level (pore diameter/water count vs time at 35 pN pulling + 30 mN/m tension), quoted sentence ''wild-type MscL and Q65R exhibited rapid and extensive pore opening over a shorter timeframe'' is qualitative -> no row. conductance ''unclear'' — no numeric in main text; Q65R ''affected the unitary conductance'' and Q65E flickering ''making it difficult to determine unitary conductance'' are referenced to supplement Fig S2 (supplement-only) -> no row. MscS numbers are reference-channel data (co-expressed/co-reconstituted internal standard; MscL/MscS ratio 1.33-1.84 = MscL-relative comparative quantitation) -> never rowed. EPR spin-label mobility and MD pore geometry are not channel parameters. Archive spans in literature/raw/extract_quotes_supplemental-v1.json.','liposome (azolectin + 0.1% rhodamine-PE) reconstituted E. coli MscL WT (Duru 2026), patch-fluorometry tension for first channel opening, Laplace''s law, +30 mV','>5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',130,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "unmapped_measurement" VALUES(7,'MAIC:UM:00007',6,'pressure_threshold',7.8,'mN/m','KEEP: proteoliposome first-opening tension threshold (not a midpoint; t50 column owns tension midpoints)','MSCL-EX-00091','In contrast, we found that Q65R increased the sensitivity of the channel to applied tension when reconstituted in azolectin liposomes, by reducing its activation threshold and thus making it easier to open (membrane tension required for the first channel opening: Q65R = 7.80 ± 0.19 mN/m, WT = 9.98 ± 0.30 mN/m (Fig. 4).','Results (lipid-dependent Q65E/Q65R sensitivity; Fig 4)','high','[supplemental_verified] [pool-external] 2026-11-07 landscape scan (PR #134) -> pool-external verification (data/mscl/literature/raw/pool_external_verified.json); supplemental-verified entry, in_benchmark=N. First-response detection threshold (tension for FIRST channel opening), NOT a Boltzmann midpoint -> pressure_threshold schema_gap (layer ruling: onset/first-opening values are never p50/t50). Tension computed by the paper via Laplace''s law from patch fluorometry (rhodamine-PE), not a direct stimulus readout — declared. n from Fig 4 legend (''n > 5 per mutant''). mean ± s.e.m. (figure legend). DURU ARCHIVE (not rowed): tau_act ''unclear'' — kinetics are central to the title but no tau/time-constant value in main text; MD ''kinetics'' are trajectory-level (pore diameter/water count vs time at 35 pN pulling + 30 mN/m tension), quoted sentence ''wild-type MscL and Q65R exhibited rapid and extensive pore opening over a shorter timeframe'' is qualitative -> no row. conductance ''unclear'' — no numeric in main text; Q65R ''affected the unitary conductance'' and Q65E flickering ''making it difficult to determine unitary conductance'' are referenced to supplement Fig S2 (supplement-only) -> no row. MscS numbers are reference-channel data (co-expressed/co-reconstituted internal standard; MscL/MscS ratio 1.33-1.84 = MscL-relative comparative quantitation) -> never rowed. EPR spin-label mobility and MD pore geometry are not channel parameters. Archive spans in literature/raw/extract_quotes_supplemental-v1.json.','liposome (azolectin + 0.1% rhodamine-PE) reconstituted E. coli MscL Q65R (Duru 2026), patch-fluorometry tension for first channel opening, Laplace''s law, +30 mV','>5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',130,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "unmapped_measurement" VALUES(8,'MAIC:UM:00008',6,'pressure_threshold',12.54,'pN/nm','KEEP: proteoliposome first-opening tension threshold, as-printed spelling (1 pN/nm = 1 mN/m exact equivalence, no conversion; not a midpoint)','MSCL-EX-00092','We observed the same loss of sensitivity when the mutant was reconstituted into azolectin liposomes, requiring a higher membrane tension for the channel first opening (Q65E:12.54 ± 0.52 pN/nm vs WT: 9.98 ± 0.30 mN/m) (Fig. 4B).','Results (lipid-dependent Q65E/Q65R sensitivity; Fig 4)','high','[supplemental_verified] [pool-external] 2026-11-07 landscape scan (PR #134) -> pool-external verification (data/mscl/literature/raw/pool_external_verified.json); supplemental-verified entry, in_benchmark=N. UNIT GLYPH HAZARD: printed as ''12.54 ± 0.52 pN/nm'' in the same sentence that prints WT as ''9.98 ± 0.30 mN/m''; 1 pN/nm = 1 mN/m is an exact unit-spelling equivalence (no numeric change) — unit stored AS-PRINTED pN/nm per the as-reported storage rule; readers comparing with mN/m rows apply the identity. First-response detection threshold (tension for FIRST channel opening), NOT a Boltzmann midpoint -> pressure_threshold schema_gap (layer ruling: onset/first-opening values are never p50/t50). Tension computed by the paper via Laplace''s law from patch fluorometry (rhodamine-PE), not a direct stimulus readout — declared. n from Fig 4 legend (''n > 5 per mutant''). mean ± s.e.m. (figure legend). DURU ARCHIVE (not rowed): tau_act ''unclear'' — kinetics are central to the title but no tau/time-constant value in main text; MD ''kinetics'' are trajectory-level (pore diameter/water count vs time at 35 pN pulling + 30 mN/m tension), quoted sentence ''wild-type MscL and Q65R exhibited rapid and extensive pore opening over a shorter timeframe'' is qualitative -> no row. conductance ''unclear'' — no numeric in main text; Q65R ''affected the unitary conductance'' and Q65E flickering ''making it difficult to determine unitary conductance'' are referenced to supplement Fig S2 (supplement-only) -> no row. MscS numbers are reference-channel data (co-expressed/co-reconstituted internal standard; MscL/MscS ratio 1.33-1.84 = MscL-relative comparative quantitation) -> never rowed. EPR spin-label mobility and MD pore geometry are not channel parameters. Archive spans in literature/raw/extract_quotes_supplemental-v1.json.','liposome (azolectin + 0.1% rhodamine-PE) reconstituted E. coli MscL Q65E (Duru 2026), patch-fluorometry tension for first channel opening, Laplace''s law, +30 mV','>5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',130,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
INSERT INTO "unmapped_measurement" VALUES(9,'MAIC:UM:00009',6,'pressure_threshold',34.57,'mmHg','KEEP: proteoliposome first-opening pressure threshold (not a midpoint; p50 column owns Boltzmann midpoints)','MSCL-EX-00093','We observed a ~60% increase in the amount of pressure required for channel first opening when reconstituted in negatively charged liposomes (Q65E: 55.75 ± 2.18 mmHg vs WT: 34.57 ± 2.14 mmHg), and a rightward shift of the activation curve of the channel (Fig. 4).','Results (Q65E in negatively charged liposomes; Fig 4)','high','[supplemental_verified] [pool-external] 2026-11-07 landscape scan (PR #134) -> pool-external verification (data/mscl/literature/raw/pool_external_verified.json); supplemental-verified entry, in_benchmark=N. First-response detection threshold (pressure for FIRST channel opening), NOT a Boltzmann midpoint -> pressure_threshold schema_gap (layer ruling). The ~60% Q65E-vs-WT increase of the same experiment is rowed separately as threshold_fold_shift. n from Fig 4 legend (''n > 5 per mutant''). mean ± s.e.m. DURU ARCHIVE (not rowed): tau_act ''unclear'' — kinetics are central to the title but no tau/time-constant value in main text; MD ''kinetics'' are trajectory-level (pore diameter/water count vs time at 35 pN pulling + 30 mN/m tension), quoted sentence ''wild-type MscL and Q65R exhibited rapid and extensive pore opening over a shorter timeframe'' is qualitative -> no row. conductance ''unclear'' — no numeric in main text; Q65R ''affected the unitary conductance'' and Q65E flickering ''making it difficult to determine unitary conductance'' are referenced to supplement Fig S2 (supplement-only) -> no row. MscS numbers are reference-channel data (co-expressed/co-reconstituted internal standard; MscL/MscS ratio 1.33-1.84 = MscL-relative comparative quantitation) -> never rowed. EPR spin-label mobility and MD pore geometry are not channel parameters. Archive spans in literature/raw/extract_quotes_supplemental-v1.json.','liposome (DOPC:DOPG 70:30) reconstituted E. coli MscL WT (Duru 2026), first channel opening pressure, +30 mV','>5','LITERATURE','2026-11-08',130,'2026-11-08 00:00:00.000000',NULL);
